window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":401,"title":"Chapter 401: Chapter 400 - Line Between the Weak and the Powerful","paragraphs":["\"This is a Watch Tower where some Elite Teams are stationed, monitoring the movements of those that are actually threats to our forces- Elite Behemoths.\"","The Grandmaster was explaining slowly as they got off the Prime Warship, their gazes only looking towards the Celestial Watch tower as they actually went past it to the region that its threats were abundant at!","The Watch Tower was built in an extremely unique manner, looking like a huge golden skyscr.a.p.er that pierced through the skies as its size passed the huge ancient trees around it.","The area in its immediate surroundings looked more like a base as numerous Prime Warsh.i.p.s were stationed, a few Celestials being seen moving in and out carefully.","\"Passing this Watch Tower means we directly put ourselves at risk of coming in contact with an Elite Behemoth, and any Tower that you pass will be considered a line that distinguishes the truly powerful and leaves the weak behind!\"","The expansive Prime Warship they traversed the long distances in would normally be stationed at these Towers, the Celestials moving to explore and hunt Behemoths themselves as the powerful vessels weren’t built for battling Behemoths. One would only achieve watching a Prime Warship get destroyed if they tried to pilot one to match an Elite Celestial Beast.","\"Stay close to me and pay close attention, I’ll walk you through your first hunt and show you exactly what to keep in mind when facing Behemoths that are proficient in Supreme Laws.\"","The members of the Righteous Fire Exploration Team nodded as even the boisterous Boru filled along with a serious expression, their hearts looking forward to seeing the strength of this wizened Grandmaster as he clashed with an Elite Behemoth!","Noah’s senses expanded around his surroundings as they passed through the guarded area of the Watch Tower, venturing further into the mystical forest of the Celestial Realm that seemed to have a foreboding silence!","One would normally hear the sounds of animals moving around, a cacophony of sounds surrounding them as they walked through such a large forest. But all that met them was silence as even the small critters knew not to make noises in this region where powerful beings roamed.","Noah thought about the words of the Grandmaster, thinking of the invisible line that they were now passing which would put them into the field of truly powerful creatures of the Celestial Realm as he prepared himself!","---","As Noah’s main body moved across the deeper regions in the Celestial Realm, his clone continued to carry out a destructive campaign in the First Realm of Hell that was reducing the numbers of Infernals at a rapid pace.","His strength that was able to stand against beings half a step into the Domain Expansion Realm was now bullying the poor droves of Infernals that were defeated as if they were bugs! This was especially so because of the armor he adorned, which had a spectacular ability that he enjoyed watching unfold as he moved rapidly across the First Realm of Hell.","The ridiculously powerful passive ability given by the complete Incandescent Flameborn Set that released a wide ring of flames around him every second acted like an attack that simply swept across an entire area that he appeared in within seconds!","It made for a ridiculous sight where he teleported amidst hundreds of Infernals, a terrifying ring of flames rushed out from him that nearly incinerated half while all those remaining were placed under the Soul Immolation effect that made them take 1000% more damage from skills of the fire element. Those that survived would only remain that way for another second before they were wiped away completely, either by another ring of flames or the terrible abilities of the Lesser Cthulhu as Portals of Terror were cast freely.","The clone had so many means possible as he went all out, freely using the mana gifted to him as he worked efficiently to rack up skill points and increase the percentage of the Infernal Lord title.","Already, in the past day that he had been moving, the Infernal Lord Title had advanced over 50%!","This goal was getting close to being completed as he also went along to achieve smaller goals, the small body of the Draconic Fire Behemoth he was bringing with him as a pet continuing to be fed Cores as its Rank already reached Transcendent over this last day. It was undergoing power leveling at a rate that nobody around Noah had the chance to, its body continuing to grow larger and larger as it began adopting the fearsome expression of a powerful Behemoth Noah had fought before.","\"Draco, let’s go!\"","His miniaturized form teleported to the back of the Dragon as he called it under the impromptu name he had given it in the past day, this fearsome Behemoth going on to be called Draco as it roared resonantly while Noah began to use a variety of skills above it!","From the series of abilities in <<Absolute Sin>> to the skill tree of the [Kin of the Ancients] and the abilities of the Vampyre Progenitor, he played around with as many skills as possible as colorful rays of destruction continued to rain down towards the Infernals in the First Realm of Hell.","While this was occurring is a similar Realm that held entirely different levels of Infernals, a being with horns that formed into the shape of a crown was floating with his back towards the blazing ground of another realm of Hell, his aura causing the numerous Void and Soul Forging Realm Infernals below him to quake in fear.","He was lazily floating in the burning skies of the Second Realm of Hell when another being just like him teleported to his side, her face that of cruel excitement as she spoke out.","\"It seems like the upcoming little Lord is working even faster in the First Realm. It should not be long before he joins us. What do you think, Rykker?\"","The newly arriving Infernal Lord asked the other Lord floating in the blazing skies, the being called Rykker that replied with a lazy smile without even turning to look towards her direction.","\"Azula, you always were a tad bit too excited for these things. Let them take their time. You know that the moment they fully hold the title of the 9th Infernal Lord, it means our future is about to become that much busier.\"","The cruel expression on Azula’s face gained an amorous expression as her hands eerily ran through her body, her head raised high with an expression of joy as she replied.","\"Why yes, I wonder who the little baby Lord will be...Aah!\"","The attention of numerous powerful Infernal Lords sensed a particular event nearing as they welcomed the future, the being in question not knowing about any of this as he enjoyed the feeling of power while coursing through the First Realm of Hell!"]},{"number":402,"title":"Chapter 402: Chapter 401 - Chaos Behemoth","paragraphs":["In a scene of a fantastical adventure, Noah and the party of Celestials he followed went deeper into the foreboding ancient trees that were scintillating with essence, the atmospheric levels in this area being off the charts as Noah shook his head exasperatingly.","\"When you become truly powerful in the future, venturing deeper into the Celestial Realm and cultivating in areas that are steeped in converging essence will become the norm. But that is only if you can handle the enemies you might come across in these deeper regions!\"","The Grandmaster spoke carefully as he led them through the shimmering foliage and trees, his gaze cautiously looking around as they went further in.","They had been walking for a few hours already, being far away from the Watch Tower where the Prime Warship they traveled here with was stationed.","\"Be ready. I can already sense the aura of chaos begin to permeate the surroundings. Tell me, what can you perceive?\"","This question was directed to Athena and Noah as the Grandmaster stared at them with an expression of a teacher asking his students.","Noah expanded his senses out slowly as the abundant fate lines in his body thrummed, using their unique power to sense the opposing law they stood against.","It felt like his eyes were expanding in multiple directions, a slight thing golden wave releasing from him at the center as it flew forward. Soon enough, it came in contact with something murky and dark, something that felt wild, its composition constantly changing as if it could not decide exactly what it wanted to be!","\"This is...chaos?\"","\"Can you feel it? The element of unpredictability. An element that is dark and constantly changing as if it could never be reigned in.\"","The words of the Grandmaster entered one ear and left the other as Noah continued to expand his senses outwards, observing more of this energy of chaos as very quickly, he came across an area where an incredible and opposite amount of this aura of chaos was congregated!","ROAAAR!","A fearsome roar shook the air around them as the Grandmaster laughed.","\"You spread your aura too far and it has found us as well. Be ready, and watch!\"","RUMBLE!","The overwhelming feeling of power began to descend down to their position as the Celestial Beast that had sensed them neared, the oppressive aura it released making Noah feel suffocated.","WAA!","The foliage and ancient trees that were extremely tough were parted aside like nothing as a magnificent creature made its appearance in front of them. Noah’s eyes shone with the reflection of this spectacular Celestial Beast that had the immense aura of chaos all over its body!","What stood in front of him was something that was only described in stories, an enormous winged tiger that was steeped in glimmering darkness all over its body, a ferocious face with sparkling white teeth and a monstrous body that neared 60 meters!","[Dark Winged Chaos Tiger].","The powerful name of this foe floated above its head as the Planetary System continued to actively portray the information gathered around Noah visually, the identity of this monstrous Celestial Beast being made clear.","Its gaze was that of extreme cruelty as its dark eyes gazed towards their group and focused on the Grandmaster, the Chaos Behemoth noticing this was the major threat as it did something horrendous right away.","[Domain of Chaos].","RUMBLE!","The clear and crisp voice of a domineering Celestial Beast rang out around them as from it, a storm of chaotic energies began to bloom!","\"HMPH!\"","The body of the Grandmaster seemed to get larger in Noah’s eyes as this wizened old man replied with a move of his own.","[Domain of Fate]!","RUMBLE!","CLASH!","From the bodies of the terrifying Domain Expansion Realm Experts, their respective Domains were released as a powerful clash of opposite elements smashed into each other and fought for control!","WAAA!","The air seemed to be crying out as it withstood this pressure from two colliding domains, Noah’s eyes focusing on the body of the Grandmaster and the Dark Winged Chaos Tiger as his heart shook. These were genuine Domain Expansion Realm experts! Not a being half a step or barely reaching, but genuine ones who had proper Domains established!","Now normally, a Behemoth at the same rank would always be more powerful than their human counterpart. So this Dark Winged Chaos Tiger should have been immensely more powerful than this single Grandmaster at the peak of Domain Expansion Realm, right?","Wrong!","RUMBLE!","The battle between the two domains was actually in favor of the Grandmaster, the clash ever so slowly pushing the Chaos Domain of the Dark Winged Chaos Tiger back as it roared furiously towards them!","\"Watch carefully, O you with Noble Fates. Watch what your level of power soon needs to reach in order for you to live to your full potential.\"","The words of the Grandmaster rang in Noah and Athena’s minds as a golden light began to permeate from his body.","Noah watched closely as he observed the rising of numerous Fate Lines to the surface of the wizened old man’s body, his long white beard swaying with the wind as Noah’s eyes opened in shock at the aurora of golden Fate Lines emitting from him!","One hundred thousand...two hundred thousand...four hundred thousand!","What!","This shocking reveal reminded Noah of the esteemed title of Grandmaster as the number of Fate Lines he could count on this old man’s body continued to grow ever so larger!","Athena looked towards the Grandmaster with a sharp look as a longing expression appeared on her face, this War Princess that was nearing one hundred thousand fate lines herself looking at this powerful teacher in front of her with a passion.","As the clash between the two Domains continued, Noah came to fully count the revealed Fate Lines coursing through the body of the Grandmaster.","The number was ridiculous as shockingly, this Grandmaster Vredral held over six hundred thousand Fate Lines!","600,000!","A shocking number when compared to his own that was currently slightly over 20,000, and even higher than the monstrous Athena that neared one hundred thousand.","But this was the strength of a Grandmaster that stood near the top of the food chain, someone acting with a few other Grandmasters to control the 7th Celestial Star!","This was Grandmaster Vredral!"]},{"number":403,"title":"Chapter 403: Chapter 402 - An Old Man Flexes","paragraphs":["[Smite of Liberation].","A soft whisper could be heard in the wind as the words of a skill Noah was familiar with was cast, yet an entering different feeling spread out through the entire area as the skies split apart, an exquisitely designed golden sword that seemed very corporeal coming out of the shattered sky with a magnificent aura as it targeted the Dark Winged Chaos Tiger that continued to fight with its [Domain of Chaos]!","SHAA!","The enormous wings of the Dark Winged Chaos Tiger flapped serenely as its body disappeared into particles of darkness, its domain being wiped away as the Blade of Liberation that was multiple sizes larger and more physical compared to what Noah and Athena could cast smashing into the area and burning up any aura of chaos in the surroundings.","WAA!","Heavy winds released as the opposing laws of fate and chaos came together, the magnificently dark shimmering body of the Dark Winged Chaos Tiger rematerializing in the skies as it glanced down towards them with an expression akin to looking at ants.","\"Arm yourselves with Empyrean Armament, and watch what else you can do with these skills as you amass more fate lines.\"","Grandmaster Vredral spoke cooly as he stretched his neck, seemingly getting ready to go all out as numerous Empyrean Guards that had a wild aura were summoned, their presence soon turning to rays of light as they moved to wrap around the body of the wizened old man!","A bright golden light pushed out any remaining aura of chaos as an exquisitely designed armor appeared on the body of the Grandmaster, his voice ringing out again as he now wielded in his hands two pulsing golden hammers.","\"Crixus was genius enough that he was able to show variations in the abilities of [Fate’s Guardian] when he just began amassing Fate Lines, but the possibilities of what you can make these abilities do only increases as the number of Fate Lines breaks into a certain point.\"","The old man was teaching as he fought, the golden armor and weapons surrounding him being filled with runic inscriptions that were not normally seen when Athena or others cast the abilities of Fate’s Guardian!","This was something attainable by those with a large number of Fate Lines, something that Noah had already begun doing because of his usage of Skill Points!","RUMBLE!","The Dark Winged Chaos Tiger took the threatening atmosphere of fate as a threat, its body expanding as it seemingly became even larger, an attack being thrown from its mouth as vicious winds began to rage around them.","[Chaotic Cyclones]!","VOOM! VOOM!","Numerous terrifying cyclones of darkness began to rush towards them, Grandmaster Vredral looking at them cooly as the other members of the Righteous Fire Exploration Team were equipped with they Armament from Fate’s Guardian.","\"When you get to this stage, you will bypass the stage of passively using Fate Lines to augment your attacks and...\"","THRUM!","The body of the old man seemed to trembled with power as the roiling Lines of Fate became high strung and tight, Noah observing the stellar essence of fate actually leaving from these Fate Lines and going towards the hammers in each of the Grandmaster’s hands.","\"...become able to actively use the strength of Fate as you momentarily take control of the Fate Lines in your body and release pure Fate Energy.\"","BOOM! BOOM!","The golden hammers in his hands waved towards the oncoming Chaotic Cyclones as a scintillating golden aura of fate shot forth from them, smashing into the cyclones as making them disappear as if they were nothing!","ROAR!","The furious roar of the Dark Winged Chaos Tiger could be heard as even more cyclones rained down, the shining lights of fate energy being swung from the Grandmaster only increasing as the battle against the Chaos Behemoth was in full swing.","\"You puny beings and your incoherent handling of fate, learn what it means to actually comprehend a law! [Ignition of Chaos- Disordered Rays]!\"","The magnificent voice of the Dark Winged Chaos Tiger rang in their ears as the sky above them changed colors and darkened, numerous dark rays of light blotting out the skies as they began rushing towards them dangerously.","The [Domain of Fate] that wrapped around them from the Grandmaster pulsed strongly, the old man himself breathing out as his body bulged up suddenly, the hammers in his hands enlarging as he spoke out seriously.","\"Defend!\"","The members of the Righteous Fire Exploration team followed these words right away as their own bodies lit up with defensive skills, Noah hoisting up the golden shield on his left hand as he covered a majority of his body and prepared for the dark rays of light shooting down!","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","The earth shook as the horrendous attacks landed, the sneaky Dark Winged Chaos Tiger not giving them a chance to react as his body disappeared in the skies and reappeared to their left side, right next to Boru who was defending from a dark ray of light!","\"Boru!\"","\"What!\"","The members of the team quickly turned their heads as they saw the mountainous claw of the Dark Winged Chaos Tiger smashing down, knowing that even the strong Boru would not be able to withstand this crafty attack as they tried to speedily move towards him.","But...they had no need to as at this moment of life and death for Boru, calm words reached permeated the surrounding as the golden aura of fate bloomed toward the oncoming dark claw.","\"You’re leaving yourself wide open, beasty.\"","ZOOM!","The words of Grandmaster Vredral were accompanied by a rushing golden spear rod of enormous size, its tip passing a few inches in front of Boru’s shocked face as it pierced the oncoming claw and stopped it in this tracks, dark blood flowing out as at this moment, tens of similarly enormous spears rained down on the attacking Dark Winged Chaos Tiger as unknowingly, this powerful Grandmaster Vredral had cast [Judgment] without anyone’s knowledge!","ROAR!!!"]},{"number":404,"title":"Chapter 404: Chapter 403 - 100%!","paragraphs":["THUNK! THUNK!","A fearsome impact of spears shining with the essence of fate smashed into the body of the Dark Winged Chaos Tiger as the sharp eyes of an old monster followed the trajectory of the beast that had been hit with his attacks.","The rest of the Righteous Fire Exploration Team reacted as their bodies lit up with colorful colors, their own versions of Blades of Liberation and sharp spears from [Judgment] erupting out as they layered their attacks on top of the Grandmaster’s!","ROAR!","The fearsome roar of the Dark Winged Chaos Tiger erupted out as its body rotated rapidly in the air, a storm of chaos elements erupting out that tainted the incoming attacks layered with the law of fate and rapidly dispersed them.","Near its neck and at the center of its claw, huge gashes lay open as dark blood freely poured out, dark energies wriggling around the wounds but the essence of fate still lingering behind and preventing any healing from taking place!","HMM!","The Domain of Fate that the Grandmaster at the Domain Expansion Realm could use expanded even more rapidly as the aura of chaos around the Dark Winged Chaos Tiger took a hit, the glimmering golden colors filling their environment as the eyes of the Celestial Beast exploded outwards with even more chaotic elements!","---","As a battle continued in the far region of the Celestial Realm against a Chaos Behemoth, a campaign of slaughter was soon coming to an end in the Infernal Realm as Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone moved with even more vigor!","In the last few hours, the percentage in front of the Title of Infernal Lord had steadily passed 90%, the number of skill points he currently had also passed 1,800!","It was a ridiculous set of numbers to imagine as he moved even faster after that, the percentage only increasing at a faster rate as he found newer ways to torment the Infernals.","\"Haha Draco, burn them all!\"","The young Dragon he was riding on top of that had now reached the Void Realm after continuing to be fed the cores in Noah’s Expansive Space was over 30 meters, its size becoming ever so terrifying as it skipped levels senselessly. Noah had even given it one of the few Soul Rank Cores he was saving to help it achieve an even faster breakthrough into the Void Rank!","Draco heard the command as a determined expression covered its fearsome face, its chest bulging out as it breathed in and gathered essence, its elevation in the skies coming lower as it sped forth like a bullet train and then opened its wide jaws, releasing an extremely intense flame.","BOOOOOOM!","Leaving behind sonic booms, Draco flitted across the skies while raining down blazing flames that smashed into the Infernals with both speed and horrendous destruction, the flight path of the dragon leaving behind a straight line of hellish flames devouring everything within it as Noah laughed gleefully at the firepower of this pet!","The figure of his clone teleported from Draco’s head as he appeared in the middle of panicking infernals a few miles away, his gaze on a skill under the [Kin of Ancients] that he had loved using recently.","<strong>[Blood Rage] (5/5) :: A destructive storm of blood begins to rotate with you at the center, raging with the capabilities of disintegrating all enemies caught within. Affected Area- 300 meters. </strong>","Without a second delay and before the surrounding Infernals could even react, the words escaped his lips rapidly.","[Blood Rage].","RUMBLE!","Large amounts of blood erupted from him as they began to rotate and expand around him, the speed of its rotations and expansions only increasing every millisecond as they soon covered an area of 100 meters, and then fully covered 300 meters in a dense atmosphere of a bloody storm that began shredding every single Infernal in this 300 meter area!","Draco stopped in the skies with its powerful wings outstretched, watching this destructive storm of blood shred muscles and bones into nothingness as he felt the aura of his Master disappear from that location and appear elsewhere again while casting the same skill, and an explosion of blood erupting out once more as this repeated.","Far across the Infernal Realm, the summoned Arch Lich Ra’Zan was still moving with a Legion of Undead and the powerful Abyssal Undead, while the mystical summoned Ancients were in another location letting out their deadly attacks that popped the heads of the Infernals like watermelons!","This coordinated attack of the summons and Noah himself had made something that should have happened much later come to fruition sooner, the percentage of the Title of Infernal Lord inching ever so closer to completion!","SHAA!","Draco felt the aura of his master appear above his head once more as he felt the strong hands palpating with energies of Aether land on his scales, hearing the words that made it tremble with a feeling of unfairness.","\"Let’s burn them again!\"","\"...Master, my mana is still recovering.\"","Draco turned his head down shamefully as he flew through the skies, only spurts of flames leaving his mouth as he had been using Dragon’s Breath numerous times the past few hours, his energy reserves nearly depleted!","This young Dragon was born with innate knowledge, and knew what was common sense and what was not. Seeing his master senselessly use mana like it was nothing these past days had made it realize the first lesson in its short life.","’My Master is too much of a monster that even the enormous reserves of a Draconic Behemoth cannot compare.’","The first lesson that Draco learned was that no matter how much it grew, it would most likely never reach the level of having similar mana reserves as his master!","Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone was about to console the feelings of the dragon that was feeling down when he felt a minute change that completely overhauled and filled his entire senses.","His gaze quickly turned towards the stat panel as he looked at the percentage next to the title.","[Noah Osmont][Title(s): Infernal Lord(100%)]","[Bloodline(s): Vampyre Progenitor(Awakening)]","[Fate Line(s) : 26,613]","[Origin Core(s) : Fire-2]","[Vitality: VOID]","[Focus: - ]","[Strength: VOID]","[Law(s) : Water-11%, Space-8%, Fate-.26%, Fire-12%]","...","Unwittingly, in the last few seconds, the percentage in front of the Infernal Lord Title had reached 100%!"]},{"number":405,"title":"Chapter 405: Chapter 404 - Infernal Lord!","paragraphs":["At certain points in time, a historic event occurs that later goes on to affect many things on a grand scale. Sometimes there is an audience when such an event happens, other times it occurs in an unknown corner where nobody is actually there to tell the tale.","But the major thing remained the same, and it was that these historic events would go on to forever change the way things were, where those involved can never bring anything back the way it once was.","In the unknown corner of the First Infernal Realm, columns of dark red lights shot forth in all directions, their targets being a singular being floating in the air. In the blazing skies, one could observe the large body of a Draconic Fire Behemoth being pushed aside by these red columns of lights as they released an inviolable energy that was directed towards a single figure!","In the distance, the eerie bodies of three Ancients looked at this scene with shining lights, their gazes being one that were shockingly able to understand what was happening. Their intrusion was joined by an Arch Lich that flew in on a Bone Dragon, a legion of Undead following closely behind as they simply stared patiently as their Master underwent a transformation.","The moment that the percentage next to the Infernal Lord Title had reached 100%, these brilliant columns of light shot forth from every corner of the Infernal Realm as they held Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone in place, a unique energy being passed through these columns and into the clone, where this energy then traversed space and began following the invisible connection that allowed Noah to use this clone as an extension of his own limbs- this energy actually followed that connection as it began entering his main body that was an insurmountable distance away in the Celestial Realm and currently battling a Chaos Behemoth!","RUMBLE!","Noah’s main body felt a shocking jolt as the energy traversed through the millions of miles across space and began wrapping around his core, his thoughts moving rapidly as he focused his attention on the ability of the Vampyre Progenitor, [Unique Origin], as he quickly began to cover up the unique energy threatening to erupt from his body!","Grandmaster Vredral’s face that was focused on the Dark Winged Chaos Tiger turned towards Noah momentarily as he blinked confusion away, his senses almost picking up on something dangerous that he had felt a few times before.","ROAR!","The counterattack of the Celestial Beast bought his attention back as he coordinated the movements of the Righteous Fire Exploration Team, their attacks flying out as they valiantly changed positions constantly while facing the unpredictable Chaos Behemoth. During the fight, Athena’s voice would occasionally ring out as she herself directed her teammates, her eyes shining a unique color as she read the movements of this powerful beast with ease!","Noah kept up the pace of the battle as his mind and body was experiencing a horrific change, the energy threatening to spill out any moment as he continued pouring mana into the [Unique Origin] skill to make sure what he showed outside of his body was only the energy and aura of a Celestial and nothing else.","The energy that traversed space from the clone in the Infernal Realm and into his body was wrapping around his very origin, the large blue Origin Core that had streaks of gold beginning to gain numerous red streaks that were quickly taking over as seconds passed!","On top of this unique energy changing his core, a portion of it went to his mind as a large inflow of memories unique only to those gaining the title of Infernal Lord were thrust to the deepest recesses of his memories.","In the Infernal Realm, the red beams of light only intensified as while Noah’s main body was pushing down any changes from showing through [Unique Origin], the extension of his limbs that was the clone experienced the full changes as all the transformation skills that were cast became canceled, the clear pale skin showing itself brilliantly and red runic sigils began to course below them!","The most prominent change was above his head, where one could see numerous rising protrusions that were slowly forming into the shape of a crown. Such a crown was only apparent on 8 other beings, and it was a crown that stood for a great significance!","RUMBLE!","The inflow of energies and memories only continued as time passed, the clone continuing to undergo visible changes as Noah’s main body underwent hidden ones, the continuing inpouring of power also beginning to shoot his rank up as the shackles of the Void Realm began to be broken away without even the use of absorbing a large number of cores.","The more seconds that passed, the more profound memories that entered into Noah’s mind as his expression was that of shock at first, then becoming stern, and ultimately becoming cold!","This was best portrayed by the Ancient Blood Clone as the more that the memories continued to pour in, the colder its expression became as a shocking secret was revealed to Noah!","The Novus Galaxy! The Light Expanse, the Dark Expanse, and the Letalis Expanse dwelling within it! The Infernals, the Celestials, and the Terrors that moved within it. Memories that were uniquely set aside for the special beings known as Infernal Lords continued to pour into Noah’s mind as the cold expression of the Ancient Blood Clone continued to grow colder, his mouth letting out a single word that seemed to depict his tumultuous mental state right at this moment with this influx of new information.","\"...f.u.c.k.\"","---","At this moment in time as the process of the coronation of a new Infernal Lord began, the truly powerful beings across the Novus Galaxy came to attention as they looked across the vicissitudes of space and towards a certain location.","From the Light Expanse to the Dark Expanse, and even the much wider Letalis Expanse- numerous auras awoke for this brief period in time as they felt the tides of change approaching!"]},{"number":406,"title":"Chapter 406: Chapter 405 - Signs of a New Era","paragraphs":["Across the multiple Celestial Stars, those that were considered at the top most positions were the ones that received the signal first, their power being the one that amassed the numerous benefits that all those below them brought in.","Whenever a directive or a mission was released by the Celestials that went on to influence a small portion of the Light Expanse, the rise in understanding of Fate and Fate Lines would go towards those that were responsible for initiating such an event.","For the missions passed down to destroy worlds or to save them, for the recent changes to allow the inhabitants living in the Light Expanse to enter the Celestial Realm...all of these events had their own cause and effect, the influence of fate they produced being taken in the most by those that actually initiated all of these things.","So the heads of the numerous Celestial Stars felt the significant and rapid rise of the chaos element first, their abilities under <Herald of Fate> extremely proficient in detecting wide ranging changes, especially those that dealt with laws!","But aside from these powerful Grandmasters standing atop these Celestial Stars, there were also a few beings that stood above them- three to be precise!","They would be considered the ones termed the Founders of the Celestial organization, the beings that made it possible for the Celestials to be where they are today.","One was chained in a golden cage beneath a certain star, another was in an unknown location, and the last one...was relaxing in a paradisiacal atmosphere deep in the Celestial Realm!","In this paradisiacal atmosphere where the mystical aurora of coagulating essence was abundant, a single man who looked to be in the prime of his life was lying back on the head of a mountainous creature that was a few hundred meters tall. This creature was one of fantasy, commonly heard about as a mythical beast with a shining white horn protruding from its head, and expansive white wings expanding on its back.","Being a mixture of a Pegasus and a Unicorn, this monstrous Celestial Behemoth called an Alicorn was blankly walking forward as this single being sat atop its head comfortably!","The being in question, one of the three Founders of the Celestials, had a wide smile appear on his calm face as his abilities showed the indication that the coming of a new Infernal Lord they were all expecting for had actually come to fruition faster than anticipated.","The Founder crossed his arms in thought as numerous bursts of information appeared on his mind, a few words leaving his mouth that only he would be privy to.","\"Well, at least it is becoming slightly more exciting once more.\"","He used his palm to pat the head of the enormous Behemoth he stood on, a unique energy shooting from his hands and entering the thick skin of the Alicorn easily as he spoke with an enthusiastic tone, the significance of the event that had just occurred seemingly not bothering him one bit!","\"Little horse, let’s go find another one of your little brothers for lunch. It’s been a few days since I’ve tasted a Supreme Behemoth.\"","OOOO!","A blank roar released from the Alicorn as it followed the given command, its enormous body turning into shades of scintillating golden lights as it moved forward at a speed even faster than light, trenching even deeper in the Celestial Realm!","---","In the Letalis Expanse, a moving mass of a being that was the size of large planets had its red eyes staring in a certain direction. As it moved across the vastness of space, its dreadful power was expressed outwards as a swirling mass of destructive elements and Aether pulsed from it. One could distinctly observe the purple-blue color of Aether lighting up the large sections of this being’s body, star-sized tentacles and feelers only seeming much more terrifying in this light. The bulging red eyes were the ones that would draw someone in the most, holding a unique charm and terror that very few could handle. These red eyes seemingly having a light of conflicting emotions as a thought passed through this being’s mind.","’Was such a thing even necessary for you to do? What exactly do you hope to achieve with all of these events?’","The thoughts of the always slumbering being were awoken briefly as it sensed the rise of the last Infernal Lord, knowing that this indicated for a new era on the Novus Galaxy, where things would begin moving yet again towards a certain direction.","Last time, this being, this Terror, interfered and actually brought an end to an Era!","It ended the War of the Righteous as it hoped the direction of things could play out differently, but it seems like they were still set to head towards the same direction.","’Very well. Do what you must. There will be no interference from me this time around, even if all of these ignorant creatures kill themselves.’","Its thoughts came to a stop as its red eyes looked upwards, where even those that were knowledgeable would never be able to understand exactly what it was looking at.","RUMBLE!","A fearsome {{Authority}} that spanned tens of thousands of miles spread out as it returned to its task, moving across the Letalis Expanse as its red eyes gradually closed yet again!","In farther reaches of space elsewhere, a similarly huge planet sized creature that held a different physiology than the aforementioned one also had similar thoughts, its attention eventually going on to what it was previously doing.","This was just another one of the many truly powerful creatures that noticed the coronation of the last Infernal Lord and felt the beginning of a new Era, each of these powerful creatures having their own thoughts as they felt the changes and prepared or returned to what they were doing calmly!","In the First Infernal Realm, the Ancient Blood Clone continued to feel the changes that it and the main body’s physiology was going through, a stellar red crown created from his own protrusions on his head lying grandly above him.","He held a devilish charm as he felt his main body stably entering the Soul Forging Realm, the clone’s aura changing as well. He began to feel the laws of the Infernal Realm wrap around him as he experienced something that the advancing Aberration had tried to do months ago before its life was ended by Athena.","The clone was ascending from the first Infernal Realm and into the one above it where multiple Infernal Lords resided!"]},{"number":407,"title":"Chapter 407: Chapter 406 - Shocking Knowledge","paragraphs":["As the coronation of the last Infernal Lord neared its completion, a stern look came upon Grandmaster Vredral as he also finally perceived this overpowering rise in chaos!","Athena’s face changed a few seconds later, her face also turning grim as she stared at the Grandmaster for confirmation.","ROAR!","The Dark Winged Chaos Tiger continued to be hit with multiple attacks as at this moment, Grandmaster Vredral’s power began rising up wildly, raining down even more attacks as he utilized the golden hammers on his hands to release deadly Fate Essence.","\"We have to wrap this up, something has happened.\"","His energy bubbled as enormous Blades of Liberation pierced through the skies, their deadly edges aiming towards the Chaos Behemoth rapidly changing positions as it continued to be swarmed from attacks of the members of the Righteous Fire Exploration Team.","Noah’s body also began rising in power as in the middle of all of this as his body stepped into the Soul Forging Realm, he used [Unique Origin] to portray a breakthrough occurring right at this moment as the essence his body gave off continued to rise and pierce through the wall of the Void Rank!","A surprised expression appeared on the somber Grandmaster as he nodded.","\"Good! Keep going!\"","RUMBLE!","The fierce battle continued as more attacks rained down, Noah himself officially stepping into the Soul Forging Realm in the eyes of the Celestials as his clone ascended from one Infernal Realm to another.","---","The 5 Infernals Realms were spread out over a wide area in the Novus Galaxy. The lowest tiered one, the First Infernal Realm, had its gate in the Light Expanse. The Second Infernal Realm was located in the Dark Expanse, the Fourth one being at the border of the Dark and Light Expanse.","The remaining two Infernal Realms where the most powerful Infernals and Infernal Lords resided were located in the Letalis Expanse that was filled with danger and mystery!","Noah’s clone ascended into the Second Infernal Realm that was located in the Dark Expanse, his body opening its eyes and spreading its senses as he found himself in familiar skies that seemed to hold a tinge of difference.","The surrounding atmosphere was much more dense than the First Realm, and he could observe huge structures in the distance that looked like devilish towering cities. The number of Infernals was not as many as in the droves of weak ones in the First Hell, but he could sense the aura of many Void and Soul Rank Infernals in the nearby surroundings!","OOOM!","Before he even got his bearings, he sensed the rapid appearance of an aura of two powerful beings rushing towards his position, the power he sensed from them being something he had never actually come across before.","It was a level of power not at the Soul or Domain Expansion Realm, but the realm above that! These two Infernal Lords that were on the Second Infernal Realm and considered to be two of the weaker Infernal Lords were standing stably at the peak of the World Rank!","From the Void to Soul, from Soul to Domain, and finally from the Domain and into the World Rank. A rank where the beings at this stage singularly had the power to destroy worlds.","These were the first two beings at this level that Noah had met, and they were the Infernal Lords ranked 7th and 8th!","WAA!","Their arrival was announced grandly as their bodies pulsed with a power that Noah now found familiar, this power being the unique essence of Infernals that he had only been absorbing, but had now also become a part of him! The bodies of the Infernal Lords release a unique atmosphere as he could barely perceive an oppressive field of power and chaos that was always surrounding them. Making any beings that neared feel a sense of suffocation!","\"My oh my... the new lord is actually not fully an Infernal, and is especially weak...\"","The curvaceous woman that held a pronounced crown similar to Noah and the other figure standing by her side spoke, her words sultry as her body curved magnificently while she spoke. Her words seemed sultry, but her power was surreal as Noah knew the identity of the two beings in front of him to be genuine Infernal Lords!","He nodded towards them as he paid respects, the woman smiling while the devilishly handsome figure of the male Infernal Lord looked gruff while glancing towards him up and down before he spoke.","\"I care not of your power now, just whether you understand your role in the future. Do you know why you are here?\"","A simple question that anyone would come across throughout their lifetimes was asked, Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone nodding with an impassive face as he faced these beings of immense power.","He held no fear towards them as the many memories he obtained the moment he became an Infernal Lord told him of many shocking secrets, and he knew that these two beings in front of him would never harm him.","The question they asked was regarding the status he obtained the moment the title of Infernal Lord was fully his, and the unique existence he became because of it!","\"Yes, I know my role extremely well, and I will be moving to rapidly enhance the level of my realm so that I can be ready to carry out what is expected of me.\"","The male Infernal Lord finally nodded with some goodwill at this, his body disappearing in particles of light as this was all he needed to hear!","The sultry Infernal Lord remained as she stared at Noah with shining eyes, and he returned her gaze as he thought about the true identity of the Infernal Lords, and exactly what his role would now be.","When comparing the identity of Infernals and the numerous other beings of numerous races he had come across over the months, they could be considered two opposing life forms.","He was a life form that stood opposite to Infernals a few minutes ago, but ever since he took the full title of Infernal Lord, he had become a hybrid of something else!","This identity came with many secrets that changed his view points and perceived notions entirely, especially so affecting how he would move from now on as among the many shocking pieces of information he had come across, one of them told him the main purpose for the creation of Infernals.","That purpose that he now had to carry out...was to destroy!","\"Ahh, little lord, let’s talk for a bit...tell me how a being like you reached a special existence such as us while being at this level. Come, oh and call me Azula. Big Sister Azula.\"","The powerful Infernal Lord at the World Rank smiled widely as she spread her arms out and pulled Noah’s blood clone forward, heading towards one of the many grand castles spread across the ancient looking cities in this Infernal Realm!"]},{"number":408,"title":"Chapter 408: Chapter 407 - Purpose","paragraphs":["Along the dredges of history, the knowledgeable beings knew that the Infernals came to everyone’s knowledge in the Battle of Righteous, standing against Celestials as in this battle, one of the weakest Infernal Lords fell.","Since the battle was ended by the monstrous Terror, things have been in a constant state of conflict as the Infernals stood against the forces of the Celestials alongside the beings of the Dark Expanse. One side apparently stood for order and balance, the other was created for chaos and destruction!","But...the many memories that Noah was granted told him a bigger story than just that!","The Infernals and the Celestials, the Celestial Realm, or really its true name- the Central Realm that is closest to the true center of the Novus Galaxy, and the many creatures that are being cultivated within it. They were all connected!","The beings called the Founders simply named themselves Celestials, and also named the Realm they chanced upon as their own- simply calling it the Celestial Realm.","But the true identity of this realm was something much grander, something that the Celestials did not and could not actually lay claim to!","But it was because of this Realm that they were able to obtain the powerful techniques and treasures that placed them in the position of power that they were in today.","The way that they used this power though...went on to directly go against the universal laws, and thus the Infernals came to be! Their rise was a singular effect from the actions of the Celestials, the spawning of multiple Infernal Realms across the Novus Galaxy coming to be for the single purpose of balancing the flow of fate and chaos!","The Infernals stood for chaos and destruction, but their true purpose was actually something that the Celestials regularly spoke of as one of their main ideals.","The true purpose of the Infernals was to actually...bring back the original order and balance that was gradually being tipped by the Celestials!","This was just what some of the shocking knowledge that the privilege of the Title of Infernal Lord told him, the information overhauling his world view and numerous possibilities of how he would move in the future were already blooming in his mind.","For now, he followed and listened to the words of the 7th Infernal Lord Azula, as he looked for the description of the Infernal Lord title that was not incoherent symbols anymore.","<strong>[Infernal Lord] (Variant) :: A special existence born for destruction and chaos, all in order to bring back balance. A holder of this title is granted powerful knowledge about the true nature of the Novus Galaxy, but restrictions exist which prevent them from acting on this knowledge as they remain strictly in the bounds of their purpose. This Variant title makes the user a unique existence that bypasses this restriction. Among the abundant knowledge obtained, the user has obtained the cultivation and martial techniques for the Supreme Law of Chaos. </strong>","A long description of immense proportions laid out in front of his eyes as much of the things he knew were affirmed, all of the information flowing through his mind also going towards the Planetary Systems as they themselves had adopted a somber atmosphere.","The title of Infernal Lord brought with it knowledge and a special entity into existence, but it also brought Noah the gift of something that only Celestials have had the pleasure of enjoying these past thousands of years!","It also gave him something that was unique to the Celestial Realm, an Inheritance of the Disciple of Chaos!","This Inheritance would have been something that he had to search for and brave horrendous dangers from the region where powerful Chaos Behemoths moved, but the Infernal Lord title granted this Inheritance as a by product.","One must know that this was an Inheritance at the level of a Supreme Law, and was most likely at the same level as the Inheritance that the Celestial Founders had come across in the Celestial Realm, the same level of techniques that they had used to strengthen themselves for the last thousands of years!","Yet now, Noah had obtained a similar level of techniques, and his sword that was aimed towards them had become even sharper as he received a clearer directive as an Infernal Lord.","But...he also gained a better understanding of the powers of beings that he was playing with. He knew that the weakest Infernal Lords in this Second Infernal Realm were at the World Rank, the mid ranked Infernal Lord at the realm above that, and the strongest Infernal Lord that took the first seat was a whooping 2 realms higher than the World Rank.","This was just the side of the Infernals that he was now on, and the terrifying thought to realize was that even with such a force, in the battle more than one thousand years ago, an Infernal Lord had still fallen as they faced their enemies- the Celestials.","This showed the horrendous power that the Celestials carried, especially so for the Founders that stood at the peak of this organization!","This made Noah realize no matter how fast he thought he was advancing, no matter how quickly he shot through the ranks, he was still utterly and completely outmatched by these powerful beings that had been alive and cultivating for thousands of years.","He did not even come close to matching the strength of a single Celestial Grandmaster that had more than 600,000 Fate Lines, his own lines of fate just amounting to twenty six thousand! This was not to even mention the creature...the being that stood at the top of the Celestials and the millions of Fate Lines that they held.","This realization made Noah shift his mentality on his rate of progress, throwing out any sort of pride or sense of accomplishment he had for getting so far in the span of a few months.","Yes, nobody had risen as fast as he had in power. Nobody had amassed the achievements he obtained, his latest one of obtaining the title of Infernal Lord being even more unique. But...in the grand scale of things as he looked at the many shocking memories this title brought...he was extremely weak!","So he continued perusing through the numerous shocking cl.u.s.ters of information as he planned for a plan of advancement in the future that would leave the speed he had been advancing so far in the dust.","He would occasionally think himself powerful or overpowered as he strolled around and even began threatening entities on the level of planets. He thought this was some great accomplishment, but there existed experts like these two Infernal Lords at the World Rank that had the capabilities to destroy planets!","No.","He was not powerful!","He was not overpowered!","Not yet, not by a long shot!","His eyes shone with a dangerous l.u.s.ter as he threw aside his old foolish thoughts and looked at things on a grander scale. Why feel a sense of achievement for being connected to a few worlds? Why feel happy for barely mastering .26% of the law of fate and amassing just 26,000 Fate Lines?","What was stopping him from moving actively to connect himself to tens, hundreds of more worlds? What was stopping him from using his unique Planetary System and finding new ways to rapidly increase his mastering of laws? What was stopping him from truly becoming overpowered?","RUMBLE!","It felt like a dam had broken loose in his heart as intense ambition and goals sprouted forth, the shocking new knowledge he obtained going on to cause something even he did not fully know the effects of!"]},{"number":409,"title":"Chapter 409: Chapter 408 - {Disciple of Chaos}","paragraphs":["\"My oh my, you’re barely paying any attention to me.\"","The powerful Infernal Lord in front of him spoke out in a pouting manner as Noah was shaken out of his thoughts and looked towards her apologetically.","\"I apologize, Big Sister Azula. What were you saying?\"","\"I asked you for your story, your journey up till now. I have to also assign you your own Infernal Legion, but that’s for later. Come, enlighten me while we enjoy some food.\"","The Infernal Lord Azula motioned for Noah to follow her into one of the huge castles Noah could see in the ancient looking cities below him, behaved Infernals moving around respectfully as they neared.","His head was filled with a variety of thoughts as he moved to entertain this powerful Infernal Lord first, choosing to move slightly later as he collected his thoughts and finalized his plans.","In the Celestial Realm, the battle between the Dark Winged Chaos Tiger was coming to an end as a furious Grandmaster Vredral threw out consecutive Blades of Liberation and [Judgement] down on the beast, the timely warnings from Athena about its movements and the other deadly attacks from the now Soul Rank Noah and other members of the Righteous Fire Exploration Team causing even more damage on this Chaos Beast.","ROAR!","It let out its last defiant roar as the Domain of Fate that Grandmaster Vredral released overpowered it, a singular last Blade of Liberation coming down to take its life!","BOOM!","Silence reigned in the region as only the brilliant aura of fate lingered in the air, Noah sensing numerous Lines of Fate descending onto the bodies of all the Celestials around him as he observed the quickest way that Celestials increased their Fate Lines.","The face of Grandmaster Vredral was still somber as he floated in the air, his body disappearing into particles of light as he left behind a message.","\"Something urgent has occurred. Dissect and divide up the Behemoth before carefully returning to the Watch Tower, there shouldn’t be any other Elite Behemoths nearby. Boru, explain the intricacies of the materials of a Chaos Behemoth and Fate lines to the junior disciples.\"","He left behind a tired Righteous Fire Exploration Team that nodded with tight expressions as he left, Boru taking charge as he began to explain a concept that Noah actually knew about deeply now because of a recent title. This time it dealt with the two Supreme Laws of Fate and Chaos!","\"Chaos is diametrically opposed to Fate, so whenever one overpowers the other, a rise in the respective beings involved increases.\"","Boru spoke while moving quickly, the other party members helping as they began to use their abilities to divide the monstrous beast into multiple portions.","\"When we defeat Chaos Beasts, our Fate Lines increase rapidly. This also applies even more so when we purify the immense essence of chaos entrenched in their bodies there after, this being one of the more efficient ways we amass more fate lines.\"","Noah listened closely as he contributed to the project, the mountainous beast soon being cut apart as everyone took their portion, their gazes turning towards the same direction that the Grandmaster disappeared in as they made their way back. They also knew that something serious had happened!","Boru continued explaining about the usage of the materials of Chaos Behemoths as Noah used this information and compared it to what he now knew, a few possibilities forming as he thought about the cultivation technique he had obtained after becoming an Infernal Lord. The first one was a similar one to {Fate’s Disciple} and {Disciple of Fire}!","<strong>{Disciple of Chaos} :: A technique geared towards cultivating the Supreme Law of Chaos. Grants the user the ability to cultivate Chaos Particles and form a Chaos Field.</strong>","Succinct words showed themselves in his eyes as the team of Celestials slowly made their way back, his attention placed on the different aspects of this unique skill that set it apart from the first two law type cultivation techniques he obtained.","The Disciple of Fire granted him a Fire Origin Core, Fate’s Disciple granted him Fate Lines, while this Disciple of Chaos granted its user a Chaos Field!","He thought back to the oppressive feeling of strength that the Infernal Lords released, especially their surroundings that always felt suffocating for anyone that neared as he glanced at the Chaos Field even more.","<strong>[Chaos Field] A field created from the unique particles of chaos, granting its user the reinforcement of the Law of Chaos passively and actively when any abilities are cast. Attacks reinforced with the chaos element bypass most defenses and reduce the Vitality of opponents directly.</strong>","A thoughtful expression appeared on Noah’s face as they continued moving forward in the Celestial Realm, his clone being the one about to actually test this unique cultivation technique at the same level as the one the Celestials had their hands on.","Back in the Second Infernal Realm, the Ancient Blood Clone looked at Infernal Lord Azula as they enjoyed a variety of unique foods he had never come across before.","\"Besides being assigned a Legion and increasing my strength for the foreseeable future, what else will I be doing?\"","Azula’s devilishly handsome face turned to the side at this question, smiling broadly as she replied.","\"A Letter of Summons from the First Infernal Lord will most likely arrive for you in the near future, detailing out a specific mission for you to carry out. Wait patiently for that as you cultivate, little lord.\"","The powerful Infernal Lord replied with a sultry voice, Noah nodding as he prepared to move.","\"Then I’ll have to be impolite and get myself acquainted with my new power first. Thank you for the great welcome.\"","He bowed towards the curvaceous Infernal Lord that replied without missing a beat.","\"Why of course. Mmm, you can dwell in the castle right next to this one for now as I get things prepared. And if you need anything...just ask.\"","His face remained respectful and impassive as these words were released from the Infernal Lord, bowing as he moved out of one grand castle and went towards another.","He simply had too many things on his plate to even think about anything else currently, and he had to start right away!","Cultivating the Supreme Law of Chaos, the Supreme Law of Fate, the Law of Fire, and many other objectives that were only ideas so far and not made into action.","He left to start on his long line of goals as he left behind a smiling Infernal Lord whose eyes shone while glancing at his back.","\"An Infernal Lord...yet not really...Ahh!\"","..."]},{"number":410,"title":"Chapter 410: Chapter 409 - Fate Lines and Chaos Particles","paragraphs":["Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone descended onto one of the grand castles that were present in this devilish looking metropolis at the center of the Second Infernal Realm, the few attending Infernals inside it bowing towards him respectfully as his aura seemed inviolable to them!","This was the aura of an Infernal Lord, and it came with many positives, but also a number of negatives as well.","The biggest negative currently was that Noah could be classified as an Infernal, and a high ranking one at that, which made it so that he could not obtain the unique energy in the form of Skill Points that was only available when beings of polar opposite existences defeated each other in the Novus Galaxy!","When the Celestials and other beings in the Novus Galaxy entered into an Infernal Realm to hunt down Infernals, they would receive this unique energy as their power and comprehension was boosted. When the Infernals defeated them, in turn they would also power up rapidly as their rank increased.","The obtainment of the Infernal Rank title had effectively made Noah a special existence that now neither stood on one side or the other, actually being a hybrid existence that took away this unique feature, but granted him so much more. But this also meant that the Skill Points he currently had were limited to this number, his gaze looking at the overall Skill Points that were hovering a bit over 2000.","His gaze was impassive as these thoughts came, simply letting him know that he had to use the Skill Points well and not waste them by permanently using them in maxing proficiencies of skills. But he held no worries as he knew in the far future, there was something which would still provide him with something along the same lines of Skill Points!","He wrapped up his thoughts as he came into a grand hall in the castle, the attending Infernals closing the doors as he finally had time for himself. He thought back to the First Infernal Realm where Draco remained alone, Noah sending the young Dragon a telepathic message to continue hunting the constantly spawning Infernals to raise its power. He would be able to leave the Infernal Realm from a Portal that was already established by Noah when the Harbingers were hunting Infernals themselves a few weeks back.","His other summoning skills were canceled as the only thing left in the First Infernal Realm was currently a Draconic Behemoth that was reaping the rewards of Skill Points.","With these things set aside, the Ancient Blood Clone began on the first pressing issue- using the technique he received as an Infernal Lord to cultivate the Law of Chaos!","He sat down at the center of the grand hall as he closed his eyes, spreading out his senses to cover his entire body and the surroundings as he activated {Disciple of Chaos}. This time, he made sure not even an ounce of chaos would show on his main body that was still moving in the Celestial Realm as [Unique Origin] was placed on overdrive.","OOONG!","A dark ripple of energy released from his as he cast this ability for the first time, this ripple of energy coming back in a circular fashion around him as it slowly began to vibrate.","RUMBLE!","This continued vibration seemed to be this circle, this Chaos Field, rapidly expanding and contracting as little by little, small dark particles began to appear within this field! These were the Chaos Particles that the {Disciple of Chaos} could form in a Chaos Field, the manifestation of chaos essence that would go on to reinforce them and their abilities!","Little by little, the reserves of essence that the clone was connected to were let loose freely as these small Chaos Particles began to appear en masse all over the Chaos Field.","The very surroundings trembled as the Infernals around the castle began to feel the convergence of the powerful aura of the Law of Chaos, respectful looks coming on to their faces as they went about their tasks.","Around the clone, it seemed like floodgates of dark energy were congregating as Noah felt a new source of strength continue to grow within him, his gaze going observing a new section on his stat panel that showed the constantly rising number of Chaos Particles!","[Noah Osmont][Title(s): Infernal Lord(Variant)]","[Bloodline(s): Vampyre Progenitor(Awakening)]","[Fate Line(s) : 26,653]","[Chaos Particle(s) : 420]","[Origin Core(s) : Fire-2]","[Vitality: VOID]","[Focus: - ]","[Strength: VOID]","[Law(s) : Water-11, Space-8%, Fate-.26%, Fire-11%, Chaos-.000042%]","The number of Chaos Particles was constantly shooting up as it changed from a few hundreds quickly and went above 1000, the convergence of essence around the area the clone was in only getting wilder as the skies above the castle began to darken.","The respect the surrounding Infernals felt only increased, while the 7th Infernal Lord Azula appeared in the skies as her gaze locked in on the castle Noah was in, a bright smile spreading from her face as the 8th Infernal Lord, the Infernal who was known as Rykker, also appeared next to her to watch this spectacle.","\"He’s at least got the talent to rapidly advance, don’t you think?\"","Azula said with a bright tone as she continued to observe the convergence of essence and chaos around the castle. Rykker replied with an impassive expression as he nodded.","\"He had to at least have some ability for him to be able to stand on the seat of the 9th Infernal Lord. Besides, anyone cultivating the Law of Chaos using the {Disciple of Chaos} for the first time initiates a change like this. It will fade away soon enough as he falls along the same grueling cultivation journey that we all take. He’ll hopefully gain some power in these next few years before the war breaks out.\"","Rykker said this with an unimpressed expression as the two Infernal Lord continued to observe the phenomenon in the air, waiting to see how long this convergence of chaos essence would continue to measure the genius of this new Infernal Lord.","Their eyes watched as their impressions gradually changed, noticing that the clouds of chaos particles were not actually reducing as time passed, but actually becoming even denser before they shot down towards the singular being cultivating within the castle!","\"...\"","\"Well, I guess it’s impressive now. It’s been a few minutes, and with such a large amount of chaos particles converging, he can be considered a genius that has obtained a few thousand during his first session.\"","Azula only smiled brightly as Rykker said this, her gaze looking forward expectantly as more time passed, the surrounding cloud of Chaos Particles actually not reducing one bit, and were actually becoming even denser!","10 minutes!","30 minutes!","1 hour!!!","RUMBLE!","A tremor ran through the minds of many of the Infernals in the Second Infernal Realm, many of them already noticing the stupendous phenomenon of intense convergence of chaos particles that only continued to get denser and denser.","Rykker’s face had turned ashen as even Azula looked forward in shock, the implication of holding the convergence of this mane Chaos Particles that continued to descend into the Castle having ahuge significance!","Similar to Fate Lines, those that were truly proficient in the Law of Fate would condense a few hundred or a few thousand Fate Lines on their first initiation of {Fate’s Disciple}, whereas they would be limited to condensing a few tens of Fate Lines or at most a hundred every day there after. This created a very long and arduous journey for those cultivating Supreme Laws, where they had to find other means like influencing the lives of millions or reaping the lives of beings proficient in the opposing Law of Chaos to increase their cultivation rapidly!","This concept stood the same for the Chaos Particles of the Law of Fate, which was why the two Infernal Lords were shocked, as they could presume the number of Chaos Particles being condensed should have long ago passed ten thousand, and it did not seem like it was stopping!","Rykker couldn’t help but let out an exclamation as he watching this confounding phenomenon.","\"What the hell is this?!\"","..."]},{"number":411,"title":"Chapter 411: Chapter 410 - Dual Cultivation","paragraphs":["Going back an entire hour as Noah first initiated {Disciple of Chaos}, the process had been going similarly as he expected from his experiences in condensing Fate Lines.","He saw the constant stream of Chaos Particles fill his Expanding Chaos Field, their rate constantly pouring in as the number soon passed 10,000 and continued forward, showing that his supposed talent for this Law of Chaos even surpassed the Law of Fate!","But it was only by this much, as he observed himself getting a few hundred more Chaos Particles before the atmospheric converging chaos began to stall and reduce. He was about to accept this result when he thought of Boru’s words on how they increased their Fate Lines rapidly through defeating Chaos Behemoths and using their materials.","Through using their body parts and purifying the enormous amounts of chaos entrenched in their bodies, one would be able to gain Fate Lines much faster!","This thought crossed Noah’s mind as he chose to become bold briefly, testing the waters and this theory as while {Disciple of Chaos} was initiated, he also activated {Fate’s Disciple}!","RUMBLE!","A tremor passed through his body as the moment the skill was initiated, a few golden lines of fate began coming towards him. But the intrusion of these fate lines was as if gasoline was poured into the fire, causing the surrounding Chaos Particles they were passing through in the Chaos Field to tremble violently as they attacked the coming Fate Lines and wiped them away entirely!","!!!","Noah observed this change with a shocked expression as the moment that these golden Fate Lines were disintegrated, the surrounding Chaos Particles became excited as even more of them converged towards him, the number that had stagnated at 10,836 pushing upwards as it broke past 11,000 very quickly.","He continued to pour mana into the {Fate’s Disciple} skill as numerous Lines of Fate descend down and tried to attach to his body, but the moment they came in contact with the Chaos Field, they were utterly destroyed even before reaching Noah’s body, the reaction that Boru talked about of increasing one’s Fate Lines by purifying Chaos actually being used the other way around, where any condensing Fate Lines were quickly wiped away by the Chaos Particles surrounding Noah as he was then rewarded with even more particles!","He felt like he was touching upon the precipice of something tremendous as he kept it going, the only thing he was burning being his mana as the number of Fate Lines remained at a constant 26,653, but his Chaos Particles were gradually increasing as he had {Fate’s Disciple} activated.","He observed for 10 more minutes as he counted more than 100 Fate Lines appear and try to enter his body, but they were ultimately destroyed the moment they reached the Chaos Field, never coming in contact with him as the normal rule where he could condense 100 Fate Lines was violated, even more of them coming down as they never actually became bound to him and continued to be destroyed!","It was a terrific cycle where Noah was only using an immense amount of mana to keep the two techniques, {Fate’s Disciple} and {Disciple of Chaos}, active while he simply watched the many present Chaos Particticles eat up the lines of Fate, their numbers continuing to shoot up as if a chemical reaction was taking place, causing the cloud of converging chaos particles to only become denser as time passed.","This brought us to the current time where it was an hour later, and Noah already had the number of Chaos Particles up to 13,000, amassing 2000 more Chaos Particles that he would have had to spend 20 days slowly condensing in just a single hour!","This situation caused his eyes to shine a beautiful splendor as a shocking thought crossed his mind. If this number remained the same...if he could really condense 2000 Chaos Particles in around an hour...didn’t this mean he could possibly have over a million in just the span of a month?!","\"...\"","This idea left him speechless as it seemed too shocking to be true!","If this same technique could be applied to Fate Lines, it meant he could possibly catch up and even pass a being like Grandmaster Vredral in the span of a month!","[...It seems to be possible.]","His thoughts were affirmed as the Planetary System of his home world chirped in, the confirmation making Noah expectant as he had come upon a way which made the heavy weight he felt from knowing too many truths about their current situation lift some what.","[The time span of a month is also if you were cultivating a single Supreme Law. If you put the Law of Fate into the equation as well, you would only make half the progress, but in both Supreme Laws.]","Noah nodded as many thoughts continued coursing through his mind.","[We’ve also tested amassing Fate Lines in the Time Space of the Spiritual Land, where the unique ratio of time actually did not affect the condensation of Fate Lines, the number remaining at 100 in terms of the real time of the Universe.]","Yes! When Noah created his Ancient Blood Clone, one of the first things he tested in the Time space of the Spiritual Land was whether he could use the passage of time in the Time Space to bypass the restriction of only being able to amass around 100 Fate Lines each day. But he had disappointedly found out that even with the enhanced ratio where days passed in the Time Space, the moment 100 Fate Lines were condensed, an entire day had to pass in the outside world before more of them descended down!","This was why even though his clone was actively in the Time Space increasing the proficiency of skills and training, the number of Fate Lines had still grown at the same rate the past few weeks!","This limitation did not get Noah down though, as he now had his hands on this unique situation that would easily allow him to amass numerous Chaos Particles and by extension, many Fate Lines for as long as he wished.","[Although, I can already see another limitation occurring in the future when you enter the stage of a million or more. I’ve observed the usage of mana to exponentially increase when you reached the 10,000 mark for both Fate Lines and Chaos Particles, which means it will increase even more as you continue in the future. This is especially so with this new method you are currently using, where the essence you burn to constantly keep both {Fate’s Disciple} and {Disciple of Chaos} is of no issue or consequence now, but it might cause a strain as you get closer near the 10,000,000 number of Fate Lines or Chaos Particles and get close to mastering these Supreme Laws through this Dual Cultivation method.]","Hearing these words from the Planetary System about possible limitations in terms of something he considered to have an infinite amount of, his eyes shone with an oppressive aura as dangerous thoughts rushed out from him.","’If a strain in energy might occur in the future as I near mastering these Supreme Laws, I’ll simply nip that problem in the bud right now.’","The Planetary System had simply mentioned that there would be a strain if he were to constantly burn mana as he kept the two skills active when the number of Fate Lines or Chaos Particles reached the millions, meaning that it still would not be that much of a problem, and would simply be a strain. But even this he did not want to hear! Because in his heart, the mana he could use was always Infinite! The thought of there being a strain should never even come when it dealt with him! His eyes shone with l.u.s.ter as he affirmed his next steps while he continued to amass even more Chaos Particles.","’If the connections of a few planets will not be enough, I’ll simply attach myself to a hundred more! If a hundred more will not be enough, I’ll simply upgrade them to become Realms! Mana...will never be a problem for me!’","Arrogant and domineering thoughts swirled in his mind as he perused through the abundant knowledge he now held about the Novus Galaxy, the ideas of Worlds and how they became Realms being extremely clear in his eyes as he looked forward to a grand future.","Outside the castle where he was dual cultivating both {Fate’s Disciple} and {Disciple of Chaos}, two Infernal Lords were looking at this scene with ashen faces as they thought the genius of this new Infernal Lord was simply too monstrous!"]},{"number":412,"title":"Chapter 412: Chapter 411 - Movements","paragraphs":["As a new Infernal Lord just chanced upon a terrifyingly rapid way to increase his strength, the powerful figures on opposing sides were moving with their own discussions and plans.","The Righteous Fire Exploration Team had returned to the watch tower where they stationed the Prime Warship, the tense air being sensed around the Tower as over the next few hours, they were briefed on future changes as the Celestials reacted to the knowledge that a new Infernal Lord had risen!","This event meant that in the near future, where it be months or years, a new war would be breaking out. The coming of the 9th Infernal Lord was just another one of the signs for this, with many more to follow.","For the Celestials, their allowance of the inhabitants of the Novus Galaxy into the Celestial Realm continued to provide them with multiplied benefits as those in high ranking positions were able to increase their progress in the Law of Fate, while also being able to bring in even more materials from the Behemoths that continued to be hunted by tens of thousands of teams currently.","With this project going smoothly, the next item on the list for the Celestials was the even more rapid rise in strength of their own forces, a few Grandmasters like Vredral putting forward the ideology that they needed to focus their treasures on a few specific individuals that would hold a tremendous amount of battle power, and not spread out all the resources to create average strength Celestials.","This brought forward the command for the seeds of Celestials like those with Noble Fates and those showing unique strengths to be put at the forefront of receiving materials and treasures, their rise in strength being favored more as they showed a different level of strength!","This made it so that a majority of the materials combining into the hands of the Celestials were directed to powerful Grandmasters and beings that held unique titles like those with Noble Fates, meaning Celestials like the War Princess Athena and Crixus the Destroyer would be freely receiving huge boosts very soon.","When the day ended, numerous new directives had been laid out as Celestials began to move with even more discipline and haste!","They were not the only ones though, as the Alliance of the Dark Expanse that was made up of organizations like the Scholar’s Guild and Ancient Clans of Vampyres and other powerful beings also continued to move forward with even more vigor.","Their spies that had made it into the Celestial Realm began moving even faster as a unique spatial connection was hiddenly established in this Central Realm at the center of the Novus Galaxy as they began reaping the rewards of the Celestial Realm in full swing.","The unique atmosphere gradually growing in the Sanctum, the central location that many being converged to sell and trade their treasures in the Celestial Realm, became even more active beginning this day as it was not just the powerful beings standing near the top that felt the gradual change in atmosphere, even the forces of numerous Prime Worlds knowing they were entering another stage.","Noah gradually absorbed all of these changes as his clone continued his stupendous Dual Cultivation of both Chaos and Fate simultaneously in the Second Infernal Realm, the watching 7th and 8th Infernal Lord glancing at this show of talent with ashen faces as it had been continuing for the past day.","His clone was currently increasing Chaos Particles, where golden Fate Lines continued to try descending down on his body and were gradually destroyed, the destruction of the Fate Lines granting Noah a never ending cycle of even more Chaos Particles.","He breathed out slowly as he glanced around the enormous Chaos Field surrounding his body, especially the thousands of Chaos Particles randomly moving around within it.","His surroundings were dark and cloudy as any nearby Infernals felt their bodies grow stronger as they were exposed to the unique environment for a few hours. His body was the one with the most changes as he glanced at his Stat Panel, the number making his ambitious thoughts grow ever stronger as they foretold countless possibilities.","[Noah Osmont][Title(s): Infernal Lord(Variant)]","[Bloodline(s): Vampyre Progenitor(Awakening)]","[Fate Line(s) : 26,653]","[Chaos Particle(s) : 45,635]","[Origin Core(s) : Fire-2]","[Vitality: SOUL]","[Focus: - ]","[Strength: SOUL]","[Law(s) : Water-11, Space-8%, Fate-.26%, Fire-11%, Chaos-.45%]","The number of Chaos Particles had risen from nothing until they broke through 45,000 in the single day that he began cultivating the {Disciple of Chaos}! The percentage under the Law of Chaos also rose to .45%! This was more than the entire progress he made over the past month as he amassed Fate Lines as Celestials normally would!","It was a shocking rate of progression, but it made him slightly less apprehensive as he thought about the strength of the beings he had to move with. The truly powerful Celestial Grandmasters in the Light Expanse, the Ancient forces moving in the Dark and Letalis Expanse, as well as the most fearsome creatures of them all...the Terrors.","With this new method of cultivating laws that was only made possible by the enormous reserves of mana, he felt a level of confidence when looking at this big picture!","SHAA!","He waved his hands as he stopped burning his mana towards {Fate’s Disciple} and {Disciple of Chaos}, the dark clouds that had been gathering for the past day beginning to slowly clear up as the aura of Chaos reduced.","Around his body, the Chaos Field rumbled as more than forty five thousand Chaos Particles chaotically moved within it. He moved his thoughts as these particles slowly settled, the Chaos Field around his body gradually becoming transparent as it disappeared, never to be seen by anyone else unless he wished it!","He breathed out as he rose, feeling the auras of the two Infernal Lords floating atop the skies of the Second Infernal Realm. He turned into red particles of light as he disappeared, reappearing in the skies in front of them as he knew he must have shocked them beyond comprehension.","Infernal Lord Azula looked towards him with shining eyes and a fervent expression, looking at his impassive face that seemed to say what he did wasn’t much. The 8th Infernal Lord, Rykker, glanced towards Noah with sharp eyes as he could not help but comment.","\"What the hell are you, really?\"","..."]},{"number":413,"title":"Chapter 413: Chapter 412 - Utilization","paragraphs":["Noah glanced at the two Infernal Lord in front of him as he replied impassively.","\"It seems I am more in tune with the Law of Chaos than I thought.\"","His answer only caused the two powerful beings in the World Rank to shake their heads helplessly at the simplification of the unbelievable cultivation session where this being most likely amassed more chaos particles in a day that would normally require one to cultivate for a month.","\"If your power rises like this, your Realm progression past the Soul Forging Realm will only become smother, the profound comprehension of a Supreme Law only aiding you in faster breakthroughs while also enhancing your strength.\"","Noah nodded at this as he spoke once more.","\"I’ll have to be impolite and leave our Realm soon. I know you all sense that I am not fully an Infernal, my unique position allowing me to move freely. I am planning on further increasing my comprehension in the Law of Chaos by actively moving in the outside worlds and realms.\"","His words brought a period of silence as Azula smiled sweetly while Rykker looked towards him carefully, the curvaceous Azula speaking with an amorous tone.","\"Just be sure your identity as an Infernal Lord is hidden so that you don’t inadvertently start the war early. We wouldn’t want the 9th Infernal Lord to die again as soon as he just took his seat.\"","Noah nodded as he glanced at the 8th Infernal Lord Rykker who also nodded, his clone casting [Unique Origin] as the regal crown protruding from his head began disappearing, the dark hair filled with silver streaks returning as he took back his actual form that was Noah Osmont.","\"A form of a human that is so seamless...ahh your talents are going to become very important in the future. Go on and be careful, I will send you a message whenever a Letter of Summons from the 1st Infernal Lord comes down for you.\"","The 7th Infernal Lord Azula said this as she waved her hand, a runic medallion pulsing with a unique power coming towards Noah as he swiped his hands and placed it in his Expansive Space.","\"Then I’ll have to trouble you, Seniors. Please let me know if I can be of help in anything.\"","Noah made a slight bow to these powerful World Rank individuals as he began disappearing in particles of light, disappearing in front of the two Infernal Lords and leaving behind a shocking atmosphere where they were still reeling from his wild cultivation session.","\"...this new Infernal Lord might be something shocking that has yet to show us all exactly what he’ll be capable of.\"","A thoughtful expression appeared on Rykker as the eyes of Azula twinkled, their bodies shooting off in separate directions thereafter as they moved to do their own tasks!","---","The Ancient Blood Clone reappeared beneath a certain volcanic mountain where an Inheritance of the Disciple of Fire was contained, the miniaturized Spiritual Land still stably floating near the Ancient Pedestal peacefully.","The clone sensed the overpowering coagulation of essence in the Celestial Realm once more as he compared it to the levels of essence in the Second and First Infernal Realm, affirming that these two realms were not even close to the level of essence in this Central Realm that was nearest to the center of the Novus Galaxy!","He moved into the Spiritual Land as he saw the state of the training Harbingers and other individuals from the multiple stars he was connected to, many of them having learned the Inheritance of the Disciple of Fire as their bodies vibrated with the fire element while trying to build a Fire Origin Core.","He sent a message to the Emperor Penguin as he wanted to gauge their distance from the volcanic mountain, they being the only ones that had not learned the Inheritance yet as they used the journey to this mountain as one of training.","The Emperor Penguin let him know that they were actually fighting a Fire Behemoth at this moment, with the Ancient Blood Clone using the Spiritual Land to check exactly what location the Emperor Penguin was in. Matching the rough coordinates with the map he had drawn for himself as he traversed towards this volcanic mountain when he was following the [Treasure Hunter] of the Spiritual Land and only marked the locations of the Behemoths he came across, he found their location as he disappeared once more.","ROAR!","He appeared in the gorgeous field of greenery and ancient trees of the Celestial Realm that he was used to, hearing the roar of a Behemoth not too far away as he sensed the auras of Elena and the Emperor Penguin, along with many other Vampyres and the Calamities of the Sea.","\"Be ready!\"","Elena was shouting valiantly as she tanked the horrendous fiery attacks of the Behemoth, the others dealing damage all around this beast as they weaved in and out. The Kraken was sending down red rays of light as an oversized goldfish, another Calamity of the Sea, released blue-gold water spear that rushed towards the Behemoth. Spatial Blades were being released from the flippers of the Emperor Penguin as the battle was in full swing, everybody contributing to bringing down this Celestial Beast at the level of Soul Forging Realm.","RAA! RAA! RAA!","The Emperor Penguin cried out expectantly as it sensed the aura of its Master, a fervent look appearing on Elena as she sensed the aura of the Progenitor!","RUMBLE!","Noah read this state of battle as he teleported once more, appearing atop the Fire Behemoth that looked like a large iguana, his feet stably landing atop the beast that soon felt the intrusion of a being stepped on it and roared loudly, fiery essence bubbling on its body as it prepared to burn whoever was so foolish to stand upon it.","Noah disregarded the bubbling power of the beast as he called out calmly, wanting to test the efficacy of the rare Supreme Law of Chaos as he came to pick up his subordinates for the future plans he had.","[Chaos Field], [Essence Disruptor].","RUMBLE!","A dark field containing tens of thousands of Chaos Particles spread out with him at the center, the deadly chaotic field going on to wrap around the body of the Fire Behemoth as the wild movements it was doing came to a halt, Noah’s clone actually going on to use one of the new abilities he obtained!","ROAR!","It let out a fearsome roar as it tried to move, the numerous Chaos Particles going on to disrupt its essence as it felt its muscles spasming and the essence of the Law of Fire suppressed!","The Pureblood Vampyres and subordinates around him looked in shock at the incapacitated Fire Behemoth, Noah himself continuing his test as he looked over the other set of abilities that came with the Inheritance of the Disciple of Chaos when he obtained the Infernal Lord Title.","He glanced at the absolute skills called <<Herald of Chaos>> and [Agent of Chaos] as his mana began moving wildly!"]},{"number":414,"title":"Chapter 414: Chapter 413 - Agent of Chaos","paragraphs":["The description of the <<Herald of Chaos>> skill was similar to the opposing skills that he obtained some time back from the Celestials, only having a few differences from <<Herald of Fate>>!","<strong><<Herald of Chaos>> :: An inheritance from the Disciple of Chaos that holds tremendous power. The mysteries of the Supreme Law of Chaos can be slowly understood while this technique is in use, understanding what true chaos is as the user moves to not just create more chaos, but to control it. Abilities include Chaos Discernment, Chaos Traverser, Chaos Concealment, and Chaos Harvester.</strong>","<strong>[Chaos Discernment] :: The clouded and abstruse movements of chaos of different entities or beings became easier to see. The Agent of Chaos can then decide how to use this information. Strict conditions must be met for any usable information to be discerned.</strong>","<strong>[Chaos Traverser] :: As one that is proficient in the workings of the law of chaos, you have more of a leeway over the chaos around you and those you are connected to . This ability allows you to traverse towards the optimum chaos that will grant you the most power.</strong>","<strong>[Chaos Concealment] :: The user’s chaos can be made hard to decipher, where others will not be able to find exactly where chaos will lead you.</strong>","<strong>[Chaos Harverstor] :: An ability given to the Herald of Chaos that allows them to grant chaos to others while reducing chaos from themselves or others. One must use it sparingly as the distribution of chaos is harder to control than expected. </strong>","The description of the abilities were very similar to the ones from the <<Herald of Fate>>, where one could even argue they seemed like a simple copy and paste! But the two laws were counter parts of one another, and having equivalent abilities would only allow Noah to see both sides of the equation, being able to discern both Fate and Chaos.","But his gaze was on the offensive and defensive skills similar to [Fate’s Guardian], these ones called [Agent of Chaos]! This was where he had obtained the skill he just used to incapacitate the movements of the huge Fire Behemoth, the skill called [Essence Disruptor]!","<strong>SOUL [Agent of Chaos](0/60) :: The title of an Agent of anything is a rare one. This skill tree gives its user the ability to confidently call themselves an Agent of Chaos. Abilities include Essence Disruptor(0/5), Chaotic Mandate(0/5), Chaos Orbs(0/5), and Void of Impending Doom(0/5).</strong>","<strong>[Essence Disruptor](0/5) :: The Chaos Particles under your control heed your call as they go on to bind and disrupt the essence and movements of the enemies that fall upon your Chaos Field. </strong>","<strong>[Chaotic Mandate](0/5) :: The user is covered with a mandate of chaos, the Chaos Field surrounding them transfusing with their skin to adorn them in a Chaos Armament. This mandate allows the Agent of Chaos to stand as a true being capable of reigning down unmatched retribution. +100% Chaos Damage, +100% Chaos Resistance, +50% Elemental Damage, +50% Defense, +50% Attack, Cast, and Movement Speed, +50% of all Damage converted to Chaos Damage. </strong>","<strong>[Chaos Orbs](0/5) :: Destructive orbs of chaos are called upon, being released upon your enemies as an area of attack ability. Each of the orbs carry with them the explosive force of a disordered star. Affected area- 50 meters.</strong>","<strong>[Void of Impending Doom](0/5) :: A void of chaos is focused on one particular enemy, this void installing the Fear and Oppressed Effect onto the enemy and disordering their mental state before deadly Doom Spikes rain down.</strong>","A set of beautifully described skills were laid out in front of his eyes, and he started by testing out [Essence Disruptor] first, the more than 45,000 Chaos Particles under his control permeating through the body of the Fire Behemoth as it tried to will it essence and muscles to move, but it was rendered unable to!","The Emperor Penguin watched this scene where his master incapacitated a monstrous Soul Forging Behemoth the moment he entered, being taken out of his stupor when he heard the calm command ring out in his ears.","\"Attack.\"","OOOH!","The Harbingers of Sin and the Pureblood Vampyres became pumped at the show of power, moving with even more vigor as their attacks smashed into the Fire Behemoth who could not even use its essence to defend itself, Noah’s clone remaining on top of the huge iguana looking beast as he continued to pour mana into the [Essence Disruptor] skills to allow the Chaos Particles in his Chaos Field that wrapped around the entirety of this huge beast to continue disrupting its essence.","With his power, this was the extent of what he could do currently, which was a terrifying thought to imagine as he cooly stopped the movements of a powerful Normal Behemoth!","He did not cast the other terrifying sounding skills like [Chaos Orbs] or [Void of Impending Doom] which would most likely wipe away everything on site, choosing to let his subordinates finish off this Behemoth and not steal their kill.","ROAAR!","A weakened roar of unwillingness was let out from the Fire Behemoth as it faced a situation where it could not even move, horrible attacks reigning down that soon took its life!","BOOM!","Its body slumped to the ground as the Order of Blood cheered, the many team members glancing towards Noah with shining eyes as they dawned a Behemoth so easily with his intrusion of a few seconds.","\"Master!\"","The eyes of the Emperor Penguin were shining as he and the fervent looking Elena were the first to step forward, Noah nodding towards them as he waved his hands to the right of the Behemoth, essence converging as a portal slowly began to form.","The sleek penguin came to the side of the Fire Behemoth as it used its spatial abilities to put away the Cores and Skill Books that dropped from it as loot to be divided for later, waving its flippers towards the mountainous body of the beast itself thereafter as it also disappeared into the Emperor’s Penguin’s own spatial inventory skill.","OOOM!","The portal finished forming as silently in the explored Northern Region of the Celestial realm, Noah came to collect the rest of his subordinates for them to begin learning the Inheritance of the Disciple of Fire, the closest plans he currently had dealing with the beasts of the Spiritual Land the most as he prepared for something that he considered a practice run for his future plans.","The thing he considered a practice run was fulfilling the requirements of upgrading the Spiritual Land to the 9th Tier, where he needed to get his hands on the core of a Small World!"]},{"number":415,"title":"Chapter 415: Chapter 414 - Herbs and Pills are Good for Breakthroughs","paragraphs":["As Noah erased the portal which led to the Spiritual Realm in the location where a Fire Behemoth just fell, he was the last to disappear as he joined everyone else beneath the volcanic mountain where the Spiritual Land stood next to the Ancient Pedestal that held the Inheritance Crystal for the Disciple of Fire.","The extremely hot environment was one where only those at higher realms could withstand, with all the newcomers that were just battling the Fire Behemoths being those who could easily learn the inheritance on their own.","He looked towards Elena as he gave out multiple directions to her and the others.","\"Gather all those that haven’t learned the Inheritance and oversee the whole process. You..\"","He pointed towards the Emperor Penguin as he continued speaking.","\"...gather your brothers and sisters. We have another power leveling session to go through.\"","He released multiple commands towards many beings, those familiar with Noah noticing the slightly colder tone as they nodded with serious faces and each went about their tasks.","The normal smile that Noah carried months ago was fading away slowly, his disposition becoming more serious when he obtained the Vampyre Progenitor bloodline, and now becoming even colder as he was hit with some of the truth about the true reality they were all in, and just how outclassed they were!","Those paying attention would recall his disposition becoming more cheerful or feeling a sense of excitement only when he explored new areas, obtained new skills, or got his hands on powerful new treasures. His emotions were gradually settling down on the more impassive and calmer side, the cheerful and excited side of himself slowly being tucked away in a corner!","Many beings went about their tasks as most were simply learning a powerful inheritance and then cultivating in the Fire Law Space to form their Fire Origin Cores, with the Spiritual Land Beasts having a different task as they were brought down to the Time Space of the Spiritual Land for more intense training.","Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone looked at the many resplendent fields of medicinal herbs and fruits spread out across the Time Space, this region that should have been one where people trained their hardest and surpassed those in the outside world slowly turning to become a region filled with farmland. He planted as much of the Spiritual Land Plants that had long growing and maturing times but gave out amazing herbs of medicinal fruits that held overflowing essence in the Time Space, using the increased ratio to grow these plants in a short period of time.","When the Spiritual Land was last upgraded to the 8th Tier, he had planted the newly available plants that were called Athramire and King’s Collard among others, where the products of these magical plants were being observed in front of him right now as he looked at farmlands overflowing with shimmering plants that dangled rainbow-colored fruits, while some were growing as scintillating herbs.","A profound aroma was released from these many fantastical fields as Noah waved his hands, collecting many of the fruits and herbs as he prepared to make pills once more while using the {Forge of the Silver Flame} that he received from a being that was shrouded in mysteries, but Noah already had a slight indication of a few possibilities!","This being that called himself the Karmic Sect master had also left him something he had not been using all that much since he received it, the item called [Lawful Nourishment] that helped one with cultivating laws. This was something that he planned to take out and use during this time as he was finally getting into the time when he was focusing on the comprehension of laws.","He put these thoughts aside as a cauldron materialized in front of his, a shining silver flame beginning to burn as the shimmering medicinal fruits and herbs that were filled with essence began to be refined and turned into pills.","He was utilizing these Spiritual Land Plants that were heavily conducive to the rise in strength of the Spiritual Land Beasts in order to achieve the goal he currently held of pushing the ranks of more than 10 beasts into the Soul Forging Realm.","He had a set of Soul Rank cores from the many Soul Ranked beings he defeated these past few weeks, but they would not be enough to push the ranks of 10 beasts from the Void and into the Soul Rank, with these medicinal herbs and fruits acting like a buffer to continue propelling the levels of these Beasts forward!","The Emperor Penguin, Arctic Wolf, Flying Spider, and 7 other of the most powerful beasts in the Spiritual Land stood respectfully near Noah as they saw the appearance of shining pills that flew towards them, their jaws spreading wide open as they swallowed and began digesting the treasures they were receiving.","On top of the pills filled with abundant essence, Noah waved his hands to bring out the Soul Rank Cores in his [Expansive Space] as they were also thrown towards the beasts, the process of raising the ranks of 10 beings from Void to Soul beginning in the Time Space of the Spiritual Land!","It was a busy time in this fantastical floating landmass as many beings were moving rapidly within it, many of them cultivating the Inheritance of the Disciple of Fire, with others excitedly being fed herbs and pills on top of Cores to push their ranks from one stage to another.","During this whole process, Noah was thinking about the other condition he had to fulfill if he wanted to bring the Spiritual Land from the 8th and into the 9th Tier.","Upgrade Conditions: 10+ Spiritual Land Beasts at the Soul Rank, A Small World Core","He looked under {Spiritual Land Management} as the words ’A Small Word Core’ shone with a blue l.u.s.ter, his thoughts moving rapidly as he thought of exactly what his actions would mean for him to obtain a World Core.","This momentary thought was quickly thrown out of his mind as his heart became firm, knowing he would face this problem head on as the time neared, and he would accomplish without fail no matter what he had to do!","His mind was already perusing through many memories of the beings he had devoured before as he searched for possible small worlds, whether it was those occupied and filled with life, those that did not have any civilizations or even those that were simply uninhabitable planets filled with unlivable environments. He had many possibilities, and did not necessarily have to destroy an entire world and its beings in order to achieve his goals!","He watched the progress of the Spiritual Land Beasts as their power continued to grow, biding his time as his mind-enhancing skills worked rapidly, his main body undergoing an entirely different ordeal as he had begun receiving even more treasures from the Celestials."]},{"number":416,"title":"Chapter 416: Chapter 415 - Treatment Reserved for Kings","paragraphs":["In the large Watch Tower that stood between the border of Normal Behemoths and Elite Behemoths, Noah and Athena were in a huge training hall to themselves as they looked in front of them where numerous materials from Chaos Behemoths were thrown down.","Grandmaster Vredral was overseeing this continuing process as numerous Celestial Disciple came in with golden rings and released numerous treasures ranging from the powerful Chaos Origin cores of Elite Behemoths all the way to materials filled with the Chaos Element.","\"You two are actually fortunate to be living in this tumultuous time, as you will experience a rapid rise in your strength that would normally take others tens or hundreds of years to do so.\"","The Grandmaster continued speaking as the treasures piled up.","\"These materials filled with Chaos in front of you would normally be spread out to hundreds of Grandmasters to continue propelling their ranks forward, but many of them were redirected towards you as we need beings with unique titles like yours to be the ones that stand at the forefront of the coming battles.\"","He moved with a serious expression as he picked up one of the","\"The Chaos in these materials can be purified to grant you an increased pace at amassing Fate Lines, which will even further increase your speed of progressing through the Realms. I’m especially happy for your fast progress in being able to keep up with your Senior Sister, Crixus!\"","Grandmaster Vredral beamed toward Noah as he said this, even Athena turning towards him with a light smile as he nodded to the Grandmaster.","\"Alright, you all go ahead and cultivate well, I will come to bring you both on hunts for Elite Behemoths during periods when you need to consolidate your power and get some practice.\"","The Grandmaster left behind his directions as Athena walked towards the mountains of materials and Cores from Chaos Behemoths, looking at Noah with a smile as she spoke.","\"We truly are blessed by Fate, Junior Brother Crixus. Who could have ever thought that something like this would have been given freely to us.\"","Noah walked towards the mountain of treasures as he hid an impassive interior with a smiling exterior and replied.","\"We should do our best to cultivate then. Don’t let me catch up to you in Fate Lines as well, Senior Sister!\"","\"Oh, is that a challenge?\"","The valiant and battle driven War Princess looked towards him as she took his words a challenge, sitting down next to the pile of treasures as grabbed a piece of a Chaos Behemoth that was entrenched with the Law of Chaos.","Her body lit up with tens of thousands of Fate Lines as she released a golden aura, this aura going on to actually burn the material that held the chaos element as it began to burn the opposing law within it!","As this process continued, yet another Line of Fate descended down from the air and stably attached itself towards Athena, putting aside the material that had lost the darkness of chaos and grabbing the next one as she looked at Noah competitively.","\"I’ll take you up on your challenge. Let’s see if you can even get near the number of my Fate Lines in the next few years!\"","The brilliance of a relationship of a senior sister and a junior brother seemed to be blooming between them as two beings with Noble Fates began using the treasures that were handed to them to cultivate!","Noah listened to the words of Athena with a smile as inside his heart, he knew he could most likely reach the number of Fate Lines that she held in just a matter of days if he was dually cultivating both the techniques under the laws of chaos and fate!","He kept these thoughts to himself as he began purifying the materials in front of his, slowly increasing his fate lines as his clone continued to do the brunt work for the both of them.","He had currently only spent a day focusing on increasing the Chaos Particles when his clone was training in the Second Infernal Realm, bringing the percentage of the Supreme Law of Chaos to .46% where he bypassed the .26% of the Supreme Law of Fate that he had obtained first.","When he switched to increase the number of Fate Lines, he would have to be careful to hide his true number from the eyes of Athena and other Celestials that came near him. He planned to show a monstrous talent that amassed Fate Lines quickly, but he could never explain his rate of amassing close to 48,000 Fate Lines in the span of a day.","When he first used the method of cultivating both the {Disciple of Chaos} and {Fate’s Disciple} where the Chaos Field around him was destroying the oncoming Lines of Fate, his Chaos Particles had increased by a rate of 2000 every hour.","This meant that in one day, he could amass 48,000 Chaos Particles, while his Fate Lines would remain the same as he was burning any incoming Fate Lines in order to continue his obtainment of Chaos Particles. For the future, he had to make a thorough plan where he purified Chaos Particles one day in order to increase his Fate Lines, and then do the opposite the next day in order to increase his progress in the opposing law.","This was also under the pretense that he spent all the 24 hours of the day simply cultivating and doing nothing else!","His mind made the calculations as he came to some crazy numbers. If he were to focus on only one law for 24 hours a day for the next month, with the rate of 2000 per hour, he would be able to amass 1,440,000 of either Chaos Particles or Fate Lines in the span of a month!","If he wanted to progress in both of them at the same rate as he divided his attention to both, this number would simply be halved as he would need to focus on Chaos one day and Fate another day. And once one took into account that he would be doing other things besides isolating himself for a full 24 hours during the day, maybe it would be possible to amass half a million of both Fate Lines and Chaos Particles every month.","This was an increase of roughly 5% in two Supreme Laws simultaneously every month...a terrifying thought that would horrify any knowledgeable being!"]},{"number":417,"title":"Chapter 417: Chapter 416 - A World Core!","paragraphs":["As terrifying calculations were carried out in Noah’s mind, his Ancient Blood Clone had finished his pill making session as he observed the swirling of different colored essence around the 10 Spiritual Land Beasts.","He spread his senses out as he monitored the continued strengthening of other beings on the wide Spiritual Land.","The numerous portals lying stably in the Underground area he was in pulsated with colorful lights as those given permission would occasionally enter the Spiritual Land while an individual like Steel Mikhail would enter and live freely as he moved to do his job on the blue planet and then returned to cultivate in the Spiritual Land.","After observing everything moving smoothly, the clone disappeared from the Time Space of the Spiritual Land as he let the Spiritual Land Beasts finish their breakthrough into the Soul Forging Realm, leaving behind numerous essence pulsating pills and cores for them to continue absorbing!","He performed a long distance teleportation this time as enormous amounts of mana was used, his body reappearing in the wide expanse of space not too far away from his homeworld.","The Ancient Blood Clone glanced at the small blue world that only he could currently see, the [World Veil] he had cast on this world and the other ones he was connected to long ago still active and hiding the world from any passing eyes.","The world in front of his eyes was already nearing the position of a Prime World as it continued the powerful feedback of essence from the many worlds it was connected to, especially the Ancient Blood World that was an entire Realm sometime in the past.","Yet this powerful and expansive world still seemed so small as he looked at it from an extremely far distance, his body continuing to move away from this blue planet as his target this time was not to check up on all the advancements that had happened so far, but to search for viable worlds he could pluck the cores of in the surrounding area!","This was something that even his own mind just a few months ago would never have been able to fathom.","The fact that someone like him could be traversing through space actually looking for a viable world to steal an entire world core and possibly destroy such a world was something extremely foreign to him, yet now about to become a reality.","His body moved across space as the [Child of Space] ability from the Lesser Cthulhu skill tree made him feel like he was in the most comfortable possible environment. His body was shooting through the vastness of space at a shocking speed, the tremendous boosts that he received from his many passive skills made it so that his speed and power was already nearing those at the Domain Expansion Realm!","He could only confidently say this when it came to those at the normal level of the Domain Expansion Realm, and this was not putting into account the Celestial Grandmasters themselves like Vredral.","He continued moving across the vastness of space as he wandered across the void looking for specific stars. The one that he was looking for was a small world that would not have any inhabitants, potentially a world that had a harsh environment that no organisms could survive in.","His heart was not fully set out to be a destroyer where he would without reservations take the core of a small world that was filled with life forms similar to his own homeworld just a few months ago, even with all the knowledge he currently held.","He did not travel far before he came upon a world filled with elemental storms and chaotic energies. It was neither a large nor a middle world, being a perfectly small world that was uninhabited by any other beings. The rough storms always raging on the surface of this world and in the skies above it making it an uninhabitable star in this wide area.","His eyes honed in on this world as he began shooting down towards it at a high speed. He felt a slight resistance as his level was so much higher than this world, but these protections were nearly nothing when it came to someone who wielded the immense energy coming from multiple stars.","He quickly pierced through the many layers that a small world would have for protection as he entered its atmosphere, and then continued shooting down towards its earth!","BOOM!","His body pierced through the layers of frozen Earth, this world holding unique qualities of destructive storms above it and frozen earth below it. Because of his extremely fast speed, he began nearing the inner core of this world in less than a few minutes.","SHAA!","He broke through the innermost layer where the core of the entire world laid as he glanced upon these slowly rotating ovular shape in front of him.","[...]","A period of silence followed as Noah looked upon this rotating core of this unknown small world, where he heard a cold static voice thereafter.","[What are you?]","The small world coldly asked this question in a manner and tone of voice that Noah was used to hearing throughout these past few months. He impassively focused on the core of this small world as he took in its words and replied calmly.","\"I would apologize to you in advance. For this is something that I do have a choice on, and I am choosing to do it regardless of its consequences in order to further my own goals. It is even somewhat hypocritical.\"","His voice was that of conflict as he had made sure to look for a specific world, one that didn’t have any life on it, one where he would not be taking or reaping the lines of billions. But still, there was one entity that would have to be affected no matter what he did.","This entity was the world itself.","He glanced upon the small world core that did not reply after it heard Noah’s words. It’s vast senses telling it that something inexplicable would be happening here today. Noah moved without any further forethought as he threw his hands out and placed them on the powerful core of this Small World as he uttered simple words.","[Devouring].","RUMBLE!","For the first time ever, in actuality and in totality, he had cast the skill from the Seven Deadly Sins, from the Sin of Gluttony- He had cast [Devouring] on an actual world!","OOONG!","A cloud of darkness went on to wrap around the rotating world core, it’s manner was that as if a beast had opened its jaws and was rapidly closing in on this resplendent core. Devouring was fully cast as the cloud of darkness had circled the entire core of the Small World in front of Noah, with essence beginning to leak out of the body of the clone nonsensically as the target of devouring was an actual world this time around, not just an enemy that was at the mythical or a legendary rank, but an entire core of a small world!","RUMBLE!","Essence leaked out of him with wild abandon as the entire surroundings of the small world were shaking. At this moment in time something that had rarely occurred in history was happening, where one existence that was on an entirely different tier from another was doing something unexplainable!","The process of essence continuing to leave his body recklessly went on for a few minutes before everything went silent and the darkness that was wrapping around the core of the small world rapidly began to reduce in size as Noah began to see cracks appearing on the layers of earth around them.","CRACK!","At the moment that the small world core fully disappeared and the devouring skill had successfully done its job and devoured an entire core of a small world, space shattered and began folding in on itself!","This destruction continued spreading throughout the area of the inner core that Noah was in, his figure teleporting out of the area as he began to see notifications of messages from the Planetary System Discerning the exact results of his actions.","He appeared in the space above the uninhabitable planet that was filled with even more destructive storms as he looked at the visible result of his actions.","CRACK! CRACK! BOOM!","In front of the already destructive world, cracks were visibly spreading all around the spherical planet, the instability of a world without a core being visible in front of Noah’s eyes as he went on to watch the destruction of something that he had caused with his own hands.","BOOM! BOOM!","Space shattered and refolded as the world had a force rapidly pulling itself in near the center of the missing core before it exploded outwards as a supernova!","Shards of the planet began to spread out far and wide as in front of Noah’s eyes, the storms gradually reduced and calmness slowly returned, the only thing left behind in front of him was palpitating destructive essence and floating debris over the wide area of space.","[A Small World Core has been obtained.]","[Error. Analyzing. Error.]","[...]","From the void of space, numerous Chaos Particles had begun appearing as they willingly fell upon Noah the chaos and destruction he had caused being rewarded as a few hundred Chaos Particles were added unto his already abundant amount. The Planetary System was also sending various messages as the results of devouring a Small World Core were slowly unfolding in front of his eyes!"]},{"number":418,"title":"Chapter 418: Chapter 417 - Possibilities","paragraphs":["In the [Large Stomach] that was created from the abilities of the Sin of Gluttony, an ovular world core was floating stably as the essence of gluttony tried to absorb it ever so slowly.","Noah felt these changes as he gave a command, everything going silent in the large stomach with the messages of the Planetary System continuing to ring out and float in front of his eyes!","[Analyzing.]","[The devoured Core is an entirely separate entity compared to you.]","[There is a high rate of failure if you try to absorb the Small World Core.]","[Two options exist after the successful devouring of a world core. The first is to use the core as a basis to upgrade a Spiritual Land. The second is to use the world core as the basis to upgrade the levels of the connected worlds. You cannot personally gain benefits from it as it is an entirely different plane of existence compared to you.]","Noah listened to these words as he nodded, his thoughts just being affirmed as he had already looked at this possibility while using <<Herald of Fate>>!","He would not have been able to even fathom if he could somehow obtain quantifiable or actual benefits from him actually absorbing the core of an entire world. Unlike him, a world did not have statistical values. It did not have vitality, strength, or focus. Nor did it have any skills or abilities. It was an entity that was bound by the universal laws!","It was him that was an anomaly! It was him that had stepped out of the bounds of his existence and actually intruded upon the existence that was a world, being able to actually devour its Core through using the large reserves of mana that he was borrowing from the many worlds he was already connected to.","He thought of the two options that the planetary system had laid out for the possibilities on what to do with world cores as at this moment, he was focusing on the first one. The use of the world core to fulfilling the requirement that the Spiritual Land needed!","In the void of space, Noah’s clone glanced at the destruction that he had caused, the debris of an entire star floating around him as he began to disappear in particles of light.","He reappeared in the underground space of the Spiritual Sand as he looked in the Time Space where multiple beasts had already broken into the Soul Forging Realm.","The emperor penguin was of course the first, with the Arctic Wolf and the Polar Bear following there after, where now only two of the spiritual beasts had yet to finish their breakthroughs!","Noah waited patiently as he thought about his recent actions, his heart not wavering one bit.","To make sure that no problems occurred for what he was about to do he teleported out of the spiritual land and made sure that everyone was contained in it, leaving behind the ancient pedestal that held the Inheritance of the Disciple of Fire as he used anchor to place the spiritual land on his body where he then disappeared once again from the volcanic mountain.","This time when he reappeared, he was actually near the Ancient Blood World that stood at the junction between the Light and Dark Expanse. This was an area that he knew very few beings would be passing by as he laid out this spiritual land in the vastness of space and let it bloom to its full size!","The spiritual land that could have been considered a floating city multiple tiers ago could now already be called a country in itself. Noah always messed around with the spiritual land’s size regulation feature, so he never really let it bloom to its full size in the past months, with the spiritual land almost always remaining miniaturized as he moved along with it.","This time around he was in the vastness of space as he let the spiritual land freely get to what could be considered its size at the eighth tier. The enormous floating landmass bloomed further and further as Noah’s figure slowly became the size of an ant. The spiritual land itself continued to expand while he pulled back further and further to observe its enormous size.","When he made some quick calculations as the fantastical landmass that was holding its large shade of white color and still keeping to its name as the Frozen Plateau Spiritual Land, he found that it was approximately around one thousand miles in size!","This was a landmass that had been obtained in the Frozen Kingdom of the Beast World. At that time this landmass was only a few tens of miles long being something that floated in the skies near the frozen kingdom.","Yet now, the Spiritual Land had grown to a size of over 1,000 miles, and from what Noah expected, after the upgrade to the ninth tier that actually required the core of a small world, this Spiritual Land was about to get even bigger!","RUMBLE!","He glanced at spiritual land management As he saw under the Upgrade Conditions for the number of beasts to reach 10 had turned green. For the requirement of a small world core, it had also turned green!","The spiritual land could already sense a core of a small world on the body of its master, and the requirements could be considered completed as now all that was needed was an immense amount of energy and essence in order to initiate the upgrade from the eight tier and into the ninth tier.","This was an upgrade that required the core of a small world, so what exactly would be the boons of it come out of it? What exactly would the possible Locked feature that was listed as [Division] for this next stage of the spiritual land hold in store?!","Noah wasted no further time as he looked at the mystically floating landmass that stably stood in space, his thoughts already moving to initiate the upgrade to the 9th Tier!"]},{"number":419,"title":"Chapter 419: Chapter 418 - An Upgrade of Enormous Significance!","paragraphs":["The mystical spiritual land floated in the vastness of space near the junction of the light expanse in the Dark Expanse it had a blue light film of light covering it in its entirety, making sure that it acted as a protective barrier between the suffocating space and the beings that were currently within the spiritual land. To them, the environment had changed from the red blazing earth and lava that was the volcanic mountain that they were under, and now when they looked to the skies of the spiritual land all they could see was the expanse of space!","Some of the more knowledgeable beings in the spiritual land knew that something grand was about to happen. This was even more so for the beings that had followed Noah the longest, as the Calamities of the Sea, along with Barbatos, Kazuhiko, Steel Mikhail, and many others that cl.u.s.tered near the center of the spiritual land where Noah had built the most pristine buildings while using the [Architecture] feature of the spiritual land.","While a majority of the beings gathered here, the emperor penguin appeared in the skies of the spiritual land, his brothers and sisters not too far behind him as the 10 of them looked out into the void of space, barely being able to see Noah’s clone through their connection that they held to this Spiritual Land Master.","Their bodies had the aurora of having just broken through to the Soul Forging Realm, completing one of the requirements as they simply waited for yet another resplendent upgrade to occur in the land that they were born in. They had a deep trust in their master, and simply bid their time as they waited for the event to start!","Noah’s clone was staring at this fantastical sight that was a spiritual land as he put aside his thoughts and commanded the item that was contained in the large stomach ability of the Sin of Gluttony.","Right in front of him, the sizable core of a Small World appeared, not rotating anymore as it floated stably in space. Noah’s thoughts then went to the {Spiritual Land Management} which showed the upgrade conditions as met and without further ado, he went ahead and initiated the upgrade of the spiritual land from the eighth year and into the ninth tier!","RUMBLE!","The world core that was standing next to him suddenly shot out with extreme speed as it was attracted onto the floating spiritual land, going through and easily passing through the blue film of light as it continued downwards. The soil that it was about to hit on the snowy area of a spiritual land seemingly opened up in front of this core as it continued to shoot down further and deeper into the spiritual land without any issues until it settled in a place that could be considered near the very center of the spiritual land deep in the underground area where the Time Space and the Blacksmith’s Forge was located!","OOONG!","In the vastness of space, the spiritual land began rumbling with energy as from Noah’s body, a ridiculous amount of mana began flowing out. The spiritual land itself was using the atmospheric essence it held along with the energies in the void of space and dropping them towards its center as the process of upgrading the spiritual land from the eighth tier and the ninth tier went underway.","If one would describe it, it would be a cacophony of colors and regality where one could observe blue essence rushing in one direction, red essence rushing in another, and a gorgeous color of white bathing every inch and corner of the spiritual land!","What many could observe before they had to close their eyes as it was shining too brightly, was actually the mana that was leaking out of Noah’s ancient blood clone. It was coming out at such a rate that one could visibly see the shining blue color that continued to descend down towards the enormous spiritual land.","Noah simply acted like a conduit as he 100% knew at this moment that he was the only being who remotely had the possibility of doing something like this, the mana that was required being something that maybe only those nearing the peak of power in the Novus Galaxy being able to provide!","This reality of upgrading this unique treasure called the Spiritual Land simply required too much mana that when he looked at people like Steel Mikhail and Kazuhiko or the Imperial Phoenix that held their own spiritual lands, he knew for sure that they would never be able to upgrade their Tiers at the stage that he was currently doing.","They would never be able to get their hands on a world core, nor be able to provide this abundant energy that was all coming out of the reserves of the many stars he was connected to!","This led him to briefly think about all the things that had brought him here. How the Beast World that was being overtaken by the demons from the Demon World was the reason for and where his journey into other worlds began. With the demon invasion and then entering the Beast world to fight off the demons until he got his hands on the Spiritual Land in the process.","He thought of all the events that led up to him obtaining this unique treasure and what had happened since then as everything seemed to be steered by the hands of fate!","He seemed to be a singular being that met the many strict conditions to do what he was currently doing because of a coincidental set of events that all led here!","It was at this stage but he evaluated many of the things that had occurred to him as he wondered, just how many of them were based on his choices and his actions, and how many were steered by an unknown hand of fate?","He actually found himself asking a question that a certain War Princess always had in her heart. What exactly did fate have in store for him?","He held no answer at this moment as he put these terrifying thoughts in the back of his mind and continued observing the upgrade of something beautiful.","He visibly watched the floating landmass that was the spiritual land continue to expand ever so larger, its size going from 1,000 miles to 1,500 and then simply doubling to 2,000 from the original size when it was in the Eighth Tier. When it reached approximately 2,000 miles in all directions, light continued to converge towards it with even more vigor. The blue thin film of light that surrounded it only getting stronger as it reached a crescendo of buildup!","RUMBLE!","At this point in time, from the circular shape of the floating spiritual land a blast of blue light released from it that went out in all directions. It was a light that announced the completion of something grand, of something beautiful, as even Noah’s eyes were blinded by the light entirely!","His eyes opened to glance at the magnificent Spiritual Land thereafter as he observed it now held an even stronger protective film of light, its grandeur stably standing in the void of space as at this moment, he shockingly heard something that could only be coming out at the center of the Spiritual Land.","[Hello, Master.]","Noah’s eyes opened wide as he heard this voice, his gaze focusing on the spiritual land and piercing through the many layers as he followed the voice to the exact center of this floating landmass where he now saw a powerfully shining blue core slowly rotating, the voice that he had heard in his mind coming from this exact location!","For the first time in the past day since he received the Infernal Lord title, Noah finally found himself having a real smile as he was faced with this new situation.","His expression was actually joyful as he realized a consciousness had appeared from the Frozen Plateau Spiritual Land the moment it absorbed the core of a small world and was upgraded from the eighth and into the ninth tier! This voice was also very similar to the voice of the Small World that he had obtained the Core from!","Furthermore, under the management skill he had always used for this floating landmass, he had seen a change of words from Spiritual Land and into Spiritual World!","...!!!"]},{"number":420,"title":"Chapter 420: Chapter 419 - A Manager!","paragraphs":["A mystically floating landmass was amazingly stationed in the void of space, its size nearing that of Small Worlds.","In the past, it could have been called a Spiritual Land. But currently, it was known as a Spiritual World!","Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone glanced at this marvel as he replied to the robot like voice in his mind.","\"You are...\"","[The essence of the Spiritual World. With your permission, I will be overseeing many of its functions, being capable of designing cities and countries, as well as using all the other features under Spiritual World Management to craft in the Blacksmith’s Forge or design the Law Spaces.]","A wonderful reply came to his mind as he explored the fantastical situation opening itself to him after the upgrade of the Spiritual World. He nodded as he glanced at the skill that was now renamed {Spiritual World Management} first!","{Spiritual World Management}","[Frozen Plateau-9]","Beasts: F-XXX, E-XXX, D-XXX, C-XXX, B-XXX, A-XXX, S-XXX, EPIC-15,285, LEGENDARY-6,613, MYTHICAL-3,163, PHANTASMAL-749, TRANSCENDENT-242, Saint- 42, Void- 21, Soul-10","Plants- Whitefall Trees, Snow Vine, Sacred Rye, Pigmy Melon, Ice-fire Persimmon, Ice Phoenix Fruits, Spirit of the Arctic, Frozen Angelica, Regal Flora, Qilin’s Cold Stone, Resonant Okra, Arctic Flora, King’s Collard, Athramire, Phantom Mulberry. Available for planting( Fire Starter, Frigid Apple)","Features- Size Regulation(Unlocked), Movement(Unlocked), Anchor(Unlocked), Boost Surroundings(Unlocked), Architecture(Unlocked), Frozen Barrier(Unlocked), Offensive Maneuvers(Unlocked), Time Dilation(Unlocked), Treasure Hunter (Unlocked), Interstellar Travel(Unlocked), Law Space(Unlocked), Blacksmith’s Forge(Unlocked), Division(Unlocked), Alchemy Hall(Locked)[email protected]#%#$%(Locked)","Upgrade Conditions: 10+ Spiritual Land Beasts at the Domain Rank, A Large World Core","A large set of words shone in a clear blue in the panel of {Spiritual World Management}, Noah glancing through all the changes as he observed the newest ones with shining eyes.","The first thing he noticed was the fairly eye catching descriptions of the new medicinal plants available for planting!","<strong>[Fire Starter] :: A unique medicinal herb that can only grow in the Fire Law Space. The matured herb will contain the essence of the Law of Fire, granting those that consume it faster comprehension in this law. Maturing Time- 10 Years.</strong>","<strong>[Frigid Apple] :: A unique fruit that can only grow in the Water Law Space. The matured herb will contain the essence of the Law of Water, granting those that consume it faster comprehension in this law. Maturing Time- 10 Years.</strong>","Noah read over the description of the plants that were the first of their kind to actually give benefits to laws. The long maturing time that was attached to them did not bother him one bit as he had [Budding Farmer] to reduce this time by a large amount, and he also planned to have many of them planted in the Time Space of the Spiritual World that was many miles wide now!","Next up, he observed the newly unlocked feature, which was called [Division].","<strong>[Division] :: The Spiritual World is unique, holding features that are rare to find across the stars. One of these features is the ability to divide the Spiritual World into connected landmasses, giving one the versatility of designing something that is only limited by their imagination.</strong>","A fairly straightforward description that also left a lot of things in the air floated in front of him, his mind already thinking of the possibilities when he heard the voice of the Spiritual World again.","[Master, this Division Feature can be used to exquisitely design areas where you can have things like different Law Spaces or special environments. The Fire Law Space could be made into its own floating island, the Time Space could have its own area, and much more.]","Noah listened to the thoughts seamlessly entering his mind as he knew he would be utilizing this Spiritual World to an even bigger potential now that it had an entity to do every single task for him.","All he would need to do was give the commands on what he wanted to be done, and this entity would carry it out in the best way possible! He already had a grand image in his mind of this Spiritual World having exquisitely designed areas with multiple environments and Law Spaces, specifically designated lands for farming and architecture from different worlds appearing beautifully all around this large Spiritual World.","These were all ideas in his mind, but this entity that now stood at the center of the Spiritual World would make them a reality in the future!","He put these thoughts aside as he continued looking through the changes under {Spiritual World Management}, seeing that all the previous features were boosted in their own ways. He glanced at the upgraded changes under the [Law Space] feature as currently, only the Fate and Chaos Spaces seemed to be remaining locked.","<strong>[Law Space] :: Fields containing a higher concentration of particular laws can be created, granting increased comprehension speed to all that cultivate within. Currently unlocked spaces: Water, Fire, Earth, Air, Time, Space, Light, Dark. Locked spaces: Fate, Chaos...</strong>","It seemed like the next upgrade of tiers for the Spiritual World would be when he would be able to make the Fate and Chaos Spaces which should be able to drastically improve how fast he condensed Fate Lines and Chaos Particles. He glanced at the changes of the Blacksmith’s Forge next.","[Blacksmith’s Forge]- Unlocked Features: [Forge] [Refine] [Repair] [Recipe Design]. Locked Features: [Evolve]...","A new feature had been unlocked, this time being the [Recipe Design]!","<strong>[Recipe Design] :: The Spiritual World Master can design Item Blueprints that the forge can then analyze the viability before they are forged with the required materials. </strong>","A simple explanation laid out in front of him, giving him even more thoughts as he knew he would be very busy in the coming days with all the things he had on his hands.","The last thing he looked at was the conditions to upgrade to the 10th Tier, requiring a similar number of beasts like last time to reach the next rank, but the requirement of a Large World Core going along with it. This was a fairly difficult requirement, as it was nigh impossible to find a Large World that was uninhabitable and did not have any beings in the billions populating it.","This was because a world only had the possibility of reaching that stage because of the fates of the beings it carried if it wasn’t already at that stage in the beginning. This meant that when the time came for him to look for the Core of a Large World, he had to be creative or end up doing something horrendous!","But he left all of these thoughts for the future as he currently focused on the task at hand. There were a multitude of things he wanted to explore in this fantastical newly upgraded Spiritual World, and he also wanted to begin the Dual Cultivation of Chaos and Fate, where he focused on Fate next as he brought the number of Fate Lines from 26,000 and pushed it further up. The number of Lines of Fate was already slowly increasing as his main body was with Athena in the Celestial Realm continuously purifying materials from Chaos Behemoths, but it’s rate did not even come close to the speed he found with his Dual Cultivation method!","His body disappeared into particles of light as he descended into the Spiritual Land first, wanting to test its new Manager as well as observe how it would carry out the features!"]},{"number":421,"title":"Chapter 421: Chapter 420 - Breathtaking","paragraphs":["Steel Mikhail glanced at the surroundings of the Spiritual Land as he had his usual cold exterior on the outside, but inside his heart was trembling at the continuing unfolding situation around him!","This Protector still referred to the landmass he was on as the Spiritual Land, but even he was wondering whether this was an apt name for such a fantastical place that was now floating in the void of space.","He sensed the overflowing essence as his gaze and the gazes of many others looked to the skies of the Spiritual Land, seeing twinkling stars above them as they became entranced by it. From the position he was at, he knew that even with the limits of where he could spread his aura, he wouldn’t be able to fully ascertain the size of this Spiritual Land that had grown immensely larger.","This wasn’t to mention the area overflowing with the Law of Fire that had allowed him to condense a Fire Origin Core after obtaining the Inheritance that Noah led them to not too long ago.","Steel Mikhail thought about this being that at one stage, he had considered to be on the same level as him! Now, he seemed so extremely far away, to the point that he did not even know which manner to talk to him anymore. The powerful air he released made him seem foreign, like an entirely different person from when he first met him in the Blessed Empire.","He had looked at this being before as a much stronger Hunter who provided much needed help to push back against the demons, but ever since then, the things he continued to do had just continued to astound and break the common sense that all the people like him had.","The things he did were so ridiculous to wrap one’s mind around that if he told himself of the events just four months ago, he would laugh as he threw them aside as lies!","There were somehow numerous portals in this being’s Spiritual Land that connected to multiple worlds. Oh and somehow, he had descended down or sent his forces into these worlds to lead them to submission. Aside from this fantastic floating land, he was able to enter the ranks of the most powerful beings of their Galaxy and seamlessly stay in their ranks, gaining access to a realm unlike anything from their imaginations.","He was also able to gain something secretive like the bloodline of the Vampyre Progenitor, where he shared other bloodlines of Vampyres like nothing to him and many others, his hands being so full that he simply created a portal connecting their small blue planet to a Prime World called an Ancient Blood World that held its own unique and amazing opportunities.","There were so many things occurring around this being that if Mikhail was to tell himself this in the past, he wouldn’t believe it!","And now, on the latest venture, he had his Spiritual Land upgraded to another tier yet again as Mikhail felt an unexplainable feeling. He had the thought that the land he was standing on actually did not feel all that different from the worlds that he had the chance to travel into because of Noah.","This thought actually scared him as the implications of this Spiritual Land being a world carried an immense weight that he could not fully fathom right now!","Steel Mikhail was surrounded by the other Harbingers as they watched spectacular changes appearing right in front of their eyes, those with high realms being able to spread their auras out as they began to observe large scale changes that shocked them to their cores.","They first watched as Noah appeared in the skies of the Spiritual Land far away from them, where they could only observe if they used long distance skills as the land they were on had become exceedingly vast after the last upgrade.","But they saw his appearance in the skies, and then felt shaking thereafter as they observed a stupendous sight of huge sections of landmasses splitting apart, some rising while others fell!","RUMBLE!","They shockingly watched as a landmass of a few hundred miles rose in the north, and others of similar size breaking off from the Spiritual Land and rising in the south, east, and west.","They were left on what could now be considered a central landmass where much of the architecture was at, their jaws agape as a coalescence of colorful essence and lights covered the four huge landmasses that were hundreds of miles long!","To their North, the huge landmass that had risen there had the Fire Law Space that they were cultivating the Disciple of Fire in before, its sheen being slight red as those whose eyes could observe more would be able to see that the Fire Law Space was expanding rapidly, going on to cover most of this floating island as the atmospheric fire elements began to wildly converge in this particular island.","The other ones did not have a Law Space initiated to be built yet, so the next thing they could observe was the formation of resplendent blue lines from each of the risen land masses as they connected to one another, and to the central landmass they were on as well!","These blue lines shimmered as they seemed to be calling forth the surrounding earth, the beings in the Spiritual World watching with agape expressions as solid earth converged on these blue lines that connected the landmasses and began forming into the shapes of exquisitely designed bridges.","It was something reminiscent of the small floating peaks of the Frozen Kingdom in the Beast World that had staircases one could climb in a matter of minutes to reach another peak, but the huge bridges and stairs being created to connect each of the landmasses that had broken off from the Spiritual World were tens of miles long, with some even being more than a hundred miles long!","It was a scene straight out of fantasy as in front of the eyes of shocked beings, four huge islands had broken off from a central one on the Spiritual Land, huge and long connections being built on each of these floating islands as a beautiful scenery was created.","OOOM","Essence gradually settled down on the Spiritual World that floated stably in the void of space between the Light and Dark Expanse. If one were to observe from the expanse of space, they would see an extremely large landmass that could be considered an entire world by its size. A blue film of light shimmered and surrounded this small world as one could distinctly see four smaller continental land masses on each of the four directions of this world!","It was a scene of a never before seen world with a unique look, but this was just the beginning as the possibilities for what could be designed in this wondrous Spiritual World were endless!"]},{"number":422,"title":"Chapter 422: Chapter 421 - Cultivating","paragraphs":["Noah glanced at the results of the Division feature of the Spiritual World as a fantastical sight of four huge land masses that could be considered Continents separated from the central landmass that held the Time Space and the Blacksmith’s Forge.","The continents were mostly filled with a similar type of essence and environment, the only thing different being the one in the North that was slowly turning fully into a fiery continent that was filled with the Law of Fire.","Many possibilities lied in front of him as he sent a message to the Spiritual World System.","\"You can handle the farming of the new plants and designing architecture and layouts of these continents?\"","[Yes. Just let me know which style of architecture you wish for, as well as any ideas you have for Recipe Design and the building of new Law Spaces. Anything you need, I can handle.]","An extremely competent reply came from the System as Noah nodded, seeing that he had placed a significant amount of time in this particular task that an entire day had passed.","He currently looked at the passing of days as extremely crucial, as his mind had calculations of what he could possibly achieve in a single day in terms of Fate Lines and Chaos Particles. If he was doing anything else and a day passed, it felt he missed out big in advancing his power forward!","The upgrade of the Spiritual World was more than worth it, as he left things in the hands of the Spiritual World System and glanced towards the few beings he had in the Spiritual World.","There were a large majority of Spiritual Beasts populating the central landmass, with other cl.u.s.ters in the risen continents aside from the fiery ones the current beasts were still major of the Ice Element.","When he came to this thought process, he couldn’t help but ask something that was on his mind.","\"The beasts that were born in this Spiritual Land were always of the Ice Type Element. If the convergence of essence in the continent that is covered by the Law of Fire births new Spiritual Beasts, will they be of the Fire Element?\"","Noah’s mind was already thinking in this manner, simply wanting a confirmation at this wondrous possibility.","[Yes. When the Earth Law Space or Fate Law Space or Chaos Law Space are established in the future, beasts of those respective elements will also have probabilities of being born.]","A spectacular affirmation came as Noah shook his head at the wonders of the Spiritual World, looking towards the Harbingers and other beings that were looking at him with reverence and a tinge of fear.","Some understood his power and knew him for a long time, others only heard stories as they now came face to face with him and looked at him in an entirely different manner.","The beasts of the Spiritual World like Emperor Penguin simply looked at his figure with shining eyes filled with strength and trust, making his heart settle with ease as the more he rose in power, the more alone he felt.","Even with the company of women like Adelaide and Barbatos, he only had a chance to be around them briefly as he was constantly moving, his heart settling down when he was around them and had a chance to relax, but most of his time was divided into adventuring into new lands or facing powerful enemies, with him doing almost everything alone.","It was a unique feeling that those on the path of power would occasionally find themselves in. A position where they seemed to be forging ahead while others were just trying to keep up!","It was the solitude one felt when they were in a position that others could not come close to! Even someone like Prince Cassius who Noah could talk freely with in the past, he could not do so anymore. The moment the prince moved together with her aunt and saw the actual picture of Noah’s true strength, a change occurred as he knew they weren’t even remotely close to the same positions, not looking at Noah the way he used to before.","Noah sighed as he sent telepathic commands to the Emperor Penguin and Elena, as well as the other major figures that over the worlds he was connected to as he cast one more skill before he disappeared from the skies of the Spiritual World.","He cast [World Veil] that now applied to this unique treasure of his, letting it stay in this expanse of space for now as he prepared to come in contact with powerful laws.","He would set no time for celebration or anything like that for this amazing upgrade that had turned the Spiritual Land into a Spiritual World, teleporting away from it as he appeared tens of thousands of miles away from the junction of the Light Expanse and the Dark Expanse where he would leave the Spiritual World briefly, letting those within cultivate as others could use the portals in the Central land mass to head back to their respective worlds whenever they wished.","His clone appeared far away in the void of vast space, feeling his eyes close as he enjoyed the weightlessness and power because of the [Child of Space] ability from the Lesser Cthulhu Skill Tree.","He felt extremely safe and content when he floated in this dark expanse of space, his heart already looking forward to when he would soon upgrade the skill tree of the Lesser Cthulhu along with Fate’s Guardian.","If one could place the things he had to do on a plate in the form of food, they would overflow as there were truly too many of them.","Skill trees, Laws, Celestials, Infernals, Ancients, the Spiritual World...there were so many things that he wished his Blood Lord ability could grant him another clone for him to do all of them!","His main body had been spending the last day with Athena as they continued their cultivation session that pushed Noah’s Fate Lines from 26,000 over 27,000 in the span of a day, this being an amazing number in the eyes of the Celestials.","But...he planned to start a cultivation session now where he would condense double the amount of fate lines that he and Athena condensed in a day...in just the span of an hour!","He looked forward to seeing the future results of obtaining close to 50,000 Fate Lines in the span of a day as he comfortably got in a seated position in the void of space he was in, clearing his mind as he initiated {Fate’s Disciple} first this time around, watching as a golden line of fate began falling down. His body pulsed as he shone gold and brought to surface the hidden Fate Lines already in his body, covering his surroundings with the aura of fate as he then slowly began also activating {Disciple of Chaos}, commanding just a few Chaos Particles to come to light as the golden aura of fate felt like it had found its biggest enemy, going forward and overpowered the few Chaos Particles as they were quickly wiped away and purified into nothingness.","This reaction of purifying pure chaos elements was rewarded with multiple Fate Lines that then went on to descend and attach to his body, this session being one where he increased the number of Fate Lines while Chaos Particles stalled, his heart at peace as he repeated the process and began wildly burning his mana as it poured endlessly into two techniques which cultivated two Supreme Laws!"]},{"number":423,"title":"Chapter 423: Chapter 422 - One Cultivates, One is Showered with Treasures.","paragraphs":["In the wide expanse of space, some starts shimmered brightly while others were dull. There were millions of these stars littered across this wide space as in a particular location, a being was floating peacefully in this terrifying void that many would not make as their home.","There was a splendor of golden color as around this being, one could see numerous lines of fate descending down consistently, the truly observant ones being able to notice the formation of a few Chaos Particles that were quickly purified by the intense aura of fate that was in the surroundings.","A calm expression was apparent on the being, Noah's Ancient Blood Clone, as he continued to make rapid progress in the Law of Fate, and this time there were no limits!","The process had already been going on for more than half a day, the area of space he was in being filled with an aurora of golden colors that spread throughout the blank void beautifully. In this span of half a day, he had already amassed more than 24,000 Fate Lines, obtaining the same amount of Fate Lines that he had spent the past weeks collecting after he first received the unique skill of {Fate's Disciple}.","The number of Fate lines he currently had was actually over 56,000 in total, his main body that was being spoiled with numerous materials and cores filled with the Law of Chaos adding on to the progression.","His Ancient Blood Clone continued the project of amassing fate lines as the plan was to complete a full day of cultivation before he moved on to do anything else. In the Celestial Realm, his main body was moving yet again through the fantastical and essence filled forests of this expansive realm. He was accompanied by the valiant Athena to his side as the Righteous Fire Exploration Team he was a part of was moving again towards the direction where the Elite Chaos Behemoths were located.","After spending a significant amount of time freely purifying the chaos materials and absorbing cores in the Celestial Watch Tower, the regiment of the Grandmaster was for them to head out once more to take down Chaos Behemoths.","This would allow for a rapid increase in their Fate Lines while giving them battle experience and the consolidation of their power that was being forcefully raised up through treasures.","With the abundant Soul Rank Cores that Noah and Athena continued receiving, Noah did not doubt that the Celestials were confident in forcefully pushing the levels of the beings they knew to be of Noble Fates to the Domain Expansion Realm soon enough!","This was a type of treatment that would normally draw in jealousy, as even the powerful Boru felt the strength of Athena nearing his while Noah was not too far away. But these beings that were following the lessons of Celestials did not show any outward signs of discontentment as they even volunteered their own materials, attributing this all for the cause of reducing Chaos and maintaining Order!","ROAR!","Yet another powerful Elite Chaos Behemoth fell in the hands of the Righteous Fire Team that was led by the returning Grandmaster Vredral, the beast holding enormous chaos essence slumping down unwillingly as the Domain of Fate that the Grandmaster Released had only gotten stronger.","This powerful Grandmaster was receiving a higher level of treatment than many others, his power also continuing to rise rapidly as he acted on a grand scale to influence the fates of beings in the Light Expanse. He was also the one that had initiated the campaign to allow the inhabitants of Light Expanse to enter the Celestial Realm, much of the influence obtained from this event also coming to him as his Fate Lines continued to increase!","Grandmaster Vredral cut through the body of the Chaos Behemoth as he pulled out a shimmering dark Chaos Core, the powerful chaos essence sizzling as it floated a few inches from his hands.","ZING!","A golden glow shined out as the powerful Domain Rank core was cut into pieces, each of them floating towards an out of breath Athena and Noah that were leaning on each other's backs as they recovered their energy after the tough battle.","They reached out to grab the pieces of Chaos Cores as the Grandmaster spoke.","\"What we are currently doing can be considered violating the natural order, rapidly enhancing the rate at which you two increase your power. But the two of you are those with Noble Fates, having a big hand to play in the future which will go on to reduce an enormous amount of chaos! So the price we pay to achieve this is very small.\"","His voice was filled with conviction as the two beings with Noble Fates looked at each other with determination. As they continued to train and move around each other, the Junior Brother and Senior Sister had gradually gotten closer, the impassive mask of Athena ever so slowly breaking down in front of Crixus as the battle driven War Princess was even leaning on the back of her Junior Brother to recuperate.","\"Since we are raising your power speedily, your realm and handling of essence will be very rough once you reach the Domain Expansion Realm. So for your next mission as you near this level is to handle an Elite Behemoth yourselves while I oversee things!\"","Stern expressions covered Noah and Athena's faces as the members of the Righteous Fire Exploration Team also looked forward seriously. With the abundant treasures and Cores that Noah and Athena continued to receive, they would undoubtedly be able to reach the next realm soon enough! With this knowledge, the Grandmaster wanted to use the opportunity to further stimulate their breakthrough as he wanted them to conduct a hunt against a Behemoth by themselves.","\"This will be one of the prices to pay for pushing your realm up so quickly, where we can at least stabilize your power as time goes on. Come, let us move on to the next one!\"","The Celestial Grandmaster waved his hands righteously as he pushed the Exploration Team to continue, an amazing event currently playing out in the Celestial Realm!","Those with Noble Fates had the full backing of this powerful organization, the abundant treasures they had collected over the years being something they could use to push the realm of whoever they wanted higher at a rapid rate. This time around as the war approached, the Celestials were focusing their resources on beings with Noble Fates like Noah and Athena, with others holding the same title not appearing in front of them yet as they were under the leadership of other Grandmasters!","Aside from those with Noble Fates, Grandmasters with high comprehension in the Law of Fate were also favored as resources continued to be taken from the vaults of the Celestials and spent wildly, leaving no risk for the coming war as they prepared.","Although just as quickly as they were depleting their treasure vaults, even more materials and cores were coming in from the half tax imposed on all the beings they allowed to move in the Celestial Realm.","Although unknown to the Celestials yet, a stable spatial connection was on the process of being established between the Celestial Realm and the Dark Expanse through the use of unique skills of certain beings from the powerful Scholar's Guild as the side they were fighting on also began getting their hands on the share of resources!"]},{"number":424,"title":"Chapter 424: Chapter 423 - A Vast Number of Abilities","paragraphs":["In the Southern Region of the Celestial Realm where Behemoths proficient in the Law of Water resided, the powerful beings from the Scholar’s guild had gathered into a nondescript area underground as they finalized their spatial connection and made sure that nothing was out of place!","\"Agrus, you are sure that even with the Celestial’s method in the Law of Fate, they would not be able to discern what we are doing here?\"","Malthus, the Spatial Magician from the Scholar’s Guild asked Agrus, the ’Walking Library’, who was relaxing in the cold underground area without a worry. The relaxing Malthus replied while stretching his hands, his eyes gazing upon the structures that a few figures had already begun building in the wide space they were in.","\"Just as the Celestials have their own mysterious abilities and means, increasing their power over the last thousand years- so have we!\"","He spoke with a slightly passionate expression as he pushed the glasses on his face up, his hand reaching into his robe as he pulled out a dark pulsing object that caused the expression on Malthus to change.","\"That is...the Chaos Wand?!\"","\"Sadly no, just an imitation of it. But this is more than enough for our uses to evade the eyes of the Celestials as we build a connection that will be able to stably transfer both materials and eventually beings to our nearby bases that aren’t under the gazes of Celestials.\"","Malthus’s gaze was still on the glowing dark stick as he asked once more, knowing full well the history of such an object that his partner held!","\"What did you say to the Elders for them to hand you a Chaos Wand, even if it is an imitation...\"","His gaze was that of envy as he looked at this powerful weapon, Agrus chuckling as he replied.","\"The Scholar’s Guild is one that operates on knowledge and power. After those old Wizards were hit with such losses from being utterly unprepared to counter attack the techniques of Celestials in the past war, they have been dutifully moving, this time associating too much with the Infernal Lords as they have been gaining large benefits in knowledge and items such as this...\"","Argus revealed secretive information as Malthus nodded his head unwillingly and sighed, knowing the treasure in his friend’s hand was something extremely valuable, actually being the main thing that would render the eyes of the Celestials and their powerful techniques powerless in this region they were in!","This was a weapon that was simply an imitation designed from the knowledge that the powerful Scholar’s Guild had been collecting since their defeat a thousand years ago, working closely with the beings proficient in Chaos, the Infernal Lords, to get to a new level of power that gave them a level of confidence against any future wars!","This was the level of power of the Scholar’s Guild, one of the forces besides the Vampyre Clans holding the Alliance of the Dark Expanse together.","Those that were knowledgeable called the powerful beings in the Scholar’s Guild Magicians, some called them Warlocks and Witches, with others even calling them mages! But those truly knowing the truth behind the scenes would know them as those with Blessed Knowledge, beings that were extremely proficient in magic as they used powerful weapons to channel the universal laws to their will!","This Chaos Wand that the ’Walking Library’ Argus held was one of these powerful weapons that was drenched in the Law of Chaos, granting a shade from the powerful skills under <<Herald of Fate>> that the Celestials could use.","Agrus had a profound expression as he continued to reply to Malthus.","\"There is a great deal of things in this wide Galaxy of ours, and Celestials do not hold all of them. There is a vast abundance of abilities that even they do not know. What the old fogeys at the top of our Guild are trying to do now is prevent the further advancement of these Celestials to the point that even with our knowledge, we will not be able to compete.\"","Malthus nodded as his body glowed with a silver light, continuing to layer more and more runic signs onto a huge portal as he completed their project with ease.","\"Our entrance into this Celestial Realm that I suspect to be near the center of our Galaxy is one of them, with many other projects that even I do not know.\"","\"What about the being moving with Elena, the one known as Noah Osmont?\"","Malthus asked the Walking Library more questions as he wondered of the being they had knowledge to have entered the ranks of Celestials as he slowly moved. Agrus thought of this for a bit before he replied.","\"He is just one of the cards that the Vampyres Clans are playing, with their aim being a special being that is locked within the 7th Celestial Star. But he is surprisingly rising fast within the ranks of Celestials that now his name has even reached the fogeys at the top of the Scholar’s Guild, working hard to discern how they can use him after he also made our entrance into the Celestial Realm even easier.\"","A shocking reply came from the Walking Library as he talked about someone that not many beings fully understood yet!","Agrus had a careful expression as he continued.","\"Though I feel there is something else with him. Elena is too careful when it comes to any information about him, and she is the one that has direct contact with him.\"","\"Oh? You think the Silver Beauty has fallen for the charms of this upcoming genius?\"","Malthus asked with a smile as Agrus continued to lazily stare at the completed connection in front of them.","\"Who knows. She hasn’t even been replying to my communications these past few days after letting me know she would be busy. Come on, let’s focus on completing our work, we already have too many Behemoth materials to transport.\"","The beings of the Dark Expanse continued moving as more and more entered the Celestial Realm, beginning their own search and collection of the treasures in this wide realm as they also planned for the future!","Within their discussions was a being they considered a minor figure, someone they knew to be called Noah Osmont and also had the secret identity as Crixus the Destroyer! Very few higher ups in the Vampyre Clans and the Scholar’s Guild knew of this information, but they simply placed this being a small piece to be played in the much grander puzzle that was chaotically moving all these years!","Many of them were very wrong on exactly what level of a role this being would play in the months and years to come!"]},{"number":425,"title":"Chapter 425: Chapter 424 - Just a Glimpse of True Genius!","paragraphs":["Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone opened his crimson eyes in the void of space, his figure’s devilishly handsome look being enhanced in this environment as he floated in darkness and had an aurora of golden colored lights and fate lines all around him.","His dark hair that had streaks of silver was growing ever so larger, nearing his shoulders once more as it shimmered with its own essence! He got up from his seated position in the void of space as he stopped burning enormous amounts of mana into {Fate’s Disciple} and {Disciple of Chaos}, the overflowing golden color brought about by the Lines of Fate beginning to die down as he finished the second cultivation session while using the method that was unique only to him.","After half a day, he had added another 24,000 Fate Lines as he brought his full amount to just over 81,000! This number already neared those who would cultivate for years, and he has achieved it in the span of a day!","At this moment in time, his Fate Lines were leading once more as the Chaos Particles remained at around 50,000, his next cultivation session would be to burn fate lines and increase the Chaos Particles as he expected them to break over the one hundred thousand milestone.","Breaking the 100,000 milestone would allow one to begin using Fate Lines and Chaos Particles in a new way, granting them the ability to release pure Fate and Chaos Energy in their attacks that were even deadlier to the opposing element!","The War Princess Athena would soon break past this point, but Noah would not be far behind as he would soon even surpass her at a rate that would shock them if they knew.","Noah’s goal was to still appear as a genius in the eyes of the Celestials, and he would expose this genius some more over the next few days as he slowly revealed his rapidly increasing fate lines at a rate that would make them think he was a terrifying genius, yet not treat him like an anomaly to be researched. But whatever he showed them would simply be just a glimpse of what he could truly do!","His expression was determined as he glanced around the void of space around him, the golden light having died down majorly as things went back to normal. His figure turned into particles of light as he disappeared from the location and returned to the Spiritual World.","He appeared above this massive and fantasy like treasure that looked like a huge landmass which was connected to four shimmering floating continental landmasses as he took in the magnificence before his energy began to flow over, activating the [Size Regulation] feature of the Spiritual World as then enormous star sized treasure began shrinking rapidly!","RUMBLE!","The essence required to use features like Size Regulation were increased by an enormous amount as the tier of the Spiritual World increased, but this meant nothing to Noah as the large treasure continued to shrink in his eyes until it was a few inches, his mind never being able to understand how the spacial mysteries worked with this feature that effectively meant he could have an entire world be the size of his thumb, yet when he entered it, it would still seem like a massive world in his eyes! It was a scene of fantasy that made one suspend their beliefs and simply enjoy the brilliance of such a treasure!","The Spiritual World was then anchored to his body as he disappeared from the junction of Light and Dark Expanse, returning to the Ancient Pedestal below the volcanic mountain as the next plans were to let the powerful beasts and Elena return to their exploration of the Celestial Realm as they increased their power, the Fire Origin Cores and powerful abilities from the Inheritance of the Disciple of Fire being put to full use as they continued their advancement.","Elena’s figure appeared in the lava filled space as she looked towards Noah with an expression of infatuation, the Emperor Penguin and others also appearing as their forces prepared to move out.","\"Master, the forces of the Dark Expanse were successful in setting up a spatial connection, and they should be able to freely collect the treasures of this realm as they increase their power as well.\"","Elena sent a telepathic message towards Noah as his eyes seemed to be asking for praise as she continued to reveal secrets about the forces that still thought she had her allegiance with. Noah nodded towards the curvaceous woman as he patted her head full of silver hair, an expression of happiness spreading out as Noah talked while glancing at all of them.","\"Be careful as you move, and if you run into any Elite Behemoths, call me right away.\"","His forces nodded with seriousness as they began to move out, their bodies equipped with powerful Bloodstained Infernal Sets from the materials of millions of Infernals that Noah had hunted while he was bringing the percentage of Infernal Lord to 100%.","He had saved an enormous amount of the bodies of Infernals as he left the job of crafting them to the Spiritual World System over the last day, many of his forces being armed with the powerful items that protected them against Flame Behemoths!","A few of them were even wearing completed Incandescent Flameborn Sets, two more sets being able to be completed as Noah used the material that his main body had received as well as Behemoths that Elena and the others had hunted. Their bodies shone with strength and power as he expected them to be able to handle Normal Fire Behemoths with ease, and this was especially so for the Emperor Penguin and Elena that held the Incandescent Flameborn Sets!","His clone had yet to begin crafting the materials of Elite Chaos Behemoths that he was slowly collecting, his heart set on collecting all materials and completing a full set instantly some time soon.","As for the next task of the clone, it was to oversee the upgrade of another skill tree as his main body continued to use it while fighting alongside Celestials, the powerful skill tree that was [Fate’s Guardian] being the next one that was ready to be upgraded!","The clone glanced at the panel that showed the information of the possible advancement paths as he began choosing which of the many Void Rank skills he had obtained as loot to sacrifice.","<strong>[Fate’s Guardian](45/45) :: As a beginner just learning the workings of fate, the role of a guardian that protects the weak and eviscerates evil is given to you. Abilities include Empyrean Guards(5/5), Empyrean Armament(5/5), Smite of Liberation(5/5), and Judgment(5/5). Two Skill Trees for evolution are possible once sufficient points and a base requirement of two equivalent level sacrificial skills are reached: >> [Devout Follower] :: A follower on the path of fate, grants the user protective abilities that will enhance their power and those around them. >> [Unruly Guider] :: A path of one that questions and forms their own rules, using immense offensive power to guide lost beings. </strong>","The two choices of advancement for [Fate’s Guardian] was either [Devout Follower] or [Unruly Guider]! The impassive gaze of the clone already knew the choice he would make as unimportant skills were sacrificed, a light of brilliance shining out as a tinge of gold covered the blue stat panel, another skill tree advancing silently!"]},{"number":426,"title":"Chapter 426: Chapter 425 - Unruly Guider!","paragraphs":["The eyes of the Ancient Blood Clone shone with splendor as he watched one skill pathway disappear and another one fully settle in under [Fate’s Guardian]. The one to disappear was Devout Follower, with the one he chose being [Unruly Guider]!","The stat panel shone as new words and abilities were shown to Noah’s eyes, the skill tree going on to add four new abilities as he glanced at their descriptions.","<strong>SOUL [Fate’s Guardian](45/45) :: As a beginner just learning the workings of fate, the role of a guardian that protects the weak and eviscerates evil is given to you. Abilities include Empyrean Guards(5/5), Empyrean Armament(5/5), Smite of Liberation(5/5), and Judgment(5/5). >> [Unruly Guider] (0/60) :: A path of one that questions and forms their own rules, using immense offensive power to guide lost beings. Additional Abilities include Empyrean Ruler (0/5), Liberator (0/5), Fate Stealer(0/5) Golden Guider(0/5)</strong>","A new set of abilities were shown strongly on the skill tree of [Fate’s Guardian]. Noah glanced over at the skills as he began putting in skill points right away, wanting to see the full uncovered potential of these abilities right away!","<strong>[Empyrean Ruler] (5/5):: The number of Empyrean Guards that the Unruly Guider can summon is increased to 12.</strong>","<strong>[Liberator] (5/5) :: The Blades of Liberation feel the strong will of the Unruly Guider, gaining their own will as they stay alongside you to bring Judgement to your enemies. +180% Physical Damage, +180% Soul Damage, and +180% Attack Speed to the [Sword of Liberation] ability.</strong>","<strong>[Fate Stealer] (5/5) :: A support ability that is only activated when an enemy that is proficient in the workings of fate stands against the Unruly Guider and faces their death. 12% of the Fate Essence that they have collected over the years will be absorbed by the Guider.</strong>","<strong>[Golden Guider] (5/5) :: All the beings that are following the rule of the Unruly Guider are blessed with his source of strength as a portion of the user’s aura of fate surrounds them. To those classified as Subordinates of the Unruly Guider: +120% Physical, Soul, and Elemental Damage, +120% Cast and Attack Speed, +120% All Element Resistance, +120% Defense.</strong>","Clear and crisp descriptions that made Noah’s eyes shine were laid out in front of him, a spectacular set of abilities being added to his arsenal as he went through them slowly. [Empyrean Ruler] and [Liberator] were geared towards strengthening the skills under Fate’s Guardian, with [Fate Stealer] being something unique that would most likely allow him to increase his percentage in the Law of Fate faster if he took down beings also proficient in it.","The last skill [Golden Guider] was a particularly interesting one, as it actually granted fairly huge boosts to those following him. He didn’t have even a slight worry of the mention that a portion of his fate would surround them as he had long since used the abilities of <<Herald of Fate>> when he first received them to hide hisown fate, the world’s he was connected to, and all the beings around him!","This Absolute Skill was just another one of the skills that Noah had active at all times which continued to suck mana to remain this way, but it gave him boundless benefits of moving covertly with his forces while holding no worries.","Even if a Celestial were to be standing right next to someone like the Emperor Penguin and glance at his fate, all they would see would be a normal fate of a unique beast that had the bloodline of a Vampyre!","So Noah himself held no worries, with the only thing he wondered being exactly what classifications there were on who was considered his Subordinate. As his thoughts wondered, in another location in the Celestial Realm, the Order of Blood with Elena at the lead had already found and were hunting another Fire Behemoth when they felt an ecstatic feeling of strength wrap around their bodies silently.","The first one to notice things was the Kraken, as it had cast its [Sea Ray] ability and was releasing powerful destructive rays of light from its reddened eyes when it suddenly noticed its output increase instantly, the rays doubling in size as they shot forth with even more vigor, and it also discerned a golden aura now moving along with these destructive rays as they actually pierced the hide of the Fire Behemoth they were fighting and caused it to release a pained scream!","ROAAR!","The surroundings shook as the skill of the Kraken was the first one to hit the beast the moment after Noah obtained the [Golden Guider] skill and placed 5 Skill Points into it. The ability had turned especially deadly as it now carried Noah’s aura of fate, which provided the abstruse Soul Damage that very few could defend against!","The others very quickly noticed the changes as they felt their bodies to be lighter and faster, using their essence to check their bodies as they felt the appearance of a warm and powerful aura enveloping them.","\"Master!\"","\"Ahh, Progenitor!\"","The Emperor Penguin was the first to attribute the change to the only person responsible, with Elena hugging her body tightly as she felt the warm aura surround her and enhance her strength.","RAA! RAA! RAA!","The Emperor Penguin waved its flippers as it released numerous [Spatial Blades], this time they were covered with a tinge of a golden aura that went on to pierce through the defenses of the Fire Behemoth easier as it let out another pained roar from the soul damage that came with it!","This stupendous situation was occurring in multiple places, as those who were labeled as Noah’s subordinates were truly too numerous to even count!","In the Spiritual World, those remaining in the Time Space to max the proficiencies of their skill trees felt this powerful aura wrap around them. Those in the First Infernal Realm of Hell like the young dragon Draco felt their bodies gain a power that allowed them to take down the Infernals with even greater ease!","Going even further, in a random created Dungeon in Noah’s home world where a Rank B Hunter had recklessly dived into a dungeon by himself and was about to die, his body felt an abundance of strength as his low ranking iron blade gained a tinge of a red aura that went on to actually defend against the blow of the troll in front of him, his gaze looking at his sword in shock as he then moved at a speed he had never moved before and slashed towards the beast.","SHAA!","The weak iron blade cut through the defenses of the troll like nothing as the hunter that had overestimated his abilities and was about to lose his life looked around in shock, not understanding what was happening as a unique thought passed through his mind.","’Was I actually born with an unknown power and am meant for great things?!’","To go even further, a man that had just become a father was playing with his child who could barely form words yet in a small city in the United Federation of Noah’s home world.","\"Say papa, say papa my little boy!\"","The father was cradling the boy in his arms with his face full of joy, the child amused by the expressions as random sounds left its mouth.","\"aha, da..da!\"","The joy on the father’s face only increased as he repeated his words, and it was this time that the unique energy of the Golden Guider wrapped around the both of them.","\"Say papa...!\"","The words of the young father stopped midway as he felt the foreign energy, his joyful expression that was observing his child seeing it adopt a never before seen serious expression as a word actually came out of the child’s mouth!","\"Papa.\"","...!!!","Numerous situations like these continued to play out across an expansive array of places as the [Golden Guider] skill that granted boosts to the beings considered to be Noah’s subordinates were shockingly applied to every single being on the many planets he was connected to!"]},{"number":427,"title":"Chapter 427: Chapter 426 - Crixus Shows Off","paragraphs":["A unique phenomenon spread out across a few stars as the beings within unexpectedly came in contact with something the vast majority of them would have never had the chance to even glimpse nor understand.","A distinct aura of fate wrapped around them as they felt their bodies strengthened and reinforced, those that were actively dungeon diving or fighting seeing this strength increase first hand.","Because of this, shockingly something that was a norm on Prime Worlds was occurring throughout the planets that Noah was connected to. This phenomenon was the one where a vast majority of the beings on Prime Worlds would be considered ’Awakened’ individuals in the terms of the Planetary System, where a vast majority of beings on Prime World would have a tinge of essence running throughout their bodies that granted them a longer life span and the possibility of getting stronger in the future.","This was only possible because of the powerful atmospheric essence that was abundant in Prime Worlds, making most of the beings in it be considered Awakened. Such a phenomenon was actually occurring right now in the numerous Planets that Noah was connected to, where those that could be considered normal beings were slowly awakening because of the powerful energy of fate that wrapped around them!","In a small apartment located at the banks of the cities in the Blessed Empire, a young man was watching the TV with shining eyes as he saw the scene of Rank S Hunters valiantly fighting against each other in the Coliseum. A thought was running through his mind as he looked at this scene longingly.","’When would I be able to cast a skill or do anything remotely as powerful as them?’","It was the thoughts and gazes of longing that many felt when they watched their phones and TVs while observing powerful hunters obtain riches beyond their wildest dreams! This young man had the same, but he shook his head as he placed his focus back on the TV, when he suddenly felt a unique energy wrapping around his body, this energy going on to unlock something within him as it directly made him awaken, his shocked eyes finding themselves watching a materializing blue stat panel in front of his eyes there after!","Shocking scenes like these continued to occur wide and far as a spectacular phenomenon continued across the few connected worlds, bringing immense joy to unsuspecting beings as this was only the beginning of it all.","Noah himself had no knowledge of this yet, until a few seconds later he heard the words of the Planetary System ring in his mind.","[That Golden Guider ability is more ridiculous than you expected it to be.]","Noah, who had already begun moving forward to another task heard the occurrences around the planets he was connected to as he glanced at the description of this skill in shock. Those considered his ’subordinates’ were simply too many...right?","Realizing the extent that the effects of this Golden Guider traveled, a variety of thoughts passed through his mind as the Planetary System affirmed and voiced out his thoughts.","[If there are other Guider type abilities in the future Skill Trees, the effects are bound to be something unique.]","A shocking thought passed through the mind of one being and the Planetary Systems of a few worlds as countless possibilities lay for the future!","Noah shook his head at this ridiculous boost that almost every being on these stars had received and what it could mean for the future, his main body that was moving with the Righteous Fire Exploration Team and Grandmaster Vredral continuing to move as they had located yet another Chaos Behemoth.","He would observe the full effects of the Golden Guider ability later as he focused on what he was about to do currently in front of these Celestials. After the upgrade of the [Fate’s Guardian] skill tree that granted him the advancement of [Unruly Guider], he planned to ’show off’ some of his genius in the next hunt for the Chaos Behemoth!","Grandmaster Vredral was slowly pulling back in the fights more and more to have Noah and Athena work together with the Righteous Fire Exploration Team to stand against these Elite Behemoths, their bodies that continued to receive numerous Origin Cores of Behemoths and their materials making them near the peak of the Soul Rank in just a matter of days.","The hand of the Grandmaster moving in front of them came up as they received the signal to stop, his voice ringing out thereafter.","\"A fairly average Elite Chaos Behemoth lies in front of us. Crixus and Athena will lead the charge, with the rest of you backing them up. I will jump in if any life threatening situations occur!\"","The calm voice of the Grandmaster allowed them to nod with serious faces as the War Princess and the Destroyer took the lead, their bodies beginning to light up as they cast [Empyrean Guards] and [Empyrean Armament].","ROAR!","Their use of these skills caught the attention of the Chaos Behemoth as the earth below them began to tremble, the mountainous beast most likely reaching their positions in a matter of seconds!","4 Empyrean Guards appeared around Athena as they soon turned into streaks of light and gave her the usual golden armor and two golden hammers with shining light wings.","Around Noah, a similar scene repeated, but the summoned Empyrean Guards did not stop at 4, or the normal 6 that the Celestials had seen him use before!","With the addition of [Empyrean Ruler] from the Unruly Guider skill tree, he could summon an additional 12 Empyrean Guards! What exactly would come out of him absorbing this many Empyrean Guards?","Grandmaster Vredral watched carefully as his eyes began to shine an intense light, watching the appearance of exactly 12 Empyrean Guards around Crixus before they all turned into streaks of light and rushed to attach to his body.","A blinding light shot out as a brand new transformation came from doubling the amount of Empyrean Guards, Noah not even using the extra 6 that he could as he only portrayed 12 overall to the Celestials around him!","ROAR!","The Chaos Behemoth broke through the resplendent foliage of the Celestial Realm as the blinding light that was Noah moved to clash with it first, his spectacular adorned figure finally appearing in front of the eyes of the Grandmaster, Athena, and the members of the Righteous Fire Exploration Team as they stood with agape expressions, Noah himself clashing with the Chaos Behemoth head on!","BOOOOM!"]},{"number":428,"title":"Chapter 428: Chapter 427 - Shimmering with Splendor","paragraphs":["BOOM!","The impact sent shock waves of Chaos and Fate elements as Noah's figure was pushed back slightly, the Chaos Behemoth being stopped in place as in a particular portion on its body, a burning mark was left behind, the strong aura of fate burning into its touch skin as the beast stared at the party of Celestials. In front of Noah's eyes, a crystal clear name floated atop it.","[Chaotic Zygosaurus]","This Chaos Behemoth held qualities reminiscent of ancient carnivorous dinosaurs, standing powerfully on four legs as it had a huge extended jaw and dark scaled skin, towering over 60 meters!","Yet this huge beast's onslaught was brought to a halt from a Soul Forging Realm being as his new form made itself clear for all to see.","In his left hand, a huge pristine white tower shield protected his body entirely, his right hand holding a weapon that could closely be described as a flail! The flail hung on a clear white chain as it had golden spear protrusions that shimmered dangerously. His body was wrapped around tightly with a golden robe that pulsed with power, one barely being able to discern a passive golden barrier of light being given off by this robe!","To his back were spectacularly erupting white feathered wings, but what was more shocking were the three objects rotating in a circular motion behind him. Similar to the hammers that Athena was currently wielding, three resplendent golden hammers were rotating in a circular motion behind Noah's back as they pulsed with power! The scintillating of Fate Lines visibly showed on his body as the Celestials watching were able to count more than 40,000!","WAA!","An air of regality spread out as Noah breathed out, wielding the golden flail in his hands as his entire figure released waves of golden essence. The three golden hammers that rotated behind him also vibrated as they shot out, moving as if they were extra hands while they targeted the enemy.","\"Haha, a genius indeed!\"","Grandmaster Vredral howled by the side as the rest of the watching members were returned to attention, the War Princess Athena looking towards Noah with sharp eyes as the Junior Brother of hers had inadvertently had another breakthrough and even unlocked another way to uniquely use the techniques of Fate's Guardian!","Noah was not done as he pointed the golden flail forward, the [Chaotic Zygosaurus] gritting its teeth threateningly as he cast another skill, the clouds in the skies being split apart as five large Blades of Liberation descended down.","\"Haa!\"","Noah himself moved as he was joined by Athena and Boru, the other members sniping the beast from a far distance as a battle without the help of the Grandmaster against a Domain Expansion Realm Chaos Behemoth began!","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","The Blade of Liberation smashed towards the beast as it dodged and absorbed some of the attacks, the watching Grandmaster and the fighting members of the Righteous Fire Exploration Team being surprised yet again when the normal scene of these Blades of Liberation disappearing into particles of light did not happen, and instead, they strongly remained in the air and began moving on their own again, chasing the Chaos Behemoth down as it was cornered in all directions!","The Grandmaster looked at this with a quizzical tone as this scene even left him too curious to understand exactly how this genius did it.","The Blades of Liberation that now moved with autonomy under the effect of the new [Liberator] ability had increased damage and speed as they weaved across the field of battle and kept the Chaos Beast fully occupied, the other members of the Righteous Fire Exploration Team being given a breather of moving around and dodging the terrifying attacks that the beast released. Huge golden blades chased it down on all sides, powerful golden hammers that were palpating with the aura of fate rotated around him to protect him and also move on their own to dish out even more damage!","\"Watch out!\"","The warning came from Athena as her unique power told her a huge skill was coming, the ferocious Chaos Beast in front of released a dark wave of power as it cast its Domain of Chaos!","\"Hmph!\"","A golden wave released from the Grandmaster as he pushed back the Domain with his own Domain of Fate, the two canceling each other as the battle continued with the beast slowly gaining more injuries as 5 huge Blades of Liberation sneaked in attacks at all times, while Noah himself moved with his powerful flail to land attacks and then defend with the huge tower shield the beast swiped its claw forward.","When this was paired up with Athena's directions, the Righteous Fire Exploration Team was actually handling an Elite Behemoth by themselves under the watch of the Grandmaster, neither of them at the Domain Expansion Realm as they battled a beast that was!","ROAAR!","The battle would go on to continue for another half an hour as the defenses of the Chaos Beast were slowly ground down, this time around Noah and Athena stably leading the pace of the battle as even Boru was left behind in how much damage was dealt. The three hammers floating around Noah as well as the Blades of Liberation that seemed to have their own wills dealt even more damage over the course of the battle, the Chaos Behemoth not being able to handle the onslaught of attacks on all sides.","A wide smile was apparent on the face of the Grandmaster as his thoughts were affirmed!","This was why they used so many treasures to train those with Noble Fates! Their power simply could not be compared as they came with their own genius that could surprise the most powerful veterans!","He looked forward to when these two beings would soon break into the Domain Expansion Realm, their rapid rise in ranks that should have been causing them slight destabilization in their essence being solved very quickly as they continued to battle powerful Elite Behemoths to get their power under control.","Grandmaster Vredral planned to ask for even more materials for these wonderful disciples of his, which would shockingly soon be able to get a similar title as him at the rate they kept going. Athena was infinitely close as her Fate Lines were about to spill over 100,00, the barrier that anyone that passed would be granted the title of Grandmaster!","'Grandmaster Athena and Grandmaster Crixus...Haha, that doesn't sound so bad at all!'","The Grandmaster thought wildly as he could tell, with figures like these on the rise, the future of the Celestials was one that would be filled with splendor!"]},{"number":429,"title":"Chapter 429: Chapter 428 - Fame","paragraphs":["Among the networks of the Celestials moving in the Celestial Realm, two names had begun popping up and shining with vigor as the days passed.","The Normal and Elite Exploration Teams had been passing around the names of the two newly arriving Celestials with Noble Fates that were rising rapidly through the ranks, their names now being placed in the same places as renowned Celestials that were moving in Elite Teams!","\"They aren’t the only ones with Noble Fates though. There are others that shine even brighter like Grandmaster Xander and Grandmaster Lila.\"","Two normal teams were enjoying a feast of simmering behemoth meat as they talked within the special locations that were exclusive to Celestials in the Sanctum.","The beings they mentioned as Grandmasters were not some old fogeys that had been living for thousands of years, but young and upcoming Celestials that had passed the point of 100,000 Fate Lines and obtained the title of Grandmaster!","They were beings that were similar to Noah and Athena, holding the title of those with Noble Fates.","\"Well, I know we place a lot of importance on those with Noble Fates, but what about the Three-Eyed Fate Child and Grandmaster Light? They don’t hold such titles, but because they are unique existences in our galaxy, they hold tremendous power!\"","A burly celestial took a large bite of the glistening meat that shone with essence as he spoke out, the topic of conversation not disparaging any of the powerful beings they were talking about, where they were simply sharing their opinions on who else was out there.","This was the atmosphere of Celestials, who were under the doctrines of maintaining Order and Balance, and thus were happy as long as powerful figures were growing in ranks to be able to better reduce the ever so increasing Chaos!","The two other beings they mentioned as the Three-Eyed Fate Child and Grandmaster Light were not those holding powerful titles, but simply beings born in unique environments which gave them innate strength that was one of a kind in the Light Expanse.","The Three-Eyed Fate Child was the last of its species, a being that was found by a roving Grandmaster in an uninhabitable planet that was filled with destructive storms. This Three-Eyed Fate Child had been able to survive alone in this star for years before the Grandmaster found him, his unique Three Eyes giving him immense talent in the Supreme Law of Fate and the Supreme Law of Time-Space. This gave birth to a being that was proficient in two Supreme Laws!","The other was a Celestial known as Grandmaster Light, a being that was born on a planet made of light, this planet going on to shatter the moment that Grandmaster Light was born. She was an existence that held a unique composition, with much of her body being made up of particles of light! There were rumors that only her heart was the same as everyone else, possibly being her only weakness as well.","As she was a being of the Light Element, she had been able to cultivate the Supreme Law of Light and Supreme Law of Fate with ease as she moved through the ranks of Celestials over the years.","Now, each of these figures were moving on their own Elite Teams as they sought to increase their power and be the ones that brought down the most order and balance.","\"Our organization is extremely united, but I feel like there will be some rifts and competitiveness soon as the number of beings with powerful talents appear. We have large amounts of treasures, but is it enough to raise multiple beings with Noble Fates and even Special Existences to the peak levels of power before the next war begins?\"","A low voice erupted from the corner of the table, a fairly intelligent robed Celestial speaking out as he caused a silence to descend onto the area, those that heard his words being made to think.","The words of this wondering Celestial were actually fairly spot on though, as when the moment that Grandmaster Vredral applied for more materials and Cores for the powerful students under him that he knew to be showing immense promise, he was soon faced with an awkward situation where he was told to wait, as much of the other resources were already diverted to other beings holding titles of those with Noble Fates or Special Existences!","This caused the Grandmaster a bit of unhappiness as he knew that the disciples he had were extremely talented, knowing they would be able to bring them the most help when standing against the coming chaos in the future.","Grandmaster Vredral had thought about this issue as he went ahead and contacted his connections in the Sanctum and the 7th Celestial Star, letting his thoughts be known similarly to when he brought forth the idea of influencing the beings of the Light Expanse more by letting them into the Celestial Realm.","Because of his recent contributions, his words held a significant influence and value as even though he did not stand near those that would be considered at the top of power when observing the large scale of the Celestials, his influence was still wide as he helped oversee a significant portion of the Light Expanse with other Grandmasters in the 7th Celestial Star.","He had sacrificed his rise in power in the past as he chose to leave the Celestial Realm and take part in the overseeing mission of the Light Expanse, where the friends he knew and had in the past who had remained in the Celestial Realm were powerful Grandmasters that had already entered the World Rank, with some of them even having the task of looking after Special Existences or those with Noble Fates!","His influence over some of the regions in the Light Expanse allowed him to easily amass hundreds of thousands of Fate Lines even while he wasn’t actively hunting Chaos Behemoths as the other Grandmasters over the years.","Thus, his words were taken seriously as the names Crixus and Athena were brought forward to the upper echelons of power of the Celestials, these two beings being put on the list among the brilliantly shining Celestials that were being groomed with the most resources for the war to come.","But this brought the problem where the exceptional Celestials were too many, with the materials and treasures needing to be spent very carefully as they were only focused on to beings that had the ultimate potential to create powerhouses that could sway the direction of the war in the future.","So how would those that were truly deserving and with most potential be chosen among the geniuses in their organization as they neared the precipice of a war?","This question would bring forth a spectacular event in the near future, an event that would be a show for the ages!"]},{"number":430,"title":"Chapter 430: Chapter 429 - Shooting Past the 100,000 Barrier","paragraphs":["Grandmaster Vredral glanced at Crixus and Athena as he had a carefully pondering expression on his face, turning to the disciples who had just taken down another Chaos Behemoth and were steadily purifying the Domain Realm Origin Core before they began absorbing its powerful essence for themselves.","He knew that the forced increase in the realms of these beings was not necessarily the best, but their bodies seemed to be able to particularly handle this ordeal as they continued battling with the powerful Behemoths!","He expected these two students to soon enter the Domain Expansion Realm themselves, but this was where hardship would begin, as treasures to push the power of those at this realm were exceedingly rare, causing the situation that had occurred when he requested more resources and actually could not be provided with any.","A solution was under way, but his students would have to work hard to get through an ordeal before they could continue advancing at such a rapid pace again.","His heart was at peace as he thought about the other beings considered Special Existences and those with Noble Fates. He truly believed in his heart that Crixus and Athena had the most potential and stood above them all! Now, the only thing for them to do was to show this to the higher echelons...","---","As events continued to be propelled forward around his main body, Noah’s clone was the one being the most productive these past few days.","His main body continued to move with the Righteous Fire Exploration Team as they went deeper in the Northern Region of the Celestial Realm, coming face to face with powerful Domain Expansion Realm Chaos Behemoths.","Since they were at the Domain Rank, each time they faced a Behemoth, the Grandmaster had to be present to cancel the powerful Domain they could cast, otherwise Noah and the others would fall into a Domain of Chaos as the fate energy in their bodies became restricted, eventually falling into the deadly hands of the beasts.","Though at the rate they were going, Noah knew he and Athena would reach the Domain Expansion Realm soon enough and be able to provide their own Domains!","A majority of the materials and Cores from the defeated Behemoths continued to be distributed to him and Athena, their titles continuing to benefit them greatly, even though he knew a limit for the benefits of these titles was soon coming. As for what would happen after that? He would take it as it came.","While his main body continued to build up his Rank and get used to the spectacular new abilities of the next stage of [Fate’s Guardian], the path of the [Unruly Guider], his clone had been using the Dual Cultivation method the past two days to break past the barriers of one hundred thousand in both the Supreme Laws of Fate and Chaos!","Noah had noticed that ever since the initiation of the Golden Guider ability that influenced the beings in the world he was connected to even more closely, he had become able to gain more and more Fate Lines at a rapid rate.","The effects of [Golden Guider] did not just extend to increasing the power of the multitude of beings he was connected to, but it went even further to increase the rate he improved in the law of fate as his influence over these many beings increased by a huge factor!","This effect was slowly causing a trickle of Fate Lines to converge towards him constantly, with him believing that it would gradually even increase over time as the beings he affected increased their strength and propagated throughout the worlds in the future.","This boost of Fate Lines from multiple sources and the Dual Cultivation method allowed for him to break through the barrier of 100,000 milestone with ease.","100,000!","The benchmark that marked a Celestial as a Grandmaster, and the place which allowed him to see a 1% next to the Laws of Chaos and Fate on his stat panel.","His Chaos Particles were hanging slightly over 104,000, with his Fate Lines shooting further ahead as even though he divided his time equally in increasing both the laws, he was originally ahead with Fate Lines by almost thirty thousand and now gained a greater amount because of the effects of [Golden Guider], which put his total number currently at 130,000 Fate Lines.","Such a number could only be achieved by tens if not hundreds of years by heavily dedicated practicing Celestials, and he had gotten it done in a few days while also keeping himself busy with other tasks.","His forces had entered a period of rapid strengthening because of the boost of [Golden Guider], the addition of the aura of fate on their bodies granting them a level of damage that decimated their enemies.","Even Noah himself thought he was still underestimating the effects of the Guider skill as it seemed like the stage of strength of many beings across the Worlds he was connected to were being boosted to a whole other level.","In the Spiritual World, the beasts were moving with vigor as they enjoyed the resplendent farmlands across the continental landmasses, many of the Spiritual World Beasts leaving lives of luxury as they cultivated and enjoyed essence filled fruits and medicinal herbs.","The paradisiacal looking Spiritual World that had four floating continents on top of the enormous central one was an environment that even the richest kings would not be able to come across, the levels of atmospheric essence in this world being off the charts. This wasn’t to even mention one of the continents now being fully changed to a land of fire, coagulation of fire elements being abundant as it was fully turned into a Fire Law Space.","This allowed for the birth of new Spiritual World Beasts that were not of the Water Element, the advent of fiery beasts coming to be in the expansive Spiritual World!","There always seemed to be new and exciting things to observe in this Spiritual World as Noah unlocked more and more of its secrets.","There was also the recently unlocked plants which granted boosts to the Law of Fire and the Law of Water being already planted in the Time Space of the Spiritual World, Noah moving to use his Budding Farmer skill as he reduced the growth and maturing rate of the plants by a large margin, expecting them to be ready for consumption in a matter of weeks and not years!","On the side of the Blacksmith’s Forge, he had already collected more than enough Chaos Materials, being able to craft a full Set Item from the Chaos Element. He planned to craft a full one some time later, and for now, he was going to upgrade a skill tree he looked forward to seeing the next stage of for a while.","That’s right, the Lesser Cthulhu skill tree was ready for an advancement to the next stage!","The ability that made it possible for him to gain the qualification of an Infernal Lord in the beginning, the one that seemed to be surrounded by mysteries- it advancements were slowly opening themselves up in front of his eyes."]},{"number":431,"title":"Chapter 431: Chapter 430 - [Kin of Terror], Bold!","paragraphs":["Noah’s clone was currently in a random location in the void of space, his gaze looking over the stat panel that showed two possibilities of where he could take the Lesser Cthulhu skill tree.","<strong>[Amorphous Space Beast] (15/15) :: Abilities- Spatial Cage(5/5), Destabilize(5/5), Shattered Star(5/5), and Miniature Space(5/5). >> [Lesser Cthulhu] (45/45)Additional Abilities- Morph(5/5), Child of Space(5/5), Portals of Terror(5/5), and Sever(5/5). Two Skill Trees for evolution are possible once sufficient points and a base requirement of two equivalent level sacrificial skills are reached: >> [Void Colossus] :: A pathway geared towards enhancing the control of space, granting a form deserving of the name. >> [Kin of Terror] :: A fledgling of a powerful existence with unique traits. Its true value lies in its future possibilities. </strong>","Two possibilities lied in front of his eyes as he read over them carefully, understanding that his choices would determine whether he reached a stage of something he had gained an insignificant amount of knowledge about so far.","The pathway of [Void Colossus] seemed to provide more battle power, especially the mention of having a form deserving of the name. The [Kin of Terror] pathway was worded similarly to the upgrade of the Blood Lord that led to the Kin of Ancients, making Noah lean more towards this choice, along with the glaring shining words that read ’Terror’!","He chose the [Kin of Terror] pathway right away as the words in the stat panel shone, an additional set of abilities being added. He briefly glanced over them with shining eyes before he placed all the Skill Points into the abilities, wanting to see their most powerful versions right away.","SOUL [Amorphous Space Beast] (15/15) :: Abilities- Spatial Cage(5/5), Destabilize(5/5), Shattered Star(5/5), and Miniature Space(5/5). >> [Lesser Cthulhu] (45/45) :: Additional Abilities- Morph(5/5), Child of Space(5/5), Portals of Terror(5/5), and Sever(5/5). <strong>[Kin of Terror] (60/60) :: Additional Abilities- Aether Reinforcement (5/5), Multiplicative Ray Support (5/5), Triple on Cast Support (5/5), Lunacy Inducement (5/5)</strong>","<strong>[Aether Reinforcement] (5/5) :: All of the abilities preceding and following the Kin of Terror Skill Tree will be reinforced by the power of Aether passively. +300% Aether Damage, +100% Aether Penetration, +60% Fate and Chaos Damage Reduction.</strong>","<strong>[Multiplicative Ray Support] (5/5) :: Laser-based abilities similar to [Sever] will be further enhanced, the released rays of Aether increasing to 6 as their power is tripled.</strong>","<strong>[Triple on Cast Support] (5/5) :: The [Portals of Terror] ability is further enhanced, where there is an 80% chance to triple the appearance of portals of terror on cast, bringing the possible maximum cast portals to 54. </strong>","<strong>[Lunacy Inducement] (5/5) :: Those with weak minds cannot stand against the Kin of Terror. Lunacy Inducement allows for the user to bring their enemies into a negative mental state as they are slowly left defenseless. The effectiveness of this ability depends on the Soul Strength of the target as well as the user. </strong>","The additional abilities under the Lesser Cthulhu skill tree were proudly showing themselves in front of Noah as he read them over a few times. There were a few differences compared to previous additional skills as two of the new ones were called support skills that simply enhanced the previous skills to an insane degree.","[Multiplicative Ray Support] and [Triple of Cast] support effectively made the Sever and Portals of Terror abilities nonsensical at this moment, even Noah himself not being able to understand the extent until he tested them out himself. Even without having tested them though, their usability already seemed ridiculous! He wiped non-existent sweat off his forehead as he thought about any pitiful enemies that would have to face such terrifyingly enhanced abilities.","[Aether Reinforcement] was straightforward, and the only one that would need more time and a closer look in was the [Lunacy Inducement] ability which seemed to have its own terrific uses.","He wanted to test these abilities right away, and would very likely have the chance to in the next task that he had the clone lined up to do!","The Ancient Blood Clone that was still floating peacefully in the void of space got ready as his body rippled with power. For his next task, it was considered something bold as while his main body continued to move through the ranks of Celestials and got stronger in the Celestial Realm, the clone’s task was to increase the number of connected worlds amidst the training of skills and amassing of Chaos Particles and Fate Lines!","It was a very busy and non-stop past few days for his clone, but not even an ounce of tiredness could be felt as he always looked forward to the next steps.","For the first world in mind, and this was also the reason why he called the next set of events bold- it was to form a connection with the Magus World that he had personally taken the lives of its strongest forces, this world now currently having celestial disciples moving within as from the words of Grandmaster Vredral, it was being used as a place for them to hone their skills in fate while influencing the lives of the beings in it.","This meant that in the Magus World, there was a high chance of there being a Grandmaster that was overseeing the operations for the world that had the massacre of its strongest forces broadcasted, and his plans of forming a connection with the world would undoubtedly cause him to come in contact with whatever force the Celestials had stationed there!","Thus, he would have to move covertly in order to establish the connection, clear out any Celestials he found there, and then do something even crazier as his teleportation currently was leading him towards his homeworld where he would be picking up something the Celestials called a Cursed Treasure, something that they used as the reason to destroy an entire world.","He considered this next venture bold as he would ultimately be pulling off a disappearing act for an entire Prime World by the end of it..."]},{"number":432,"title":"Chapter 432: Chapter 431 - World Engine","paragraphs":["Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone appeared serenely back in his homeworld, above the wide blue seas as he took a deep breath and glanced towards his surroundings. He took in the calmness as his body began descending down into the sea, moving at such a speed that in only a matter of seconds, he could already see the shining lights of an underwater continent that was the New Atlantis.","He observed the unique futuristic mixture of magic and technology that the Atlantians and Merfolk showed, the appeal of such structures returning to him as he made a mental note to have an entire area in the Spiritual World built similarly.","His presence was already sensed the moment he neared the underwater continent, the being that he had sent a telepathic message some time ago already floating in the lit-up sea with a party of Atlantians and Merfolk to welcome him.","\"O Great Benefactor, we have everything ready.\"","The one at the forefront, the being that continued acting as the Ocean Master these past few months, bowed towards Noah while pointing to a huge square compartment that shone with blue and gold runic lines.","Before he teleported here, Noah had sent a telepathic message to the Ocean Master to have one of the World Engines that had finished being created ready for him to take away for his own use, and the Ocean Master had delivered as Noah could sense the pristine fluctuations of something powerful in the square compartment!","He nodded towards the Ocean Master while speaking.","\"May I?\"","\"Why of course. This is one of our most recent ones that runs even smoother, a few changes made to the rune overlays that allows the flow of mana to be evenly distributed and even faster, achieving the result of spatial warping in a much shorter time frame.\"","The Ocean Master spoke with a confident expression as Noah went forward, waving his hands and opening the square compartment as a circular treasure that seemed to constantly have runic lines moving over it shone resplendently.","{World Engine} :: A unique treasure that was created by the combination of technology and magic by the Atlantians. It allows for the spatial warping of an entire world, and requires the permission and cooperation of the will of the world itself before it can be operated. The user must be standing with the World Engine in the innermost core of the targeted world before it can be activated.","A description that foretold exactly what to do with the world engine floated in front of his face as he nodded, waving his hands as the entire square compartment containing the Wold Engine entered his [Expansive Space].","\"Amazing work as always. I can’t wait to see what other innovations you come up with.\"","He gave a light smile to the Atlantians that could sense the overwhelmingness of his power, the Ocean Master bowing again as he spoke out.","\"Whatever we can do to help. Please let us know if we can be of use at any time.\"","Noah nodded towards the Ocean Master as he gave another glance to the continuously expanding futuristic underwater world around him, his figure disappearing thereafter as he made his way to the Magus World!","The moment he left, huge sighs and breaths of relief as bubbles from the Atlanteans and Merfolk as it felt like they could finally breathe after an instance of meeting that powerful figure. One of the Merfolk turned towards the Ocean Master as he asked with an ashen expression.","\"Sire, are you sure that is the same Benefactor?!\"","The Ocean Master had a relaxed face as he glanced at his subordinates and nodded, even he not being able to completely withstand the overwhelming aura the being that had just disappeared released!","It wasn’t that his rank and power were overflowing freely for all to see, they actually could not even guess what realm their Benefactor was at as his body did not release any essence fluctuations. What filled them with the overwhelming sensation was his eyes! Whenever he glanced at them, they felt like his eyes could see through everything they had, having a level of power capable of decimating them in an instant.","The relaxed expression on the face of the Ocean Master only increased as he affirmed that they had allied themselves with a powerful being, his forces never having to fear for their lives again!","\"Let’s go. I want to see if we can finish the Plasma Warship in the next few weeks. As soon as we are able to get the inscriptions correctly, we can produce many working ones quickly!\"","The innovators of Atlantis returned to their underwater kingdom as they went about their work, their Benefactor appeared on the surface of the Magus world silently, his body not releasing even an ounce of energy.","---","The Magus World was a huge Prime World that held billions of powerful Magi, their power being something that many forces feared in the past. But this power would forever remain in the past as their strongest organization had gotten decimated some time ago!","Currently, the Inhabitants of the Magus World felt a sense of loss as even though their lives were gradually returning to normal, they felt a stifling sensation in their hearts as they never became able to reclaim the sense of identity as beings of a powerful Prime World.","This was especially so when the Celestials, those responsible for carrying out the decimation of their strongest forces in the first place, were freely descending on their world as they seemed to be helping the many scattered forces and organizations come together and bring back an ordered Prime World.","A few days ago, a Celestial Warship that was a level lower than a Prime Warship had docked on the central lands of the Magus, a Grandmaster that brought along a few Celestial Disciples just beginning in the study of the Law of Fate coming along as he also monitored the evolving situation of the Magus World.","This Grandmaster was a fairly powerful Celestial at the Domain Expansion Realm, his power ranking around the middle when looking at the larger forces that held the Title of Grandmaster among the Celestials.","He was meditating serenely in the Celestial Warship as golden essence surrounded him, <<Herald of Fate>> being used slowly as he tried to decipher his own fate and of those around him. At this moment, his eyes shot wide open as out of nowhere, he found that his fate had turned dark and murky, something he never expected!","A quizzical expression passed through his face as he calmed down and tried discerning fate again, thinking it was some sort of mistake.","Unbeknownst to him, an Agent of Chaos had silently begun drilling towards the core of the Magus World, the next few hours being something that all the beings in this Magus World would never be able to forget!"]},{"number":433,"title":"Chapter 433: Chapter 432 - The Magus World","paragraphs":["Noah's clone was covered with the aura of [Unique Origin] as well as the concealment techniques of <<Herald of Fate>> and <<Herald of Chaos>>. He was covertly moving and hidden so well that nobody could find out anything about him, whether they were looking for it or not.","His body seamlessly pierced through the layers of earth in the Magus World as he went deeper and deeper, his abilities being so adept that he seemed to be flitting through the grains of sand. A few minutes passed as he streaked through the earth, soon breaking past numerous layers as he entered the innermost layer of the Magus World and came face to face with the core of the powerful Prime World.","[...]","The World Core was unexpectedly taken aback and did not even speak, Noah being the one to take the initiative as he glanced at the circular rotating mass of mystical essence that stood as the center of a Prime World.","\"I apologize for intruding, but I came to reclaim something that I made possible to still be living today.\"","He spoke out curtly as he neared the World Core, the immense mystical power that was bound by universal laws which it released not affecting him one bit as he heard the reply of the World Core.","[What exactly are you talking about? Do you even know what you are currently standing in front of-]","\"Yes yes, it will be easier if I simply share something with you. Can I get some help?\"","Noah spoke nonchalantly to the core of the Magus World as his last sentence was directed to his Planetary System. From Noah, a manifestation of lights that were actually memories were released, nearing the mass of rotating core as a surprised voice came out.","[Such a thing should not be possible for an entity like you, what is-]","[...!!!]","The information that was uniquely passed from the Planetary System and onto the core of the Magus World as a shocking level of silence followed, an entire 5 minutes passing as Noah stood calmly in front of the core that did let out any more words!","This was because the information that was just passed to it was about the plans of the Celestials to fully destroy the Magus World, and the intervention of Noah that allowed for this world to continue living, even though it had to lose its most powerful forces!","[It is you that massacred the beings I raised for so long.]","\"Yes.\"","[It is you that saved everything else, even me.]","\"Yes.\"","[...What do you want to do?\"","A sly smile appeared on Noah's face at these words, giving a speech he had given to many worlds before as this one did not hold any sort of threats.","[A connection?]","After a while, the core of the Magus World ascertained while thinking carefully, voicing out something that would be the biggest worry for the undertaking that Noah was about to carry out.","[If everything you say is correct, you would be putting yourself and this entire world into even more danger, as Celestials can simply come and do what they wish even if this connection is successfully established. There are also a few on them on this world at this very moment.]","\"Let me worry about that, I have your agreement?\"","[...Yes.]","With the agreement of the World Core of the Magus World, Noah's eyes shone as he stretched his neck and prepared to begin!","The first thing he did was use the abilities of <<Herald of Fate>> and <<Herald of Chaos>> to discern his own fate and the fates of the many beings in the Magus World. A large inflow of information rushed to his brain as with the use of both absolute skills that involved the Supreme Laws of Fate and Chaos, he felt like he was seeing even more, the simile of seeing both sides of the same coin appearing in his mind as he sensed the bright fate and chaos auras located in the Magus World as many plans flowed in his mind.","He also pulled out the Dagger of Time as it rotated rapidly in front of him, using the ability of [Insight] as he foresaw many possibilities of the next few minutes, nodding his head as he breathed out slowly, getting himself in the right mindset as he was about to pull off a bold heist!","\"Let's do this silently, why don't we?\"","He sent his thoughts to the Planetary System and the core of the Magus World as a bright light that signified a connection shot from him and into the core of the world, a fantastical process beginning as from Noah himself, a beautiful circle of blood began to spread out with him at the center.","Both [Blood World], [World Veil], and [Unique Origin] were cast simultaneously as powerful covert techniques went on to begin wrapping around the entire Magus World with extreme speed and precision!","The beings on the world felt only a slight tremble at first, and the more powerful ones felt an overpowering essence pass through them as the cast Blood World and World Veil very quickly covered the entire planet.","The Grandmaster that was meditating with a troubled expression shot up rapidly as he looked to the skies, noticing a color red overtake it as his warning bells rang, finding that much of his connection to the outside world and his fate abilities were being hindered!","He took out a medallion as he prepared to recall the Celestial Disciples currently moving in the Magus World, realizing that what he discerned before might not have been a mistake as something troubling was occurring.","\"Get back to this Warshi-\"","SHAA! BOOM!","Silently and explosively, right behind the Celestial Grandmaster, the expressionless figure of Noah's Ancient Blood Clone appeared as the Domain Expansion Realm was hit with a sneak attack!","[Void of Impending Doom].","[Armageddon].","RUMBLE!","Overpowering darkness, terribly blazing flames, meteors, and chaos erupted out and closed in on the Celestial Grandmaster as the ability Void of Impending Doom from the [Agent of Chaos] and Armageddon from <<Herald of Flames>> were cast for the first time.","...!"]},{"number":434,"title":"Chapter 434: Chapter 433 - Assassinating a Grandmaster!","paragraphs":["Grandmaster Luo had been meditating in the Celestial Warship with a troubled expression when he first felt the waves of chaotic power pass through his body.","He did not even have a chance to react as a second later after he realized the passing energy was a technique that cut off communications from the outside world, an enemy appeared to attack him out of the blue!","RUMBLE!","The skies cried and the earth rumbled the moment this being rushed towards him, teleporting extremely closely as the whispers of two skills, [Void of Impending Doom] and [Armageddon], were heard.","It was an immensely dangerous situation for the Grandmaster as he felt the weight of the entire world falling towards him, numerous chaos essence converging all around him as he saw the formation of dangerous chaos spears from all directions. This wasn’t all as below him, the ground was bubbling and melting as fiery eruptions occurred, his senses indicating to him that above them, there were also numerous terrifying meteors raining down that were already ripping the Warship apart!","\"FIEND!\"","The face of the Celestial Grandmaster was filled with immense anger and slight fear as the golden aura of fate erupted from his body, choosing to release the power of his Domain right away in order to escape this dangerous predicament.","BOOM! CRACK!","The impact hit, the collision and repulsion of fate and chaos spreading out, debris from the shattered warship smashing to the ground as the fiery earth continued to bubble forth and meteors smashed down, it was exactly a scene of what the skill described as for miles around, it was the scene of Armageddon!","The Celestial Grandmaster himself had blood leaking from his right shoulder as the Void of Impending Doom ability had not been completely evaded, even his spread out Domain of Fate could not completely prevent the destructive chaos elements.","Grandmaster Luo looked at the enemy that was now under the oppression of his domain as his eyes shone with splendor, feeling the chaos elements tearing apart his shoulder as he winced and spat out wrathfully.","\"You dare to sneak attack a Grandmaster of the Celestials?!\"","His words rumbled with power as he increased the output of energy towards his domain, numerous Fate Lines appearing on his body as they thrummed with power. On his body, one could count the swirling Fate Lines to tower over 200,000!","He glanced at the attacking enemy who was being pushed down by his Domain of Fate, his surroundings lighting up with numerous Empyrean Guards that soon became streaks of light and rushed towards him speedily, transforming into a golden armor, hammers, and wings!","The enemy looked towards the Grandmaster’s bleeding shoulders with an expressionless face as he uttered simple words.","[Chaotic Mandate].","RUMBLE!","A field of chaos particles first became apparent as it began spreading out wildly, trying its best to fight against the overpowering Domain of Fate as a glistening armor of darkness enveloped the expressionless being.","The armor shockingly shimmered in darkness as in his hands, two long serrated blades that released chaotic energies stood dangerously! On his back, wings of devouring darkness erupted out in grandeur as a tug of war between two supreme laws went underway!","In the air, the opposing battle between the Domain of Fate and the released Chaos Field continued, the much greater strength of the being releasing the Domain exceeding in pressure, but the newly armored enemy whose body palpated with dangerous chaos particles was holding off the pressure as he stood strongly.","Noah glanced at the Grandmaster that had evaded his attack with a heavy injury, the 200,000 Fate Lines thrumming with power making him feel slightly suffocated, but that was all!","This was because he himself had more than 100,000 Fate Lines, and also had Chaos Particles that passed that amount as well.","His figure held on tightly to the dark serrated blades as he streaked forward like a streak of light, the blades going for the head of the Grandmaster!","\"Vile creature that has fallen in the hands of chaos! PERISH!\"","An enormous Blade of Liberation pierced through the skies of the now apocalyptic landscape, numerous spears of Judgment also descending towards Noah as he weaved in and out them expertly.","It seemed like it wasn’t chaotic enough as his eyes rapidly followed the trajectory of the golden spears and the Grandmaster that was gradually healing with a golden aura, his thoughts moving to cast even more terrific skills as he tested what it would take to bring down a Grandmaster.","[Portals of Terror]. [Portals of Terror]...","RUMBLE!","A terrible skill was cast multiple times, this skill being made even more terrifying by the [Triple on Cast Support] that caused the blooming portals releasing immense destruction to come in numbers of three, quickly increasing in number in the surroundings as more than 50 Portals of Terror soon occupied the Grandmaster that was at the very center!","\"...\"","His gaze was ashen as he stared at the overwhelming number of pulsing Portals of Terror that he felt a foreboding feeling from, his heart tightening as he felt like he was standing in the direct center of an explosion.","BOOOOOM! RIIP!","The portals released their numerous varying disordered and destructive elements as the being shining grandly in gold on the middle was quickly overshadowed in a colorful yet deadly array of colors.","OOOOM","The space cracked and reformed as things gradually calmed, Noah walking forward while adorned in the powerful [Chaotic Mandate] that let each part of his body act as a weapon that released Chaos Essence.","He walked towards the center of where the numerous portals had congregated as he observed space to reform, revealing the disfigured Celestial Grandmaster within as his Empyrean Armament was tattered and broken, half of his right hand missing as he looked toward Noah with a terrified gaze.","\"You..!\"","ZING!","Noah wasted no time as he cast [Sever], the skill now supported by [Multiplicative Ray Support] releasing numerous rays of Aether that went on to pass through the body of the Grandmaster and cut it up into pieces.","Noah Ancient Blood Clone remained impassive as he neared the mass of flesh that remained, his gaze watching shattered Fate Lines that were rising from the body of this powerful being and coming towards him because of the effect of a particular skill.","<strong>[Fate Stealer] (5/5) :: A support ability that is only activated when an enemy that is proficient in the workings of fate stands against the Unruly Guider and faces their death. 12% of the Fate Essence that they have collected over the years will be absorbed by the Guider.</strong>","He watched with cold eyes as more than 25,000 Fate Lines raised from the body of the dead Celestial Grandmaster, the death of this being only bringing one thought in his mind as he prepared to hunt any other Celestials on the Magus World before he did something even more spectacular.","He used [Devouring] on the body of the dead Grandmaster just by habit, swirls of information crossing through his mind as he moved forward, but he had to come to a stop as while the life of the Grandmaster Luo was playing out in his mind, he actually came across information that pertained to someone he never expected, the War Princess- Athena!","He stopped briefly as he glanced over this information, his eyes shining as he unexpectedly got his hands on something good. He put this information in the back of his mind for now though, the task in front of him being crucial and time sensitive, so he continued forward, not even paying heed to the fact that he had just taken down a Grandmaster at the Domain Expansion Realm, a being that had over 200,000 Fate Lines!","Dead, and in under a minute!","The terror and immensity of the constantly enhanced abilities in the numerous Skill Trees he held were only now beginning to show their capability, their possibilities for the future being something that even Noah did not yet fathom..."]},{"number":435,"title":"Chapter 435: Chapter 434 - A Prime World Disappears","paragraphs":["The instant the Grandmaster on the Magus World perished, any other Celestials on the Prime World faced similar fates as Noah wordlessly located their positions and took them down.","He was keeping emotions out of it as he moved with a single goal that was extremely time sensitive!","The few powerful beings of the Magus World at the Soul Rank that still remained alive already felt the shocking waves of power spreading out where the Celestial Grandmaster was located, their figures only appearing thereafter as they saw the scene of destruction.","Noah had already teleported back to the inner layer where the core of the Magus World resided, his sight faced with the newly established connection as the Will of the Magus World underwent a similar process to the past worlds. From shock at their boldness to violating universal laws to acceptance as they were now all on the same boat, this process went by quickly as Noah pulled out the compartment containing the World Engine.","\"Ready?\"","He sent his thoughts towards the world core as the mystifying World Engine began floating in front of Noah, taking a position in the middle of him and the core of the Magus World.","[Let’s do it.]","An affirmation came from the core of the Magus World as pure world essence began to leak from it and into the World Engine, Noah simply watching as he did not really need to provide any energy, this planet now connected to the reserves of many and having more than enough! Still, his mana flowed towards the World Engine as the treasure still needed the location of where it was warping this Prime World if they did not want a random movement of the star.","RUMBLE!","His eyes closed as he thought back to the void of space not too far from his home world, the World Engine that was receiving enormous amounts of essence having blue runic lines seamlessly moving across it as it expanded and released a unique energy that began spreading throughout the inner layer of the Magus World and further out!","It was a new type of energy that Noah was not entirely familiar with, only noticing the spatial essence within it as this energy went on to wrap around the entirety of the Magus World, a few quakes spreading out as the inhabitants felt an enormous change occurring.","If a being that could pierce through a [World Veil] and a [Blood World] were to be standing in the void of space watching the Magus World at this very moment, they would notice an eerie spatial energy wrapping around the entire world as it began to look as if it was folding in itself, and then instant later it fully disappeared from the location it was at!","Seamlessly!","Silently!","Powerfully!","An entire Prime World had disappeared out of nowhere, powerful beings only finding out about this shocking information some time later...","On the 7th Celestial Star, the being that oversaw a majority of the operations on this star, Grandmaster Ramiel, shot up from his meditative position as his eyes shone dangerously.","An overabundance of Fate Lines erupted on his body as his eyes shone gold, his usage of <<Herald of Fate>> that was exceedingly done in an expert fashion confirming the shocking revelations in his mind as his face turned sour. He opened his mouth as he released a powerful voice that rolled throughout the 7th Celestial Star.","\"A Grandmaster has been murdered in the Magus World! Leave all tasks behind and get there as soon as possible. Be prepared for battle!\"","WAA!","A shocking command reverberated in the ears of every Celestial Grandmaster of the 7th Celestial Star as many golden figures of Grandmasters moved without a second of delay, their bodies either teleporting onto huge Warsh.i.p.s that were powered up instantly and began shooting from the shimmering star, or others jumped onto established portals that connected to worlds near the Magus World that the Celestials held sway over.","From the 7th Celestial Star, numerous golden lights shot out as Prime Warsh.i.p.s of varying sizes erupted out with maximum speed, Grandmaster Ramiel being the first one to move the moment he finished his rallying call as he was shockingly moving through the void of space alone and without the use of a Warship, but his speed was multiple times faster as he shot through at speeds that seemed to be surpassing light! In the void of space, ruptures continued to spread out as he shot forward.","This monstrous Grandmaster was shooting through the void of space so speedily that in only 10 minutes, he had traversed from the far away 7th Celestial Star and at the exact location where the Magus World was...or where it used to be!","His face was colored black as he swept his energy all around, turning even darker when he found that where the Magus World used to be, fluctuations of spatial energies were freely flowing, but the world itself was missing. It was missing along with Grandmaster Luo who was stationed here a few days ago with a few disciples.","His gaze became sourer and sourer as golden waves of fate began spreading around the area, his essence utilizing <<Herald of Fate>> even more a monstrous number of fate lines rolled around his aged body. They seemed insurmountable as one could barely make out that their number most definitely passed a million, if not higher!","He utilized the Absolute Skill to try and decipher exactly what had happened here and who was involved, but he shockingly found out that he could not get even a semblance of knowledge on the being involved, nor could he locate anything about their fate.","All that met his peering gaze was a void of darkness, where he also saw spurts of shining light!","His gaze continued to get more and more chilling as the time passed, soon enough sensing the arrival of numerous Prime Warsh.i.p.s and other Celestial Grandmasters as they all surrounded where the Magus World used to be, their eyes almost popping out of their eye sockets as the location where one of them had fallen...was actually missing.","They glanced towards the leading Grandmaster Ramiel as they did not know how to move, because simply, something like this had never happened before!","In the past 1000 years after the War of the Righteous, not a single Grandmaster had fallen to enemy forces, much less assassinated.","So who exactly was bold enough to kill a Grandmaster, and how powerful were they that this entire group of Celestials could not find out anything about them?!"]},{"number":436,"title":"Chapter 436: Chapter 435 - A Declaration!","paragraphs":["Grandmaster Ramiel floated in the void of space as he stared at the empty plot where the Magus World used to be, numerous thoughts floating in his mind as a few stood at the forefront.","As he looked at the situation in front of him, multiple things came to his mind, but the biggest one was a similar occurrence of such an event when it pertained to a Large World that was already destroyed in the past, and by their commands as well!","A Large World that had the capabilities to warp across space, holding a Cursed Item that defied the universal laws and increased Chaos! They had sent the order down for this world to be destroyed long ago, so this occurrence should not be connected to it, but the cursed treasures of that world might have just fallen into some else’s hands.","He continued to think as his expression was that of wrath, but it wasn’t for the reason that many were thinking of. The death of a Grandmaster was a big loss, yes. But the even bigger loss was the slap in the face as an enemy actually targeted the Celestials.","The eyes of Grandmaster Ramiel twinkled as he combined the many thoughts in his mind, thinking of ways to bring about the best results from this event. He looked towards the surrounding Celestials as he thought about the the recent state of affairs, a dangerous gleam appearing in his eyes that nobody could foresee as he spoke out with a rambling voice.","\"This...is an affront to the honor of Celestials, as cowards actually think they can target and take the lives of our people!\"","His gaze was cold as he stared at the Grandmasters on Prime Warsh.i.p.s and others that were floating angrily in the void of space.","\"Those who did this are enemies of Celestials, and in this wide Novus Galaxy of ours, we only have a single enemy!\"","Shock coursed through the minds of the listening Grandmasters as they soon caught wind of where the words of this leading Grandmaster on the 7th Celestial Star was saying.","\"Our enemies are the cowards hiding in the Dark Expanse, and those slumbering in the Letalis Expanse!\"","RUMBLE!","Fate Lines that crossed the 1 million point thrummed strongly on the body of the Grandmaster as his body adopted a holy aura. Outwardly, he had a wrathful holy expression while inwardly, he was smiling at having found the perfect way to bring about immense results in the form of increasing their power and influence, as well as be the one to earn the most influence and increase in Fate Lines at the end of it all.","\"Today, from their cowardly actions here, they have effectively declared war!\"","OOOM!","Essence of fate rumbled out a singular event that would propel a sequence of events towards a terrible future began, the surrounding Grandmasters watching the play that Ramiel was acting out as their eyes twinkled, getting on board of the train instantly.","\"A declaration of war!\"","\"We must avenge Grandmaster Luo!\"","\"We must bring Order to all of this chaos!\"","\"War!\"","\"War!!!\"","RUMBLE!","A wide smile appeared over Grandmaster Ramiel’s face as he watched this scene. He cared not whether the killer of this Grandmaster was a being that had obtained the Cursed Weapon from a world they destroyed long ago. He cared not whether the little mice in the Dark Expanse were involved or not. All he wanted was to use this event to increase his influence and the influence of Celestials the most, sparking the conflict they all knew was coming, but had not found the right spark for it just yet!","The assassination of a Grandmaster...was all he needed to use as an excuse to paint the beings of Dark Expanse as their enemies once more, and begin the gradual process of a war that would influence the lives of trillions.","The skies shimmered gold as Fate Lines had already begun descending onto Grandmaster Ramiel even before he moved to further propagate his own campaign. His face shone with the splendor of a holy aura as he spoke out towards the watching Celestials.","\"For the Order and Balance of our Novus Galaxy, let the war against these savages begin!\"","OOOOOOH!!!","Resounding roars of affirmation met him as in the location where a Prime World used to be, one of the initiators of a terrible war began.","In another location, a Prime World had seamlessly warped across vast distances and appeared near a blue panel, a splendor of essence still apparent around the world.","Noah, who was standing within the world, felt the descent of numerous Fate Lines and Chaos particles, his eyes shining as it seemed his actions had brought about something even bigger than he thought.","He held no worries though, as he planned to do what he did today multiple times over the span of the next few days.","He planned to expand the connected worlds from the low number that was still under 10 and multiply that as much as possible as he trained in two Supreme Laws, while his main body moved in the Celestial Realm to obtain even more treasures.","[When do we begin the process of Realm Creation?]","A question that would have scared any knowledgeable being was heard in Noah’s mind, the Planetary System bringing the topic of something that it was very much looking towards to as Noah had a thoughtful look.","\"As soon as we have the proper requirements to create something at least on par with the Infernal Realms. For now, we can steadily build up to it!\"","Noah replied calmly as he himself was looking forward to this event, the information he gained from the Infernal Lord title letting him know exactly what he had to do in order to uniquely achieve the goal of making a Realm, something that rarely occurred, and especially rare for there to be a singular being that caused it!","But for now, he enjoyed the achievement of connecting to the Magus World, his gaze on the inhabitants in this wide world that would soon join his forces as he prepared to send some beings down to properly manage this world.","The one at the forefront that had been moving tirelessly the past weeks was the Guardian of Blood that continued to oversee the Ancient Blood World and monitor the progress of the Vampyres that Noah made, but this Guardian was versatile in its abilities and should have no problem looking over a few other worlds!","The clone’s figure disappeared as he went off to repeat what he did just now to a few more worlds, staying true to his goals of simply attaching more worlds to retain his supremacy over mana!"]},{"number":437,"title":"Chapter 437: Chapter 436 - Rapid Breakthrough","paragraphs":["As his clone moved to increase the connected worlds, Noah’s main body was currently in an expansive training room of the Celestial Watch Tower that stood between the border that left behind Fire Behemoths and had the Chaos Behemoths that were located further out.","The aura of fate was abundant in the room they were in as Grandmaster Vredral stood in front of them, his hands releasing warm essence of fate as he calmed the unstable aura around Noah and Athena.","That’s right! The power leveling that the Grandmaster was putting Noah and Athena through was finally coming to fruition, as these two beings that continued to be given materials and cores from Chaos Behemoths were finally forcefully breaking through to the Domain Expansion Realm!","The resources and treasures that would have gone to multiple Elite Exploration Teams and Celestial Grandmasters were given to the two beings with Noble Fates, their strengths being raised at a rate rarely seen as they broke through ranks that would normally take even geniuses years to break through.","Grandmaster Vredral would not have proceeded to continue pushing their realms up forcefully if their bodies showed any instabilities from not being able to handle the rapid rise, but Noah showed no issues while Athena only showed slight instabilities! After putting through numerous battles against Chaos Behemoths, their rapid rise only became solidified as they were now breaking through into the next rank with ease.","In their hands, the last Domain Expansion Realm Cores faded away into dust as both of their bodies rumbled with power, the unique strength of a Domain that was only present in this realm beginning to wrap around their cores as touched upon a level that would have taken them a significant amount of time to achieve with normal means.","\"Good, keep it steady and manifest the domain around your origins, this will allow you to stably step into the Domain Expansion Realm!\"","The Grandmaster said gravely as his power continued to descend onto their bodies and aid them, another few minutes passing before a change began to occur on Athena first, a golden glow surrounding her as she turned into a being clad in golden light!","An ecstatic expression appeared on the Grandmaster, the smile becoming even wider when the exact same situation happened to his other student, the two successfully establishing domains in their origin as the powerful aura at the Domain Expansion Realm began to leak out from them.","\"Haha!\"","A prideful look was on Grandmaster Vredral as he stared at his terrific students, Noah returning an excited smile as he laughed in his mind, these Celestials not knowing exactly who they just helped advance the realm of!","He and Athena had been given so many Domain Cores that he could have reached the reached a few days back because of the smoothness that the Planetary System allowed him to absorb cores, but he waiting until the Senior Sister that had always been ahead of him to break through before he did it himself.","At this moment, he had to give heartfelt thanks to the Celestials that had granted him such a large amount of treasures and brought up his rank rapidly. For the first time in a while, his rank had advanced first before he upgraded his skills.","Much of his skill trees currently remained at the soul rank, which will need the clone to spend some time out of its planned schedule in the Time Space raising the proficiencies of the skills before they could advance forward. This would be for later though, his attention currently turning towards the joyful Grandmaster that he stood on the same Realm as. The only thing missing being a few hundred thousand Fate Lines that he saw himself reaching not too long from now.","\"Hmm, terrific geniuses indeed. You’ll work to stabilize your new realm the next few days before we can set off again. I wanted your power to be as high as possible before you began joining any skirmishes of the coming war, but...\"","His gaze of joy turned difficult as he continued.","\"...I just received word that Grandmaster Luo of our 7th Celestial Star has been assassinated, and the Dark Expanse is to blame. This...is a Declaration of War!\"","Noah’s eyes opened wide as he heard this, his clone that was already locating another world to form a collection to also pausing in surprise as it heard the shocking results of its actions. Noah had known that at most, the Celestials would connect the disappearance of the Magus World to the technology of the Lost World of Atlantis they destroyed long ago, but they would never be able to find out exactly who was involved, as he was expertly guarded by both Fate and Chaos techniques!","Yet somehow, the Grandmasters had attributed the death of their own to the Dark Expanse in an effort to use it as one of the excuses to start the war.","A war between such huge forces did not begin and end in a day, where even the campaign of war that the Celestials carried in the War of the Righteous more than a thousand years ago, the war had lasted tens of years as the Celestials gained more territory and power.","This war that was about to begin would not end in a few days or a few months, the beings involved being too many and too powerful, where even Noah knew after he gained his burst of knew knowledge that it could take years! But, this was all without him in the picture. If he actually had a hand to play in this war as he increased his power....","He kept his thoughts to himself as he looked towards Athena, the memories of Grandmaster Luo letting him know that there was a connection between them! Athena looked towards the Grandmaster with an angry expression before being the one to speak out.","\"Grandmaster, I know our rise in strength has been going against the natural order, where the rate simply does not conform to the norm! But since our strength will allow us to bring forth even more order, I will gladly continue raising my power, and I know Junior Brother Crixus will do the same!\"","She had a valiant look on her face as she continued speaking.","\"In this large scale war, beings at the Domain Rank will be of great use, but those of higher levels will be the true decoders of the war! What can we do, Grandmaster, in order to attain such strength before the conflicts begin?\"","Unexpectedly, Noah did not see the reaction he expected from Athena as she straightforwardly asked Grandmaster Vredral how to further increase their power, the old man looking towards them with shining eyes and replying.","\"I was going to mention this to you after you had stabilized your realms and were ready to move forward, but...\"","\"...as there are numerous powerful Celestials that are special existences or those with Noble Fates, resources have been equally decided so far and are getting scarcer. This is even more so for resources that are useful to beings at the Domain Expansion Realm!\"","The Grandmaster spoke seriously as Noah considered his words about resources that could help someone at the Domain Rank. One must know, the Grandmaster was at the peak of this same rank, and even he had not broken through. Whatever resources that would be useful to him and Athena, they would also be useful to the Grandmaster! But this aged man did not even mention this as he seemed to focus his entire attention on the two of them.","\"The resources to help a being in the Domain Expansion Realm are scarce, but it does not mean they do not exist. But because of their rarity and the fact that there are so many qualified beings in this realm that desperately need such treasures to increase their power...something has to be done to determine which Special Existences or being with Noble Fate is holding more potential and more deserving of such treasures!\"","The words of the Grandmaster were explosive, Noah and Athena listening closely as they waited to hear exactly what the Celestials had in store. How would they be determining who is more deserving of treasures that were useful to even the most powerful of Grandmasters?!","The answer was in the form of battle!"]},{"number":438,"title":"Chapter 438: Chapter 437 - To Be Matched Against Special Existences","paragraphs":["\"The deciders of the direction of the war are the strongest beings, with players at the World Rank or the ranks above being the ones that will ultimately decide which battles we win or lose \"","Noah listened closely as the Grandmaster continued, his mind going towards the cultivation ranks the Grandmaster mentioned as he already knew what was above the rank of World.","After a being established a Domain to cover their origin, the next stage was the World Realm as they fused their Domain to their core, being able to bring out power that could destroy Small or Large Worlds!","After the world stage, one would embark on the path to strengthen their origin as if they were forming a world itself at their very center, the realm above this being called the Star Forging Realm!","Experts at this realm legitimately had the force of a star thrumming at the very center of their strength, Noah knowing that the middle ranked Infernal Lords occupied this level, as well as some of the more powerful Grandmasters.","Above the Star Forging Realm was the realm that the experts standing at the top of power in this expansive Novus Galaxy, it was the realm where one had to shatter the very Star they forged which stood at the center of their origin, allowing the explosion of the dying star to form what was the next stage after this- Nebula!","A Nebula was a giant cloud of dust and gas in the vastness of space, and it was this cloud of dust and gas where new stars formed. Experts at the Nebula Realm were those standing at the peak of power as any one of them could have a Nebula that already birthed multiple stars, the levels of strength being wide ranging as the fire power of such a realm was shocking to even understand.","As far as Noah knew, the strongest First Infernal Lord was at the Nebula Realm, along with the Founders that stood atop the Celestials!","But this was only what his knowledge led him to, he could always be wrong. He stopped dwelling in his thoughts as he continued to listen to the Grandmaster before him.","\"Celestials at the World Rank or higher are held with great esteem, being one of the powerful weapons that could even match against the weakest Infernal Lord if multiple of them work together. Thus, any treasure that can possibly help a Celestial step towards the World Rank is treated with utmost importance!\"","\"Such a treasure...does exist in our hands. It is something that is completely out of my reach, and will only be given to the most promising Special Existence or a Celestial holding the title of Noble Fate. This treasure is something that we found in the southern region of the Spiritual Land where Fate Behemoths are abundant, a treasure that I only know by the name- Luminescent Rainbow Dew!\"","The eyes of the listening students shone as a treasure was mentioned, something that even Grandmaster Vredral himself could not get his hands on.","\"You two have the chance of obtaining this Luminescent Rainbow Dew, but only if you can prove that your potential and power is greater and more deserving than the other beings at a similar standing as you. The way to do this is simply...through battle. In order for you all to experience a rapid rise in strength similar to the past few weeks and enter a Realm that will grant you the power to make a difference in this war, you will have to fight for it.\"","Noah thought of many possibilities as the abundant treasures of the Celestials continued to help him greatly, and this treasure that was being hyped up by the Grandmaster was one that could possibly bring him to yet another stage that would allow him to catch up to some of the monsters he was facing.","\"Who do we expect to be facing, Grandmaster?\"","Noah replied with the conviction that seemed to say they would do whatever it took to increase their power, the Grandmaster nodding with a received smile as he continued.","\"In a soon to be specified location, a Battle of Geniuses will be held where those joining will be faced with beings holding Noble Fates and Special Existences that have immensely powerful innate abilities. Coming out on top of this tournament will grant you some of the most valuable treasures that we have collected over the last thousand years!\"","A resounding reply rang out in the training hall they were in as they received the information on just how they could advance their strength further, Athena turning to look towards her Junior Brother with a determined look as the both of them nodded towards each other, turning their gazes to the Grandmaster as they replied.","\"We will not let you down, Grandmaster!\"","Noah continued to play the part of a genius disciple well as even more opportunities landed on his lap. As the cultivation and information session with the Grandmaster was coming to an end, he looked at the change that had appeared in the Stat Panel after he stepped into the Domain Expansion Realm.","[Noah Osmont][Title(s): Infernal Lord(Variant)]","[Bloodline(s): Vampyre Progenitor(Awakening)]","[Fate Line(s) : 162,735]","[Chaos Particle(s) : 135,234]","[Origin Core(s) : Fire-2]","[Domain(s) : Water, Space, Fate, Fire, Chaos]","[Vitality: DOMAIN]","[Focus: - ]","[Strength: DOMAIN]","[Law(s) : Water-11, Space-8%, Fate-1.6%, Fire-14%, Chaos-1.3%]","Among the many additions that continued to be added over the last weeks, there now stood another one that was titled [Domain(s)]!","Included in it, the laws that Noah was currently cultivating were available, meaning that if he so chose, he could release a domain of any of these laws to pressure his enemies. The higher his percentage of the laws increased, the more powerful the domains would become. For now, all he had to do was continue the monotonous work of cultivating Fate and Chaos, as well as have his clone move in the Celestial Realm once more to look for an Inheritance that dealt with the law of water.","This was because normal universal laws like water and fire were much easier to raise up, and Noah knew if he could repeat something similar to what he was currently doing by dual cultivating both fate and chaos, raising the laws of water and fire should be even easier!"]},{"number":439,"title":"Chapter 439: Chapter 438 - Atop a Dragon Searching for Treasures","paragraphs":["Noah glanced at the Grandmaster that gave him and Athena more information of the Battle of Geniuses where they would have to face the terrible power of Special Existences and being similar to them with noble fates in order to get his hands of treasures that could help those in the Domain Rank.","For now, his main body would participate in this tournament seeming event as his clone continued to do the brunt work. At this moment, his Ancient Blood Clone had formed a connection with a Large World that Noah found viable in his memories, the beings within not having too many connections and not being of high strength.","Much of these types of worlds came from the memories of the Demon Emperor Baal who was very active in targeting middle and large worlds as he expanded his forces. This recent world achieved Noah’s goal of passing 10 connected worlds, the most recent ones being brought near his homeworld through the use of World Engines, with Noah casting a [World Veil] thereafter to hide all of them from prying eyes!","These newly added worlds did not even need to be identified by name or unique qualities, as none of that would matter in the coming weeks as he soon planned to carry out the grand plan of a Realm Formation. Such a plan...would make the identities of worlds null.","His eyes shone with splendor as the meeting with the Grandmaster moved along, thereafter obtaining more information on the recent events where Grandmaster Luo was assassinated and the resulting actions that came thereafter.","The leading Grandmaster on the 7th Celestial Star, Grandmaster Ramiel, had already formally filed for permission to move his Battalion that was made of numerous Prime Warsh.i.p.s and Celestials towards the border between the Dark and Light Expanse, sending them as the preliminary force as they initiated what would be a long period of war.","Some Celestials were opposed to this as they wished for a longer preparation period to orderly move all forces, but even more were for it as it meant they could begin their conquest that would lead to more influence over many beings’ fates much sooner!","The request of Grandmaster Ramiel would most likely soon be given a green light after it was passed to the Founder, what happened thereafter only being etched in history.","Something new that came at the center of this was the prepared command that would be given to the powerful beings of the Prime Expanse that were moving in the Celestial Realm. They would be told that for them to continue exploring and enjoying the boons of the wondrous realm, they had to send a specific number of beings from their worlds as soldiers to fight alongside the Celestials! They had to fight for the peace and order of the Light Expanse that was being disrupted by the Dark Expanse!","This command would cause for the influx of millions of beings to be in the front lines in the coming war, this conflict of attrition eventually benefitting the Celestials as they would be losing very little of their own forces as time passed.","Thus, many waited for the okay to get things started, Noah absorbing all of the information himself as he continued preparing in his own ways. The Spiritual World continued to bubble with essence, numerous things being accomplished every day by the System that stood as the center of the Spiritual World.","The building of the Water Law Space had already been completed on one of the four continental landmasses of the Spiritual World, Noah actually choosing to reduce the Fire Law Space to cover half of the Continent, and for the Water Law Space to cover the other half. This created the unique environment where two opposing Law Spaces had an inch of a barrier that stopped them from flooding into the other. This was all in preparation for the obtainment of a new inheritance in the Law of Water that would allow Noah to perform Dual Cultivation with these two laws as well!","The Ancient Blood Clone finished forming the connection of another world as he sent numerous telepathic messages to his competent forces to handle this transition, Steel Mikhail and even Kazuhiko that seemed to never want to leave the Time Space that he was using with extreme efficiency to raise his skill proficiencies being put to use.","The clone moved without rest as he reappeared back into the Celestial Realm, his body currently pulsing with power as his main body had stepped into the Domain Expansion Realm. When this was paired to his continued advancement in two Supreme Laws, many beings would feel their souls shaking if he didn’t cover up the pressure of power that he released.","This time, the clone had appeared in a region not too far from the Sanctum, his gaze going towards a certain direction. This time, it wasn’t the North where the Fire Behemoths and Chaos Behemoths resided, but the South where one could find Water Behemoths and Ice Behemoths, his goal being to look for the treasures and inheritances here as he increased the efficiency of his cultivation even more!","His rapid rise in Chaos Particles and Fate Lines was going in the right direction, but his Fire Origin Core had remained with a slow progression where even the Supreme Laws could soon surpass it.","\"Draco, come back.\"","He sent a telepathic message to the Draconic Fire Behemoth that was moving in the First Infernal Realm to pass through the portal there and return to the Spiritual World, the huge beast materializing in front of Noah a few seconds later as he came out from the miniaturized world.","RUMBLE!","\"Master!\"","The voice of the humongous beast reverberated as its head that was now multiple times larger than Noah went forward to nudge him, the clone smiling as he got on its wide back, and the dragon took off into the skies!","Its size now towered close to 40 meters, Noah already pulling out numerous Cores from his [Expansive Space] to begin power leveling the rank of this beast towards the Soul Forging Realm.","Then, he took out the wondrous miniaturized Spiritual World as he activated [Treasure Hunter], an eruption of essence coming out as a direction was picked.","He sent his thoughts into the ability to try and steer it towards what he wanted, but this would only steer it towards a certain direction, where the actual results would be hard to know.","SHAA!","The figure of an enormous dragon shot through the fantastically glowing trees and vegetation around the Celestial Realm as Noah’s clone continued on towards the South fearlessly, his heart looking forward to whatever treasures or inheritances waited for him there!"]},{"number":440,"title":"Chapter 440: Chapter 439 - Growth, Treasures","paragraphs":["As Noah made his way south, his forces propagated various areas of the Celestial Realm as their increased power only allowed for more efficient and effective cooperation that took down behemoths with ease.","Not to mention their own recently upgraded ranks and cores from Soul Rank Behemoths continued to flow towards their hands, the boon from the [Golden Guider] skill was so overpowered that when they faced the Fire Behemoths to the north, they could take them down much faster as each of them held a hint of the law of fate in their attacks.","Most of the forces were now actively moving as the things around Noah became more and more expansive, even the lazy Barbatos joining the Order of Blood Exploration Team as her own specialized legion of undead joined the fights.","Others were either put on tasks to manage the newly added worlds or hunting Behemoths for their resources, with these resources being transferred into the Spiritual World through the Emperor Penguin that held ever so powerful spatial skills.","These abundant materials would then be processed by the System at the center of the Spiritual World as they were forged into Items in the Blacksmith's Forge, powerful Sets of armors and weapons that had overwhelming effects being created with ease.","Currently, the number of Blood Stained Infernal Oath Sets made from the bodies of Infernals were the most numerous as Noah had simply hunted too many of them to obtain his Infernal Lord title. The Incandescent Flameborn Set was next in production as more and more materials from Fire Behemoths were obtained, these powerful Sets that had a 6 piece bonus of an Immolation ability that allowed the wearer to deal 1000% more damage being something extremely deadly.","As Noah's forces gradually became equipped with these terrifying Items and the boosts from the Golden Guider, their power was spilling upwards exponentially as they were growing to become a powerful force!","It was not just Noah that was currently rapidly advancing through ranks, his forces were also following along!","His Ancient Blood Clone continued flying through the mystical forest of the Celestial Realm, the young dragon Draco enjoying the return to the overflowing essence of the realm as it broke the sound barrier to shoot towards the direction that its master directed it towards at high speeds.","\"Slow down.\"","Noah sent his thoughts forward as he felt the golden arrow from the Spiritual World beginning to blink, the dragon slowing down and reducing its altitude as Noah came to view the environment to the south of the Celestial Realm with more clarity.","Huge ancient trees with blue colored leaves were abundant, with numerous lakes that sparkled clearness and serenity spread out all around. As he spread his senses further out with the dragon slowly moving forward, he could see rushing rivers, and even further locations being areas of frozen lands where he even spotted an Ice Behemoth.","In the South of the Celestial Realm, one could come across Behemoths proficient in the law of water, whether they were plain Water Behemoths or the specific Ice Behemoths.","ROAR!","The arrival of a Draconic Fire Behemoth in the skies drew the attention of a nearby Ice Behemoth, but Noah ignored it as Draco continued towards a certain location, Noah following the blinking arrow closely as it pointed towards a sparkling and expansive lake that was surrounded by trees.","Draco hovered over the pristine lake as Noah saw the arrow to be pointing down, sending his thoughts to his pet as Draco was transferred back into the Spiritual World, the figure of the clone shooting down towards the clear lake speedily as it went to see just what exactly the [Treasure Hunter] feature had found now.","SHAA!","His body pierced through the waters with ease as he began descending down, the lake being very deep as he spent a few minutes diving down and watching the area around him.","His body was filled with covert skills after he sent Draco away so that he did not get discovered too easily if there was something powerful down the lake, and his senses already caught one Water Behemoth happily swimming a few miles away.","After achieving the Domain Expansion Realm, Noah felt an astounding level of control of his energy as the Domain that wrapped around his origin allowed him to feel a sense of stableness that he never came across before. He saw that his progress in the Fire Origin Core even increased after achieving the Domain Rank, seeing that higher realms held their own secrets and surprises to unfold as he continued on in the future.","His figure continued shooting down the lake for another few minutes before he neared the bottom the area around him becoming colder as his eyes came across a cold hard floor that shone with a blue crystalline l.u.s.ter!","His senses tried spreading through this layer of earth to see what lied below it, but he surprisingly found that he could not spread his aura past it, whatever the Spiritual World was pointing down towards still not known.","His fingers tapped onto the earth as he found it to be extremely hard material, but its uniqueness lied in the fact that even a being at the Domain Rank could not spread his aura past it. Noah chose the less destructive way as he became extremely small and minute through [Unique Origin], using his very small size and immensely boosted strength to drill through this unique earthen layer.","It wasn't even that thick, his body being able to pierce through the other end in a matter of minutes as he entered into the hidden space that lied below the frozen floor at the bottom of the lake.","His eyes looked around as they shimmered a color of blue, this color being reflected by everything he was seeing as the place he had entered...looked to be a huge stalagmite mine!","Numerous Crystals littered the area, his eyes seeing that the space was not even that huge, maybe the size of a football field. But this space held an array of Crystals Stalagmites that shone with a deep blue hue, Noah sensing a congregation of the Law of Water deeply entrenched into every single one of them.","Though the blue crystals were many, they were not the most eye-catching thing in this hidden cavern. The most eye-catching thing was that at the center of this place, there laid an even more enormous crystal in the shape of a spiked crown, most of the energies around this place congregating towards it! Noah's gaze landed on this vibrantly dense blue crystal as a few words popped up in front of his eyes.","<strong>[Unique Material- Aquamarine Mesrandite].</strong>","His eyes shone with understanding as he laid his eyes upon the first-ever Unique Material that he came across, his goal of searching for an inheritance leading him to another treasure entirely as he actually came across something which could be used to refine Supreme Treasures, or even possibly create one!"]},{"number":441,"title":"Chapter 441: Chapter 440 - Materials","paragraphs":["In a brightly blue lit up underground area, sparking crystal stalagmites exposed the brilliance of the area as the brightest one that stood at the center had more descriptions rise up gradually in front of Noah’s eyes.","<strong>[Unique Material- Aquamarine Mesrandite] :: A material that has collected an abundant amount of the essence of the law of water, granting it the unique title. Can be used to refine Supreme Treasures or in the creation of one in the Blacksmith’s Forge of the Spiritual World.</strong>","Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone had actually come across a material of great value in his search for an inheritance, something that thrummed with the power of the Law of Water, a material that he could use to either refine the Trident of the Sea, or possibly create another Supreme Treasure!","His eyes shone as he waved his hands towards this enormous [Unique Material- Aquamarine Mesrandite], watching it disappear from his eyes as his gaze turned towards the numerous other crystals that weren’t nearly as bright as the one he had just pocketed.","<strong>[Water Crystal] :: A crystal holding the essence of the Law of Water, can be used as a material to refine normal Items or further refined with the locked feature of the Spiritual World, [Alchemy Hall], into Soul Jades.</strong>","The less bright crystal stalagmites were Water Crystals that were similar to the Fire Crystals he had obtained as materials before from his first Fire Behemoth, but he noticed the additional descriptive words added to the item as the Planetary System hinted to a feature he could not even use yet.","\"You are able to foresee the possible uses of the future features of the Spiritual World already?\"","He asked the Planetary System as a reply came a millisecond later.","[The veils of secrecy for the natural order and existence of things is gradually becoming thinner as we gather more information and connect to more worlds, your elevation to an Infernal Lord granting us access to a profound bank of knowledge that allows for fairly accurate possibilities.]","Noah’s clone nodded as he was reminded of the information that would make many tremble to their cores, the powers of the beings standing atop this Novus Galaxy being so terrifying that nobody would ever think of matching themselves against them.","When faced with beings that had established a Domain and then entered a realm where they could destroy worlds, and then they went even further ahead to forge an entire star at their core before they shattered this star to form a Nebula that could birth even more stars...many would simply run away!","But Noah received this knowledge as it made his fear at first, yes! But he reminded himself of his own power, and just how rapid he could rise through the ranks compared to anyone else.","An example was how in just a period of the past few weeks, he had gone from the Void Realm and into the Soul Forging Realm, and just now he had stepped into the Domain Expansion Realm!","What speed!","What genius!","With such an overpowering power behind him and his own confidence for the future, he saw himself in no way lesser than the beings that already stood near the top.","He shook himself out of his reverie as he glanced at the many Water Crystals around him, waving his hands as the wide expanse that was the size of a football field began to be emptied until the brightness was gradually gone. Every single shining crystal that had even the tiniest l.u.s.ter was taken into the Spiritual World as the place where a treasure trove had been laid barren, Noah’s figure bringing out the Spiritual World thereafter as he used [Treasure Hunter] once more, another golden arrow appearing as he was led to another direction once more!","He disappeared from the barren underground area as he teleported to the skies, having finally attained the Domain Expansion Realm that allowed one to fly freely in the Celestial Realm. But, he liked the feeling of flying on an enormous Draconic Fire Behemoth even more, so Draco reappeared in the skies with a shaking presence as Noah landed on its head, a slight smile on his face as he patted the enormous dragon that began leaving embers of flames as it began shooting through the skies!","---","In another location, his main body was in an expensive lodging of the Celestials in the Sanctum, having returned from the far region where Chaos Behemoths were abundant in order to consolidate his realm and in preparation for the battles between Special Existences and beings similar to him who held noble fates, or so the commands from Grandmaster Vredral stated.","His main body was planning on how to best move within the ranks of the Celestials to maintain the most benefits, especially this treasure known as Luminescent Rainbow Dew that even Grandmasters at the peak of the Domain Expansion Realm wished for. He was thinking of how to move while gaining all of these benefits, but he was also thinking of the overall results he wanted to obtain from this organization!","His thoughts went towards Athena, another figure that would play a central role in the events to come as at this moment in time, he saw her as a viable scheme to play. He had already placed himself in the War Princess’s life until her guard was completely down around him, and he recently obtained even more information that pertained to her from the Grandmaster Luo that he took down in the Magus World.","The information was something that was only a bit of history, but it could be used to create an amazing opportunity for the future. So while his clone continued to move in search of treasures and the continuing cultivation of laws, Noah was currently scheming, and at the heart of the scheme was the valiant War Princess!","In the expansive room he was in, Noah turned his head towards the door as he waved his hands to make the Dagger of Time that was slowly rotating in front of him disappear. The past few hours, he had been using the [Insight] feature of the Dagger to look at a few possibilities of how his plan could play out, and was confident in it somewhat as he heard a knock on his door soon after.","He went over the plan a few times, changing what he was wearing as he also used [Unique Origin] and then walked towards the door and opening in as in front of him was the War Princess herself, her face holding a vibrant expression as Noah saw on her body, she was adorned by a unique golden robe that only signified one thing, and it was a type of status that very few Celestials held in the Light Expanse.","\"Senior Sister, they’ve already given you a title of Grandmaster?\"","Noah smiled as he spoke to the War Princess in front of him, a scheme that would be one of the deciders for a few major events in the future beginning to play out at this moment. He had not done anything these past weeks as he was around this Senior Sister, but he would be making his move today!"]},{"number":442,"title":"Chapter 442: Chapter 441 - Inducement, Behind a Waterfall!","paragraphs":["\"Senior Sister, they’ve already given you a title of Grandmaster?\"","Noah’s gaze was steady as the girl in front of the door looked to be slightly taken aback as she saw him because at this moment, he had made it so that when he opened the door, he was standing in front of her with a fresh towel wrapped around his waist, another white towel on his hands as he dried his hair damp as if he has just taken a shower.","Athena looked at him as she shook her head with a smiling expression and replied.","\"I’ve long since passed 100,000 Fate Lines, it was long overdue. I wanted to come tease my little Junior Brother about how he was lagging behind and take you with me to spar, but you don’t seem all that down.\"","Noah smiled as he looked at where they were standing, having an expression of not wanting to be impolite as he invited Athena in.","\"Please, come in and have a seat. Tell me of the perks you have now that you can be called a Grandmaster.\"","The expansive dwelling Noah was in could be considered an entire house, having a wide living room area and a few other separate rooms. Athena came in and sat at the exquisitely designed table as she replied.","\"Not that many perks and just more responsibilities. It’s just a title that many Celestials have, even the Special Existences and other beings with Noble fates that we will be facing soon holding the same title as many of them have achieved more than 100,000 lines of fate. By the way...Junior Brother Crixus, are you just expecting me to ignore the fact that you only have a towel wrapped around you this entire time we’ve been talking? What exactly are you trying to pull off?\"","The eyes of the War Princess squinted carefully as she asked, Noah laughing as he waved his hands and changed to plain white clothing.","\"I thought I would catch Senior Sister off guard by showing her something she rarely sees, but you seem as impassive as ever.\"","\"Oh, did you expect me to jump on you the moment you took your shirt off?\"","Athena replied teasingly as she looked towards Noah, this not being the first time that the senior brother and sister were bantering, their time spent together the past few weeks being abundant.","\"Maybe not with my shirt, but what if I cook for you again?\"","Noah asked with a smile as he went towards the kitchen and waved his hands, taking out behemoth meat that was filled with essence while looking towards the senior sister that was now looking at him with shining eyes. His food had been the one thing that caused her to speedily open up to him, being something that she never tasted before! A conflicting look appeared on her face, but not for a long as her eyes quickly regained their normal valiant look.","\"Hmph, I came over here to ask you to go spar with me to celebrate my ascension to a Grandmaster, but it seems all you want to do is play around.\"","Noah’s eyes shone the moment he heard these words, the things he foresaw playing in the proper direction as he moved in right away.","\"What if we did play around, Senior Sister?\"","OOOM!","Silently, essence moved as Noah activated a skill he had not utilized since he first received it, dipping his hands into one of the Seven Deadly Sins available to him- the Sin of L.u.s.t! He had never used this skill before, and even using it now on this War Princess wasn’t something he would normally do, but he had to move things along as he set up the sequence of events to possibly control this being in the future.","The skill he used at this moment was the last listed ability under the Sin of L.u.s.t, it was [L.u.s.t Inducement]!","<strong>[L.u.s.t Inducement] - The user can increase the l.u.s.t other beings feel. This will make it easier for the user to manipulate said being. </strong>","Noah’s eyes shone red as they glanced towards the War Princess that reflected a similar color briefly, her strict demeanor changing as she looked towards Noah and the behemoth meat ready to be cooked on the table. She seemed to think for a bit before she replied.","\"I’ll only stay for the food. No funny business, little junior brother.\"","At these words, Noah only smiled as he lit up a fire and began roasting the essence filled meat. If there was an analogy to describe what had just happened at this moment, it would be akin to a fish taking the bait, and now he was just reeling it in as on this day, he planned to initiate a scheme to bring this being with a Noble Fate under his heel.","His gaze was looking forward to a distant future when he could manipulate her as he wished to deal a decisive blow or even multiple of them in the coming war!","---","As his main body schemed in the Sanctum, Noah’s clone was shattering the sound barrier atop Draco as they shot off in another direction that [Treasure Hunter] pointed him towards.","The mystical Celestial Realm continued to reflect on his eyes as he went forward, passing numerous Behemoths below him and finding very little flying Behemoths, these being more common near the regions where Elite Behemoths resided.","He even came across a particular Exploration Party from one of the Prime Worlds that looked to the skies in shock after hearing a booming sound, only finding embers of flames left behind.","A few hours passed in this manner, the gaze of the clone continuing to watch the golden arrow that led him to an unknown location in the Celestial Realm, where it finally began to vibrate when they neared an area filled with raging rivers, as well as an enormous waterfall that smashed down to hard blue rocks.","Draco slowed down and eventually came to a stop as the golden arrow from the Spiritual World pointed down towards the waterfall below them, the young dragon being sent away yet again as Noah began to shoot down towards this waterfall.","He couldn’t feel the presence of any beasts, the only sound he heard being the roaring waves of crashing water. The rapidly vibrating arrow led him right in front of the waterfall and pointed forward, his gaze remaining firm as he floated towards it and pierced the rapid waters.","SHAAA!","A crystal blue covered his eyes as he passed through the water, his senses observing there was actually a hidden location behind this waterfall!","No beast of human was in sight as he passed through, coming into a blue glittering cavern that sn.a.k.e.d forward. The golden arrow from the Spiritual World continued to vibrate faster as he went further in, the hidden space opening up in front of his eyes until he came into a much wider clearing where a pool of extremely crystalline blue water peacefully laid. Near this mystical pool of water, an ancient pedestal that held a huge blue crystal could be seen.","Noah smiled as his eyes landed on the pedestal, but in front of his gaze, it was shockingly two descriptions that came up, one from the essence-abundant pool of water, and the other from the pedestal!","[Prismatic Aurora Spring Water]","<Inheritance of the Disciple of Water>","...!"]},{"number":443,"title":"Chapter 443: Chapter 442 - Plucking Treasures Left and Right","paragraphs":["When the hours were passing as his clone neared a particular waterfall where treasures laid within, Noah’s main body had plucked another treasure in the Sanctum.","In the dwelling that he was in, there was an expansive bed that would put even a memory foam mattresses to shame, his well-built body was covering the things below his waist as a senior sister that had lost her usual ponytail, her glimmering dark hair sprawled out in a rough manner as she rested her head on Noah’s chest.","\"You know, a junior brother should not be doing those types of things to his Senior Sister.\"","Athena spoke with a light tone as she had an expression of relaxation, her fingers tapping on the defined abdominal muscles as she counted with a cloudy expression.","\"It was the least I could do. The only thing I’ve seen you do is battle and cultivate that I was starting to wonder if you had it in yo-\"","Pah!","A light slap landed on his chest as Noah stopped his sentence, Athena looking towards him with a threatening expression as he smiled and stared at the ceiling. A second later, he spoke again, this time in a softer tone.","\"I am curious about something though, in regards to the news of Grandmaster Luo. I did not expect you to react the way you did.\"","Athena raised her head slowly as her cloudy eyes looked at Noah’s, replying with a sigh as her curvaceous body that was always hidden from the eyes of many stood up, a simple robe wrapping around her thereafter as she began fixing her hair back into a ponytail.","\"It is what fate laid in store, so I don’t particularly have any strong feelings.\"","Her tone was reminiscent and slightly cold as she spoke, Noah’s eyes shining as he continued.","\"He was the one to find you in your ruined world and take you to become a Celestial, I thought it would hit you hard.\"","\"We know the risks we take in order to maintain balance in this galaxy of ours. Fate is written for some of us to fall, and some of us to continue towards a larger goal. We lost a great Grandmaster, and we will be sure to make those responsible pay for it, using it as an opportunity to bring about even more order!\"","Athena replied strongly as even when faced with the death of the being that took her from her star to become a Celestial, she viewed it the same as how she viewed her disciples that died during the last Infernal Hunt.","What she didn’t know was that those disciples and even the recent Grandmaster Luo had all perished from Noah’s hands!","The biggest thing was not this though. In Noah’s mind, the biggest boon he received from killing Grandmaster Luo was the memories he obtained, the memories that told him the true story behind the planet that this War Princess was on, as well as Grandmaster Luo who just ’happened’ to be on this planet to discover a girl that had a Noble Fate.","He held a shocking secret about this event that he planned to use in the future as he continued to bring this senior sister under his heel, what he began here today being just the start as he planned to utilize the abilities of the Sin of L.u.s.t to manipulate the War Princess as much as possible, planning to use her as a weapon against the beings she currently stood with!","He spoke towards the robed Athena that already had her usual ponytail up, the simple robe covering everything he was just seeing.","\"Alright. Why did you get dressed though, we have at least another few hours?\"","\"No, we have to prepare for the powerful beings we will be matched with soon. Not all of us are crazy geniuses that are obtaining Fate Lines faster than anyone thought possible.\"","Athena replied with a firm expression as she spoke once more with a light smile.","\"Let’s go spar again, maybe if you win this time...I’ll entertain the thought of returning to this room again.\"","Noah’s eyes squinted as he nodded, going with the flow as his relationship with this War Princess had moved forward to another stage, continuing his intrusion into the Celestials and their forces as he prepared for a few things!","One was the plan for the War Princess, the other was the battle with Special Existences and beings with Noble Fates that would decide whether he received amazing treasures that might even allow him to break into the World Rank at a rate he never expected.","To achieve such a rank, either he had to do the impossible thing of fighting a being at that rank and winning, obtaining their cores to make his breakthrough. The other way would be to traverse the Celestial Realm until he found a treasure similar to what the Celestials currently had as the prize for the coming battle between powerful geniuses.","His clone had actually come across a treasure that wasn’t just an Inheritance in the Celestial Realm just now, Noah’s mind paying attention to the description of the things that his clone was seeing in the hidden space behind the waterfall far to the south region from where his main body was.","Moving from the scene of the vibrant Senior Sister and Junior Brother that were leaving their living quarters to begin a different sort of spar, Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone neared the shining pond and the Inheritance of the Disciple of Water as their descriptions appeared in front of him!","<strong><Inheritance of the Disciple of Water> :: Left behind to those fate intended, this inheritance grants the unique cultivation ability {Disciple of Water}, as well as the Absolute Skill <<Herald of Water>> that are meant to create a master of the water element.</strong>","<strong>[Prismatic Aurora Spring Water] :: An enriched spring water that is soothing to the soul and good for the body. One cup grants +100% Health and Energy Regeneration and +100% increased Damage to all Water-related Abilities for 30 minutes. Even more benefits can be gained if the spring water is taken away and used for the plants in the Spiritual World, or especially so in the locked feature of [Alchemy Hall].</strong>","The description of the <Inheritance of the Disciple of Water and the other treasure that he got his hands on were clearly detailed, his eyes being drawn towards the ancient pedestal that held the inheritance, but also glancing towards the spring water with even more curiosity.","He spread his senses to cover the entire spring that was half a mile wide, finding a glistening blue pearl at the very center. His attention was grabbed as he dived into the pool of spring water, sensing its abundant essence that already began rushing towards him on all sides. He couldn’t help but take a few gulps as he felt the rushing of essence coursing through him, this spring water being something that could make anyone feel like they were in their prime!","He quickly reached the bottom where the pearl was located, wrapping it in his hands as its description became clear to him.","<strong>[Prismatic Aurora Pearl] :: A pearl capable of releasing Prismatic Aurora Spring Water in a region of half a mile. A unique treasure that is hard to find.</strong>","The treasure capable of releasing the wondering spring water was obtained as he transferred it to the Spiritual World, giving a command to the Spiritual World System to place it in the continent that held both the Water and Fire Law Space, the pearl to be placed on the region filled to the brim with the essence of the law of water!","He then waved his hands towards all the surrounding spring water as all of it went to his Expansive Space, his gaze moving towards the ancient pedestal holding the Inheritance of the Disciple of Water. This would be the treasure that would allow him to rapidly cultivate two normal laws at a speed nobody thought to be possible before!"]},{"number":444,"title":"Chapter 444: Chapter 443 - Disciple of Water","paragraphs":["Noah glanced at the ancient pedestal holding the resplendent crystal, expecting for the skills and descriptions of the Inheritance of the Disciple of Water to be very similar to the counterpart of Fire. His thoughts were affirmed as he placed his hands on the huge crystal and the enormous flow of information began rushing towards him.","The first thing was the technique that would help him cultivate the law of water itself, it was the unique skill, {Disciple of Water}!","<strong>{Disciple of Water} :: A technique geared towards cultivating the Law of Water. Grants the user the ability to form a unique Water Origin Core.</strong>","It was very similar to the Disciple of Fire, Noah not needing to comment anything on it as he moved on to the Absolute Skill contained in the Inheritance.","<strong><<Herald of Water>> A technique coming from the inheritance of the Disciple of Water that strives for the aspect of extreme in the Law of Water. Abilities include Ice Age, Incarnation of Water, Elemental Soul Reinforcement, and Summon Tsunami.</strong>","<strong>[Ice Age] :: The Herald of Water had the right to call forth an entire field of unstable and frigid water elements onto a wide ranging area. Enemies within will have extreme cold seeps into their bones as the Slow and Frozen Effects are applied while the user gets increased speed and power within the world of ice. Current Enhancement- +0%</strong>","<strong> [Incarnation of Water] :: You continuously release particles of water from your body, creating large bodies of water rapidly as it can be manipulated to form varying shapes depending on the comprehension of the user. The Stage of the Water Origin Core will determine the enhanced damage. Current Enhancement- +0%</strong>","<strong>[Elemental Soul Reinforcement] :: A unique shield of water rich in the elemental law of water wraps around the soul of the user, granting increased protection from any sources of Soul Damage. The Stage of the Water Origin Core will determine the enhanced reinforcement. Current Reinforcement- +0%</strong>","<strong>[Summon Tsunami] :: A disaster materializes in front of the Herald of Water as a tsunami made up of water particles whose only purpose is to drown their enemies descends forth. Current Damage Enhancement- +0%</strong>","The abilities of the Disciple of Water were laid out clearly in front of Noah, a few of them being similar to the abilities from the Disciple of Fire, with some distinct ones. One thing that could be noticed now was the fact that for their enhancements, they were all at 0% as currently, he had not even formed a Water Origin Core yet.","Once he formed one at the First Stage, the enhancement would go to 100%, with the second Stage granting him 200% and on and on.","Noah watched the new skills and abilities settle in his already expansive Stat Panel as he used [Anchor] to place the Spiritual World near the Ancient Pedestal, entering within as he appeared in the skies.","He watched the mystically floating continents on all four sides and the central one that he could see large scale changes on, the Spiritual World System already beginning to renovate and use the [Architecture] feature to fully build a magnificent city of Noah’s wildest dreams.","He thought he was creative, but his thought did not stand a chance when compared to the System that lied at the center of the Spiritual World!","The Central Continent of the Spiritual World had futuristic buildings that were reminiscent of the dreams of the people in Noah’s home world on what a future would look like, with huge skyscr.a.p.ers and exquisitely styled buildings that would take one’s breath away.","Not all the areas of the Central Continent were changed like this, a majority of it still left in a natural state as huge trees rose up, the Spiritual World Beasts still living in the habitats they enjoyed.","Of course, the higher leveled Spiritual World Beasts like the Emperor Penguin preferred the quality of comfort that could be found in the exquisitely built buildings, especially the places with hot springs and beds that made one feel they were sinking down endlessly.","Noah put the spectacular advances of the Spiritual World out of his mind as his figure teleported to the Northern Continent of this wondrous treasure where both the Law Spaces of Water and Fire resided, his figure entering the Water Law Space first as he wanted to form the Water Origin Core similarly to how he first formed the Fire Origin Core without trying anything out just yet.","While he did this, he sent telepathic commands to the Harbingers and his other subordinates to tell them that yet another Inheritance waited for them!","Those that were moving within the Spiritual World simply needed to go out to the luminescent hidden space where Noah anchored the Spiritual World right next to the Ancient Pedestal holding the Inheritance of the Disciple of Water, while those who were not on the Spiritual World would simply have to use the portals in whatever world they were in to return and partake in yet another unbelievable opportunity.","Many of them were already growing numb at all the treasures and opportunities they were receiving, and in such short periods of time at that as they had not even fully devoured the gains of the previous treasures.","For many of his subordinates, they were still just finishing forming their Fire Origin Core at the First Stage, where even the second Stage might take them months or years to achieve. Yet now another Inheritance that would allow them to create another Origin Core landed on their laps!","Many beings in the light expanse would only dream of being subordinates that received such a treatment, but it was not even a possibility for them!","Noah would allow his people to learn the inheritance in the next few hours while he himself began forming the Water Origin Core by using the {Disciple of Water}, where he would try the Dual Cultivation method thereafter to see exactly what stage he could reach with the laws of water and fire.","After this task finished, he would check on exactly how he wanted to use the other treasure he obtained today, the [Unique Material- Aquamarine Mesrandite] that he could use to either refine the Trident of the Sea or possibly create a brand new Supreme Treasure.","As always, he felt like there were so many things he had to do, and just too little time!"]},{"number":445,"title":"Chapter 445: Chapter 444 - Water Origin Core!","paragraphs":["The Water Law Space located on the Northern Continent of the Spiritual World was an area filled with blue, the plants fitting to become aquamarine vegetation and the land itself holding vast expanses of lakes and rivers, with numerous waterfalls created from the different elevations of multiple areas as the water flowed in a circular fashion throughout the continent.","Elemental particles of water danced freely in the surroundings as Noah went towards the very center of this Water Law Space where the Spiritual World System had already placed down the [Prismatic Aurora Pearl] that released spring water filled with water element essence.","The pearl had been placed on an area of depression that would contain the spring water it would release, Noah already seeing more than half of the half a mile area already filled with the sparkling Prismatic Aurora Spring Water as he dipped his body into it.","He would cultivate at the very center of this Law Space, inside the valuable Spring Water from the treasure he recently obtained!","He prepared himself as he settled deep within the area, feeling the overpowering essence of water all around him as he smiled...and then activated {Disciple of Water}.","RUMBLE!","It was like a match had been lit as the instant the skill was initiated, all of the surrounding essence filled with the law of water rushed towards Noah’s clone, making him feel a tinge of pain as it rushed too fast towards the Origin of his main body!","The energy flowed in freely as he soon felt the appearance of a small clear blue dot to the right side of his main Origin Core, the Fire Origin Core that lied to the right of his main core still sitting stably.","Essence filled with the law of water rushed in, and so did his own mana as it all converged towards the ever so enlarging blue dot. Noah knew that the formation and rise of the Water Origin Core would be much faster as he already had 11% in the Law of Water, but he didn’t expect it to be so vigorous.","SHAA!","In the Prismatic Aurora Spring, there was a swirl of essence forming as it rushed towards Noah’s clone like a black hole, passing through him and going towards his main body through the unique channel they shared, the clone simply acting akin to a limb as his main body kept [Unique Origin] ability active with even more care these days to make sure that none of the changes that were brought upon by his clone cultivating the laws would ever outwardly show.","OOOM!","In a matter of moments, the first stage of the Water Origin Core formed as a shimmering blue circular core formed near his origin, beginning to rotate even faster as his mana continued rushing in.","After achieving stage one, just half an hour later, it doubled in size as it reached Stage 2!","Similar to the Fire Origin Core, whatever energy the Water Origin Core drank, it used it to get bigger while also releasing a unique energy that went on to wrap around every single cell in Noah’s body, the energy once again permeating though the clone before it rushed towards Noah’s main body in the Celestial Realm.","He could feel the dual strengthening of both the unique energy that the Fire Origin Core released, as well as the new one from the blue shimmering Water Origin Core.","The fiery one made his body feel more explosive, like his speed and power just continued to break through all bounds!","The calm blue energy permeating within him now slightly calmed the fiery energy, even slightly bolstering it, as Noah felt an overabundance of defense and resiliency with every passing second that his two bodies were washed by this energy. The process continued for quite a while, Noah enjoying the effects of it fully!","The essence of water continued to pour into the core for thereafter, only settling down a few hours later as Noah observed it to be slowing down its rate of energy absorption similar to what the Fire Origin Core had done, but it was still faster as he was located in an area extremely dense with the law of water, the Prismatic Aurora Spring only enhancing the environment more.","His eyes wandered to the shining blue box only he could see as he observed the stat panel for the new addition.","[Noah Osmont][Title(s): Infernal Lord(Variant)]","[Bloodline(s): Vampyre Progenitor(Awakening)]","[Fate Line(s) : 174,274]","[Chaos Particle(s) : 146,164]","[Origin Core(s) : Fire-2, Water-2]","[Domain(s) : Water, Space, Fate, Fire, Chaos]","[Vitality: DOMAIN]","[Focus: - ]","[Strength: DOMAIN]","[Law(s) : Water-19%, Space-8%, Fate-1.7%, Fire-18%, Chaos-1.4%]","The number of Fate Lines and Chaos Particles continued their rapid growth as he broke through any established norms to amass even more of them. His eyes focused on the Water Origin Core that had reached the same stage 2 as the fire counterpart, its percentage even catching up as he did not completely see through the Stages and how they correlated with the percentages. Stage 2 didn’t simply translate to progressing 20%, and it seemed he had to break past this stage to see exactly how the percentages would move thereafter.","To do this, he shifted his body as he teleported from the Prismatic Aurora Spring Water and went towards the area where both the Fire and Water Law Space met.","His gaze landed on these areas that portrayed two different worlds with just a movement of his eyes, where to his left was a blazing earth filled with fiery outbursts, and to his right was a calm blue shimmering earth filled with water.","It was an interesting contrast to observe as he went forward and positioned himself right in between where these two areas met, his body standing right in the middle as half of it was in the Fire Law Space, and another half was in the Water Law Space.","He sensed the two opposite elements as he closed his eyes, the slowly rotating Origin Cores of Fire and Water slowly continuing to circulate by taking in his mana and releasing vibrant essence that went on to strengthen him. His eyes never left these two origin cores as he activated both of the unique skills, {Disciple of Water} and {Disciple of Fire} simultaneously!"]},{"number":446,"title":"Chapter 446: Chapter 445 - Fire and Water","paragraphs":["Behind a rushing waterfall in a particular location of the Celestial Realm, there was a hidden space where an Ancient Pedestal stood, gloriously holding up a vibrant blue crystal that held the Inheritance of the Disciple of Water.","Near this pedestal, there was a barely discernible floating Spiritual World where few creatures came out of every so often, learning the inheritance before they went back into the paradisiacal world. Most of them rushed to the floating continent on the North of the Spiritual World, this continent being divided in half by a thin line that had fiery environments on one side and a watery environment on the other.","The beings rushed to the side where the particles of the Law of Water were abundant before beginning their cultivation, the continental floating landmass being so wide that they didn’t even near a particular position where an explosion of blue and red lights was beginning.","At the very junction between the Fire and Water Law Space, a singular clone was sitting meditatively as his senses focused on his body, feeling the minuscule changes as he watched the two Origin Cores for fire and water slowly begin to rotate the moment both of their unique skills were activated.","From one side of his body, the elemental particles of fire rushed in and went towards the Fire Origin Core, and the opposite side of his body had the elemental particles of water rushing into the Water Origin Core.","BZZZZ!","Friction seemed to occur for a millisecond as the opposing energies seemed to bathe Noah half and half, their point of contact causing a rapid repulsion as they began to vibrate in extremely close proximity to each other. Yet at the same time, there continued to be a sense of attraction as the two cores pulled this energy towards them, Noah feeling as if his body was becoming a battle ground.","Every time that the particles of the two opposing elements came in contact as they went towards his Origin, they became agitated and pushed against each other, making them aggressive as this reaction caused them to rush towards his Origin faster!","The moment that they entered, they rushed to their respective Cores, whether Fire or Water, before even more of the elemental particles continued to rush in as the reaction became faster and faster.","The colliding particles of water and fire continued to agitate each other and senselessly rush down Noah’s body, creating for a rapid progress in the rotation of the Fire and Water Origin Cores as they absorbed the essence rapidly while releasing its unique energy that coursed through his clone and then through his main body!","At this time, a smile of accomplishment would have passed over Noah as he performed the successful Dual Cultivation of the Laws of Water and Fire, but his current expression was one of grim pain as unlike Fate and Chaos, the reaction of the oncoming particles of Fire and Water used his body as the battlefield to become agitated before they rushed towards their respective cores speedily.","The reaction that occurred with his body at the center made for a very painful experience as he could feel the impact of the opposing elements damage him, observing his body being put under strain as even some muscles were torn!","It was at this instant though, that the unique energy being released from the Fire and Water Origin Core permeated through his body, washing over the torn muscles and aching areas as the millions of cells around these locations hungrily drunk the energy and were reformed right away, the strength they had increasing ever so slightly.","Noah observed this reaction as he grimaced in pain, but a smile came on his face nonetheless as he felt the minute strength gained from the unique energy released from the two cores repairing his torn muscles made them stronger than when it was absorbed by his cells normally while only cultivating a single law.","Thus, for the effects of the Dual Cultivation of both Fire and Water, Noah could conclude that it was bound to be an extremely painful experience, but it allowed him to bypass the rate at which energy entered into the Origin Cores at a turtles pace, the flow being constant and even increasing every so often as the energy the cores released went on to heal and even further strengthen his body that was acting like a battle field for the opposing laws!","RUMBLE!","The essence of water and fire from the two different sides of the Law Spaces cl.u.s.tered around Noah as they began forming a resplendent cloud of light, a unique cultivation session that had never before been done continuing in the Spiritual World.","---","In the wide Sanctum that Celestials controlled, there was a bustle of activities recently as among the ranks of the Celestials, word had been getting passed around that soon, the future powerhouses of their generation would be getting assessed on who among them had the greatest potential in the form of combat!","These words became a reality a few days later as it was announced to all that in the next few days, a spectacular tournament would be held at a specified location in the Celestial Realm. This tournament would involve beings that many rarely saw in their lifetimes as they were always moving with extreme efficiency deep in the Celestial Realm to increase their power.","It would be a tournament where beings holding Noble Fates and Special Existences took to stage, each of them fighting a battle of supremacy to see who exactly would come out on top!","This tournament was open for all to watch, being made into a huge festive event where the Celestials planned to reveal the beginning of a long paused conflict with the Dark Expanse. The Celestials wanted to use this tournament to announce the initiation of a grand campaign!","It would be located around a particularly clear field of land to the east of the Sanctum where the slightly docile Earth Behemoths resided, this wide expanse of land being perfect for the huge and spectacular battles about to take place.","Among the Special Existences and Celestials with Noble Fates, the upcoming geniuses known as Athena and Crixus would be making their grand entrance into the eyes of many who had only so far heard of them, or knew nothing about them..."]},{"number":447,"title":"Chapter 447: Chapter 446 - Even if its you!","paragraphs":["Noah's main body was sparring with Athena in one of the huge training halls while his clone continued the Dual Cultivation of the Laws of Fire and Water, the unique energy passing through his two bodies continuing to strengthen him.","BOOM!","The golden floating hammers around him stopped the strikes of the War Princess that was clad in an empyrean armor, her own hammers that she held in her hands striking the ones floating around Noah away as she tried to land attacks on him. But every time she neared, they stood in her way, and this situation was made even worse as five enormous blades of liberation were on standby to strike towards her anytime she left a gap in her defenses.","Noah himself was floating in the skies as he glanced at this sight, a smug smile on his face as Athena's sharp eyes found him.","\"Are you deliberately trying to annoy me, Junior Brother?\"","The frustrated Athena called out as her body began to shine gold with numerous fate lines erupting out, the essence of fate beginning to shine brilliantly around her as she sprung forth like a cannon towards Noah.","BOOM!","With every swipe of her hammers, powerful fate essence erupted out, this ability being something that only those passing the 100,000 Fate Lines milestone could use. The strikes filled with fate essence smashed back the three floating hammers around Noah as Athena closed in, her gaze filled with bloodl.u.s.t as she spoke.","\"Very soon, you will be facing Special Existances that have been in the Domain Expansion Realm far longer than you have!\"","BOOM!","Her flurry of attacks swiped away all the three hammers, being thrown away a great distance as Athena's curvaceous body weaved through the glistening edges of the blades of liberation and neared Noah, her two hammers landing on the huge tower shield that he raised up.","DONG!","Golden light erupted out as Noah was pushed back, yet fully protected as not a single bit of damage got through to him. He raised his tower shield as he glanced at the huffing War Princes and spoke with a smile.","\"If I can handle your attacks this easily Senior Sister, I think I'll be just fine.\"","\"Oh? Let's really put that to the test!\"","A provocative light bloomed in Athena's eyes as he pointed her hammers forward and called out- [Judgment]!","OOONG!","Numerous large spears formed around Noah, his figure at the very center becoming serious as the tower shield in his left hand was raised, his golden flail in his right hand already moving to deflect a dangerous golden spear that already rushed from his right side.","DONG!","His body shimmered with a brilliant l.u.s.ter as he moved his body to dodge the onslaught of a powerful skill, his shield blocking many of them as they sent shockwaves through his body, his flail directed towards any others as he rapidly knocked them away and dodged.","In the middle of all this, Athena appeared in the skies as she pointed down, a huge Blade of Liberation descending under her command as it went on to 'overwhelm' the surrounded Noah and smash him towards the ground!","BOOM!","His body acted like a shell as it made a dent into the floor, the Senior Sister finally reigning some light in her eyes as she looked down with concern, only to find her junior brother protected like a turtle behind his golden tower shield, his head peeking out with a smile.","\"Hmph, and that was me going easy on you. The Special Existences we are up against are on an entire league entirely, with some of them even being proficient in multiple Supreme Laws.\"","She went down towards her junior brother as she helped him up, pushing his roughed up hair away to the side as she looked directly at his eyes in a teaching manner.","\"You may be able to block my attacks, but your enemies will have been in the Domain Expansion Realm Longer than you and have more experience, with the most obvious choice for them being to just attack you until you run out of energy, all of these defensive skills you have around you being rendered useless.\"","Noah's eyes locked against this War Princess as he nodded with a smile, his face moving forward to quickly sneak in a kiss as a surprised Senior Sister sprang backwards with an admonishing expression on her face.","\"Stay focused!\"","Athena said this as she looked around the training room and spread out her senses to see if there was anyone watching, her slightly angered gaze landing back on Noah who was wiping the dust off his body while speaking with a calm expression like nothing ever happened.","\"What if I meet you in one of the matches, my dear Senior Sister?\"","The question caused a serious expression to appear on Athena's face, her gaze locking with Noah as she replied with conviction.","\"I would go all out. The treasures given to the winner of these upcoming battles are enough to create a powerhouse- meaning whoever takes the title will most likely be the first one to enter the World Realm!\"","Yes! The treasures that the Celestials had collected were many over the years, especially the really unique ones that were so potent in their unique essence that they allowed beings to quickly break through a rank!","Just the [Luminescent Rainbow Dew] mentioned by the Grandmaster was enough to send any knowledgeable Celestials crazy.","\"I still seek to understand exactly what my fate is in this chaotic universe, I will stop at nothing to achieve that goal. That does not change, even if it is you that is standing against me, Junior Brother.\"","The gaze of the War Princess was filled with conviction as she finished, Noah looking at this with a hidden smile as he nodded, an imperceptible red light crossing through his eyes that reflected on Athena's eyes as well!","\"Very well. Let's continue the spar, Senior Sister. I won't be going easy on you this time.\"","\"Hmph, come!\"","RUMBLE!","..."]},{"number":448,"title":"Chapter 448: Chapter 447 - Domineering!","paragraphs":["In the Spiritual World, a few hours had passed as Noah's Ancient Blood Clone sat in the center point of an elemental storm with bubbling fire and water elements continuing to rush towards him.","He finally felt a sense of stabilization from the two opposing energies as they ravaged his body and healed it soon after, his heart knowing he could now handle it with ease and continue to bear the pain for as long as he wanted.","But at this critical juncture, his face hardened as he prepared to do something wild- something that nobody would even come close to thinking or comprehending when it came to cultivation.","His eyes shone with a golden l.u.s.ter as while he already had activated the two cultivation techniques for the Law of Water and the Law of Fire, he domineeringly opened his mouth and activated another two cultivation techniques, and this time they were for two Supreme Laws!","{Disciple of Chaos}! {Fate's Disciple}!","RUMBLE!","Yes! In his thoughts as he began cultivating the Law of Water and Fire he had asked himself- As he began that cultivation session, what stopped him from simply activated the techniques for the Law of Fate and Chaos at the same time?","For others, it wouldn't even cross their minds to cultivate the opposing techniques of two different laws, much less four of them at the same time.","But for him, he actually found himself questioning what exactly stopped him from doing it?","The answer was- Nothing!","He had the mana! He had the skills! He had everything! All that was left was for him to actually do it, and so he did.","RUMBLE!","The storm of essence around him raged even more as the golden color appeared in the skies, the formation of small Chaos Particles beginning to form soon after as the golden Fate Lines lashed towards them quickly for the sake of purification. The Fate Lines then descended towards the clone and established themselves tightly, no issues occurring as Noah did something outrageous!","Since his mana permitted it, he was actually cultivating not just two, but four Laws at the same time! The appearance of the golden aura of fate and occasional Chaos Particles calmed the raging water and fire elemental particles as the pain they gave towards Noah lessened, the calmness causing a smoother absorption as an insane cultivation session went underway.","A few hours passed.","A day passed. Two days! Three Days!","A few days passed, and Noah continued to keep the four unique skills active at the same time as he made insane progress in the Laws of Fire, Water, Fate, and Chaos. He alternated between the two Supreme Laws that required one to increase while the other stalled, having a similar rate of progression for both of them.","It had been such a long and grueling process, but as the elemental storm and overpowering auras of fate and chaos raged on, he had finally seen the percentage of the Laws of Water and Fire shoot past 31%, the Stage for them also entering 3! At the same time, he was able to amass more than 80,000 Fate Lines and the same number of Chaos Particles, shooting the progress of the two Supreme Laws even higher.","RUMBLE!","An influx of essence rushed in as Noah breathed out slowly, watching calmness gradually settle in as he began stopping the supply of mana to activate the {Fate's Disciple}, {Disciple of Chaos}, {Disciple of Fire} and the {Disciple of Water} unique skills. The last influx of essence caused the Fire and Water Origin Cores to shine bright red and blue respectively before they settled down, a sense of immense power emanating from them. The Fate Lines flowing within his body thrummed with strength as the Chaos Field that contained numerous Chaos Particles rolled around him with strength","He glanced at the updated stat panel as he marveled at the rapid speed he continued to show.","[Noah Osmont][Title(s): Infernal Lord(Variant)]","[Bloodline(s): Vampyre Progenitor(Awakening)]","[Fate Line(s) : 256,243]","[Chaos Particle(s) : 224,276]","[Origin Core(s) : Fire-3, Water-3]","[Domain(s) : Fate, Chaos, Water, Fire, Space]","[Vitality: DOMAIN]","[Focus: - ]","[Strength: DOMAIN]","[Law(s) : Fate-2.5%, Chaos-2.2%, Water-31, Fire-31%, Space-8%]","Noah's clone and main body also felt a vibrant energy continuously course around to every part of muscle and bone, the unique energy that was released from the Fire Origin Cores going on to wash over every single cell in his body as he felt like his muscles were packed with an astounding explosive force and his bones were hardened to insane degrees!","For the Law of Water and Fire, they seemed to heavily influence his body's strength and defense as they enhanced it to levels he never thought possible, with the other boost they provided being the percentage attached to the Absolute Abilities contained in the <<Herald of Fire>> and <<Herald of Water>>.","They were determined by the Stage that the Fire and Water Origin Cores were at, and the current boost had moved to 300% for all of the abilities.","The thrumming Fate Lines and vigorous Chaos Particles swimming in his Chaos Field made him feel even more powerful, his heart feeling a sense of profound accomplishment for such a fast rate of progress!","Noah calmed his aching body that felt in top shape, the pain he continued to feel while dual cultivating the two laws completely forgotten as he got up to test his strength.","BOOM!","The instant he tapped his feet on the ground that was the junction of the Water and Fire Law Space, his figure shot to the skies as he broke the sound barrier, reaching supersonic flight instantly as his speed was enhanced to insane degrees from his body being constantly strengthened with the unique energy his two Stage 3 cores provided!","He came to a halt in midair as he smiled, feeling the explosive force in his fists as he calmed his energy down and disappeared from the skies of the Northern Continent of the Spiritual World."]},{"number":449,"title":"Chapter 449: Chapter 448 - Supreme Treasure","paragraphs":["Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone teleported deep in the Central Continent of the Spiritual World where the Blacksmith’s Forge lay. He had spent a significant amount of time cultivating the four laws that he currently had the cultivation techniques of, and planned to get to the task on how to best use the [Unique Material- Aquamarine Mesrandite] that he obtained from the southern region of the Celestial Realm.","It was a treasure that could either be used to forge a new supreme treasure, or be used to [Refine] an already existing one.","His current mindset was leading him towards creating another one, as he had very few to begin with, and using the material to refine his only existing one would only give a boost, himself having no knowledge of exactly how big this boost would be.","He was thinking of using the Unique Material to create a Supreme Treasure in the form of an armor since he already had one in the form of a weapon. One weapon, one armor, two Supreme Treasures!","His gaze was clear as he went towards the [Hearth] of the Blacksmith’s Forge and communicated with the Spiritual World System.","\"Is the process of forging a Supreme Treasure any different from the Item Sets we’ve been creating?\"","[Yes. It will take a significant amount of time to create one depending on the unique material and expected treasure.]","Noah gave a light nod as he waved his hands and pushed the [Unique Material- Aquamarine Mesrandite] towards the hearth, a blue light shining as the large crystal material that was double Noah’s own size was scanned thoroughly.","[This unique material is fully capable of creating a complete Supreme Treasure, with a possibility of a few scraps being left to perform a refinement in the future. Do you have any specific requests for the design of the treasure? The [Recipe Design] feature can be used in this instance.]","The Spiritual World System that understood everything happening on it asked in a monotone fashion, Noah smiling as he knew this entity which was connected to many planets through his own connection with it as its master had access to enormous vaults of information.","He had access to this information as well, but his mind was nowhere near as close to what the Planetary Systems could contain and process, thus he left a majority of the minute small details on all the planets he came across and their abundance of information to the Planetary Systems. When it came to items, he had some ideas on what he could design himself based on his imagination and his own experiences, but he knew that the Spiritual World Planetary System could come up with something multiple times better than him just because of its special identity!","\"Use the information of all the suits of armor we’ve come across recently from the different worlds and organizations. Design something that is a combination of all of their strengths to create a Supreme Armor.\"","Thus, he left the design of the powerful treasure to the entity with enormous reserves of information to make something at the peak of quality and usability.","[Understood, Master. Any specific name for this Recipe Design?]","Noah thought closely at this question before he replied, a smile spreading across his devilishly handsome face as he glanced at the water elements dancing around the [Unique Material- Aquamarine Mesrandite].","\"Staying with the theme of water, let’s call this Supreme Treasure...-[Hydromancer’s Mantle].\"","[Understood, Master. It should take approximately 72 hours.]","RUMBLE!","Essence began to converge around the Blacksmith’s Forge as the huge [Unique Material- Aquamarine Mesrandite] was taken further into the Hearth, a blue flame beginning to wrap around it as it shimmered strongly under the heat.","While the material was being broken down, the Spiritual World System was compiling large reserves of information on all the armors that the numerous worlds Noah was connected to held, a database of information that even the strongest information groups would envy freely flowing into it from the connection it shared with Noah.","At this moment, a resplendent armor that very few would know the name of but closely remember its unique design was being created. The [Hydromancer’s Mantle] would have its design started today, with its creation being completed some days later!","With this process underway, Noah’s clone continued forward as there were simply too many things that fell on its hands. He was currently at the Domain Realm, but his skill trees were at the Soul Forging Realm. On top of increasing the percentage of laws, he had to increase the proficiency of his skills while preparing for a busy future.","His main body had been using the abilities of {Herald of Fate} and {Agent of Chaos} to foresee many things with more clarity these past few days, grasping a few abstruse pieces of information that dealt with the Infernal Lords. His title as the 9th Infernal Lord would not all be for naught, and he foresaw that he would be called upon sometime soon in the future for him to begin carrying out his duties!","The clone continued forward as the main body was moving side by side with Athena and the members of the Righteous Fire Exploration Team. Boru was still as boisterous as ever- he talked towards the two beings holding titles of Noble Fates with more respect as they were now an entire realm above him.","\"You two have gathered the information on your possible opponents and rewards?\"","The gaze of Boru was shining as he mentioned the rewards, just the rumors released on exactly what was at stake in the upcoming tournament making the hearts of powerful Celestials quiver!","Noah smiled as he replied to Boru with shining eyes.","\"One of the biggest rewards in the Luminescent Rainbow Dew, something that was found in limited quantities by the Founders more than a thousand years ago, a treasure that guarantees a being an advancement to the World Realm!\"","Yes! Just one of the rewards up for grabs for battling Special Existences and beings with Noble Fates was something that would create an expert capable of affecting the direction of the future war. Experts at the World Realm were rare, where even the lowest leveled Infernal Lords stood at the peak of this level! Treasures that allowed for one to enter such a realm...were nearly nonexistent in the hands of others. In this coming tournament, just what other treasures lay in store? Just who would stand against them vying for these same treasures?!"]},{"number":450,"title":"Chapter 450: Chapter 449 - No Chance of Winning!","paragraphs":["The Sanctum was bustling with activities as word spread of the magnificent battles to take place soon.","Those in the ranks of Celestials were looking forward to seeing the geniuses at the forefront of their organization while those from the numerous Prime Worlds in the Light Expanse looked forward to the show of power from the overlords that stood over their Light Expanse.","Among these many forces, there were also the hidden figures from the Dark Expanse that wanted to use this opportunity to learn more about their enemies!","It was an opportunity to assess the supposed geniuses that would be taking charge in the upcoming battle, this tournament actually being something that could reward them the most in this venture in the Celestial Realm as it provided a rare commodity about the Celestials- Information!","Many beings moved with their own motivations, but it was ultimately to watch the stupendous battles that would soon be occurring.","Amidst the bustle of activities, Noah was moving with the Righteous Fire Exploration Team where the boisterous Boru continued to talk about the beings they would be facing.","\"The toughest Celestial Grandmasters you will have to watch out for are Grandmaster Light and the Three-Eyed Fate Child, the Special Existences that run their own Elite Teams and have been moving in the regions where Fate Behemoths are abundant.\"","His eyes were serious as he said this, their steps taking them towards the specified location in the Celestial Realm when one could find the less aggressive Earth Behemoths roving around. The path they followed made them seem like ants as they stood within droves of beings that went towards the same direction, Celestials and normal beings from the Prime World alike.","\"I say this because unlike the other beings similar to you and hold the title of those with Noble Fates, these Special Existences are beings that are cultivating not just the Supreme Law of Fate, but also another Supreme Law!\"","The gaze of Boru shone with splendor as his burly body thrummed with power, just mentioning these powerful Celestials making one feel the adoration and wariness he had at their power.","\"So while you are proficient in the Law of Fate as they are, they also have another Supreme Law aiding their power. Grandmaster Light is someone that cultivates the Supreme Law of Light, a being that very few can even damage, while the Three-Eyed Fate Child is very proficient in the Supreme Law of Time-Space, a very abstruse law that combines the Law of Time and the Law of Space. Those that spar with him do not even understand why they are defeated, they just find out that they are. So-\"","\"Junior Brother Boru, why are you only bragging about Senior Sister Light and Senior Brother Three-Eyed? Are the rest of us not worthy?\"","From the front, a strong and confident voice spoke towards their group as a man surrounded by a group of golden robed Celestials caused the crowds of beings to spread out, his gaze locking on the figures of Noah and Athena while he sent a question towards Boru.","The burly Boru smiled wryly as he called out to the being that had interrupted his speech.","\"Senior Brother Xander, I haven’t seen you in over a year. You’re as confident as ever.\"","The Celestial Grandmaster called Xander looked forward with squinting eyes and a wide smile as he came in front of their group, his eyes filled with shining lights locking with Athena and Noah.","\"So, am I not an opponent our new Junior Brother and Sister holding the titles for Nobe Fates should be looking out for? I do hold the same title if I recall.\"","Grandmaster Xander did not relent, continuing his question as Noah glanced at this being he had already collected information about.","Grandmaster Xander- Dark-haired, gold eyes, age 233, roughly 264,927 Fate Lines, and a being holding the title of one with a Noble Fate!","\"My oh my, are you bullying the younger disciples again?\"","Another voice came out from the distance as another figure appeared, the situation turning into one where multiple people just invited themselves into the conversation as the two beings at the center of it were Noah and Athena!","Xander turned towards the new figure as he glanced at her with a smile, his eyes shining with carefulness.","\"Senior Sister Lila, I hope you’ve trained enough for these upcoming battles, or it won’t be just the younger disciples I would be bullying.\"","A provocative sentence was released from Xander towards the newly appearing being that was also someone that held the title of a being with a Noble Fate!","This time it was the Celestial known as Lila- Blue hair, dark eyes, age 229 and around 250,000 Fate Lines, a woman with deadly proficiency in close combat.","\"I like that you’re still so confident, Xander! Now let’s take a look at the Junior Brother and Sister who will be fighting for the treasures with us this time around. Crixus and Athena, is it?\"","Yet another combatant in the upcoming tournament came to introduce themselves to them as the woman whose body vibrated with power came close, her gaze when looking towards Noah and Athena being one of an a.d.u.l.t looking at upcoming young ones!","Athena nodded as she replied.","\"Nice to meet Senior Brother Xander and Senior Sister Lila. We look forward to learning many things in these upcoming matches.\"","Her words were those without disrespect, but also expressing that they would be giving it their all in the coming battles. Lila smiled sweetly as she patted Athena on the head, the collection of 4 beings holding Noble Fates coming together all at once occurring in the Sanctum of the Celestial Realm!","\"So cute. Use this opportunity to increase your battle prowess and learn from your seniors. You’ll have many more opportunities in the future.\"","Grandmaster Lila said this as she patted Athena’s head, seeming like a caring Senior Sister taking care of her junior.","Her demeanor and the demeanor of Xander made one thing abundantly clear- in the upcoming battles, Noah and Athena were not even considered serious combatants, their few years cultivating and recent breakthroughs in realms not even landing in the eyes of these powerful experts that had been moving for more than 200 years!","As far as what was known, Athena had just broken past the 100,000 Barrier of fate lines recently, with the other junior brother Crixus still not even passing that yet.","These other beings with Noble Fates, barring the even more powerful Special Existences they had not met- none of them believed that Athena and Noah even had a shot of winning the bountiful rewards!"]},{"number":451,"title":"Chapter 451: Chapter 450 - [Luminescent Rainbow Dew]","paragraphs":["A hidden smile appeared on Noah’s face as he followed the collection of Celestials to the East of the Sanctum where the docile Earth Behemoths were abundant. The Senior Brother Xander and Senior Sister Lila that were also beings holding the titles of those with Noble Fates were having their own conversation in front of them, the party that Noah was with following closely behind.","\"What do you think our odds are against Grandmaster Light and Senior Brother Three-Eyed?\"","Lila asked the confident Xander with a smile as they made their way towards the predetermined location, an impassive look appearing on Xander’s face as he replied.","\"They both are proficient in two Supreme Laws, but I don’t see us going down so easily! They have to spread their focus to two laws while we focus on one, this is where our edge lies...\"","The Righteous Fire Exploration Team continued following behind them as they listened to their conversation, awkward looks appearing on the faces of Boru and the others as they saw the moment the Senior Brother Xander and Senior Sister Lila introduced themselves to Crixus and Athena, they completed disregarded them as actual combatants in the upcoming fights.","Noah glanced towards Athena, the War Princess having eyes shining with lights that longed for battle as he chuckled. Athena saw his gaze as her eyes turned sharp and she sent him a telepathic message.","\"Don’t falter and try your best in the battles ahead. And I better not see you trying anything funny around everyone.\"","Her eyes held a dangerous glint as they focused on Noah, his head bobbing up and down as he nodded and replied teasingly.","\"Nothing around everyone, but when we’re alone?\"","\"Hmph.\"","The War Princess turned her head away as the procession of Celestials continued forward, their party coming in contact with two other powerful beings holding Noble Fates as they made their way towards a specified location for the upcoming Tournament!","Among the many beings rushing force, a particularly arrogant Emperor Penguin was moving with the curvaceous Elena, Barbatos, and other Harbingers that were moving in the Celestial Realm.","Barbatos had a bored expression as they went forward, the curvaceous Elena giving glances to this woman that was around her Progenitor more than many others as they all made their way forward. There were many beings moving, each with their own goals and emotions, but the central figures always remained the same.","Hidden within the masses of beings were also the forces from the Dark Expanse, where Malthus, the Spatial Magician, was leading a group of beings for the mission of collecting more information on the powerful beings within the ranks of Celestials.","Each with their own ideals and goals, but they all went towards a single location!","Far away from the Sanctum, the place where everyone was congregating at was a wide expanse of land that had very few of the huge ancient trees that towered grandly. It was a field of a few miles of clearing that was surrounded by trees in a circular fashion, giving an extremely clear look at everything that would be happening within it.","It was a field of resplendent greenery that was surrounded by even more mystically glowing trees, always making one feel the wonder and magic of the Celestial Realm.","Around the perimeters of the huge circle, numerous figures were already present and spread out. Some were standing on the ground, others had climbed the large trees as they perched on them like thousands of ants, each of the huge ancient trees holding thousands of beings on their branches and leaves as they all prepared to watch the spectacle.","Near the clear green field that would act as the arena, one could see multiple Prime Warsh.i.p.s stationed above in the skies. Many Celestials present here as they also watched on with great interest.","The cl.u.s.ter of beings and bustle of activities only increased as time went on, the recognizable figures of those participating in the tournament arriving as many carried out their own discussions.","The ones more knowledgeable and having discussions worthy of note were the throngs of Celestials on the Warsh.i.p.s or those on the ground, their eyes correctly locating the combatants today as many proposed their own theories while seeing them roll in.","SHAA!","A blinding flash of light erupted out at a certain location as a being appeared magnificently, the bustle of discussions moving towards her appearance.","\"Grandmaster Light has finally arrived. My goodness, I can’t even see through her Fate Lines with how blinding her achievements in the Supreme Law of Light are.\"","\"If you’re looking for someone striking, look over there where Senior Brother Thee-Eyed is. His third eye locks you in and makes you feel like you can never look away.\"","The Celestials that the discussions moved to were the beings that were called Special Existences, their sheer appearance pulling the attention of all beings there as even the forces of the Dark Expanse had dark looks!","\"The upcoming Junior Brother Crixus and Junior Sister Athena are also here. They should have some chance to show themselves a little right?\"","\"Against Special Existences like that and 10s of Grandmasters that have been in the Domain Expansion Realm for years? I wouldn’t be so sure!\"","The cacophony of noises and discussions reached their peak as many of the participating Celestials arrived.","OOOONG!","At this moment, a blinding light appeared in the skies above the very center of the clear field where the battles would be taking place, a figure of an oppressively powerful being appearing.","He was adorned in a golden robe, his face aged and wise with an excellent long beard and white hair trickling down to his shoulders.","THRUM!","His body rumbled with power as he purposefully and wildly released the lines of fate kept tightly in his body, the Celestials present being able to count more than 3 million Fate Lines strongly rolling around this being’s body!","\"I am Grandmaster Onillus, and I have left my post deep in the Celestial Realm to oversee this little tournament here today.\"","His voice was resounding and strong, being able to be heard by every single being around the 10 miles area as he stroked his beard profoundly.","\"It is being made a show of for a reason that will soon become apparent, with one of the biggest things being...this.\"","The powerful Grandmaster Onillus holding more than 3 million lines of fate waved his hands, a single multicolored water-drop shaped object appearing in the skies!","\"One of the prizes for today’s winners, and something that I want many of you here today to remember.\"","It was only 10 inches in size, but it released a blinding rainbow colored light that reflected on the eyes of every single being watching. Noah himself glanced to the skies as the identity of the item became visible to him!","<strong>[Luminescent Rainbow Dew] :: A consumable treasure found in the deeper locations of the Celestial Realm. Can be used to propel the rank of a being all the way to the World Rank, with the condition that their bodies can withstand the energy released by this treasure. Its rarity does not need to be stressed.</strong>"]},{"number":452,"title":"Chapter 452: Chapter 451 - The Battle of Geniuses!","paragraphs":["<strong>[Luminescent Rainbow Dew] :: A consumable treasure found in the deeper locations of the Celestial Realm. Can be used to propel the rank of a being all the way to the World Rank, with the condition that their bodies can withstand the energy released by this treasure. Its rarity does not need to be stressed.</strong>","Noah’s eyes squinted at the description only apparent to his eyes as a hungry light erupted from him. The others only looked at this scintillating rainbow colored dew with fascination as the wizened Grandmaster Onillus continued speaking.","\"Some of the geniuses that you may or may not know will be fighting in randomly selected battles in order to get their hands on this, a treasure that is capable of bringing a being fully into the World Realm.\"","...!","\"What?!\"","\"This...\"","\"Holy!\"","RUMBLE!","A buzz of essence and sounds rumbled out as a luminous treasure was given the identity of as if it was nothing. The Celestials only had shining eyes as they glanced at the treasure, while those from the Light Expanse looked at it with envious and longing eyes.","Those from the Dark Expanse had ashen faces as they saw a treasure that would most likely produce a World Realm expert to stand against them in the future, and they most likely had no way to prevent it as just the overseeing Grandmaster seemed to be in the World Realm himself!","World Realm experts were extremely rare, only those at the peak of powers being the ones to enjoy this mystical realm. Yet in this tournament they would watch, a Celestial would be given a treasure that would simply create a World Realm expert.","While their thoughts were troubled for the future, it made their desire for the Celestial Realm where this treasure was found to grow ever so higher!","Malthus the Spatial Magician was using his unique magic item to portray all that was happening here back to his forces in the Scholar’s Guild. So it was not just the beings here that were witnesses to what was about to occur, but the leaders of the powerful forces of the Dark Expanse as well.","\"This Luminescent Rainbow Dew is the top treasure that the number one genius will be receiving, with the others getting varying levels of treasures that are in no way near this one in efficacy. As for the geniuses themselves, step into the field!\"","The voice of Grandmaster Onillus reverberated out as figures of multiple beings stepped forward, the figures of Athena and Noah being among them as they grandly entered into the eyes of many.","From the circular ring of tens of thousands of beings surrounding the clear field, 32 beings stepped out. Shockingly, each of these beings were releasing waves of energy at the Domain Expansion Realm, with very few being in the lower Soul Forging Realm.","\"These geniuses you see before you are the future defenders of the Light Expanse, but they have to prove their capabilities and show who shines the most among them.\"","Grandmaster Onillus waved his hands as 32 streaks of light shot out from him towards the geniuses that stepped forward. Noah grabbed the object shooting towards him as he found it to be a crystalline ball that pulsed with a hint of essence.","\"The way to prove their capabilities is through combat, as we only care about which one has the most potential for us to foster! The White Crystals you have all received will act as your number. The moment it lights up, you will step forward and battle another genius who also had the White Crystal light up. The winner will advance forward, while the loser will step out!\"","Clear guidelines for the matches to follow were laid out as many listened with shining eyes. There were 32 beings competing, so there would be 5 rounds to determine the ultimate winner. In the first round, only 16 winners will continue on. The second round will have only 8 continue forward, with the 3rd round having 4 continue, the fourth round having 2 continue, and these last two would fight in the final 5th round for the title of the Strongest Genius!","\"Understood? Now step back once more so we can soon begin.\"","Grandmaster Onillus waved his hands impatiently in the air as the 32 geniuses pulled back slightly, many of them being powerful enough to hold the title of a Grandmaster, but they listened dutifully to the powerful World Rank Onillus.","Noah was looking at the White Crystal on his hands, his senses spread out in the surroundings to observe the beings he would be facing as he noted the names he had come across already.","The two Special Existences known as the Three-Eyed Fate Child and Grandmaster Light. The two with Noble Fates known as Grandmaster Xander and Grandmaster Lila.","There were a few others with genius Celestials, some with unique bodily compositions, and others who simply had monstrous comprehension abilities that allowed them to quickly master the techniques of fate and advance forward.","He was thinking of how he would act to take down those that stand against him when he heard the telepathic message of a particular Grandmaster in his mind.","\"You two are faced with powerful opponents that have been cultivating even longer than you. Still, try your best to pass through the rounds and get a good position. Even if the Luminescent Rainbow Dew is out of reach, a high ranking will allow for even more resources to go to you!\"","The strong voice filled with the care of Grandmaster Vredral rang in Noah and Athena’s ears as the two of them looked at each other, their gazes filled with confidence in their own abilities, even if others did not fully believe in them!","In one of the Prime Warsh.i.p.s, Grandmaster Vredral was watching with a group of Grandmasters that had teaching roles of bringing up talented Celestials. The Commanding Officer Raizel who had a post overseeing a portion of the Sanctum that Noah and Athena had met when they first came to the Celestial Realm was to his right, his head shaking as he glanced at the two that he had seen first not too long ago.","\"When you brought them into the Celestial Realm, weren’t they still at the Void Realm? You’re really having them face other disciples at the Domain Expansion Realm after pushing their levels up so speedily?\"","Commanding Officer Raizel asked his friend as he was in deep thought, a shining light passing through Grandmaster Vredral as he replied.","\"Even though I cannot see the fates of those holding the title of Noble Fate, I have a feeling that these two will bring a great surprise to us in the future. I will stake my entire reputation on it!\"","The words of the Grandmaster were filled with belief as they prepared to watch the matches that would soon begin."]},{"number":453,"title":"Chapter 453: Chapter 452 - First Match: Athena!","paragraphs":["The World Rank Grandmaster Onillus looked at the masses of beings, Celestials and non-Celestials alike, as he waved his hands while domineeringly floating in the skies.","\"Then we shall get started. The first match will be...\"","RUMBLE!","Two lights released from him as they circled above his hands randomly, thereafter shooting out as they went to light up the White Crystals of two beings!","\"...Athena and Lila!\"","WAH!","Murmurs spread among the Celestials as above in the Prime Warship where Grandmaster Vredral stood, an ashen look had appeared on his face when he heard the first match to be between his disciples and one of the more powerful beings with Noble Fates.","In the first match, Athena was actually placed against one of the four beings they were told to watch out for the most, the same Grandmaster Lila that had patted Athena on the head like a younger sister!","\"Sigh...\"","\"Haha, Vredral, it looks like our disciples are the first ones up!\"","Commanding Officer Raizel let out a pitiful breath as another voice perked up thereafter, a wide looking Grandmaster that could be considered to be a fatty entering the Prime Warship that Vredral and Raizel were in.","This was Grandmaster Rock, the one who had brought in Lila as a student, the powerful genius at the Domain Expansion Realm being his disciple!","Vredral turned to look at Grandmaster Rock with a calm expression as he observed the vibrant power of this being at the peak of the Domain Expansion Realm, the Fate Lines this Celestial Grandmaster held being even more numerous than Vredral himself.","\"I didn’t think you’d be joining us, Rock.\"","\"How can I miss my two disciples showing off their strength after all this time? Both Lila and Xander have been training hard in the dangerous areas these past years, they deserve the treasures coming out of this little tournament.\"","The fatty Grandmaster Rock sat next to Grandmaster Vredral and Commanding Officer Raizel jovially, revealing that he would similarly be watching the results of two beings holding Noble Fates that he guided, similarly to Vredral!","\"But your disciple is truly unlucky to be matched with Lila as the first match. Her potential would have at least placed her in the Top 8 if this hadn’t happened.\"","Rock spoke out again with a smile as the Grandmaster watched the figures of Athena and Lila step forward in the center of the field of battle. Grandmaster Vredral was quiet before he replied calmly, his gaze being as clear as water.","\"It matters not, as it is simply what fate had ordained. Let us see exactly what the results would be.\"","A calm reply unlike what Grandmaster Rock expected came out, the Grandmasters turning their senses down as the two curvaceous women in the center of the field were about to start!","---","When the match was first called, the White Crystal in Athena’s hands had lit up, making Noah turn towards her as her opponent was someone that did not hold the two of them in any regard in their past interaction.","An impassive look appeared on Athena’s face as she stepped out silently, Grandmaster Lila following thereafter with a smile as the two of them wordlessly went towards the center of the miles-long field.","\"Junior Sister, I’m sorry to cut your ranking off so quickly. I really didn’t expect for both me and you to be picked first.\"","Grandmaster Lila had an apologetic expression as she looked with smiling eyes towards Athena, who had already begun summoning Empyrean Guards and casting Empyrean Armament to prepare herself.","In a stellar fashion, a golden armored and winged Athena holding two huge hammers appeared in the clear field, her languid eyes locking on the smiling figure of Grandmaster Lila as she replied impassively.","\"The victor is yet to be decided, Senior Sister. Let us see what fate has in store!\"","Noah stared at the two women facing off as he smiled, the outcome of this battle having been long decided the moment that the two of them were picked to stand against one another.","On one side was the War Princess at the Domain Expansion Realm, and her enemy was someone who had been in this same realm over many years, and even had more than double the Fate Lines that she held. So many beings were seeing a clear dominant winner, but would that be so?!","OOOOOOH!","His eyes shone as the watching crowd made vibrant noises at the stellar figures of these two women facing off, the clear and resounding voice of the floating Grandmaster Onillus reaching them thereafter as a spark was lit.","\"Start!\"","BOOM!","\"YAA!\"","With a glorious cry, Athena shot off the ground like a cannon as she rushed towards Grandmaster Lila who was still smiling sweetly, her body glimmering with Fate Lines as numerous Empyrean Guards were cast and absorbed by her instantaneously.","A resplendent set of armor and wings similar to Athena was adorned on her, having a few distinct differences because of their levels of comprehension in the law of fate. The smiling eyes of Grandmaster Lila found Athena’s eyes filled with battle as she grasped the slightly larger hammer in her hands and struck out towards the oncoming attack!","BOOOM!","A golden shockwave spread out as the spectating combatants that would be called upon later watched closely.","The three glimmering eyes of the Special Existence known as Three-Eyed Fate Child rapidly moved as he began following the figures of the two fighting women in the field of battle.","The other Special Existence known as Grandmaster Light was simply watching on impassively as her body that was majorly made of particles of light brightened. The one with Noble Fate, Xander, also watched his Senior Sister under the same master as all of them waited for a singular result from the battle, the winner already decided in their eyes a long time ago.","In the distance, the forces of the Dark Expanse with Malthus the Spatial Magician at the forefront were using a hidden device to portray all the occurring events in real time towards the Scholar’s Guild where many powerful beings were watching!","From many directions and on all sides, many beings had begun watching as the first fight in this Battle of Geniuses began!"]},{"number":454,"title":"Chapter 454: Chapter 453 - Outmatched","paragraphs":["WAAAAA!","Cries of wonder and fervor rang out from the tens of thousands of spectators as a battle with rarely seen abilities unfolded in their eyes.","Many from the Prime Worlds did not get a chance to see the skills of Celestials in action, the masses being given access to watch the coming battles using this opportunity to the fullest as they pledged to see the power they wanted to achieve themselves.","On a nondescript side of the circular field where Athena and Grandmaster Lila were battling, an Emperor Penguin exuding deep arrogance was being carried by Elena as their forces of Vampyres were stationed around an enormous tree not too far from Malthus.","The being sending a live feed of the occurring events to the Dark Expanse was messaging with Elena telepathically over the past few minutes as numerous things were discussed.","\"The one that is working with us, Crixus, how do we see his chances in these battles? The old fogeys have been wanting to use him more ever since they found out he had somehow reached the Domain Expansion Realm this fast, even though his mission to release the prisoner from the 7th Celestial Star has not been accomplished.\"","\"Bah, take things slow and as they come. As for his chances in this battle? Hmph, just watch like all of us.\"","An irritated reply came from the Royal Vampyre as she held the fluffy Emperor Penguin tightly, the Kraken at the side watching with jealous eyes as they kept their gazes towards the continuing battle!","SHAA!","Ever since the battle began, those with keen and observant eyes had begun noticing a shocking fact with the constantly moving figures of Athena and Lila.","When the battle began, Grandmaster Lila who had been in the Domain Expansion Realm much longer than Athena was fending off her attacks with ease, even maintaining the light smile behind her armor as her Fate Lines that were double her opponents gave her even more support.","Yet as time passed, it felt like her support and ease was gradually leaving, things getting so serious that her smile was completely wiped off a minute later when a hammer swept to her left and forcefully lifted her off the ground!","In the Prime Warship, the veteran Grandmasters were watching the battle with shining eyes as they stroked their beards, Vredral’s impassive face gaining a smile as Commanding Officer Raizel spoke.","\"This is...Battle Sense? The battle was in favor of Lila in the first minute, but she soon fell into a particular rhythm that Athena began, almost as if it was a...\"","Grandmaster’s Vredral’s face smiled as his beard shimmered, finishing the words of Commanding Officer Raizel.","\"...dance!\"","Yes! What many people were witnessing was the expert control of battle that only the War Princess had because of a unique ability that only she held, an ability that allowed her to foresee and perceive the strikes of her opponents as she relentlessly used this knowledge to hammer their defenses and evade their attacks in such a way that it looked like she was conducting a dance!","The face of the fatty Grandmaster Rock was dark as he watched his student actually begin to be cornered, the valiant eyes of Athena seemingly shining with light as she relentlessly pursued someone that many knew to be stronger than her. Grandmaster Rock’s flaps of fat could not even turn to the Grandmaster Vredral that he was gloating towards a few minutes ago as he remained quiet!","\"As I said, we must always wait to see exactly what fate has in store for us.\"","Grandmaster Vredral cooly said as his gaze remained on the ongoing battle where Blades of Liberation and sharp spears of Judgment had begun weaving around majestically.","BOOM! BOOM!","Enormous Blades of Liberation thundered down while golden spears filled the skies, the two combatants weaving in and out of them with ease. Athena was evading the ferocious attack within a few inches as she used the least required movements to get closer and closer to her opponent, her hammers being able to reach her as she entered into close combat- something that was her forte.","SHAA!","Grandmaster Lil saw her bending her body backwards as she evaded a golden hammer smashing straight to her face, her body letting out rapid breaths as her eyes angrily glanced towards the Junior Sister that was actually putting her in a tight spot!","But something horrendous occurred in the next instant as the hammer that was swiping from left to right that Lila evaded by bending down had somehow stopped its horizontal trajectory instantaneously right at her position, the tout muscles in Athena’s arms bulging as the golden hammer changed directions to smash down vertically, right on her wide open and full chest.","BOOOM!","\"What!\"","\"Grandmaster Lila!\"","Shocked Celestials that knew Lila called out concerningly as she took the blow straight on, the watching masses glancing at one another as they raucously cheered by the resplendent move.","OOOOH!","Noah was watching by the side with shining eyes as what he expected occured, the terrifying battle skill of the War Princess exceeding the 100,000 Fate Lines difference as Athena’s hammer smashed into the opened defenses of her opponent to deal a deadly strike.","She didn’t get complacent though, as the moment her strike landed, she jumped back from the position of the shockwave as a wrathful Grandmaster Lila erupted out with glowing Fate Essence preparing to unleash a last ditch attack, but all that met her was air as Athena had already moved far away! Her golden hammer was pointed towards Lila silently as her valiant eyes shimmered, Lila feeling an oppressive feeling as her sense of danger rang wildly, her gaze only being able to rise to the skies briefly before she saw a golden Blade of Liberation smashing right at her position.","BOOOM!","...","Silence.","After the first hammer strike that had smashed onto the chest of Grandmaster Lila, Athena had moved back as she summoned a Blade of Liberation right at her position to finish off the battle.","Valiantly!","Ruthlessly!","This was the War Princess, this was Athena!","\"WAAAAA!\"","Cheers rang out as the dust cleared, one being able to see a bloodied Grandmaster Lila with broken pieces of golden armor, a large scar on her shoulder as her wrathful gaze shakingly looked up at Athena. The eyes that met her were calm, as if they weren’t the cause of the horrendous injuries, making this Senior Sister Lila feel even more anger as she stared at the Junior Sister that she was domineeringly patting the head of just an hour ago.","\"Winner, Athena!\"","The impassive voice of Grandmaster Onillus floating in the skies rang out, Athena’s armament fading away into particles of light as she calmly made her way back towards where the other combatants were, coming to stand right beside the Junior Brother Crixus as she leaned on his shoulder for balance.","Very few could notice her hard breathing as Noah smiled, the first battle of the Battle of Geniuses concluding gorgeously as soon after, Grandmaster Onillus called the next fighters!"]},{"number":455,"title":"Chapter 455: Chapter 454 - Those Watching","paragraphs":["\"Reiner and Zula, you’re next!\"","The World Rank Grandmaster Onillus randomly picked the next two combatants as two Celestials brimming with power stepped out.","Both were at the Domain Expansion Realm, with their Fate Lines fairly close to one another.","But each of them was a genius in their own way, with one being proficient in the law of water on top of the law of fate, and the other being proficient in the law of air. Mastery of two laws paired up with extremely deadly techniques allowed them to be called geniuses, many of the other beings in the group of 32 participating Celestials being this way!","There were very few like Noah, Athena, Lila, and Xander that held the titles of those with Noble Fates, with the Special Existences like the Three-Eyed Fate Child and Grandmaster Light being even rarer.","The match between the genius celestial Reiner and Zula was much longer than the first one, with the two Celestials being very close in power. They put up a delightful fight that was nothing like the first one, but their mastery of two different laws caused many beings to turn their eyes as the winner was decided to be Reiner!","\"Elias and...Crixus, you’re next!\"","As soon as the battle finished and the field cleared, Grandmaster Onillus called for the next match, his words causing Noah’s White Crystal to light up as he stepped forward calmly.","His entrance towards the center of the field of battle caught the attention of not just the Grandmasters that were with Vredral in one of the Prime Warsh.i.p.s, but even more so the forces of the Dark Expanse that were watching.","As they heard the name, Elena and the others had their eyes shining with strong emotions, the being they all followed stepping up grandly to face a celestial that was considered a genius.","Malthus the Spatial Magician was near Elena as he had a dark pearl on his chest that acted as a button to close his robe, this dark pearl being one that sent back a feed of all the events occurring in front of their eyes to the Scholar’s Guild in the Dark Expanse.","Although Malthus was sent this item a few hours after he informed his superiors that the Celestials were putting up a tournament with their most promising geniuses and grandly showing it to the public with no worries, even he did not know exactly what beings were watching on the other side.","Were he to know, he would be shocked to the point of choosing to change his demeanor as he held the dark crystal and attached it to his robe! This was because in an expansive ovular hall at the center of the Dark Expanse where the Scholar’s Guild was located, powerful auras that would shake beings to their cores were watching.","There were a decent amount in this ovular room that was located in a famous Mage Tower of the Scholar’s Guild, but the ones of more importance and worthy of note were few.","One was the current Guild Leader of the Scholar’s Guild, the one known as the Grand Magician, Edrusim!","Another was the ruler of the Archeon Clan that represented all Vampyres in the Dark Expanse, Vladivostok!","Last and not least, a more shocking figure that very few would be expecting to be casually sitting with others...was actually an Infernal Lord.","To be exact, it was the 2nd ranked Infernal Lord, Voldred!","He was lazily glancing at Edrusim as he spoke out.","\"Did you really call me here to watch the battles of Domain Expansion Realm beings, Young Edrusim? So what if one of them is a future World Realm expert, even the weakest Infernal Lord can match ten World Realm experts with ease.\"","The Grand Magician Edrusim looked at the Infernal Lord as he replied coldly.","\"It’s a good chance to learn more about the enemies we will face, and it’s better than beating you at chess again.\"","\"Hmph.\"","A grunt was all that met Edrusim as he turned to the leader of Vampyres of the Dark Expanse, Vladivostok.","\"How much control does your Clan have over this Crixus? He has yet to use the vial you procured from me.\"","On the face of Vladivostok, a wide smile that showed the huge canines spread as he replied calmly.","\"You know that Vampyres all follow the ranks of bloodlines. I have one of my trusted soldiers, Elena, who has a purer bloodline than most and comes even close to me watching this Crixus. I control Elena, she controls this Crixus. A command from me would be all it took if you really want to hurry the release of that prisoner on the 7th Celestial Star.\"","\"... let’s watch what his skills are exactly first. He has somehow gone from the Void Realm and into the Domain Expansion Realm in a matter of months, so it seems he really does have a talent in the law of fate. We do not want to carelessly throw this piece away if he was able to climb the ranks of Celestials this fast. Imagine if he got an even higher position as the war begins...\"","Edrusim replied to the Vampyre Ruler Vladivostok calmly as they watched the figures of Noah and the other genius Celestial called Elias enter the field of battle, the command to start being given by Grandmaster Onillus!","Over the side, the 2nd Infernal Lord was looking closely at Noah’s face, his expression that of confusion as he seemed to have sensed something he should not be able to sense from looking at the moving image on the screen, this feeling causing him to tilt his head as his lazy eyes tried to discern exactly what he felt.","The other beings in the ovular room of the most powerful Mage’s Tower kept extremely quiet as they felt the oppressive strength of an Infernal Lord, a Vampyre Ruler, and one of the strongest Magicians in the Dark Expanse.","All of them were watching one thing, a battle that was in full swing as the scene of it brought surprising expressions to their eyes!"]},{"number":456,"title":"Chapter 456: Chapter 455 - In a Matter of Seconds!","paragraphs":["From the oval room atop the highest position of the Mage’s Tower in the Dark Expanse, the eyes of Edrusim shone with surprise as he looked at the ongoing battle.","It had begun similarly to the others where the combatants adorned themselves with the energy of fate, one of the surprises being that the adornment that Crixus had was different from everyone else drastically.","A golden robe wrapped around him as one could observe a brilliant circle shield of light protecting him, in his left hand holding a huge tower shield while his right hand held a flail! Three bright hammers rotated around him peacefully as he stood in the skies grandiosely.","This transformation brought surprise to the eyes of many Celestials, and even those watching from the Dark Expanse as they were also familiar of the abilities of Celestials.","Adorned with this armament, Crixus went on to completely dominate the other genius known as Elias, the proficiency of this opponent in the law of fate and his Fate Lines spilling above 150,000 not being able to deal any damage to the heavily protected Crixus, yet the flail that this brilliantly shining being was attacking with let out deadly attacks that slowly broke down his defenses.","When Elias was about to release an all-out attack to try and overpower Crixus with pure Fate Essence, something unexpected happened as the people nearby could barely pick up a whisper of a word!","[Sever].","SHAA!","At the speed of light, rays of destructive purple-blue Aether erupted out from Crixus as they completely wiped away the fate essence released by his opponent, half of the Aether Rays going on to pierce the shoulder of Elias as he felt his energy overturned and move chaotically!","He stared at Crixus in shock as he knew if his enemy had chosen to aim those powerful Aether Rays anywhere other than his shoulder, he would have perished.","His gaze hardened as his armament turned into particles of light, his head bowing towards Crixus as he stepped away from the field of battle.","\"Winner, Crixus!\"","Grandmaster Onillus announced impassively as his eyes shone, looking at the remnants of baleful Aether as he nodded.","The figures watching in the Dark Expanse were also surprised by the appearance of multiple rays of Aether as Edrusim spoke out.","\"Something that you would rarely find even in the Letalis Expanse...why is a being proficient in Aether appearing in the Light Expanse?\"","His gaze was that of pondering as he turned to the Vampyre Ruler that had the same look as him, his gaze thereafter going to the 2nd Ranked Infernal Lord who actually seemed to have a glimpse of understanding before he began laughing boisterously.","\"Haha! Wow, now this is unexpected!\"","Edrusim’s eyes sharpened as he asked the laughing Infernal Lord inquisitively.","\"What did you find?\"","\"You all haven’t come across Aether in its natural form or when it is used by a being unless you traversed the Letalis Expanse, so you might not really be able to tell the difference when looking at it. This Aether that this Crixus released...haha, I have seen a similar type before!\"","A look of enjoyment appeared on the Infernal Lord’s face as he laughed and spoke thoughtfully.","\"Of course, this is only a guess and I could be wrong but...I’m curious to know why a being connected to THAT is playing around with the Celestials.\"","Edrusim’s face became sour as the Infernal Lord did not give any straight answers, asking once more for clarification.","\"What exactly did you find out?\"","\"Hmm? It’s probably nothing, Young Edrusim. Come, let us keep on watching. This might not be a waste of time after all.\"","An inquisitive Genius Magician and a lazy Infernal Lord watched on with more attention to the Battle of Geniuses continuing in the Celestial Realm, another pair of names being called forth as the battles continued!","---","In the perimeters of the circular arena, Noah was standing with Athena as the senior sister continued to speak with him telepathically.","\"Very few beings will be able to counter your Aether strikes, especially now that there’s multiple of them. When did that happen?\"","The gaze of the War Princess was filled with light as she asked, the battle going on in front of them being reflected in their eyes as another two Genius Celestials were fighting resplendently.","\"I don’t only make breakthroughs in the law of fate you know. Aether was the thing that got Grandmaster Vredral to take notice of me, and it’s still the thing that has the most firepower in my arsenal! I’m afraid even you might not be able to handle it, Senior Sister.\"","\"Hmph, you have your talents and I have mine. We will see!\"","The strong-willed voice of the War Princess travelled to his mind as the battle in front of them wrapped up, another winner being declared.","\"Three-Eyed Fate Child and Volador, you’re next!\"","Grandmaster Onillus continued the battles swiftly as murmurs spread throughout the clearing, many beings paying attention to this Celestial that was known as a Special Existence!","The Three-Eyed Fate Child stepped forward with light steps, his gaze looking coldly towards the other genius Celestial known as Volador. His three eyes stood on his tan skin eerily, dark hair flowing down to his shoulders as he had the wild look of an unkempt beast.","The one called Volador was also at the Domain Expansion Realm, being a genius that amassed 200,000 Fate Lines in less than a hundred years!","He saw the gaze of the Special Existence as he steeled his heart, preparing to go all out the instant the battle began as he wanted to give it his best, even if the strength of this being was insane as many foretold.","Grandmaster Onillus watched the cold faced Three-Eyed Fate Child with a light smile as he nodded happily for the first time before he initiated the battle.","\"Start!\"","SHAA!","The instant that Volador heard the command to start the battle, he moved his essence to begin summoning Empyrean Guards, but his words were caught in his throat as his eyes opened wide, shockingly somehow finding the Three-Eyed Fate Child already standing a few inches away from him!","His hand was raised as a dark blade of light that palpated with the aura of Space and Time was actually held against the neck of Volador, this genius Celestial feeling a sharp pain just from the edge of the blade stationed at his neck.","\"...\"","Silence reigned in the field of battle as the eerie eyes of the Special Existence stared at his enemy with a blade ready to strike. Were this actually a real battle, this young genius Celestial would have fallen right here and now without even understanding why!","\"Winner, Three-Eyed Fate Child!\"","WAAAAA!","The dark blade of light dissipated into lights as Volador looked towards the back of the already leaving Special Existence with a terror-filled gaze.","Those with normal cultivation levels were still looking at this scene in shock as they did not understand what had just occurred, just knowing the battle had ended in less than 5 seconds!","This was the power of the being proficient in two Supreme Laws! This was the power of the Special Existence that cultivated the Law of Spacetime and the Law of Fate!"]},{"number":457,"title":"Chapter 457: Chapter 456 - The Title of Special Existence","paragraphs":["Noah had his awareness spread out to observe every single thing that occurred in the clear field of battle in front of them, so when the Three-Eyed Fate Child moved, he saw it all very clearly.","From the eyes of others, the being had simply moved his legs and instantly appeared in front of Volador with a dark glimmering blade placed at his throat, but Noah saw the movement of essence that he was familiar with, the essence of Time, and that of Space!","This being had actually either accelerated or slowed himself with time while also making use of a teleportation technique to cast a skill before his enemy even noticed it, their neck only feeling a cold blade that could take their lives at any instant.","His eyes turned serious as this was an extremely deadly enemy.","If he wasn’t fast enough or he could not keep track of his movements as the enemy interfered with time and space, he could find himself in a similar position as this Volador. Of course, if he was able to use the Ultimate Treasure that was the Dagger of Time, this would be an entirely different case.","But his identity as Crixus prevented him from using a majority of his skills and items, especially a dagger that was considered a Cursed Item by the Celestials. He knew that he would have to be very careful when he faced this powerful Special Existence!","\"Next up, Light and Xander\"","The one to step up next was the other being that was a Special Existence, the one known as Grandmaster Light! She held a unique body composition that was actually made up of particles of light, her prowess lying in the Law of Light and the Law of Fate.","She stepped into the field of battle as she glanced at her opponent with calm eyes, the white light shining off of them showing a type of serenity rarely seen in the Light Expanse.","She had a humanoid form that seemed to shift every few seconds as the white light that made her moved around, her head shaped beautifully as tendrils of white lights flowed down to her shoulders. Her eyes shone with a hint of blue l.u.s.ter as she actually gave a nod of acknowledgment towards her opponent, the being known as Xander- someone that held the title of a Noble Fate and was currently standing in front of her before the battle began.","\"Start!\"","The command was given for the battle to start, Xander’s face serious as he began by casting Empyrean Guards and Empyrean Armament.","RUMBLE!","Essence converged as a gorgeous set of armor wrapped around him, his gaze watching Grandmaster Light who was simply watching him serenely to finish his transformation!","The moment he was finished, she moved with light steps as her figure turned into a streak of light towards him, her fair hands stretched forward as she came on to grasp a blade of white light on her right hand and a blade of golden light on her left hand.","This wasn’t any type of skill, it was simply the manifestation of Fate Essence on the left hand and Light Essence on the right hand!","Noah did not know what the prerequisite was in order to utilize Light Essence with ease, but he knew one had to pass 100,000 Fate Lines in order to do so with Fate Essence.","This Grandmaster Light has actually mastered the Law of Light to a similar extent as the Law of Fate, her hands expertly using the essence of each of these two elements to attack her opponent.","BOOM!","Her blade made of Light Essence landed on Xander first, his hammer parrying the blade as a white light erupted and pushed him back. The blade made of Fate Essence arrived a millisecond later as it smashed down and repeated the same thing, Xander being pushed back again as his face became increasingly serious!","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","Shockingly, Grandmaster Light kept her calm smile as she continued to lightly swing down the two blades she held in her hands, using simple pure Fate and Light Essence to land attacks that caused Xander to not even be able to retaliate.","What Noble Fate?!","What genius?!","In the face of this Special Existence utilizing the Law of Light and Fate, she was using their pure essence to overwhelm Xander until all he could do was defend!","CRACK!","He wasn’t able to release a single attack as he defended the entire time, the hammers he was using to shield himself finally cracking as two pulsating blades of gold and white came near his neck, ready to finish him off at any time.","\"...\"","Haggard breaths were leaving Xander as his eyes contained great shame at not even being able to withstand this being’s attacks. He had heard of the prowess of this Senior Sister, but never did he think it was this overwhelming.","\"Winner, Light!\"","OOOOOH!!!","The crowd cheered the dominating show by the mystical being made of white light as she took light steps back towards the remaining combatants.","Shockingly, the first round of the Battle of Genius ended with some of the most powerfully known Celestials being kicked out. Two particular beings with noble fates that people expected to at least enter the top 4 were kicked out in the first round, not even making it to the top 16!","Those advancing forward were the two Special Existences, two unlikely beings with Noble Fates known as Crixus and Athena, as well as twelve other genius Celestials.","Grandmaster Onillus wasted no time as he began the second round, the matches continuing on speedily.","In the second round, Noah and Athena did not meet the most powerful Special Existences that many dreaded facing as it would most likely mean the end of their battles in this tournament!","They showed off their skills against Celestials known as Geniuses, many of them ranging above 200,000 Fate Lines as Noah used his transformation after absorbing 12 Empyrean Guards to stand against them, their strikes not even passing through to damage his body that was hidden behind a huge tower shield as he then released attacks with his flail or deadly rays of Aether.","Athena used her unique ability to create a scintillating dance as she controlled the pace of the battles to always wear her opponents down until they faced deadly attacks that cost them the match!","But like this, Noah and Athena passed the second round and entered the top 8 with no issues.","Of course, it was the same case for the two Special Existences, the Three-Eyed Fate Child and Grandmaster Light who both passed through by dominating their enemies in a shocking manner.","The second round was passed in this manner, and whether by chance or fate, it went exactly in the same manner for the third round that decided the top 4 of this Battle of Geniuses!","In the third round, neither Noah nor Athena met the Special Existences, cruising through with their abilities as the both of them showed great battle prowess that overwhelmed their enemies and made them smoothly enter the top 4!","In one of the floating Prime Warsh.i.p.s, Grandmaster Vredral had a beaming smile as he laughed, Commanding Officer Raizel glancing towards him as he shook his head with an unbelievable expression.","\"What kind of monsters have you raised that they are able to smoothly pass to the top 4 of all current geniuses of this generation?!\"","..."]},{"number":458,"title":"Chapter 458: Chapter 457 - Crixus!","paragraphs":["Top 4!","The first three rounds of the tournament were over, and the beings that smoothly entered the top 4 ranks were not what many expected.","The powerful Celestials holding the title of Noble Fates, Xander, and Lila, were taken out in the first round!","The two Celestials holding a similar title but much weaker cultivation experience were actually the ones to replace them and take their spots, creating a clear path as they swiftly made their way to the top ranks.","In the Mage’s Tower where powerful auras were watching the ongoing matches, Edrusim had turned to the Vampyre Ruler Vladivostok with a careful gaze as he spoke.","\"This Crixus is more of an important piece than we all realized. You really only sent a Soul Forging Vampyre to oversee him?\"","\"...I didn’t expect for him to be this much of a genius. I’ll make the proper preparations.\"","Vladivostok replied with a shining gaze as his expression looked like someone that had gotten his hands on something he did not want to let go of.","\"If you all are smart enough, you will work hard to keep the identity of this Crixus under wraps and use him as a deadly blade at a crucial junction of the war, not risk his life freeing some old loser who was already defeated once.\"","The voice of the 2nd Infernal Lord rang out lazily to the side as his sharp eyes followed the events portrayed in front of them.","\"That benefactor was the one that allowed many of us to come out alive in the last war, bringing him back to our side is only natural!\"","Edrusim replied sharply while the Infernal Lord shook his head deploringly.","\"And this is why you all have been left behind by the Celestials. You’re too habitual in your thinking that even veering off the course a little is too much for you.\"","\"Hmph!\"","Slight disagreements occurred as the powerful figures watched the ongoing battle, the Vampyre Ruler by the side of the Infernal Lord and Grand Magician having a serious look as he sent communications to his forces in the light expanse while re-evaluating this being called Crixus.","In the Celestial Realm where the tournament was about to proceed, Noah and Athena were given a break before the final two rounds resumed, their figures actually being in the floating Prime Warship where Grandmaster Vredral and Commanding Officer Raizel were.","The fatty Grandmaster who was the teacher of Xander and Lila had long since left as he could not handle the proud look of Grandmaster Vredral, the wizened old man now looking at his two disciples with nearly tearing eyes.","\"You two have exceeded my expectations, but there is an even harder- nay, near-impossible task ahead of you!\"","His face was serious as his prideful gaze was filled with somberness.","\"You have been watching how the two Special Existences, the Three-Eyed Child and Light, have carried out their battles. While knowing your own skills, what do you think your chances of winning are?\"","The gaze of the Grandmaster first went to Athena as she looked at him with a calm look before she replied.","\"60%, Grandmaster.\"","\"What?!\"","Commanding Officer Raizel by the side looked on with a surprised expression at this number, his experience as a Grandmaster telling him that the Special Existences would be very hard to take down with the skills that these two disciples held.","Grandmaster Vredral looked at Athena carefully as he nodded while asking.","\"Why 60%?\"","\"If I am matched against either of them, I can use my unique ability to prolong the battle as much as possible, using my close combat skill to possibly wear them down after a sufficient time has passed. Of course, their skills are terrifying enough that all my plans could be rendered worthless, but I will still give it my best!\"","A valiant light erupted forth from her as she let out words of extreme confidence, Grandmaster Vredral nodding his head as he turned towards Noah. What did his other disciple see his chances at? His aged gaze stayed on Noah as the moment this disciple of his opened his mouth, the wrinkles on his face began trembling.","\"100%.\"","\"...\"","Silence!","Commanding Officer Raizel looked incredulously towards Noah while Grandmaster Vredral’s body trembled, his shining eyes locking onto this disciple as Noah opened his mouth and continued.","\"I have made a breakthrough while studying Aether and the Law of Fate these past few weeks, and I am confident in matching these Special Existences with my current abilities.\"","Yes! Noah was expanding the skills he could use against the enemies he would soon face, as he saw that their abilities were something that his identity as Crixus would struggle against unless he had a breakthrough in the middle of the battle or beforehand. He would continue exaggerating the genius of Crixus as he planned to use more abilities in the [Kin of Terror] skill tree, enjoying the heavily boosted abilities like [Portals of Terror] that were made even more terrifying from the recent additional abilities like [Aether Reinforcement] and [Triple on Cast Support].","The surrounding Grandmasters were looking at him incredulously as Commanding Officer Raizel shook his head in a non-believing way. Athena gazed towards him with shining eyes as even she did not fully believe him!","\"If your words are actually true, you will be obtaining the Luminescent Rainbow Dew that will grant you strength even higher than mine. If you can have such strength...you can begin fully exploring the wonders of the Celestial Realm as you go to locations that have similar treasures like the Luminescent Rainbow Dew!\"","Grandmaster Vredral spoke with a passionate expression as he stared at Noah, half believing his student about his shocking words that were filled with arrogance.","He spoke of the possibilities is Noah really was able to live up to his words, obtaining the #1 spot as he passed the fourth and fifth round where only four beings remained.","Him, Athena, Grandmaster Light, and the Three-Eyed Fate Child. Just who would come out on top?","Would Noah really be able to stand against the powerful Special Existences?!"]},{"number":459,"title":"Chapter 459: Chapter 458 - Two Battles, Different Results I","paragraphs":["As their rest time came to a close, Noah and Athena went out of the floating Prime Warship and went toward the clear miles long arena where two beings calmly remained.","The onwatchers locked their eyes onto their figures as a bustle of discussions erupted on who they believed would take the title.","Most were looking at the eerie Three-Eyed Fate Child as the eventual winner, the way he passed through his matches being in an extremely domineering manner!","His expert use of the Law of Fate and Law of Spacetime was at such a level that even some of the veteran Grandmasters were threatened by this being’s power.","Those that many were surprised by but expected them to be the eventual losers were Athena and Crixus! The two beings had rocketed into the top four, but many believed this would be where their journey ends, the matches of the fourth round only allowing the Three-Eyed Fate Child and Grandmaster Light to continue forward to fight for the championship.","\"Alright!\"","Grandmaster Onillus appeared in the skies again as his voice echoed through the field, his gaze carefully looking at the four genius Celestials below him.","\"The fourth round matches will be completed consecutively, with the fighting pairs occupying half of this field!\"","RUMBLE!","Grandmaster Onillus waved his hands as he created a clear line that stretched for more than a mile, the expansive field being split in half as he pointed in one side, energy leaving his body as the White Crystals which chose the combatants shone on two genius Celestials’ hands.","\"On this field will be Fate Child and Athena.\"","His gaze was impassive as he listed a match that made Athena adopt a heavy expression, his hands waving to the other field as he continued.","\"On this field will be Crixus and Light.\"","WAAAA!","The matches were decided as the crowd thrummed in excitement, their hearts looking forward to seeing the resplendent skills again.","RAA! RAA!","One could distinctly hear the loud bellows of an Emperor Penguin as he hiddenly supported his Master from the shadows, the eyes of the watching forces of the Dark Expanse shining as they looked forward to the results.","\"You four are good seedlings, and will have no shortage of resources in the near future because of the ranks you have gained. But the winner will gain even more, so continue working hard, and get ready to start!\"","Grandmaster Onillus waved his hands as the four combatants stepped into their respective fields.","Noah glanced at his opponent, the Special Existence that was born on a star made of light, a star that shattered the moment this being was born!","She was someone that was extremely proficient in the Laws of Fate and Light, and he had seen the domineering fashion that she used to straightforwardly release Fate and Light Essence to overwhelm her opponents.","He planned to show off the brilliance of Crixus even more with this battle, this time around planning on using the full amount of 18 Empyrean Guards he had available to him.","With 12 Empyrean Guards, he was adorned with a golden robe that released a resplendent thin protective shield along with a flail and a tower shield, as well as three rotating golden hammers that followed his thoughts.","RUMBLE!","He began summoning the full amount of Empyrean Guards as many Celestials looked forward with shocked eyes, not being able to believe that the skill they had been using all their lives could have such a difference in usage based on who was utilizing it.","12 Empyrean Guards! 18 Empyrean Guards!","OOOOH!","A burst of essence erupted out as the numerous Empyrean Guards all became streaks of light and attached to Noah, the newest form becoming clear in the eyes of all as one could only describe it in one word- Majestic!","Two pairs of golden wings erupted from his back, both of his hands holding shining weapons as one held an extremely sharp golden blade and the other held a glistening flail. Around his armored body, 6 golden hammers flowed freely around him, but they were accompanied by the enormous presence of 3 tower shields made of a thin film of light that circled Noah protectively on all sides!","He held two weapons in each hand to attack with, two pairs of wings for even more speed and versatility, another 6 weapons that were freely floating around listening to his commands, and three rotating tower shields to defend any attacks that came his way.","He looked like a moving golden tank that would not be taken down by even the most fearsome of attacks!","Grandmaster Light looked at this opponent as her calm eyes shone with splendor, summoning her pulsing blades of Fate and Light as she burst from her position and rushed towards Noah at once.","On the other field, Athena wasted no time as she used Empyrean Armament herself, knowing that many of the past opponents of the Three-Eyed Fate Child had lost in a matter of seconds as this being appeared from nowhere to finish the battle.","She planned to use her unique ability to predict the path of attacks of this opponent who was proficient in the Laws of Spacetime and Fate, the moment she got the rhythm of the attacks giving her a chance to counterattack herself!","RUMBLE!","Energy erupted out as two battles began on the separated fields of battle. The eyes of those watching were rapidly shifting from the four moving figures as they watched an array of abilities be put to use.","Elena was watching the ongoing battles with rapt attention when she received a message from the Dark Expanse, and this time it was directly from the Vampyre Ruler that oversaw much of the Archeon Clan!","The contents of the message were simple- more importance was being placed on the being called Noah, with the Archeon Clan needing daily briefs about his movements as they prepared for the future. Whether for good or bad, the spotlight shining on Noah was gradually opening up the interest of many beings, the eyes of the powerful Celestial Grandmasters that were watching also honing in as they watched the ecstatic battle prowess he continued to show when matched against other geniuses.","BOOM!","The two battles of separate fields began as other beings communicated and planned behind the scenes for the future, the winners of the fourth round not being clear!"]},{"number":460,"title":"Chapter 460: Chapter 459 - Two Battles, Different Results II","paragraphs":["RUMBLE!","Essence roiled in the field of battle as the first rounds of impacts occurred. The beings watching had their eyes locked on to the first exchange as for the first time in a while, the matches did not end with the first move.","When it came to Athena and the Three-Eyed Fate Child, the less experienced War Princess had somehow been able to foresee where the strike of the Special Existence would land as she smashed the hammers in her hands in a particular direction, and the hammers actually came in contact with the palm of the Special Existence that was about to clasp onto her fair neck!","In the battle between Noah and Grandmaster Light, the being made of pure light had summoned her golden and white blades, using pure fate and light essence to smash towards Noah’s tanky exterior.","The three shields rotating around him absorbed the essence released, the damage being further mitigated once they passed through the thin barrier of light being given off by the armor he was adorned in.","At the same time, the six floating hammers followed his thoughts as they circled Grandmaster Light on all sides, his multiple pairs of wings flapping rapidly as his figure turned into a streak of light that continuously released attacks every time the being made of light dodged the rushing hammers!","Grandmaster Light finally had a serious expression as essence moved around her, Empyrean Guard and Empyrean Armament being activated, along with another ability.","[Holy Light]!","Her clear voice rang out for the first time as her body exploded with white light, the numerous hammers circling around her looking for a point of weakness being pushed back as this exuding and overpowering light continued.","BOOM!","At the same time, Noah felt the expansion of her domain as he released his own, the two of them clashing and canceling each other as his attacks towards her accelerated. He wanted to give her no time to adapt as he didn’t want to show off too much of his power here.","[Smite of Liberation]!","OOOM","Numerous huge golden swords rushed from the clouds as they descended towards Grandmaster Light mercilessly, those watching being shocked to find these huge blades of liberation moving with their own will as even more weapons moving by themselves now attacked the defending Light.","In their field of battle, one could spectacularly see the movement of numerous golden hammers and swords around a defending Grandmaster Light, Noah himself moving expertly with a flail and sword in hand to dominatingly take the pace of the battle!","In the other field, a surprised Three-Eyed Fate Child had his body begin to release on overpowering light that began folding the space around him, his hands moving eerily in various directions to grasp onto Athena.","The War Princess had her gaze locked onto the numerous movements as she used her unique ability to see their trajectory.","SHAA!","She dodged the dangerous hands coming for her as her mind had an epiphany at this moment, where she actually realized that her eyes were causing her reaction time to be slower as this being in front of her affected both time and space. She let out a deep breath as she trusted her instincts and shockingly...closed her eyes!","WAA!","Those watching their battle closely rose from their figurative seats as they saw the War Princess actually close her eyes in the middle of the battle, but they were shocked even more as they saw her movements had become even swifter thereafter as the dangerous hands of the Three-Eyed Fate Child were dodged with even more ease.","\"What...\"","\"Genius! Truly genius!\"","Many Grandmasters looked on with shining eyes as they observed these spectacular talents that would soon surpass them in strength, their gazes especially so favoring Athena and Crixus as they were actually able to stand against Special Existences.","Their titles of Noble Fates seemed to hold more true than the other two that were taken out in the first round, their rapid rise in strength that allowed them to actually be at the stage they were in currently being the most surprising event out of this entire tournament.","In the battle with the War Princess and the Three-Eyed Fate Child, the former was slowly giving the battle more gravity as his body shone with numerous colors, Athena only showing more battle prowess as she trusted her ability and senses, moving with closed eyes!","Noah continued his domineering usage of skills that allowed for him to lock down the powerful figure of Grandmaster Light who was glowing brilliantly while releasing numerous abilities from the Light Element.","The abilities seemed to be more geared towards support as they bolstered her defense, her body occasionally releasing sharp swords of white light that were soon reflected by Noah’s boisterous defense.","\"The winners of the two fights seem to already be decided.\"","Grandmaster Onillus whispered to himself in the skies as his sharp eyes squinted, a light passing through them that nobody else would understand!","He watched as in the matches, the genius Crixus gained more and more of an edge while cornering the Special Existence, Light, who could not get through his defenses even though she held much more Fate Lines and understood 2 laws.","\"This Crixus seems to be more of a genius, he hasn’t even shown his Aether abilities in this match. He believes in himself to win this match and use all his abilities in the final match? Hmm...\"","A look of pondering appeared on Grandmaster Onillus as he turned his gaze to the other field, where he could already see who the victor that would stand against Crixus in the final match would be.","Even as Athena brought the battle to her pace by continuously dodging the strikes of the Three-Eyed Fate Child, this was all she could do- just dodge!","Her energy and mental energies required to keep up her constant movements were soon drained as the victor on this battlefield would also soon be decided.","\"The pair of disciples are about to have different results in their battles...\"","Yes! In the two fields where two battles were on going and nearing their conclusions, for the disciples of Grandmaster Vredral- they were about to have very different results!","Noah was moving valiantly with numerous golden shields and hammers surrounding him, even more blades of liberation descending from the skies to portray the image of a grand being with Noble Fate, the victory of the battle soon going to him.","Athena had her armament wrapping around her as she moved around with closed eyes, showing the image of a valiant War Princess, but this War Princess would soon be overpowered by the Special Existence that was proficient in two Supreme Laws.","Two battles, but there would be different results!","OOOOH!","Those watching felt their blood boil as they were given a show of resplendent abilities, many looking forward to the last match that would give a glorious victor taking the title of Strongest Genius. This would be the victor that would obtain the named treasure, the [Luminescent Rainbow Dew] that was capable of creating a World Realm expert.","Unbeknownst to many of them, their wishes for a final battle...will never be fulfilled as something even more shocking was about to occur!"]},{"number":461,"title":"Chapter 461: Chapter 460 - Magisterial!!!","paragraphs":["In the clear and expansive field to the east of the Sanctum where the docile Earth Behemoths could be found, tens of thousands of beings had gathered as they watched two battles near their glorious end.","Among those in the crowd, the forces from the Dark Expanse watched with hungry eyes at the power these young genius Celestials showed, and this was especially so for the one called Crixus!","They knew Crixus to actually be on their side, so the higher he rose in the rankings and obtained valuable treasures, the better.","Malthus the Spatial Magician was standing stably as he fixated the dark pearl on his robe to continue sending the feed of the entire field in front of them to the Dark Expanse, the beings in the Mage’s Tower of the Scholars Guild continuing to watch while discussing carefully.","\"If this Crixus actually gains the number one ranking, it will mean he will soon be brought to the World Realm by the Celestials!\"","The Grand Mage Edrusim spoke with shining eyes as he thought about gaining a World Realm powerhouse, and one that was actually raised by their enemy at that.","The 2nd Infernal Lord looked with slight interest with his gaze focused on Noah, his mind convincing himself that he found some sort of secret with this being because of the abilities he showed before.","Meanwhile, the Vampyre Ruler was looking on with a happy expression as he knew this Crixus held a Vampyre Bloodline, and he could control anyone with such a bloodline!","There were very few beings alive that held the same level of bloodline purity as him, Elena and a few others being special cases as the masses of Vampyres could be brought under his command no matter their power level, the uniqueness of bloodlines running this deep.","He himself was a Star Forging Realm Expert, an entire realm above World- so he looked forward to gaining such a genius subordinate in the future.","The beings in the Dark Expanse and those in the Celestial Realm, all of them watched the fourth round matches with rapt attention as they neared their conclusion.","The Special Existence that was known as Grandmaster Light was gradually getting more and more cornered by Noah’s attacks, his relentless golden hammers and blades of liberation that moved with their own wills as well as his own attacks not giving the woman made of light even a chance to retaliate.","Her Fate Lines that towered over 200,000 were no use over the Noah that was boosted by numerous passive and active skills, each of them with their own powerful boosts that would rack up huge percentages if one were to fully count them all.","One would only have to talk about the boosts from [Child of Space], and then from the singular boosts that just one Empyrean Guard gave when they were absorbed into his body using Empyrean Armament. Just these two alone were enough to add up percentages that would shock a mathematician!","RUMBLE!","His body shone with a golden glint as he moved even fiercer against Grandmaster Light, his counterpart in the other field of battled doing the same as the Three-Eyed Fate Child increased his attacks against Athena, the War Princess not being able to keep up any longer as the attacks filled with the power of Spacetime and Fate smashed into her relentlessly.","Two beings filled with power, each of them gradually cornering two powerful beings that were giving it their all.","OOOOH!","Reverberations of power spread out as Grandmaster Light was smashed away by a convergence of blades of liberation and golden hammers, something similar occurring in the other field as the War Princess was smashed head on with an attack from the Three-Eyed Fate Child.","BOOM! BOOM!","Their two figures coincidentally flew towards each other as Athena and Light neared the borders where their respective arenas were, smashing towards the ground and forming craters not too far from each other!","Their bodies were riddled with injuries as they got up in a difficult manner from the craters, their gazes looking at their opponents who were no longer looking at them.","Noah floated in the air above Grandmaster Light as he stared into the arena where Athena and the Three-Eyed Fate Child were fighting, his gaze not even glancing towards Grandmaster Light as he stared at the being also floating in the air in front of him.","The Three-Eyed Fate Child was looking coldly at Noah, his gaze completely passing over Athena as the two victors both looked towards the opponent they would have to face in the Final Round.","One had the dark energies of Spacetime rolling around his body, wisps of golden fate lines showing every now and then as his three eyes locked forward.","The other was a winged being surrounded by rotating golden shields and hammers, enormous blades of liberation pointing themselves towards the being with three eyes as they were ready to strike at any moment.","WAAA!","Their sheer presence was shocking to see as a majestic scene of two powerhouses grandly played itself for all to see.","\"These are the geniuses of this generation? Not too bad I suppose.\"","RUMBLE!","At this moment, an oppressive voice that seemed to be coming from all sides reverberated across the expansive area where every single being was watching the matches of the Celestials geniuses.","This voice was not just oppressive, it contained a hint of authority that made those who heard it tremble deep in their souls!","In the skies, Grandmaster Onillus heard this voice as his face immediately changed, his figure shooting down from the skies as he landed on the ground and kneeled.","That’s right, kneeled!","With him as the first, all the numerous Grandmasters that were on the few Prime Warsh.i.p.s surrounding the expansive arena all teleported or turned into streaks of light as they appeared on the ground, all kneeling!","The lesser ranked Celestials and Celestial Disciples looked at the behavior of the Grandmasters as they followed it themselves, their hearts feeling a sense of terror they had never felt before.","Noah was still floating in the skies as he shockingly looked around for the source of his voice when he suddenly felt an overpowering force also pulling him down, a pressure beginning to appear all around them that called out to be respected!","In the skies, an enormous figure of a mountainous Celestial Behemoth appeared, an indistinct being that was even smaller than the minute hairs of this behemoth standing powerfully atop the head. This being was indistinct, but all the beings around could make out that he was there as the oppressive and overwhelming pressure released from him.","The Celestial Behemoth shone with a golden hue, its eyes blank as it held a shining horn piercing the skies and expansive wings covering the earth. The mixture of a pegasus and a unicorn shone with splendor as its power that stood a level above the World Rank, stably at the Star Forging Realm, was completely overshadowed by the being standing on it!","The Alicorn, a Supreme Behemoth that was ridden on by a single being had arrived and cast a shadow on every single area occupied below.","The being standing atop it could be sensed by all as he arrived with a magisterial pressure, a pressure that caused all those in the skies to descend down to kneel, a pressure that accepted no other beings in the skies when he was there!","Noah’s eyes looked up in shock as the image of the overwhelming being became clear on the mountainous Alicorn, the figure of someone that should have not made their appearance any time soon actually stepping into the limelight..."]},{"number":462,"title":"Chapter 462: Chapter 461 - Magisterial!!! II","paragraphs":["From the aura released, one would only be able to feel emotions about this being that would scream out one word- Magisterial!","It was a feeling of majesty from someone that had great accomplishments, of someone in a realm that very few could claim in the Novus Galaxy!","\"Your skills are sufficient enough as the new weapons to be forged, but that is actually not what interests me more.\"","His voice was the only one ringing out over the expansive area of beings as they picked up another thing that caused them the feeling of terror they were experiencing.","From the voice of this being, they could feel extreme apathy, a tonation of a being that portrayed to have no emotions whatsoever as he spoke. It was akin to the way a human would speak to an ant, their hierarchy being extremely clear as one knew they could step on the other easily whenever they wished.","It was this feeling of being looked at as if they could be stepped on whenever this being wished that filled them with terror!","His image was clear in the eyes of many, his hair being a unique light gold color, his eyes as dark as night. His body was only adorned in vibrant white pants with his chest bare as one could sense the aura of wildness around him.","\"What interests me are the few rats that have taken the bait to sneak into my realm, and are even bold enough to believe that I would not know about it. The geniuses shall be rewarded after these rats are taken care of.\"","His apathetic voice now contained a direction as his gaze turned towards the ring of tens of thousands of beings, landing in a particular location where the forces of the Dark Expanse that Malthus moved with were situated.","\"The filthy aura of the Dark Expanse is strongly bouncing off of you, you know?\"","\"...!\"","Many beings watched as the figure floated off the expansive Alicorn that covered everything in their sight, standing generously in the air as he stared towards the frozen figures of numerous beings from the Dark Expanse that had adopted horrified expressions!","Noah’s main body had a reverent expression on the outside, but he was shocked at the development of events as the next ones made the situation even more drastic.","\"Others may not be able to notice it, but coming from someone that has nearly mastered a Supreme Law, I must tell you that it is too obvious.\"","His gaze moved from Malthus as he was talking, going to the side as he stared directly at the nearby Elena that was looking upwards with a fearless expression. Her face trembled at the pressure that was directed towards them even more, but she remained fearless nonetheless!","\"The most powerful Vampyre here seems to also be from the Dark Expanse? Let’s see...Ah from the Underworld. Treacherous creatures as always, I shall start with you for your race’s eventual extinction.\"","...","Shocking!","Drastic!","Fastly deteriorating!","The situation became worse and worse as this singular being, one of the Founders of the Celestials, stretched out his hands towards the forces of the Dark Expanse along with the Vampyres that Elena was surrounded with.","This also included the vampyric beasts that were the Emperor Penguin, Barbatos, and other beings from Noah’s Spiritual World!","The watching Grandmasters and Celestial Geniuses from the sidelines had also woken up from their stupor as their bodies glittered in gold, their strong eyes turning towards the collection of beings pointed out by their Founder as the bright light of skills began to be cast.","Noah himself shimmered with bright light as he turned his gaze filled with hostility towards those exposed as from the Dark Expanse, but his mind was moving rapidly as he sent numerous commands to his subordinates, the backup plans he never thought would see the light of day being initiated!","Things had changed just too fast! This was not the way that he expected anything to be progressing, but he would try to adapt as fast as he could.","RUMBLE!","Essence converged as the white hand of the Founder crossed miles, nearly reaching the position of the forces of the Dark Expanse in an instant.","It was at this moment where many figures were still frozen in shock with very few even being capable of using their essence that between the forces of the Dark Expanse and the dangerous white hand, a figure of a dark-haired man appeared!","Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone with a grim look and a vibrating body grandiosity appeared as he saw the palm descending down, a palm that he knew even his main body would not be able of withstanding if he was directly hit.","His mind worked rapidly as he looked at how fast the palm was approaching, and he knew that he would not even have the chance to teleport one or two of his subordinates before this palm came down and pulverized the rest!","His heart was grim as he went with the first plan that would buy him time for a second, the plan of spamming!","[Destabilize][Portals of Terror][Dawn of the Blood Lord][Blood World][Nightmarish Descent][Blood Rage][Arch Demon Lord Transformation][Lesser Cthulhu][Ancient Blood Scion][Blood Rage]...[Blood Sea]!!!","RUMBLE!","The activation of numerous skills that caused the bubbling of erupting essence akin to an exploding volcano occurred, a stupendous sight of numerous transformations taking place as a disfigured giant rapidly took form, numerous terrible portals releasing destructive elements and destabilizing space, a bloody moon appearing in the skies as a veil of blood erupted outwards, and eventually an expansive blood sea began expanding outwards!","It was an entire array of abilities cast wildly, something that no normal being would be able to do from the influx of mana that it required.","But all of these abilities were cast just to stand against a single palm!","A strong, domineering palm!","RUMBLE!","The beings around watched in shock as the white palm came in contact with the expanding sea of blood and the conflagration of a being that was bubbling within it, this single palm utterly erasing everything it came in contact with as the rumbling portals of terror faded into nothingness and nearly 90% of the sea of blood was wiped away in an instant.","The Founder had an apathetic face as he stared at the remainder of the intruding being, his eyes shining brightly as his voice reverberated again.","\"A chimera of demons, ancients, and vampyres...with an aura of a Terror? Interesting.\"","He said blandly with a cold voice as Noah felt the life force of his Ancient Blood Clone being nearly depleted with one strike, even with all of the transformation abilities and even skills like [Blood Sea] that negated 50% of all physical damage, the single palm of this being that was not even acting seriously nearly taking the life of his clone!","Only a wriggling mass of flesh remained as it formed into a head and a hand!","OOOOOM!","His reformed eyes watched in slow motion as a bright light of a domain unlike anything he had ever seen before begin to release from the body of the founder, his mind moving on to another back up plan as he realized him stopping the advancement of the palm did not bring himself even a second required to take away the Emperor Penguin and others from here.","Watching the slowly expanding domain, a purple-colored dagger covered in a sheath appeared in his only reformed hand, his mind going towards the plan of reversing the situation if it had deteriorated this much already!"]},{"number":463,"title":"Chapter 463: Chapter 462 - Inviolable!","paragraphs":["Seeing the appearance of the dagger, the eyes of the Founder shone with more light as he felt a unique energy be released from it, this unique energy of Time going on to wrap everything around the area as the enormous Domain he was releasing began to recede into his body.","He then began moving backwards in time as the events that took place slowly reversed, time unwinding as this majestic being actually chuckled!","\"Standing against me with just an item? Truly brave.\"","RUMBLE!","In the reversing time, his voice reverberated in Noah’s ears as his main body and clone both moved in reverse along with everyone else, many of the powerful being feeling this weird sensation but not being able to do anything about it.","The events had only gotten to the point where the shadow of the Alicorn was about to disappear along with the being that it carried above its head when the apathetic voice rang out again, this time in the form of an ability.","{Fate Lord’s Authority}.","WAAAA!","A golden air put a stop to the reversing time as the Founder spoke simply, using an authority only given to those that had mastered more than 50% of a law as he used the authority of fate to instantly stop the reversal of time of an Ultimate Weapon like the Dagger of Time!","Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone saw the Time Essence in the Sheath that powered the dagger drain even faster as it tried to resist this authority, but it was not able to as it was soon drying up, his reversal of time in this particular event not even going back a few minutes.","But the minutes that he did reverse by...would have to be enough!","RUMBLE!","Time seemed to be stabilizing again as the clone moved with extreme precision, his senses telling him they had only gone back to a millisecond after the Alicorn had first appeared.","He teleported near Elena, Barbatos, and all the other Beasts of the Spiritual World as he waved his hands towards them, teleporting them away in this destabilized space through the use of <<Astral Connector>>!","He began with the most important figures first as he could feel the oppressive Authority of Fate rush forth from the Founder in the reversed time, the powerful being not wasting a second as those that were weak only came to find the appearance of an enormous Alicorn, a being letting out an overpowering pressure atop it that already began releasing an ability that made them tremble to their cores.","Noah’s main body was still facing the Three-Eyed Fate Child as they both turned around to the location of the beings from the Dark Expanse, most of the powerful Celestials having felt the reversed time and knowing exactly what had happened before!","Noah’s main body, followed along by the Athena, Light, the Three-Eyed Fate Child and numerous other Grandmasters that were near the spectating group of beings now exposed to be from the Dark Expanse released their own attacks towards them as they moved rapidly.","Noah’s clone had only managed to teleport away the beings he considered the most important when the attacks reached them, his mana that was going towards the terrified Malthus coming to a stop as the expanding golden {Fate Lord’s Authority} reached them!","WAAA!","Shockingly, it was not just mana that was held in place, Noah finding out that his clone could not move a single muscle, every single being remaining in the area experiencing the same phenomenon as the voice of the Founder was heard once more.","\"You actually managed the escape of a few with me here, I have to give you props for that. Let’s see now...\"","The figure of the Founder appeared near the frozen beings, his eyes glancing at Noah’s Blood Clone curiously as they also went towards Malthus. His apathetic eyes lingered on Malthus as his energy picked up a unique signature on the body of this operative of the Dark Expanse, it was the dark pearl that was attached to his robe!","\"Bold enough to even show what was happening here to others? Now now, who’s out there watching?\"","His languid voice filled with apathy was still the only thing ringing out in the surroundings as the Celestials pulled back the moment they saw the Founder arrive amongst the enemies, their hearts trembling at the level of his strength as none of the enemies could even move a muscle.","Noah’s main body was observing the situation with an expression that matched all other Celestials, but his heart was grim as his clone found himself not being able to move an inch while under {Fate Lord’s Authority}!","He was able to teleport away all of his people, and even some of the operatives of the Dark Expanse, but there were still many left behind as those of importance to note were Malthus and his clone, all others being nameless operatives.","The Founder continued to move at his own pace as more and more shocking words came out from him, Noah finding his methods more and more unfathomable as the next thing he said shocked him even more.","\"You think you can peer into my Celestial Realm without me peering back? Hmm...an Infernal Lord, a little Magician, and a scurrying Vampyre...I remember your auras from the last war.\"","Shocking words that the masses who were watching with rapt attention nearby digested rang out, the information that the ongoing matches were not just being watched by them, but also by the powerful figures from the Dark Expanse becoming apparent to them.","The powerful figures themselves that were within the Mage’s Tower of the Scholar’s Guild had stood up with sober expressions, their eyes locked onto the rapidly changing scenes as Edrusim had an angry expression, the 2nd Infernal Lord nearby looking forward with an expression that was actually smiling in excitement, the destructive energies of his body seemingly bubbling up just waiting to be released!","\"I see. This is good. I can relay my message to you all right away.\"","The apathetic voice of the founder continued as his hands reached for the dark pearl which was showing the feed of everything occurring to the forces of the Dark Expanse, his other crystal white hand grabbing on the head of the frozen Malthus who wore the robe that had this pearl.","His hand landed atop the frozen being’s head as it continued to descend down as if it was pressing against clay, skull and brain matter spurting out as the genius Spatial Magician was killed simply!","He then released golden flames from his hands that rapidly began to burn the lifeless body, his other hand grabbing onto the pearl as he watched with bored eyes as the being known as Malthus burned to ashes.","He grasped the pearl in his hands as he then turned towards the frozen clone of Noah, his gaze that of slight interest as he spoke into the pearl!","\"Are you still watching?\"","...!"]},{"number":464,"title":"Chapter 464: Chapter 463 - Puppets! Freedom!","paragraphs":["Noah watched the attention of the Founder turn towards his clone as he watched on coldly, having saved all those he could as the death of the one called Malthus was out of his hands.","As for his own clone?","In front of the founder that was already reaching out towards it, Noah simply stopped supplying mana to the ability of Ancient Blood Clone, cutting off the connection with the mass of blood and flesh right away before any more damage could be done by this terrible being!","He had already sustained horrible damage to his origin just from the pressure passed from {Fate Lord’s Authority}, and would not allow any more as he had already saved those most important to him. Now, all he could do was watch as this being that should not have appeared came into play in front of his eyes. Many questions were swirling in his mind, but he held no answers to any of them. Why had the most powerful Celestials appeared right before the last round of the tournament? Why did he move to act at this exact moment? What exactly were his goals?! No answer came to mind as the shocking events continued to play out.","The Founder watched the frozen body of his clone turn into a mass of bloody goo as his face scrunched up, waving his hands as golden flames embroiled it and turned it to ashes instantly.","His hand then focused the pearl sending the feed to the Dark Expanse on the remaining forces of Vampyres and other beings that were with Malthus, golden flames erupting from him as they went on to leap from one being to another, eating them all up with ease as numerous figures burned until nothing remained of them!","\"Do you see how easily I can erase you all? Are you still watching?\"","The Founder spoke as he waved the dark pearl showing the feed of everything upward, making it float in the skies as he turned his gaze towards the many Celestials and beings from the Light Expanse.","\"I will use this opportunity when every side is listening to declare that war shall begin yet again. The enemy is one who you have seen, the beings constantly moving in the dark to sow disorder, the savages of the Dark Expanse!\"","His apathetic voice had more emotion as his rumbling power was directed to the tens of thousands of beings around the clearing. He turned to the pearl floating above him as he spoke out towards the listening Infernal Lord and Grand Mage.","\"I imagine you all must have somber expressions while thinking of the future and the billions of lives that will be lost. I will tell you now, cheer up. There is no need for such somberness in this little playground we are in!\"","His voice was gradually rising in volume as his apathetic eyes that drew in all those watching shone in a peculiar l.u.s.ter while staring at the device sending the feed of everything in the surroundings to the highest echelons of the Dark Expanse.","\"It is this little playground that I plan to break out of, and I will take you all with me. To a place where we can make our own choices, a beautiful place that is wider than anything you’ve ever seen...\"","A pause appeared on the face of the Founder as he glanced around him. His languid eyes watched the reverent and terror-filled gazes of the tens of thousands of beings in the surroundings along with the figures of the Dark Expanse that were watching through the dark pearl. He spoke the next words slowly as he seemed to be reminiscing.","\"In this Novus Galaxy of ours, we’re all puppets, puppets flowing across the river of fate...\"","A look of hatred spread across the handsome yet terrifying figure of the Founder as he talked about a playground and the mention of puppets, his gaze seeming forlorn!","\"I plan to break the strings that are constantly moving the innocent souls in this playground of ours, until all of us can no longer be considered puppets. I will set you all free. I...will set us all free!\"","RUMBLE!","A terrifying shock spread out to the minds of any that were listening, not fully understanding the meaning of the words just said as they only sent deep terror to their hearts!","The Founder had a lost look on his face as he seemed to be reminiscing, his gaze looking afar at something nobody else could see. His mouth moved by itself as he seemed to be lost in a monologue, giving a show of only him to the terrified audience in the surroundings.","His gaze focused onto the dark pearl where he knew the forces that were his enemies were watching, continuing his monologue with no interruption.","\"Return to your holes and hold your families close. Spread the word to the other rats and prepare, because I’ll be sending my forces towards your direction now.\"","OOOOM!","The Founder finished his words as he pinched his hands towards the dark pearl, destroying the device and cutting the feed that the powerful beings in the Mage’s Tower were receiving right away. He only left behind an air of power as the authority he was releasing slowly receded.","WAAAA!","An air of madness and uncertainty spread out across the expansive field, the many Celestials and Celestial Grandmasters were already on the ground kneeling as this Founder rose to the skies.","\"Scour my Celestial Realm for any remaining forces from the Dark Expanse, and get a Warship to make haste towards the Underworld that has been hiding them. Destroy it all with no trace left remaining.\"","RUMBLE!","A command rang out in the ears of every Celestial Grandmaster as they placed their right hands on their chest in allegiance and understanding.","\"The four geniuses showing most promise...take them to the Golden Bastion and finish forging them into the best weapons before they join the coming conflict. There should be another Luminescent Rainbow Dew there for the final two champions. Spare no efforts to raise their realms.\"","More commands released from the Founder as an air of majesty spread out, his gaze calm and apathetic as he landed back on the Alicorn overshadowing everything around with its sheer size.","\"Onillus, you shall lead the Squadrons for the first wave of attacks in this war. Prepare to take on the title of a Commander and lead the first forces of the numerous Prime Worlds and Celestials to the border where our forces await. As of now...we are officially at war!\"","OOOOOH!!!","\"It is a war for Liberation, for Order and Balance! For breaking free of the chains that bind us in this playground we are in!\"","WAA!","\"For Order and Balance!\"","\"For Freedom!\"","...!","Noah watched the roaring of essence and power from thousands of Celestials and powerful Grandmasters, his heart beating wildly as a scene of paramount importance played itself out in front of him. Athena had come to inexplicably stand by his side as she looked forward with shining eyes.","The beings from numerous Prime World watching were shaking in the places they stood as the show of power was too much for them, those that could still think knowing that many of them would be heading into a war soon!","A tournament that was meant to observe the genius of a few Celestials had ended in the most shocking of ways, a single being appearing as he overhauled everything happening, killing numerous forces from the Dark Expanse and announcing the beginning of a long war!"]},{"number":465,"title":"Chapter 465: Chapter 464 - Rapid Movements","paragraphs":["In the Mage’s Tower of the Scholar’s Guild, the Grand Magician Edrusim had on a wrathful face why the Infernal Lord had an expression of excitement.","\"I see why our existence was necessary to oppose this being! Does he not know what his words truly mean? Haha!\"","The second ranked Infernal Lord spoke out as wild waves of power emitted from him, the other powerful beings in the room already beginning to send telepathic communications based on what they just saw.","The leading figure of the Celestials had just outright declared war, and they had to prepare!","Edrusim’s wrathful gaze came down as the provocation of the Founder gradually lost its effect, the gaze of the Grand Magician going towards the Vampyre Ruler Vladivostok.","\"You forces in the Underworld are about to be taken out.\"","Vladivostok had on a grim look as he replied less than a millisecond later, his robe fluttering behind him as he stepped out.","\"I’ve already sent word for them to begin moving out, I’ll have to excuse myself for now.\"","\"Haha! Hahaha!\"","Voldred, the 2nd Ranked Infernal Lord, continued to have a glimmer of excitement on his face as he laughed, Edrusim turning towards him as well as he voiced out.","\"I’ll depend on you to get word to the other Infernal Lords...as well as their assistance.\"","\"Ahh, no worries Young Edrusim. After all...we were created just for this!\"","RUMBLE!","Essence blasted out as the body of the Infernal Lord disappeared, the only one left behind in the expansive room of the Mage’s Tower being the Grand Magician Edrusim who was accompanied by a few other High Wizards.","\"What shall we do, Milord?\"","Many of them dressed in grey robes glanced at Edrusim with tight expressions, the Grand Magician replying simply as he pulled out a commonly seen weapon in the Dark Expanse, the tool that many wizards and witches carried with them- it was a majestic wand that released an air of ancientness!","\"We prepare. Assemble the Battle Mages of our Guild and work with the Vampyres to begin creating different Legions. The first Legion of the Celestials will most likely head towards that location, so station the first forces there.\"","His face had erased all of its wrath as he held a chilling expression, vibrant essence beginning to roll around the Ancient Wand in his hands as the air of a Grand Magician was properly portrayed.","\"As of now, we are at War!\"","RUMBLE!","Essence reverberated from the wand he held as it coursed through the uniquely designed runic circles in the room they were in, causing this room and the larger Mage’s Tower it was connected to, to begin shining brilliantly as a single message began to spread across the Dark Expanse.","This message only told of one thing, and it was war!","---","In the Celestial Realm, Noah was moving inside a Prime Warship with Athena and Grandmaster Vredral, along with the two beings termed as Special Existences.","A moment after the words of the Founder to take the four geniuses that were fighting in the fourth round before the shocking interruption was heard, Grandmaster Onillus transferred numerous treasures and authority to Vredral, allowing him to lead the Warship and take his disciples as well as the two Special Existences towards a particular deeper area in the Celestial Realm.","The location they were heading in was further to the south past the Water and Ice Behemoth, the location where Fate Behemoths were abundant, and the place where the most powerful Celestials were always trying to explore.","It was an area where Elite Behemoths freely ran rampant, and one could occasionally spot a Supreme Behemoth if they went far enough!","Grandmaster Vredral was taking the four geniuses to this location per the orders of the Founder, in his bag of holding lying the [Luminescent Rainbow Dew] and numerous other treasures as he steered the Prime Warship forward with a serious expression.","Noah and Athena were standing not too far behind the Grandmaster as each was lost in their own thoughts, the two Special Existences could be seen in meditative poses not too far away from them.","Every single person was lost in their own world as the events they had just seen were too shocking!","The power they had just witnessed from the founder made many of them receive the reminder of something they only had in their wildest dreams, the remainder of the power they all wanted to achieve.","They looked at the Founder that had required respect just from his sheer presence as exactly the power they wanted to achieve, each of them lost in their own thoughts.","Some time back and unbeknownst to the beings around Noah, a drop of blood had slowly formed from his heart, abundant Origin Essence going into it as it then swiftly disappeared from inside his body, never to be seen by anyone else as even the essence fluctuations were hidden.","Inside his own body, he had activated the [Ancient Blood Clone] ability once more as a drop of blood filled with his own origin formed inside of him, this drop of blood disappearing thereafter as it was teleported to a singular location- the Underworld!","After having saved Barbatos, Elena, and the others from certain death in the hands of the Founder, he moved without haste to a Prime World that was facing its destruction soon. These were his own thoughts, as well as the frantic telepathic messages from Elena and Prince Cassius for the Vampyre King and the other forces stationed in the Underworld.","The moment that the Founder released his command to destroy this Prime World for hiding the treacherous Vampyres, the Celestials passed word as the forces nearby were soon activated, any close Prime Warsh.i.p.s and Grandmasters setting off right away.","It was a race against time as Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone reformed from the drop of blood rapidly in the bleak atmosphere of the Underworld, its body already beginning to rush down towards the planet’s core as he moved fast!"]},{"number":466,"title":"Chapter 466: Chapter 465 - Missed by a Second!","paragraphs":["The body of the Ancient Blood Clone was finishing the process of formation as it pierced through the layers of earth, not even taking a few seconds before getting into the inner layer of the Prime World.","His gaze was impassive as his emotions were turbulent after having just seen the immense power of just one of the beings he was up against, his current power not even being able to withstand a single attack.","[You...What?!]","He put his thoughts aside as he heard the words of the Core of the Underworld and worked in conjunction with his Planetary System as he portrayed the images of the particular time when the Founder had called for the destruction of the Underworld.","[...]","Silence reigned as slight trembling could be felt from the core of the Underworld, Noah not wasting any time as he initiated the process of forming a connection while talking.","\"There is no time. If you want to survive...\"","What always happened when he formed new connections with worlds repeated, a rumbling of essence occurring as something else approached the Underworld!","Two Prime Warsh.i.p.s with the hardened faces of righteous Celestial Grandmasters at the lead were using their energy to pierce through the void of space as they neared the Underworld, having received word that the mission came directly from the Founder, and it concerned a world that was harboring the forces of the Dark Expanse.","They moved without a second delay as they were nearing the Prime World, their hearts set on destroying the entirety of this world as they prepared to join the war.","RUMBLE!","They felt immense fluctuations of energy ahead of them as they neared, their Prime Warsh.i.p.s arriving as they observed with shocked eyes, where the world used to be, only a void of darkness laid!","\"Rubbish!\"","One of the piloting Grandmasters called out as he spread out his energy, a surprised look overtaking his wrath as he sent out a message.","\"It is only invisible, aim the World Cannons and obliterate it!\"","OOOOM!","Essence rapidly converged around the Warsh.i.p.s as the huge cannons around them vibrated, gaining a glimmer of red as they aimed at the invisible Underworld in front of them.","Deep in the core of this Prime World, Noah’s clone had already successfully finished the formation of the connection as another stupefied reaction was released from this Prime World as well, his mind working fast as he pulled out the [World Engine] from the Expansive Space that he shared with the main body, activating the treasure right away as a unique energy spread out with the core at the center.","He had already cast [Blood World] and [World Veil] to wrap around the entire world, preventing the coming Celestials from seeing what was occurring within it and turning it invisible, but this only earned him a few seconds.","These few seconds...were more than enough!","The unique energy released from the [World Engine] wrapped around the entire world as outside it, the enormous cannons meant to strike down at the core of the Prime World had readied enough energy, destructive rays of red lights shooting out as they went towards a singular location.","OOOOONG!","The rays of red energy left destructive energies in the void of space as they thundered down, the Grandmasters piloting the Warsh.i.p.s watching with eyes burning with passion as they sensed an enormous fluctuation of energy at this moment, and then observed with unwilling expressions as the red rays of destructive lights they shot out...actually hit nothingness!","\"...!\"","Silence reigned as they watched the rays pass through where they sensed a planet was just a few seconds ago, nothing being there now.","They grit their teeth as they were knowledgable of a similar incident with the Magus World not too long ago, they just didn’t think it would happen again, and not so quickly!","This also meant that the culprits for the disappearance of the Magus World were also the forces of the Dark Expanse, being connected in some way with that world as well. These were the conclusions that the Grandmasters arrived at anyways.","\"Savages!\"","One particular Grandmaster grit his teeth as he gave out a command.","\"Head back to report the findings. I’ll scour the surrounding areas to see if I find anything...\"","Thus, a wild goose chase that would give nothing began, while Noah’s clone was already in a completely different quadrant of the Light Expanse near his homeworld, numerous connected worlds veiled in different areas all around this quadrant.","His clone had already disappeared from the inner layer of the Underworld as he reappeared inside the Spiritual World that he had anchored in a nondescript location of the Celestial Realm as small as a grain of sand before he jumped to save everyone from the single palm of the founder.","He appeared in the Time Space as he did not even go communicate with his forces that had come close to death under the hands of one of the most powerful beings in the Novus Galaxy and were currently sitting with troubled expressions.","He wanted a moment of silence and contemplation as his main body was itself surrounded by numerous Celestials, his clone being the only one that truly felt free right now.","He appeared in the skies of the time space as he floated and closed his eyes, just wanting to get a momentary time to think!","Things seemed to always be happening so fast, but he breathed out slowly while looking at the results of recent events. All around him, numerous lines of fate and chaos particles swirled towards him in great abundance, as he had just created an enormous amount of chaos and changed the fates of billions from utter destruction in the Underworld.","He had participated in the tournament that was so extravagantly interrupted, the results now giving the treasure that could push someone’s rank to the World Realm to two beings.","The last command from the founder was to take the last 4 Geniuses- Him, Athena, Light, and the Three-Eyed Fate Child- deeper into the Celestial Realm to be forged into the sharpest weapons!","He would soon enjoy this treasure that would push him up an entire realm as his thoughts then moved to the consequences of the Founder appearing, the remaining forces of the Dark Expanse in the Celestial Realm, as well as the War that had just begun..."]},{"number":467,"title":"Chapter 467: Chapter 466 A Grand New Area, Summons!","paragraphs":["The recent events had caused rapid developments, and Noah still did not know what the full results of these events would be.","His clone floated in the skies of the time space as he spent a few hours just thinking, numerous new pathways opening up in his mind as he looked on how to move forward next.","When it came to the forces of the Dark Expanse, there was another being called Agrus, a ’Walking Library’ that should still be hidden in the location that they established in the Celestial Realm.","The problem of the Founder still remained as this being was powerful enough to point out the beings of the Dark Expanse from his power, so any of them that were still moving in the Dark Expanse would have to be extremely careful!","This also came to his forces, who could no longer freely traverse the Celestial Realm to take down Behemoths themselves as they were quickly associated with the forces of the Dark Expanse as they were under the lead of Elena.","After this, they would have to increase their strength in the Time Space of the Spiritual World to max their skill trees proficiencies as well as raise their percentages in the Law of Fire and Water in the Fire and Water Law Space.","Another pathway was the Dark Expanse which should have many opportunities to move in as well, especially with the war heading towards them right now.","The War made Noah also think about when he planned to use the vial he had received from Elena weeks ago, a vial that would free a powerful being from the 7th Celestial Star. He would have to make a plan to also use this sometime in the near future!","His eyes opened as they glimmering with strength in the Time Space, his figure disappearing thereafter as he began moving once more, this time starting with the worried subordinates as he moved to check on them, as well as the stabilization of the forces of the Underworld.","His identity would be revealed to the forces of Vampyres in this world as he stopped any information from leaking to the forces of Vampyres in the Dark Expanse by using his authority as the Vampyre Progenitor.","His clone began moving as his main body arrived in a different location further south of the Sanctum past all the Water and Ice Behemoths.","The area they landed the Prime Warship on was an exquisitely designed bastion of a city, enormous golden structures rising to the skies as numerous Warships floated all around.","This was one of the bigger strongholds of the Celestials, something that was placed close to where the Fate Behemoths resided- the location where the most powerful Celestials moved around in!","\"Welcome to the Golden Bastion, the place where you all will truly step into power before setting out to make a name for yourselves.\"","The voice of Grandmaster Vredral rang out as the two beings with Noble Fates and the Special Existences looked towards this city, their eyes shining with anticipation.","The Grandmaster turned towards them with a smile as he focused on Noah and the Three-Eyed Fate Child.","\"I’ve received a message that the Founder would like the two beings who would have fought in the final match to both receive the treasures that will push their levels to the World Realm, so the both of you will be receding the last two Luminescent Rainbow Dews in existence!\"","RUMBLE!","He waved his hands as a single dew shaped item that shone with splendor flew towards Noah.","\"I have one of them on me, the other is in the hands of Grandmaster Lukas in this Golden Bastion.\"","He said this towards the Three-Eyed Fate Child who would be receiving his own Luminescent Rainbow Dew later on as he then turned towards Athena and Light.","\"The two of you will receive the remainder of the treasures, and it will depend on your talent whether you can breakthrough from the Domain and into the World Realm, as the process will simply take too long and is too arduous unless a treasure like the Luminescent Rainbow Dew is used.\"","The two that lost on the fourth round nodded as the Celestials descended into the Golden Bastion, Noah putting away the extremely valuable [Luminescent Rainbow Dew] as he smoothly achieved gaining a treasure that would propel his rank rapidly to another stage!","It was at this moment that Noah also received a telepathic communication, and this one came from a unique being- the 7th Infernal Lord, Azula, had sent him a message that relayed shocking information.","A Letter of Summons had arrived from the 1st Infernal Lord, and it concerned him!","His mind quickly processed this information as his Ancient Blood Clone that was moving in the Spiritual World discussing the recent events with the Harbingers and Elena had to stop the discussions, having to be the one to head back to the Infernal Realm.","\"Draco, Barbatos, help Elena with the stabilization of the Underworld. I’ll be stepping out briefly.\"","His subordinates nodded with serious looks as they saw the clone disappeared into particles of light, their gazes looking at each other as they seemed to come to an agreement from their hearts!","The subordinates that were boosted heavily by [Golden Guider] and still experienced just how powerless they were next to a truly powerful being felt a stifling feeling in their heart, wanting to get stronger so that they weren’t constantly saved by their Master.","Their hearts burned with ambitions as they moved to do their tasks, Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone teleporting back into the Second Infernal Realm with his body changed to that of the Infernal Lord adorned with an exquisite crown.","The dreary and fiery lands reflected in his vision as he saw that there was a bustle of activity in the grand metropolis of this Infernal Realm, the movements of numerous Infernals in an orderly fashion reflecting in his eyes as they formed into numerous large groups.","\"My oh my, already in the Domain Expansion Realm. You rise up first, O 9th Infernal Lord.\"","The curvaceous figure of Azula materialized in front of his eyes as a sultry voice rang out, the 7th Infernal Lord appearing while waving a glistening red letter in her hands!"]},{"number":468,"title":"Chapter 468: Chapter 467 Directed Towards the Dark Expanse","paragraphs":["Noah stared at the curvaceous Infernal Lord in front of his eyes as he nodded respectfully, the 7th Infernal Lord waving the letter in her hands towards him.","\"The time is nearing for the War, and the 1st Infernal Lord has sent his summons for you. You are to take up an Infernal Legion to assist the forces that will come in conflict first!\"","His clones waved his hands towards the red letter that shone with essence, his Origin sensing a sense of Authority from it as the moment he touched it, it released a proud and strong voice that reverberated in his mind.","\"Lead a Legion to the Verittas Fortress where the first point of contact of this war will occur. Prove your worthiness as an Infernal Lord there by claiming the first victory in this war!\"","RUMBLE!","The voice echoed in his mind as if it was to be completely obeyed, its authority dying down thereafter as it faded into strands of red light. He glanced up to the smiling Infernal Lord Azula as he asked.","\"The Verittas Fortress?\"","\"Ah yes, a literal fortress floating in the vastness of space, here are the coordinates. It is a fairly interesting stronghold that the Wizards created as one of the first points of defenses against Celestials. You will be reinforcing them as those expected to clash in this war are the weakest of all forces, with the 1st Infernal Lord using this opportunity to see your personal strength and your strength as a commander.\"","Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone nodded as he glanced at the numerous moving Infernals below him, their numbers hitting in the tens of thousands. Azula glanced in their direction as she continued.","\"You will be using the Second Infernal Gate that is actually located not too far from the Verittas Fortress to get there swiftly. The only thing you’ll have left to do is command the Infernal Legion as well as work together with the little Wizards and Witches there to push back the advancing Celestial Legions. Fun, isn’t it?\"","The voice of the Infernal Lord was filled with blood lust as it seemed like she wanted to go in this battle herself, finishing her words in a teasing manner as he nodded towards her.","\"Understood. I will head out right away.\"","He affirmed at the Infernal Lord as he had his own thoughts rapidly moving, seeing this as an opportunity to be involved in the first conflict of the war in a huge capacity that he would not be able to be in as Crixus yet.","But as the 9th Infernal Lord...he would be standing against multiple Grandmasters and Celestials that were aiming their blades to conquer more lands and increase their amount of influence.","It was this influence that they coveted, as it would allow their influence over the fates of many beings to increase, which would in turn increase their power!","Noah saw this as one of the biggest motivations for the Founder who had proclaimed the declaration of War. As the being that influenced the huge organization raving through the Dark Expanse, the Fate Lines he had collected over the years were insurmountable, where he would not be too surprised if this being was not too far away from mastering the Supreme Law of Fate.","His power was already massive, and if he could increase his own strength while stopping the expanding influence of the Celestials and their rapid increase in strength, he would gladly do it as it was killing two birds with one stone!","He descended down towards the ground where orderly and armored figures of Infernals stood.","His eyes counted more than 10,000 that made this Legion, and it was all shockingly majority of the Infernals at the Void Realm, with about 3000 in the Soul Forging Realm, and even 10 at the Domain Expansion Realm!","Their gazes glanced up towards him as he made his Chaos Field visible with all of its glory, causing many of them to have their knees buckle at its pressure as the 7th Infernal Lord Azula in the skies looked on in shock.","RUMBLE!","Noah did not hide his advancement in the Law of Chaos when it came to this Infernal Lord, because he knew it was a Special Existence that was made for a single purpose- Destruction!","In her Origin, there stood no plots or schemes, just following orders and directions from the strongest Infernal Lord as they awaited to carry out the goal they were created for. Thus, Azula only felt shock at seeing the number of his Chaos Particles that were rapidly nearing the three hundred thousand milestone.","He glanced at his Stat Panel that had continued its improvements, especially so in the number of Fate Lines and Chaos Particles as he continued to influence more and more things around him.","[Noah Osmont][Title(s): Infernal Lord(Variant)]","[Bloodline(s): Vampyre Progenitor(Awakening)]","[Fate Line(s) : 289,258]","[Chaos Particle(s) : 269,362]","[Origin Core(s) : Fire-3, Water-3]","[Domain(s) : Fate,Chaos, Space, Fire, Water]","[Vitality: DOMAIN]","[Focus: - ]","[Strength: DOMAIN]","[Law(s) : Fate-2.8%,Chaos-2.6%,Space-8%, Fire-33%, Water-33%]","He was already nearing the mastery of 5% in just a matter of days, and he saw himself achieving the 1 million milestone soon enough as long as he continued to act on the grand and much larger stage.","The Legion of Infernals that felt his strength as they smashed the weapons they were holding or their feet towards the ground with fervor.","\"Ready to serve! Ready to Destroy!\"","\"Ready to serve!\"","\"Ready to destroy!\"","OOOOOH!!!","A coalescence of dark red mana erupted out as the Infernals chanted, Noah feeling a connection forming with the 10,000 Infernals in this Legion as one of the unique abilities of the Infernal Lord appeared in front of his eyes- the simple ability to command Infernals under his banner.","He glanced towards them as he raised his hand, their boisterous yells stopping instantly as they looked up with shining eyes.","Noah then glanced at a humongous gate in the distance which would lead them to the location where a doorway towards this Second Infernal Hell stood in the Dark Expanse, the region where they would head towards this Verittas Fortress and clash with the on coming forces of the Celestial Legion!","\"Set off!\"","RUMBLE!","He let out a commanding voice as the Infernals moved orderly, their eyes set as they looked forward to the destruction..."]},{"number":469,"title":"Chapter 469: Chapter 468 The Dark Expanse","paragraphs":["Noah’s Ancient Blood clone passed through the large gate that stood within the Second Infernal Realm. The legion of infernals followed behind him closely as they passed through with utter cordiality- It looked like the procession of a king that was leading his troops to battle!","RUMBLE!","They passed through the gate as Noah felt the changing of spatial locations, his eyes and senses opening up as a brand new world and folded itself in front of him. The void of space was not too different from the one that he was used to, but he felt a peculiarity that made him know that this was not the Light Expanse.","This peculiarity was hard to pinpoint, but his sense told him that he had fully arrived into the other side of the Novus Galaxy, the Dark Expanse!","OOOOM","The Infernal Legion passed through the gateway easily and appeared behind him as the surroundings of this particular Infernal Gate that led to the Second Infernal Realm was not actually surrounded by numerous warships as the first one that he went in through to conduct the Infernal Hunt with the Celestials.","The large gate stood alone in the vastness of space without a single soul in the surroundings. This was because there was a certain agreement between the beings of the Dark Expanse and the Infernals.","The leaders of both forces knew that their enemy was not among each other, but something even larger that stood to threaten all of them. Thus, there wasn’t any measure of protection or watch surrounding this gate as Noah glanced around the empty doorway that led the infernal realm and began to take the legion under him towards the coordinates where a certain Verittas Fortress was.","This would be the location that the first collision of this war would occur in!","RUMBLE!","The strong force of ten thousand infernals that consisted of a majority void ranked and the remainder being at the Soul Rank and even the ten at the Domain Expansion Realm thundered forth menacingly as they followed behind their infernal Lord.","Noah ignored any of the surrounding planets, whether dead or alive that he passed as you continued forward for a few hours, eventually coming across a bustle of activities as he began to see exquisitely designed warships that were much different than what the celestials wielded move across the void of space. These vessels were only similar to the ones Celestials used in shape, seeming more like imitations that could never live up to the real thing when actually put to the test.","He could also sense numerous figures at the void realm or above streaking as lights across the vastness of space, their faces serious as they prepared for something big. Noah glanced at the appearance of these beings from the Dark Expanse as he neared the Verittas Fortress.","They weren’t all that different from the beings it was used to seeing in the Light Expanse, with most of them being humans and the remainder being collective beings of other races. Many of those he came across glanced at the fearsome ten thousand army force that went towards the vast Verittas Fortress.","But they only watched on as relieved expressions actually appeared on their faces, their hearts seeming more at ease as these fearsome looking Infernals appeared in front of them.","This was an extremely stark difference compared to how infernals were viewed in the Light Expanse where they were feared and even told as ghost stories to scare kids. In the Dark Expanse, Infernals were welcomed as they represented a force of protection against the raging celestials!","Noah continued forward until he came across a collection of beings that actually came towards him with their heads bowed down respectfully. The beings had conical hats that would make one assume for them to have the profession that was fairly unique but wide-spread in the Dark Expanse- the profession of a Wizard!","Wizards were also called Mages, beings that wielded incredible magic to affect the essence in their surroundings and produce spectacular spells that could even weave the very reality itself when utilized at their peak.","10 Wizards came bowing towards Noah, stopping his procession of 10,000 infernals. The beings had power at the level of the Soul Forging Realm, the one at the forefront standing at the Domain Expansion Realm speaking.","\"It is an honor to have the aid of an Infernal Lord. Please, let us guide you.\"","The ten beings respectfully pointed towards a certain location, their eyes slightly shaking as they stared at the field of Chaos that the being in front of them freely released. Noah nodded and went along with them, where inn front of his eyes the appearance of this spectacular location known as the Veritas Fortress became apparent.","It was worthy of being called a fortress as shockingly, he found it to be a literal planet-sized fortress that was floating in the void of space. It was not circular like most of the planets he had come across. It actually seemed more like a floating island that was even bigger than his Spiritual World, but this floating island was built in the terms and designs of a unique fortress.","There was a truly exuberant numbers of beings that could be sensed within and around this planet sized Verittas Fortress, being the highest number of beings that Noah had seen clustered in one area at once. Numerous vessels moved around it as beings of all species and races moved in out, the busy bustle of activities only getting wilder as he moved closer.","His eyes observed a purple field of light surrounding this entire fortress that looked to be even bigger than most prime worlds and infinitely neared the rank of a Realm.","Looking at this grandiose Verittas Fortress, he knew that he had arrived in the Dark Expanse. He had arrived at the location where the first battle against the celestials would take place. He had arrived at the location where the 9th Infernal Lord would make his presence known!"]},{"number":470,"title":"Chapter 470: Chapter 469 World!","paragraphs":["As his clone made his entrance in Verittas Fortress, his main body was in the Golden Bastion of the Celestial Realm where he glanced at the [Luminescent Rainbow Dew].","It was a treasure that only two beings would have the chance of consuming, with him holding one, and another being in the hands of the Three-Eyed Fate Child!","It was a treasure that forcefully rose a being’s realm to the World Rank, with the prerequisite that their body would be able to handle it. Noah glanced at this treasure with hungry eyes as he put everything else in the back of his mind, throwing this treasure inside his mouth and swallowing it whole.","RUMBLE!","A rainbow colored light shot out as beautiful colors filled the room he was in, an enormous convergence of essence beginning to wrap around him as he broke all known norms to move to another rank with a speed never before seen.","The Luminescent Rainbow Dew was something that propelled the rank of a being all the way to the World Realm. It was a treasure that was overbearing in nature, something that contained a tremendous amount of energy. This was the reason why in its description, it mentioned that it would only work on someone that could actually bear the wild energy!","This overbearing energy began to spread throughout Noah’s body, the rainbow colors only being an aftereffect as they shot out vibrantly all around his body. He’s Origin Core that was now surrounded by the Fire Origin Core and the Water Origin Core hungrily sensed this energy as it began to absorb it without a second delay.","OOOM!","The Origin Core shook as the domain surrounding it became more and more solidified, its size getting ever so larger as it absorbed the pure energy from the Luminescent Rainbow Dew.","Noah could feel his stats continuing to shoot up as more and more of the energy was absorbed. Whatever barrier existed in the domain expansion realm quickly being hammered down as he infinitely neared the world realm. This was the rank where one contained the singular force of an entire world. It wasn’t to be mistaken of one being a world of themselves or creating a world within their origin. It was the stage where a being with their pure physical force could match that of a normal world!","When one moved past the physical force that it would apply and then took this to their skills and abilities, they were elevated to insane degrees.","WAAA!","Brilliance erupted from him as Noah raised his head high, feeling the shackles of the domain expansion realm breaking as his body stepped into the World Realm! A rank that was actually achieved in a matter of days after his last breakthrough...","The energy of the Luminescent Rainbow Dew still remained in his body as he finished absorbing it, looking at his hands and feet as they glowed bright gold and black. The energies from the law of fate and the law of chaos were resonating the moment he finished his advancement into the realm, his body feeling the power of these laws even more. A calmness returned around him thereafter as he had a smile on his face, sensing the feeling of power that continued to get ever so larger.","This smile remained even when he thought about the Founder that had recently appeared. He thought about this being’s motivations and exactly what he wanted to do. He thought about his words of them being puppets on a huge playground as he had his own ideas on exactly what this Founder meant, but the confidence in himself only grew as he thought about all of it. He rose up as his body felt the coursing strength of an entire world, saying something that only he could hear.","’If this is a playground, what is stopping me from flipping all of it over and making it my own?\"","OOOM!","The reverberation of power gradually calmed as he stepped out of the room he was in and went towards an expensive training hall in the Golden Bastion where he sensed the auras of two particular figures to be sparring.","It was the War Princess Athena, and the other was the opponent who had fallen under his attacks, Grandmaster Light!","Their gazes were filled with battle spirit as they were the only ones to receive lesser treasures than Noah and the Three-Eyed Fate Child. While the two of them had gotten a [Luminescent Rainbow Dew] each, Athena and Light had received Elite Behemoth materials and other treasures that also promoted their strength, but it was nothing remotely close to the effects of the treasure that the two beings who would have found in the final round of the Battle of Geniuses received. The spar was stopped as Athena glanced towards Noah, seeing his body rumbling with power as her gaze only shone with even more spirit.","\"Junior Brother, you’ve actually pulled ahead from me now.\"","Noah smiled at these words as he replied.","\"I’m sure it won’t be for long. Where is the grandmaster?\"","Athena revealed the location of Grandmaster Vredral as Noah left the two sparring Celestials, sensing the gaze of Light boring into his back and ignoring this defeated Special Existence for now as he went to have a discussion with his supposed teacher.","As he had achieved a rank of power greater than many Celestials right now, he was going to ask to move with more freedom in this Celestial Realm! When a celestial reached the level of the World Realm, they were considered a true powerhouses at the peak of power, and the beings that could truly explore the Celestial Realm. He now wanted to be one of these figures.","While his clone was acting as the 9th Infernal Lord and actually stopping the advancement of Celestials in the Dark Expanse, his main body would continue the exploration of the celestial realm as he went through the locations where the Fate Behemoths were abundant, collect more treasures and materials, and even find more inheritances for him to master even more laws. Before all hell broke loose, before he met the founder again as an enemy on the battlefield, he still had many things to do!"]},{"number":471,"title":"Chapter 471: Chapter 470 Stationed and Waiting!","paragraphs":["Noah’s ancient blood clone followed the ten mages towards the Verittas Fortress, the enormous planet-sized fortress becoming bigger and bigger in his eyes as they descended towards a particular location where he could sense the numerous congregation of powerhouses.","As they descended down the smaller details of the Verittas Fortress became apparent in his eyes as he could see ancient styled castles that rose to the skies. The castles seemed to be depictions of the Verittas Fortress itself, just on a much smaller scale as one could see enormous walls surrounding each of the congregations of buildings. It was a unique style of dome-shaped castles that looked like grand churches of an ancient era as they gave off a feeling of ancientness and magic!","Noah could sense a unique type of essence in the air, his mind curious on exactly how differently these beings called wizards or mages lived out their lives. There were a variety of forces in the Dark Expanse that made the Alliance, with those being proficient in magic being the majority.","Some termed themselves Mages, other groups preferred to be called Wizards, Witches, or even Warlocks. But almost all of them utilized mana the same way, just from different ancestry.","He followed the group of robed Wizards towards a grand castle that was placed at the very center of a tightly defended city as he stationed his ten thousand Infernals in a field outside the fortress where the castle was located.","Seeing the Infernal Lord reign in his forces to calmly remain in that area, the leading figure of the ten men pointed forward while speaking.","\"This is one of the central commands of our Verittas Fortress, a place where some of the leaders meet to discuss and plan out the future events.\"","Noah’s clone nodded as they brought him further down, where he was able to find even more numerous bustling figures of mages moving around. Many were clad in dark or purple robes with conical hats above their heads being the only thing that nearly all of them wore.","Far away from this location, you could see other beings that seemed to be coming from different planets, but all were congregating together for the oncoming war. He continued observing his surroundings as the 10 Mages had led him towards the inside of the large castle and into an expansive rectangular hall where a bustle of discussion was underway.","His entrance caused the eyes of many to turn towards him as they had relieved expressions in their eyes. All of them looked at the unique styled infernal crown above Noah’s head, this crown letting them know that this was one of the Infernal Lords that was siding with them in these times of war!","One of the more powerful auras in the room came forward as he nodded towards Noah, the power of this being vibrantly standing at the World Rank. His eyes shimmered with aurora colored lights as the conical hat that he adorned came off as he spoke towards Noah.","\"We are glad for the help. Come, let us brief you on our forces and everything we have so far.\"","Noah nodded impassively as he went towards the wide table where the discussions were taking place, his seat being near this powerful being who introduced himself as Commanding Mage Turner.","This was one of the leaders that was taking the reins of the operation to defend the Verittas Fortress. This Fortress was a place to defend and the place where the Celestials would attack simply because it acted as the doorway that led to many of the parts of the Dark Expanse that were populated by many beings.","If the Verittas Fortress fell, it would mean the free entrance of Celestials further into the Dark Expanse. This would allow them to achieve their goal of getting even more beings under the influence and thus once more increase their power in the law of fate!","Noah listened in to the discussions as he gathered more information about the defenses of the Verittas Fortress and got to understand more about the Mages and Wizards that had the task of defending this enormous gateway of a planet.","After an hour, the discussion came to an end as he became acquainted with the important figures around the Verittas Fortress as well as the forces that they should be expecting in their coming days before the clash with the celestials occurred.","Commanding Mage Turner spoke towards Noah as he led him out of the expansive hall where the discussions were taking place and towards another location in the castle, letting him know that their forces would be continuing to work together and distribute the coming reinforcements, and that they would call upon him and distribute all the information simultaneously whenever the Celestials made a move.","Noah nodded as he sent a command to the waiting Infernal army of 10,000 to remain still outside of the castle. He entered into a grand room that the Commanding Mage Turner directed him to as he wanted to use the few days before the Celestials descended in the Time Space of his Spiritual World to max the proficiencies of his skill trees and upgrade them into the next rank.","He felt ashamed to say that shockingly, his abilities were actually at the soul forging realm when his main body’s power had just reached the World Rank! His realm this time had simply raised too fast that even his skills fell behind.","He planned to use the increased ratio of the Time Space of the Spiritual World to the fullest in the next few days, as even a single day in the outside world would be more than 50 days in the Time Space. Even though the rate of increasing the percentage of his laws would not benefit from the ratio of the time space, his skills would still be able to advance rapidly as long as he placed the time into them.","He had done numerous tests in the past to try and use the loophole of the Time Space to rapidly increase the gathering of Fate Lines and Chaos Particles, but every time he cultivated them inside the Time Space, they still followed the time of the outside world where their rate of gathering was slowed to insane degrees! This made for an event where if the time dilation in the Time space was 1:50 and he spent 50 days in the Time Space, the rate of progress would still be equivalent to the 1 day that passed in the outside world as the descent of Fate Lines and Chaos Particles was slowed by a factor of 50 times.","This simply showed him that the increasing law comprehension always followed the Universal Laws, where even his Time Space could not be used to swiftly make him comprehend the laws to 100% in a matter of days. It was too balance breaking of an idea to even fathom!","These few days that remained before the battle started, he would see if he could bring all of his abilities into the domain expansion realm, and even possibly have a skill tree or two in the World Rank.","He took out the Spiritual World that was anchored to his body and placed it on the ground of the room he was in, entering it thereafter as he began a training session to boost his skills even further before he clashed with the Legion of Celestials.","The coming army of Grandmasters and their Warships had no idea that in the camp that they would soon clash with, they had just created a World Rank combatant by giving him a unique treasure willingly! This same being they continued to foster and raise the strength of was about to oppose them on their conquest of expansion..."]},{"number":472,"title":"Chapter 472: Chapter 471 Fledgling Blood Ancien","paragraphs":["In another location, the Vampyre Ruler Vladivostok had a frustrated expression as his communications with Elena, the one being who had access to the Crixus that shone brightly in the hands of the Celestials-was cut off.","He had sent numerous messages towards her and the forces in the Underworld that he controlled, only to get no replies as time passed!","His troubles seemed to only be compounding, as he knew his position in the Alliance would waver if he could not even maintain a handle on such a powerful spy that they placed into the ranks of Celestials.","He turned towards one of his subordinates as he asked irritatingly.","\"The force towards the Verittas Fortress has set off?\"","\"Yes, Master. The Royal Vampyre Rokku and his forces should arrive within a few hours.\"","The Vampyre Ruler Vladivostok nodded as his red eyes shimmered. He knew this first battle against the Celestials was pivotal, and would even set the tone for the remaining battles that came after.","He had sent numerous Vampyres down to reinforce the defenses of the Mages there, their other forces moving to tighten their defenses in other important areas as they prepared.","He put the thoughts of Crixus aside for now as he focused on the current matters at hand, the vibrant power of this being at the Star Forging Realm moving forward.","---","In the Verittas Fortress, three days had passed as Noah’s clone enjoyed the treatment of the Mages while he trained to max the proficiencies of his skill trees.","While only three days had passed in the outside world, he had spent more than 3 months in the Time Space! This was a truly ridiculous number to even imagine, but it made possible for the rapid advancements of raising proficiencies of skills and then combining them.","Two skill trees had already met the requirements and were taken into the Domain Expansion Realm as he worked double to combine solo skills he wasn’t using into the Domain Rank and then sacrificed them into the skill trees. The other two Skill Trees were not far behind as they only waited for the required sacrificial skills at the moment!","The ones he worked to upgrade first were the [Kin of Ancients] and [Kin of Terror], their advanced skill trees actually taking on similar names as he chose the path where both of them were termed \"Fledgling\".","He advanced these ones first as they would be the ones he would most likely use the most in the coming days, the Arch Lich Ra’Zan and Fate’s Guardian being left behind for now. After these, the next one of great importance that had taken even longer to raise up was the [Agent of Chaos] skill tree that directly opposed the Law of Fate!","But for now, the first one was the [Kin of Ancients] skill tree that had the abilities of the Blood Lord at their base. This skill tree was expanded to a pathway that was called [Fledgling Ancient]!","DOMAIN [Blood Lord] (45/45):: Abilities- Dawn of the Blood Lord(5/5), Blood World(5/5), Drain Life(5/5), and Nightmarish Descent(5/5). >> [Kin of the Ancients] (60/60) :: Ancient Blood Scion(5/5), Ancient Blood Clone(5/5), Summon the Ancients(5/5), Blood Rage(5/5) >>[Fledgling Blood Ancient] (75/75) :: A fledgling of a race of powerful creatures that occupy the Letalis Expanse, the skills of this particular fledgling leaning more towards the control of blood. Abilities Include Blood Summoner(5/5), Blood Clone Support (5/5), Drain Master Support (5/5), and Domination (5/5)","[Blood Summoner] (5/5) :: When the abilities Dawn of the Blood Lord and Ancient Blood Scion are simultaneously active, the user can summon 30 Blood Ancients to aid them.","[Blood Clone Support] (5/5) :: The Ancient Blood Clone is further strengthened, now being able to exhibit 100% of the main body’s strength.","[Drain Life Support] (5/5) :: The Drain Life ability is enhanced, its effects not limited only to attacks dealt as an aura of blood will passively erupt to leech the life force of the targeted enemies around you. The Life Steal effect is increased from 5% to 10%.","[Domination] (5/5) :: The eyes of the Fledgling Blood Ancient release a dominating light that enthralls any with weak souls. The bodies of the dominated can then be controlled to either replenish the Blood Ancient with [Blood Bag], or deal damage to surrounding enemies by [Blood Bomb].","A set of shining new skills were displayed in front of him, his eyes going over them a few times as he largely understood them all without needing to go over them.","The Drain Life Support and Blood Clone Support were straightforward, with the latter being even more useful by granting his Ancient Blood Clone the power to exhibit the entire strength of the main body. This now meant that there were two of him that could effectively release his entire power at full capacity!","Although one would have to wonder, did the previous percentage cap of 60% even limit the clone’s power in any significant way when one thought about the mana available to it?","Noah then moved on to the other two, the Blood Summoner being a fairly unique one as it allowed him to summon 30 new combatants as long as he had two specific skills active. If these Blood Ancients were anywhere close to the power of the Ancients that he could call upon with the [Summon the Ancients] ability, he would not have to worry at all about their fire power.","The last one was the most unique one, the ability called [Domination] that made him actually look forward to trying it out on the battlefield! Shockingly, this ability allowed him to bring to his command those with weak souls, and those dominated souls only had a single fate- the blood and body be used to replenish him or as explosions to damage those around them!","It seemed like a very flashy and destructive skill that he could not wait to put to use when imagining the Legions of Celestials nearing this location.","With this skill upgrade, he sadly did not come across any other Guider type jobs similar to the [Unruly Guider] ability that stemmed from [Fate’s Guardian], and this stood the same as he glanced at the upgraded skill tree of the Kin of Terror, which had added 4 new abilities under the next advancement- [Fledgling Aether Terror]!"]},{"number":473,"title":"Chapter 473: Chapter 472 Advancing Legion","paragraphs":["On the 7th celestial star, Grandmaster Ramiel had just left a hidden underground prison where a certain individual lay with his body pierced with numerous golden spikes. He had gone down to this underground area to once again one sidedly monologue towards his teacher about the recent events, as well as the initiation of a war that he would be at the forefront of.","When he left the golden cage that continued to seep the strength of the powerful figure, Grandmaster Ramiel once more missed the hidden smile that had appeared on the bleeding and disfigured being’s face.","This had been the last time that this Grandmaster was going down to ramble to his teacher, the last time that he would converse with one of the founders of Celestials.","Unbeknownst to grandmaster Ramiel, this was also the last time that he would see his master, because in the journey that this Grandmaster was about to undertake, he would not get the chance to return to this Celestial Star!","But this knowledge was not one that was privy to him at this moment as he left the Celestial Star with a strong demeanor. He looked at the celestials around him as they all boarded numerous prime warships, the single 7th Celestial Star forming one of the small squadrons that were going to combine with the large Legion that someone from the celestial realm would be leading towards the Dark Expanse.","RUMBLE!","Grandmaster Ramiel gazed at the numerous prime warships that littered the void of space, the procession of beings from the Celestial Realm passing near the 7th Celestial Star as his job was to only combine in their ranks and follow along in this venture.","All the Celestials were under the lead of Grandmaster Onillus, a being in the World Realm and someone that had more than three million fate lines thrumming strongly in his body!","If Grandmaster Ramiel could be considered just at the entrance of the World Realm, then Grandmaster Onillus was nearing its peak as the time that he spent in the Celestial Realm granted him versatile skills and abilities, as well as improving his techniques in the law of fate.","This was why the Founder had chosen this Grandmaster to be the one that led the forces in the first battle of this war. It was because this being was looked at with extreme confidence as it was someone that participated in the war more than a thousand years ago and knew the ins and outs of being a commander!","The many prime worships that would make any surrounding planets tremble continued on moving as Grand Master Ramiel entered the largest one at the forefront. This was the main vessel that contained many of the leading grandmasters. One could sense numerous powerhouses at the World Realm, with the majority being at the domain expansion realm and even more at this soul forging realm. But the largest percentages were of course those of the void rank.","A stark difference in the legion that was being led towards the Verittas Fortress in this war compared to the previous war was that the head count for the celestials was actually rather small when one compared to the numbers of individuals that came from numerous Prime Worlds that were also currently moving within the Celestial Legion!","The Celestial Legion had not yet reached the Verittas Fortress because they were passing through Specific regions in the Light Expanse collecting more and more powerful figures from chosen Prime Worlds that were selected to provide soldiers for this first conflict.","As they moved across the Light Expanse, in just a few days the number of celestials actually became the minority in this advancing force as hundreds of thousands of powerhouses at the void realm from numerous prime worlds came under their banner.","Those capable steered their own vessels towards the dark expanse with even more being taken into the prime warships of the Celestials. The forces from the World of Cultivation were even more vibrant as they were actually given special treatment from the Celestials. The reason was because the World of Cultivation was the place where the being with Noble Fate who would soon enter the ranks of experts, Crixus, came from!","Those especially proud were the cultivators from the Profound Astral Sect, especially the Elder that was Crixus’s father who enjoyed a position as the leading figure that was overseeing the forces of the World of Cultivation. The power of the Profound Astral Sect had gradually expanded in the cultivation world because of the shining name of Crixus, and now they found themselves serving at the forefront as they actually saw this chance as an honor.","Their gazes were those of responsibility and slight fear, as all that they knew was that they were going to defend their home. They were going to defend their Light Expanse from the hands of the savages that had already made two prime worlds disappear. They had acted and somehow taken the lives and the entire world that was formerly known as the Magus world and even more recently they had entered the wondrous celestial realm and caused conflict while also erasing another powerful prime world that was known as the Underworld.","Many of the forces from the numerous prime worlds were acting under this assumption, as this was the only news and propaganda that the Celestials had spread, a propaganda that began the moment the Founder declared war after the Battle of Geniuses!","A majority of them knew that they were going in this war to defend their homes, but those even more knowledgeable and those that could see behind the scenes knew that they were only pieces being played on a chessboard. But could they refuse? Could they say no?","They had lesser power and they had no strength, so they could only go along as a grand procession passed through the Light Expanse as it looked like a large blade that pointed itself towards the Dark Expanse!"]},{"number":474,"title":"Chapter 474: Chapter 473 Fledgling Aether Terror!","paragraphs":["Back in the dwelling that Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone was staying at in the Verittas Fortress, he was looking at the advancement of the skill tree that stemmed from [Lesser Cthulhu]. It was the skill tree that made many of the things he had at this moment possible, being the one that opened the doorway for him to become an Infernal Lord!","After Kin of Terror, the next name that came with 4 new abilities was termed [Fledgling Aether Terror]! The other skill tree that he could have chosen from was something called [Devouring Aether Beast], but he stuck to the names that continued to lead towards the terrifying being that he only knew from his memories. The abilities of [Fledgling Aether Terror] did not disappoint.","DOMAIN [Amorphous Space Beast] (15/15) :: Abilities- Spatial Cage(5/5), Destabilize(5/5), Shattered Star(5/5), and Miniature Space(5/5). >> [Lesser Cthulhu] (45/45) :: Additional Abilities- Morph(5/5), Child of Space(5/5), Portals of Terror(5/5), and Sever(5/5). >> [Kin of Terror] (60/60) :: Additional Abilities- Aether Reinforcement (5/5), Multiplicative Ray Support (5/5), Triple on Cast Support (5/5), Lunacy Inducement (5/5) >> [Fledgling Aether Terror] (75/75) :: Additional Abilities- Aether Emission (5/5), Aether Chain Support (5/5), Fatal Ailment Support (5/5), Size Distortion (5/5)","Aether Emission (5/5) :: The body of the Fledgling Aether Terror passively emits the baleful energies of Aether. This ability also allows the boosts of [Aether Reinforcement] to apply to any skills used by the Fledgling Aether Terror.","Aether Chain Support (5/5) :: The Aether Rays emitted by the Fledgling Aether Terror can chain between selected enemies. Supported ray-based abilities can chain +10 times","Fatal Ailment Support (5/5) :: The essence of Aether is destructive by nature, causing chaos in the body of those affected. All abilities preceding and following the Fledgling Aether Terror skill tree deal an additional 70% damage over time as Aether continues to cause chaos in their bodies.","Size Distortion (5/5) :: Striving for unmatched strength, the body of the Fledgling Aether Terror can be expanded up to 250 meters.","As soon as Noah finished placing all the required Infernal Skill Points into the newly opened Fledgling Aether Terror skill tree, he felt his already strong body rumble with power as the energy of Aether leaked freely from him!","WAA!","The baleful energy caused the air to scream as those within the grand castle he was situated in also felt an oppressive aura of energy coming from the location where an Infernal Lord was residing, their faces actually filling up with happiness as they sensed this fearsome power, as it actually brought them comfort when they thought about the coming enemies.","Noah reeled in the Aether to only stay within a meter around him as it seemed to just continue expanding, his gaze going towards the additional skills after this skill tree was brought up to the Domain Rank.","The [Aether Emission] was what explained what just occurred with his body, so he moved on directly to the skills that had ’Support’ attached to them as he was coming to particularly love these types of skills more and more.","Those with the addition of ’Support’ always enhanced his current abilities to even greater heights, not simply adding more and more skills for him to try and keep track of and maybe not even use as time passed.","The two support abilities this time were [Aether Chain Support] and [Fatal Ailment Support]! The former made it so that when he released the numerous rays of Aether through [Sever] that was already enhanced by [Multiplicative Ray Support], these Aether rays would actually chain between the bodies of up to 10 enemies!","This caused for a shocking lethality as the rays of Aether were already destructive enough, but were now made even more insane. The [Fatal Ailment Support] was another unique support skill that was equivalent to poisoning any being he hit with abilities from this skill tree as they would suffer damage over time. This damage over time would continue until their death or if they somehow had the means to purify the baleful energy of Aether from their bodies. Again, it simply made his abilities all the more terrifying!","This was the reason why he particularly loved skill trees, and would continue to pursue them to their peak until he saw just how crazy all of these abilities could become.","The last skill was a simple one, [Size Distortion] allowing him to expand his size to actually become 5 times the normal mountainous size of Behemoths. It granted him the ability to expand up to 250 meters! It was ridiculous to even imagine his size larger than the Behemoths he was fighting, so he was excited to try this ability in the coming battle when he faced hundreds of thousands of enemies.","As his thoughts were coming to a close, he received a message from the Spiritual World System.","[Master, the Hydromancer’s Mantle Supreme Treasure has finished being forged.]","The sweet words of even more spectacular things occurring rang in his eyes as his figure disappeared into the miniaturized Spiritual World and went directly towards the Blacksmith’s Forge.","Inside the expansive Forge that was now much bigger than when he first entered it, there were numerous shining armors and weapons that were beautifully placed on the walls of the Forge.","The Items forged from the materials of Infernals and Behemoths that were not yet distributed to his subordinates were all grandly displayed in the Forge, the workshop turning into a brilliant showcase of powerful armors as Noah went towards the one that shone with a luminescent blue brilliance.","The [Hydromancer’s Mantle] looked like a blue battle robe that fully covered the wearer from head to toe, even having a fearsome looking helm with a design only veteran commanders would be adorned in. Blue runic sigils swam around the Mantle mystically as it gave off a feeling of power and strength!","Noah’s eyes shone as he neared the [Hydromancer’s Mantle] to take a look at exactly what abilities and boosts it provided. Would it be as crazy as the Trident of the Sea, or something even more wondrous?"]},{"number":475,"title":"Chapter 475: Chapter 474 Hydromancers Mantle","paragraphs":["Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone thoughtfully stared at the description of the newly forged Supreme Treasure, [Hydromancer’s Mantle], that was floating serenely in the Blacksmith’s Forge.","[Hydromancer’s Mantle] :: A supreme treasure geared towards extreme defense, absorbing any attacks thrown at it as the wearer experiences extreme comfort. Abilities include Sea Domain, Hydromancer’s Banner, Hydomancer’s Pride, Seaborn","[Sea Domain] (Active) :: With the user at the center, the surrounding 1 mile can instantly be turned into a domain of the sea. Within this Domain, the wearer of Hydromancer’s Mantle absorbs 50% of all damage and reflects 20% more, while the enemies are granted the Slow and Restrictive skill effect. The Defense of the user is tripled in the Sea Domain.","[Hydromancer’s Banner] (Active) :: A banner of the one loved by water descends on the battlefield, granting the Aura of Water and Seafarer abilities to all those standing with the Hydromancer that allows them to move unhindered in the Sea Domain while enhancing their abilities.","[Hydromancer’s Pride] (Passive) :: +500% Physical and Magic Defense, +300% Water Element Resistance, 5% Chance to block all damage.","[Seaborn] (Passive) :: The wearer of the Hydromancer’s Mantle is loved by water, granting them 100% comprehension speed when trying to understand the Law of Water.","Noah’s eyes stared carefully at the blue shining mantle as numerous ideas about the abilities shown passed through his mind.","[When forging, I tried to steer the resulting abilities towards things that you did not already have, the results being somewhat satisfactory.]","The voice of the Spiritual World System rang out as Noah smiled.","\"This is more than enough.\"","Yes, this was more than enough! The abilities were stupendous, especially [Seaborn] that insanely doubled his comprehension in the Law of Water! He was currently working to refine Soul Jades from the Water Crystal materials he had obtained while traversing the southern area of the Celestial Realm in order to use them on the neglected [Lawful Nourishment] item that he received from the Karmic Sect Leader in order to increase the rate at which he comprehended the laws.","The future plan was to find the equivalent materials to enable him to collect numerous crystals of all the laws he was working on to further enhance his speed, so he never expected an item to actually just casually double his rate of progress in one law.","If the Hydromancer’s Mantle gave just this, he would have been happy. But it did even more as grand abilities like Sea Domain, Hydromancer’s Pride, and Hydromancer’s Banner appeared to further protect him and reinforce his power.","Noah’s clone wasted no time as his hands reached towards the Supreme Treasure, adorning it for the first time to see its spectacular descriptions in action!","---","As legions moved closer and closer towards each other, Noah’s main body was moving alone in the celestial realm.","Grand Master Vredral had looked at this disciple with shining and proud eyes when he stepped into a realm that was even above his own and was even courteous enough to ask his teacher still for the permission to explore the Celestial Realm by himself. The Grandmaster had shaken his head proudly as he waved his hands telling Noah that he could do whatever he wished!","He was an expert at the World Realm now and that title came with a status. A status that would first award him the title of a Grandmaster even though his fate lines had yet to reach and exceed 100,000. Before he left the Golden Bastion, Noah had received the Golden Robe that was adorned by the many Grandmasters of this Celestial Realm.","In the span of a few months after Noah first stepped onto the seventh Celestial Star as a disciple, in this short period of time he had actually risen from that lowly rank and had gotten the name of a Celestial, and now held the proud name of a Grandmaster.","Of course, this meant nothing to him as he left the Golden Bastion adorned in the golden robe and went further south of the Celestial Realm to begin exploring and hunt down behemoths in full. Even as people neared war, he still had to strengthen himself and his forces, where now a majority of the Harbingers of Sin were in the Soul Forging Realm with not a single one in the Domain Expansion Realm.","The current plan was to of course explore the uniqueness of this Celestial Realm while obtaining the cores and skills of Behemoths that he could absorb himself and also pass down to his subordinates.","He had already been on this venture for the past three days, having actually come across more than 20 Fate Behemoths.","These celestial beasts that were proficient in the law of fate would have been particularly difficult for Elite Explorations Teams to take care of, as they were more than likely more proficient in the law of fate than the Celestials that were following the inheritance of the disciple of fate.","But for Noah, these beasts that were in the Domain Expansion Realm fell under his abilities very easily!","The ones he came across were the same mountainous beasts that towered over 50 or 60 meters, with their traits being very similar to the animals from his homeworld that he had always come across before with their major difference being in color, and of course power.","Among the ones he had seen was a golden Phoenix that he took down through using attacks that were layered with the power of chaos, making sure that he had [Unique Origin] active and other covert skills so that even if someone was watching, they would not be able to understand the true extent of his power. This was simply him being more careful, and he most likely did not have anything to worry about.","He met a variety of fate behemoths the past few days, each of them holding golden feathers or golden furs with their skills being resplendent as they utilized the law of fate.","As for the loot, these Behemoths did not just drop cores, but they also dropped fancy-looking skills related to the law of fate that were not contained under the [Fate’s Guardian] skill tree. Many of these skills utilized mana to either form offensive abilities or defensive abilities in the forms of shields or weapons. An example of some of the skill books that he obtained were [Blades of Fate], [Fate Armor], [Golden Berserker], and a few more abilities that were unique to the type of celestial beasts themselves.","There were various abilities, but in his eyes none of them even came close to the abilities under the Fate’s Guardian skill tree that continued to expand more and more, each of the abilities within them boosting the entire skill tree to unimaginable levels. The percentage of boosts from these skills already at the Domain Rank actually did not even match the compounded boosts he was receiving from just a single skill in the still Soul Rank Skill Tree.","If he were to pay attention to all of these skills that dropped as loot from the fate behemoths and even the many other beings they had taken down, he would have thousands of skills in his stat panel without even knowing which one to use or utilize. So, many of these skills would be used as sacrificial skills for [Skill Combination] and to bring up his powerful skill trees to even greater heights, with the rest being given to his subordinates for them to gain equivalent level skills for when he granted them cores of the Domain Expansion Realm as well.","RUMBLE!","Yet another fate behemoth fell as the brilliant light of loot erupted from it, cores and skill books erupting out as they quickly turned into lights and faded away, entering Noah’s Expansive Space in the span of a millisecond.","All of the beasts that he had taken down could be considered Elite Behemoths and there were still all in the domain expansion realm. For him to meet the beasts above that, those that were titled Supreme Behemoths, he had to venture deep into the Celestial Realm to even come across these powerful celestial beasts that were at the World Rank or even more terrifyingly above that.","But this would all come later, as his focus now remained on hunting more Behemoths!"]},{"number":476,"title":"Chapter 476: Chapter 475 A Sense of Pressure!","paragraphs":["Noah’s main body continued moving as the cores and the skill books that he placed in the Expansive Space were then quickly accessed by his clone and transferred into Spiritual World for his subordinates to use right away.","The ones prioritized were the Harbingers of Sin, as well as beings like Elena. The domain expansion rank cores and skill books would be even more useful to them as they didn’t have the ability to very rapidly max proficiencies of their skill trees and upgrade them as quickly as Noah could. So even with the rapid power leveling that he continued to do with them, their skill trees almost always lacked behind their ranks because of how fast they rose.","He would keep a sufficient amount of Domain Expansion Realm skill books to use as sacrificial skills for his skill trees and give the rest to his people for them to be able to use powerful skills at the level that they enter. He planned to strengthen his subordinates well and have a few of them enter the Domain Expansion Realm and actually participate in the coming conflict of the Celestial Legions and the Legions of Mages, Wizards, Vampyres, and Infernals waiting for them at the Verittas Fortress.","He had also prepared numerous sets of armors from Flame Behemoths and from Infernals for them to equip, along with some completed Chaos Sets made from the many chaos behemoth materials that he had been collecting while hunting with Athena and the Righteous Fire Exploration Team before the tournament.","Only three of the Chaos Sets were able to be completed, and the three strongest combatants that entered into the Domain Expansion Realm before the war began would be given for them to wear.","His main body continued forward in this Celestial Realm as he hunted more behemoths and kept an eye out for any treasures. His gaze was bright as he waited for his clone that could now move with 100% of his strength to clash with the coming Celestials!","---","The first thing that was eye-catching was the scintillating colors that now surrounded his body, the passive emission of the purple Aether from the Fledgling Aether Terror abilities and the sparkling blue water elements constantly given off by the Hydromancer’s Mantle giving off an eerily beautiful contrast when also putting into account his devilishly handsome looks.","The Hydromancer’s Mantle had a particularly unique style as one could almost feel as if waves of clear blue water were constantly moving at the edges of the blue mantle.","His body shone with an aura of a boss monster that he would only find in late game content of the games he used to play in the past, this type of boss monster being able to drop the most valuable loot!","Noah found himself smiling as his thoughts briefly went back to times of extreme ignorance and bliss, times when he could just play games and read novels while he went on with his life.","Those were the times when his mind was free with no responsibilities whatsoever on his shoulders, his life simply going along with the flow as he enjoyed the things around him.","A slight look of reminiscence appeared on his face as he quickly shook himself out of it and breathed out, adopting a serious expression as he thought about the current him.","He was still going along with the flow of things, even moving himself to steer their flow and the flow of fate to the direction he wanted. And now, the things he would have considered to only be in his wildest dreams and as just fantasy were actually right in front of his eyes!","So he shook himself out as he stopped reminiscing and made himself focus on the task at hand, his heart set on continuing forward.","As expected, while wearing the Hydromancer’s Mantle, the progression of the Law of Water had nearly doubled, with the water particles rushing towards him much faster than the fire particles.","Even though the Seaborn effect was only for the Law of Water, the faster progression also propelled the opposing fire elements to run slightly faster!","The clone nodded its head as he continued on for another few hours before the tests came to a stop, his figure disappearing as his main body had placed yet another bountiful loot in the Expansive Space.","He waved his hands to take it out as his figure reappeared next to powerful auras of numerous beings training in the Time Space of the Spiritual World.","The Harbingers of Sin and the powerful Spiritual World Beasts were all here training to break past the Soul Rank and step into the Domain Rank as this was the prerequisite that Noah had set for anyone that wanted to participate in the war at the Verittas Fortress!","He was unconsciously becoming more and more protective as he saw that anyone in the Soul Forging Realm only had a chance of surviving in the coming war, and he didn’t want any deaths that could be easily prevented.","A particularly arrogant Emperor Penguin raised its beak towards its master as it swallowed a Domain Rank Core, its flippers sticking out with no shame as Noah waved his hands for another similarly ranked core to fly towards him.","He pulled out more and more Domain Rank Cores that his main body continued to place in the expansive space as he hunted down Behemoths, all of them going towards his subordinates as he could sense the auras of many of them about to spill over into the next realm soon.","The Spiritual World Beasts entering into the Domain Rank was an even better situation as it signified that one of the requirements for the next upgrade of the Spiritual World was complete, the only thing remaining being the obtainment of a Large World Core.","This was something Noah would worry about for later as he focused on the current events, continuing the preparations for the war as besides giving his subordinates numerous Cores and Skill Books, he put the task of designating the Item Sets to the Spiritual World System whenever one of them stepped into the next rank.","Among the subordinates currently training, a few others were not in the Time Space as they were busy stabilizing the newly connected Underworld and moving around the Spiritual World thereafter, with others still looking over the many new worlds that were now connected.","He was not the only one busily moving, the forces he was connected to all feeling a sense of pressure as they collectively moved towards a brighter future!"]},{"number":477,"title":"Chapter 477: Chapter 476 Ahh! My Progenitor!","paragraphs":["Elena was floating in the skies of the Spiritual World as her face was that of immense wonder and infatuation.","A few days ago, her Progenitor- nay, her Master, had brought her into this wondrous land once more after saving them from the clutches of the Celestial Founder.","Her Master had actually duplicated his body as he ingeniously still kept his identity as a Celestial while also working against them simultaneously to save her and many others from certain death!","It was something beautiful and resplendent, something that only her Progenitor would be able to do!","She had great worries about her little brother in the Underworld the moment the Celestial Founder called for its destruction, and her Master had somehow been able to do something as ridiculous as teleport the entire Prime World away while dominating its core at the same time.","It was at this moment that Elena realized that she really did not know her Progenitor as much as she thought she did!","What type of being could subjugate entities that were the centers of entire worlds? Who could then even teleport such an enormous entity to an entirely different quadrant in the Light Expanse?","What energy was required?! What grandeur! What magnificence!","’Ahh! My Progenitor!’","She found her hands clutching her chest as her thoughts went in this direction while she floated in the skies of the Spiritual World.","She had already stabilized the newly added Underworld as she gained the knowledge that her Progenitor already had numerous worlds like this connected, each of them with their own set of beings that were all being taken care of by him.","She flew along the paradisical worlds as her gaze traveled to the Central Continent of the Spiritual World and flew towards a certain location there.","Not to just mention the four floating Continents that were beautifully seen all around her, she actually found the Central Continent to be more wondrous as within it, she found the unbelievable land known as the Time Space, as well as the location where her Progenitor created fearsome armors and weapons that nobody else had ever seen.","But even more than this was the collection of portals that one could find at a particular area of the Spiritual World.","Her eyes gazed upon different colored portals that were ordered in a circular manner on a large snowy clearing.","There were names floating above these portals that would make one tremble when they realized exactly what their meaning was. She could see the titles above the portals as such- [Demon World Portal], [Ancient Blood World Portal], [Beast World Portal], [Underworld Portal]...","Her shining eyes saw many of such portals spectacularly laid out, figures of beings of different colors and races occasionally seeing coming in and out of these portals as they actually transferred from these many worlds and into the Spiritual World.","Almost all of the beings coming in and out of these portals had one singular thing on their faces- wonder and amazement as they came and went with their own assigned jobs.","Many of them did not even have jobs perse, as what they were doing was simply coming into the Spiritual World to be granted paradisiacal Medicinal Herbs and Fruits that were spread out all across the Spiritual World.","This was another thing that caused Elena’s heart to beat even faster. In the Spiritual World, she found that across all the continents, the majority of their lands were covered by farming fields that had shimmering fruits and herbs filled with essence growing within!","Aside from the Spiritual World beasts that enjoyed these medicinal herbs and fruits the most, the beings entering and leaving the Spiritual World were coming and going mostly for these resources as they took them back to their own worlds.","She had seen her Master’s figure travel through the fantastical floating landmasses of the Spiritual World as he went to each of these fields and waved his hands above them. Every time he did this, a green light would descend down and wrap around the medicinal herbs or trees, causing them to have rapid growth and achieve maturity in a matter of minutes compared to the days or months that were required.","He had such a wide array of abilities that Elena wondered, could she be able to find something that her Master could not do?","Even something as simple as cooking- the one time that she tasted it she nearly blacked out from pleasure! She even found herself wondering why he would even excel in something like cooking, but it just added to the charm that he had! But the wonder of him being a farmer on the side overtook her mind momentarily as her thoughts wandered even more.","Her Progenitor was so magnificent that he actually took the time to be a farmer and plant all of these wondrous things for them, things that were actually filled with so much essence that one could consider them prized treasure gardens of powerful sects.","Yet all of them could freely be seen spread out in the Spiritual World as the followers of her Master enjoyed them to the fullest while also using them to bolster the strength of the many worlds her Master was connected to.","The more she learned about her Master, the more reverence and infatuation Elena had as she found her fangs unintentionally coming out while she licked her lips.","She closed her eyes in the skies above the portals where many beings went in and out, ignoring their gazes as she recalled the sensation of her Progenitor sucking blood from her weeks ago. That amazing feeling she was able to feel then...she had not gotten the privilege to feel it again ever since!","She reminisced as she wondered.","’My Progenitor, just when will you feed on me again? My blood is quite good you know? Ahhh...’","The matter of feeding war paramount, especially to the Vampyre Progenitor. She felt like he had been suppressing his urges for far too long, and the day that he chose to get lost in them would be the day to remember.","Her eyes were closed as her body wiggled curvecously in the air, her mind filled with her Progenitor as her thoughts soon went towards those closest to him.","Her face instantly turned hard as she thought about the women around her Master. The closest ones she could see was the one called Barbatos- all she saw in her eyes was a small woman with somewhat decent looks, but she would never question the tastes of her Master. This Barbatos was simply too lazy in her eyes, only training and accompanying her Master when he had the time, but the way she referred to him was not the way one should address someone such as him!","The other was a fair little queen known as Adelaide who always came to her Master with a shy expression that just asked to be spoiled. Her royal countenance was always reserved around others, but one could see a much rosier appearance whenever she was around the Progenitor. This one seemed to at least fit Elena’s requirements, but there were still many things to be worked on.","All of these women surrounding her Master seemed gorgeous and perfect to others, but to her- they weren’t enough!","Does nobody not know the majesty of her Progenitor? Do they really think his desires would be satisfied by the presence of merely two women?!","Her Progenitor was someone grand that was already taking over numerous worlds, with a future that many of them could barely even imagine!","Soon enough, even these women would start to find themselves inadequate in the presence of her Master, and that was when she would go in to allow her Master to do whatever he wished with her. If it was high quality blood- she had it! Anything else- she had it!","She would accompany him to her death as she carefully chose the beings deserving to be around him and experience his grandeur with her.","This was the future she awaited for with her Master, her cloudy eyes clearing up as she thought of this, her figure disappearing from the area of the portals as she went on to join the others that continued to be spoiled with treasures from her Master.","She did not even have the patience to reply to the figure leading the Vampyres in the Dark Expanse, the Vampyre Ruler Vladivostok, as she focused on her own strength. His message was releasing commands that were filled with bloodline power to ask her to reply or return, but this Vladivostok did not know that someone way above him had already given separate commands to her. If a subject received the command of the King and then received another set of commands from another subject of the King, who would she listen to?","’Hmph!’","The powerful figure overseeing the Clans of Vampyres in the Dark Expanse at the Star Forging Realm was just like another subordinate of her Master. So what if he was a whole rank above the World Realm? What if he had lived for thousands of years?","As her Master was now playing the Dark Expanse, she knew that the entire faction of Vampyres that made up the Dark Expanse would soon fall into his hands. After all, who could deny their Progenitor? Who would be able to look at the being with the purest bloodline of Vampyres alive and say no to him?","She was one of the few permitted to feel this reverence, so she knew she had to work hard. She also had to increase her strength if she wanted to be around him!","In the skies above the portals that she just left, the beings moving below finally breathed out again as they went on with their tasks once more, whispering words only a few of them could hear.","\"Who was that demoness wriggling her body in the skies?!\"","\"You...shut up and move faster. You don’t want to offend any of the experts under the Spiritual World Master, do you? It doesn’t matter how weird they are!\"","\"Stop gawking and hurry you fools!\"","Hushed words passed between them as their bodies brimming with strength from Noah’s all around buff caused by the Golden Guider coursed through them, their gazes bright as they moved across the Spiritual World while also seeing a bright future ahead of them!","Many of the beings from the numerous connected worlds that were granted permission to enter the Spiritual World only knew of Noah from those that stood at the upper echelons of their worlds, with very few of them actually coming in contact with him.","But they all knew of his grandeur and power as they worked diligently, grateful to be placed under such a person’s wings!","As these numerous beings continued to have their lives changes affected, their fates steered towards directions entirely different than what was ordained, the one responsible would continue to benefit immensely as time passed.","The Founder was able to increase his power and Fate Lines by indirectly influencing and changing the lives of many worlds in the Light Expanse, and his power had risen to the peak of many in the Novus Galaxy in the past thousand years. What of someone like Noah who was directly and actively steering the fates of numerous planets and their inhabitants then? How long would it take him to scramble to the top as he continued to expand his scope of influence?!"]},{"number":478,"title":"Chapter 478: Chapter 477 Dark Guider!","paragraphs":["Another day passed in the outside world as Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone was able to bring yet another skill tree to the next rank, this time being particularly exciting as yet another Guider Type job appeared in front of his eyes!","When the prerequisite sacrificial skills were given with the skill tree hitting maximum proficiency, the options of either [Chaos Guider] or [Chaos Relegator]. He naturally chose the one that had the name of Guider, seeing how the previous selection of [Unruly Guider] under the skill tree aligned with the Law of Fate granted him ridiculous abilities. He placed all the required skill points as he viewed the new additions at their peak.","DOMAIN [Agent of Chaos](60/60) :: The title of an Agent of anything is a rare one. This skill tree gives its user the ability to confidently call themselves an Agent of Chaos. Abilities include Essence Disruptor(5/5), Chaotic Mandate(5/5), Chaos Orbs(5/5), and Void of Impending Doom(5/5). >> [Chaos Guider] (75/75) :: A path of a being that revels in unpredictability and the comfort of chaos. Additional Abilities Include Dark Guider (5/5), Chaos Bearer (5/5), Aura of Chaos (5/5), Desecrate (5/5)","[Dark Guider] (5/5) :: All the beings that are following the rule of the Chaos Guider are blessed with his source of strength as a portion of the user’s aura of chaos surrounds them. To those classified as Subordinates of the Chaos Guider: +120% Physical, Soul, and Elemental Damage, +120% Cast and Attack Speed, +120% All Element Resistance, +120% Defense.","[Chaos Bearer] (5/5) :: Any chaos that the Chaos Guider causes is amplified, granting them +50% increased comprehension in the Law of Chaos.","[Aura of Chaos] (5/5) :: The distinct aura of chaos wraps around the body of the Chaos Guider and allows for all cast abilities and skills to be layered with the chaos element. +100% Chaos Damage to all utilized abilities.","[Desecrate] (5/5) :: A wide area ability that creates a Desecrated Space where Chaos Elements are abundant as far as the eyes of the Chaos Guider can see. Within this Desecrated Space, the Fear, Slow Mana Regulation, Debilitated, and Blind debuff effects are applied to all enemies.","Abilities that satisfied his heart were shown in front of his eyes, once more granting him a wide array of extra abilities that he could utilize on the coming battlefield. His enemies were beings proficient in the law of fate this time around, and the opposing abilities of the law of chaos would be one of the best counters.","When he saw the [Aura of Chaos] and [Desecrate] abilities, a smile appeared on his lips as these abilities essentially allowed all of his attacks to be layered with the power of Chaos, as well as release a wide debuff domain that further lowered his enemy’s defenses and even granted them horrible debilitating effects.","Then there was the [Chaos Bearer] ability that actually enhanced his rate of progression in the Law of Chaos! This was similar to the ability that the Hydromancer’s Mantle provided, but cut by half. It was an unexpected surprise as the gathering of Chaos Particles always lagged behind the Fate Lines.","This was because he initially began with the law of fate, and he also had the [Fate Stealer] ability which allowed him to actually get 12% of the Fate Essence of the beings that he killed. In the upcoming battle, it was actually this single ability that excited him the most!","With the thousands of Celestials coming towards him, especially the big bosses like Grandmaster Onillus that had more than 3 million Fate Lines...he was actually going to increase his progression in the Law of Fate at a pace that would break any remaining common sense in the Novus Galaxy.","In his eyes, he foresaw himself easily passing the 1 million mark, and even going above it just with this single coming battle! That was how domineering this [Fate Stealer] ability was!","His progress in the Law of Chaos was bound to be left in the dust, but it would still increase even faster because of the newly gained [Chaos Bearer] ability.","The last ability that did not just give him joy, but granted even more happiness to his subordinates was the [Dark Guider] ability.","They were already boosted by the [Golden Guider] from the skill tree stemming from the Law of Fate, and now there was another Guider Type ability that essentially doubled the boosts they already had!","At the same time, they now had the auras of both Fate and Chaos coursing through their bodies. This was an aura of two Supreme Laws that were freely coursing through the bodies of billions of beings...at this point in time, even Noah himself would not fully know the effects of this until much later.","RUMBLE!","The instant the ability was activated, Noah felt the surging of Fate Lines and Chaos Particles once more as he greatly influenced billions of beings, some in more ways than he expected as huge changes occurred throughout the planets he was connected to once more!","In the quadrant of Light Expanse where numerous of the connected Worlds were hidden behind layers of a Veil, essence dispersed freely as the singular addition of another Guider Ability caused another Supreme Law to descend onto these worlds, their targets being the numerous inhabitants of these worlds that fell under the category of Noah’s \"Subordinates\".","When the prior [Golden Guider] from the Law of Fate was activated, the multitude of beings had experienced a period of rapid advancement in their strength as with the backing of a Supreme Law, they were able to do things they never considered before. With the widespread project of creating dungeons not just in Noah’s homeworld but in the many connected worlds, the phenomenon of beings diving in dungeons to enhance their strength only propagated further.","With the boost of [Golden Guider], those diving in dungeons saw firsthand how they could defeat monsters that were a rank above their own as they took advantage of the boon and became rapidly stronger. Yet at this moment, as if the first boon was not enough, [Dark Guider] arrived and brought with it another Supreme Law!","Dark auroras of pure chaos energy descended onto the numerous worlds and wrapped around their inhabitants, another point of widespread change occurring as it was not just the addition of another law to their bodies. It was the inclusion and utter synchronization of two opposing Supreme Laws in the bodies of billions of beings that could be considered relatively weak.","It was something that should have never have the chance of happening, but it did! And it brought with it too many changes and opportunities...","Noah was about to look into everything that was changing when he felt the presence of the Mages in the castle he was supposed to be in come closer, stopping his strengthening session as his body teleported away from the Spiritual World and into the room.","\"Lord, our scouts have begun to see the Legions of the Celestials. Commanding Mage Turner has tasked us to ask to grace the other Commanders with your presence!\"","The words of a strong mage rang in his ears as he waved his hands, the many fearsome and colorful skill effects of numerous elements that surrounded his body gradually fading and turning invisible as he opened the door and followed the inviting Mages.","He would let the worlds and beings he was connected to experience the changes as he enjoyed the boons from it himself as time passed, setting his gaze towards this coming battle for now.","His aura spread out from the location he was in as he sensed even more forces within the expansive Verittas Fortress, the auras of many new Vampyres from the Dark Expanse being apparent, as well as numerous more powerhouses he had yet to come across.","The unique attire of the Mages and Wizards along with the shimmering wands they carried beneath their robes gave Noah a mystical fantasy feel of this Dark Expanse, especially the wide and dark halls of the dreary castle he was walking in.","It reminded him of the imaginative stories he used to read in the past about the grand abodes of wizards with pointed hats that lived in the darkness of the world. The castles of these actual Mages and Wizards of the Dark Expanse had their own unique style, their halls lined up with small floating shining lights that added on to the air of magic and mystery.","There was a bustle of activities everywhere they went as Noah saw floating animals that he recalled to be Familiars of Wizards move along with them, his observation also seeing the unique way these beings used magic as he could see floating utensils cooking by themselves when he passed a dining hall, or things link ink brushes and pens moving on their own to write manuscripts in huge rooms where discussions were taking place. It truly was a place where the beings around it utilized magic fully in their daily lives, even to the smallest details!","Noah wanted to explore more of this culture and their techniques if the time came in the past, curious at the wand-shaped weapons that boosted the abilities they cast by a large degree as wondered of the wide array of techniques that the Wizards and Mages of the Dark Expanse used.","He already had so much on his plate in terms of skills and abilities that he felt the addition of even more was just him continuing to go overboard, where he might not even get a chance to utilize them all. But he would wait for the time to come when he could truly observe the culture and techniques of the beings within Dark Expanse, his figure currently going towards one of the command centers as it looked like the clash with the Celestials would soon begin, their Legion being close!"]},{"number":479,"title":"Chapter 479: Chapter 478 Simultaneous Breakthroughs","paragraphs":["In the Time Space of the Spiritual World, a particularly arrogant Emperor Penguin raised its beak high as it felt the course of a new Supreme energy travel through his body.","The aura of chaos that normally destabilized the essence of those it entered felt like a docile stream as it passed through his vessels and core, his breakthrough into the Domain Expansion Realm that was at the cusp of occurring actually happened right away with the addition of this new energy.","RAA! RAA! RAA!","He let out fearsome battle cries, but he wasn’t the only one as many of the other Harbingers and beings that were receiving Domain Rank Cores from his Master the past few days were all experiencing breakthroughs into this realm simultaneously!","RUMBLE!","Essence rapidly converged around the numerous beings stepping into the Domain Rank as they all felt the newest boost from the addition of the new Guider Type Ability- Dark Guider.","Apart from the golden energy of fate coursing through them, a dark scintillating energy of chaos was now vibrantly coursing through them as well, their bodies feeling the boost in power once more.","They could be considered bonafide beings at the Domain Rank, but their power was unlike any others at this realm as they were receiving huge buffs from two Guider Type Abilities!","The Emperor Penguin rose to the skies as he felt this fearsome power, his fanaticism towards his master only growing as he sought to prove his strength in battle.","[Come to the Forge.]","His thoughts were cut short as he received a command from the Spiritual World itself, his arrogance being cut short as this was the only entity besides his Master that could push him around.","A silver light flashed as the figure of the Emperor Penguin appeared outside of the Blacksmith’s Forge, entering it thereafter as he was met with a floating item set that shone with the luster of chaos!","[As the first beast of this Spiritual World, you represent all of your brothers and sisters whenever you move. Master gave me the right to choose who will be wearing the created Chaos Set Items, and I’m going to be biased and give you one of them! You must live up to your name as the Emperor Penguin.]","The voice of the Spiritual World that seemed more commanding when communicating with the arrogant penguin rang out, the beak of the penguin nodding up and down as it received the item set that nobody else had gotten their hands on yet.","[Baleful Chaos Bringer Set] :: An item set made from the materials of Chaos Behemoths. Contains a scimitar, breastplate, briefs, boots, arm guards, and helm. Varying levels of boosts are given when the set items are worn simultaneously. 2 Set Items- Reduces the cooldown and mana cost for all Chaos Abilities by half, as well as doubling their effects. 4 Set Items- Grants the wearer a Chaos Barrier that reflects 30% of all incoming damage back to the caster. 6 Set Items- A passive Chaos Storm is initiated by the resonance of all 6 Set Pieces. This Chaos Storm swirls around the wearer as it tears down the defenses of their enemies while boosting their own attacks. +250% Fate Element Resistance, +250% All Element Penetration, +250% All Element Resistance, +100% Chaos Damage applied to all abilities.","The set bonus of the spectacular [Baleful Chaos Bringer Set] became apparent in the eyes of the Emperor Penguin as he glanced at the smaller descriptions of the items themselves and all of their boosts. His eyes shone with brilliance as he adorned the Item Set, his fluffy body being covered by the dark chaos armor as it was soon fully hidden, only a fearsome shape of an armored penguin wielding a Scimitar that shone with a deadly edge becoming visible.","RUMBLE!","A Chaos Storm erupted from him as he enjoyed the feeling of strength the Item Set provided, but this didn’t last long as he felt an immense pressure descend down on him a second later as the Chaos Storm continued to spread out in the Blacksmith’s Forge.","[Don’t get conceited and damage the things in the Forge. Remember that all of this strength is made possible by the Master. Just try to be more useful now to him now.]","The cold voice and pressure of the Spiritual World descended on the Emperor Penguin as his beak pointed down in a docile manner, stopping the advancement of the ability given the 6 Item Set boost while also being reminded once more that beside his Master, the entity that was the Spiritual World was the only other one that could take him off his pedestal no matter his strength!","This was because he was a beast born from this unique World, his Origin being tied closely to it.","\"I shall go acclimate to my new Realm and Items while waiting for Master to call us...\"","The Emperor Penguin spoke out with a tone of someone bullied but it still held a tinge of arrogance as he flashed away from the Blacksmith’s Forge, going on to test his new strength and abilities in the Time Space of the Spiritual World.","Besides him, numerous beings in the Spiritual World broke into the Domain Expansion Realm thereafter as they were also adorned with their own Set Items!","The remaining two [Baleful Chaos Bringer Set] went to Elena and Barbatos, their realms breaking through the fastest while also holding their own unique strengths.","Aside from the limited Chaos Sets, the Spiritual World System was working to rapidly produce Set Items from the Fate Behemoths that Noah’s main body continued to take down in the Celestial Realm.","Even though standing against Celestials with the opposing Chaos Sets was ideal, having armors made from Fate Behemoths also provided a level protection from the element itself, thus other beings would be adorned with newly created Fate Item Sets that were being created right at this moment. They had to be lucky enough to first enter the Domain Expansion Realm, and for the war to not break out too soon before the creation of the Fate Set Items were finished!","But just on Noah’s side, numerous beings were stepping into the Domain Rank as they were fitted with fearsome Items. All of them were waiting...waiting to participate in the first battle of many in a war that would later be known in history as...the Last War!"]},{"number":480,"title":"Chapter 480: Chapter 479 Primed!","paragraphs":["Commanding Mage Turner was glancing at the numerous powerhouses around the war room as his eyes carried a trace of seriousness.","In the war room, a majority of the beings were releasing unique auras of the World Realm, these figures being some of the revered powerhouses that were fairly well known in the Dark Expanse.","Besides the World Rank Mage Turner, there were three other beings that stood in this same realm as him who would be leading their own forces against the Legions of Celestials in the coming battle. One was the fearsome Royal Vampyre known as Rokku, one of the generals under the Vampyre Ruler Vladivostok. The other was the Dark Wizard Shanora, a powerful being from the faction that preferred the mantle of Wizards instead of Mages.","Of course, the last being to join them was the 9th Infernal Lord whom they only knew by that title still!","Four World Rank Experts- Turner, Rokku, Shanora, and an Infernal Lord.","These were the beings standing against the coming Legions of Celestials, there being a tacit understanding between the two sides that they would not be releasing the peak powerhouses at the Star Forging Realm in this first clash. Those were the types of forces used near the end of the war as they represented the peak power of both sides, and this war...was just beginning.","\"We expect their vessels to pierce into the Dark Expanse in a day or two, and we have our own ships and forces distributed in a defensive wall around the Verittas Fortress to stop their advances.\"","Commanding Mage Turner spoke out in a serious tone as the powerful figures looked at each other around the room. The Dark Wizard Shanora who was dressed in what Noah would describe a cliche witch costume was glancing in the direction of his clone with shimmering eyes that held great interest, the essence of darkness swirling around her being agitated as time passed.","\"We can talk about strategies and defenses all day long if we want Turner, but why don’t we get to know each other’s...strengths some more? It’s not as if we get to be in the presence of an Infernal Lord everyday.\"","Her gaze shone with luster as she stared at Noah, his own gaze remaining impassive as he didn’t spare the wizard any look, turning towards the Commanding Mage Turner and speaking.","\"Where do you want my legion?\"","The Commanding Mage nodded as he pointed towards the table in front of them that had a projection of the wide Verittas Fortress and displayed some of the forces around it, his hands causing the appearance of a miniature legion of red figures that signified Noah’s Infernal Legion to be right at the center- at the forefront of the battle!","\"We will have to rely on your power to withstand the attacks of the Celestials head on...while we release our spells and magic from the sides to stop their advance and pick them off little by little until all of their strength is depleted.\"","Noah’s eyes shone as he heard these words, the meaning of this strategy plainly being that they wanted him to be a tank that withstood the damage of a huge boss while they dished out damage to slowly bring it down!","\"We excel in offensive tactics and destructive spells, but our defenses cannot compare to the power of Infernal Lords we have observed before. Is this strategy viable?\"","The Royal Vampyre Rokku spoke out carefully as he sensed the bubbling strength stemming from Noah’s body, the Dark Mage Shanora still having her gaze locked on him as Noah replied.","\"It shouldn’t be a problem!\"","RUMBLE!","His words reverberated with power as relieved expressions appeared around the room, Commanding Mage Turner continuing.","\"Alright, let’s talk logistics...\"","The meeting continued for another few hours as the powerful beings familiarized themselves with each other’s forces and talked about possible plans in case things went wrong.","The Dark Mage Shanora who continued to glance towards Noah’s vibrant aura of Chaos was the most peculiar, not exactly explaining why her gaze was locked on him for so long. At the end of the meeting as Noah was stepping out, he heard a telepathic message released from her enter his mind.","\"I must apologize for the abrupt introduction and interest, but we don’t usually have beings with such a thick aura of Chaos swirling around them such as you. If we are able to survive this little war that is coming up, I would love to discuss something with you. It somewhat pertains to the Dark Expanse, and someone with your advancements in Chaos would be most fitting for it!\"","Words that seemed to have a tinge of fanaticism rang in his mind as he didn’t even turn towards her, simply nodding as he left the room. The figures of the Dark Expanse really held Infernal Lords in much too different regards!","He would leave all other thoughts behind as he continued to look forward to the Legions of Celestials first, his heart expectant on all the treasures and loot they were planning on delivering to him.","As the legions of Celestials advanced forward and neared the Dark Expanse, the forces at the Verittas Fortress fortified their defenses as they prepared for the eventual clash.","It was a bustling scene of numerous forces that numbered in the hundreds of thousands preparing to participate in the war, the highest ranking powerhouses conducting the movements of their forces like a well-oiled machine as they worked together to ensure a chance of victory.","Noah was creating even more powerful forces in the Spiritual World as more and more of his subordinates entered the Domain Expansion Realm, his main body continuing to work efficiently in the Celestial Realm as he took down more and more Fate Behemoths at the Domain Rank, getting a taste of the ability of [Fate Stealer] early as he saw his Fate Lines continuing to jump higher every time a Fate Behemoths fell.","As he went further and further south of the Celestial Realm, he was gradually nearing the locations that would be considered largely unexplored, the wide areas where very few Celestials traversed and were filled with mysteries!"]},{"number":481,"title":"Chapter 481: Chapter 480 Ready to Serve!","paragraphs":["In the unexplored regions that Noah was currently nearing, the Behemoths would continue getting stronger and stronger, where after passing the area where the Domain Rank Fate Behemoths appeared, the danger level rose by a factor of 10!","The reason for this was that the unexplored regions of the Celestial Realm were extremely unpredictable, where one could come across a Behemoth at the World Rank, or they might just as well come across one at the Star Forging Realm!","There were no laws that said in this location you would find Behemoths at this realm or another, and it was completely wild and unexplored mystical lands holding their own secrets.","This was also the reason why even after 1000 years, the Celestials had only ever been confident to say they explored a bit over 10% of it, only their powerful peak figures like the Celestial Founder and the few at the Star Forging Realm being the ones to go even deeper into the Celestial Realm!","Celestials at the World Rank like Noah still had to be careful how deep they went, as the moment they came across even a single beast a realm higher than theirs, it was game over.","At this moment as his clone prepared to clash with Celestials, Noah’s main body was standing in a vibrant golden shining forest filled with huge ancient trees as he glanced at the direction ahead of him.","If he continued any further, he would be entering the unexplored regions where even the Celestials had not fully documented.","Powerful figures like the Founder and other Celestials might have passed through these regions and found nothing of note, but as of now, no information existed for them!","His face was serious as his body began shimmering with essence, [Unique Origin] and other abilities being used as he chose to go in covertly, the possible levels of enemies varying by a large amount in these locations.","The beauty of the Celestial Realm he was seeing right now had already become the norm, the tall trees where one could visibly see golden essence flowing through its leaves like sand only making him appreciate the scene of serenity. It was a scene that only those confident and powerful could consider serene, as the deafening silence would make others trembled while they traversed through.","SHAA!","His figure silently disappeared among the thick foliage around him as he ventured further into the Celestial Realm, keen to know exactly what secrets it held!","---","In an advancing Prime Warship that was followed by many just like it, Grandmaster Onillus had a bright face as he felt the aura of the Dark Expanse, the Legion under his command successfully passing through the junction between it and the Light Expanse as he continued forward!","The boons from the Celestial Realm were many and filled with wonder, but they did not come close to the number of Fate Lines one could gather when they changed the course of history for trillions of lives.","He would be one of the forces at the forefront of this change in this coming war, and would gain much from the eventual results that would change the landscape of the entire Novus Galaxy!","His mood was jovial as he asked a Grandmaster below him.","\"Have the vessels containing the citizens of those Prime Worlds lead as we near this so-called fortified fortress of the Alliance. We shall proceed with caution, I want no mistakes!\"","\"Yes, Grandmaster!\"","RUMBLE!","Word software affirmation rang out as some ships veered forward while others went back, a shuffling of forces occurring as Onillus counted the beings under him.","He had 5 other World Realm Grandmasters under his banner spread out into their own vessels, with another World Realm Expert that actually stemmed from one of the more powerful Prime Worlds in the Light Expanse taking the lead of those forces.","One of the few beings not under Celestials and having power at the World Realm, an existence known as Master Brightstar, a being that was the first born of a Prime World on the cusp of becoming a Realm! His birth absorbed so much essence of his world that even now it still remained at the Prime World level, but it created for an astounding genius that had lived for many years, where he now gained a powerful level even without joining the ranks of Celestials.","This meant that for the Legion of Celestials heading for the Verittas Fortress, there were a total of 7 World Realm experts at the lead!","Grandmaster Onillus’s face was bright as they neared the supposed fortress, his eyes not hiding the hunger for war as his heart felt like it was screaming.","’Throw the best you have at me! Let me inscribe my name as the first general to gain victory in this war...let the name Onillus ring out across the Novus Galaxy!’","His eyes shone with dangerous luster as his hungry gaze remained forward, the powerful Celestials around him showing similar lights as they looked forward to a grand battle.","---","Around the Verittas Fortress, four distinct forces could be seen surrounding the enormous planet as an aura of oppressive power leaked out.","One force was led by the Royal Vampyre Rokku, another by the Dark Wizard Shanora, the third by the Commanding Mage Turner.","Last but not least and standing at the very center of these forces like the sharpest point of a blade was an impassive Infernal Lord that floated above a 10,000 army of Infernals that were letting out fearsome battle cries that were setting the tone of the coming fight.","OOOOH!","\"Ready to serve!\"","OOOOH!","\"Ready to destroy!\"","OOOOH!","Even the faces of nearby wizards, vampyres, and mages were trembling as a fearsome tune gradually took the soon to be battle field.","Commanding Mage Turner was watching the boisterous forces with eyes of hope as he waited to see the fearsome power of an Infernal Lord, his eyes noticing the appearance of beings that were not there originally when the Infernal Lord first came, but their bodies were releasing bursts of strength that caused his belief for this battle to be raised even higher!","Around the Infernal Lord, numerous armored figures began to appear, varying in all shapes and sizes.","Commanding Mage Turner blinked his eyes at certain times to make sure that his eyes were not playing tricks on him, as he could clearly make out the shape of a penguin that was covered in a spectacular set of dark armor releasing an abundant aura of chaos.","There was also the figure of an armored Kraken with deep red eyes that seemed to hold great excitement and vengeance as they stared out in the void of space, as well as the small humanoid figure of an armored woman also clad in an armor wrapped in chaos, her hands beginning to move as the aura of numerous undead began to spread out from the already numerous Infernals!","The surrounding beings watched with agape expressions as around the Infernal Lord, numerous figures began to appear en masse, the army of 10,000 continuing to expand as vibrant War drums rang out.","\"Ready to serve!!!\"","OOOOOH!!!"]},{"number":482,"title":"Chapter 482: Chapter 481 Ready to Destroy!","paragraphs":["\"Ready to destroy!\"","OOOOH!","The drums of battle only became louder as the forces around the Infernal Lord continued to increase.","The auras of beings that were all in the Domain Expansion Realm appeared around the Infernal Lord continuously, with many of them fitted in matching armors and weapons that only added to their fearsome aura.","From those clad in items drenched in Chaos, some could be seen with armors that blazed with the element of fire, and most recently appearing beings caused the forces of Dark Expanse to rub their eyes in shock at the armor they adorned seemed to actually be releasing an aura of...fate!","Fate! Forces that came from an Infernal Lord actually released the blinding gold aura that Celestials were known by, giving a huge shock to the World Rank experts that were leading the forces of the Verittas Fortress as they spread out their auras to see if their eyes were deceiving them.","But it was genuine as around Noah, numerous Spiritual World Beasts, Calamities of the Sea, and even some of the humans and beasts from his homeworld and the Beast World that were power leveled to the Domain Rank stood around him powerfully!","An enormous Draconic Fire Behemoth appeared to steal the show as he towered over 50 meters in the void of space, Draco appearing with all of his glory as a golden armor actually wrapped around the entirety of his body, the Set Item from the Fate Behemoths actually fully adapting to whatever the form of the wearer was, causing a shimmering enormous golden dragon to appear magnificently near Noah.","Kazuhiko was also one of the few clad in a Fate Item Set, his hands dual wielding to beautifully inscribed long blades as his eyes could not contain their excitement. The Imperial Phoenix was next to him in her humanoid form as she adorned a similar set, those being lucky enough to receive the newly forged Item Set from Fate Behemoths being truly blessed as its boosts were nothing to scoff at!","Kazuhiko was still incredulously looking over every single description of the four items as his gaze went towards the description of the Set Item itself.","[Raiment of Fate’s Guard] :: An Item Set made from the materials of Fate Behemoths. Contains dual swords, breastplate, briefs, boots, armguards, and helm. Varying levels of boosts are given when the set items are worn simultaneously. 2 Set Items- Every time an enemy falls from the hands of the one wearing the Raiment of Fate’s Guard, a Fate Charge is gained. 1 Fate Charge grants +30% All Damage Increase, +30% Chaos Resistance, +30% All Element Penetration, and expires after 10 minutes. 4 Set Items- After collecting more than 10 Fate Charges, Blades of Liberation begin to descend for every Fate Charge thereafter. 6 Set Items- Each Fate Charge brings with it two Blades of Liberation that follow the will of the user for as long as the Fate Charge remains. The expiration time for Fate Charges increases to 20 minutes.","Kazuhiko’s pupils were shaking as he read over the descriptions of the full set bonus again and again. In his mind, he was just imagining how everytime he defeated a being, the set bonus of this item set would allow him to gain a single Fate Charge that brought with it two Blades of Liberation and a huge boosts to his power.","The more beings he defeated thereafter, the more charges and autonomous Blades of Liberations that would surround him! His mind was imagining a scene where tens of Blades of Liberation followed his every command as he descended into battle, his single figure surrounded by numerous golden swords!","OOOOOH!","\"Ready to serve!\" \"Ready to Destroy!\"","The yells of the Infernals only took him out of his stupor as his eyes looked forward, his expanded senses just being able to feel the rushing force and essence of many beings nearing them.","The Celestial Legion was here.","RUMBLE!","A wave of power spread out as the appearance of the enormous golden warships became visible, many more appearing thereafter as Noah’s face finally showed more than just an impassive expression, his body rising higher in the void of space as a sparkling blue armor appeared around him.","He adorned Hydromancer’s Mantle as a brilliant blue light pulsed from him, his thoughts then letting the ability from the Fledgling Aether Terror run free as [Aether Emission] was let loose, the purple energy of Aether beginning to leak out and swirl around him menacingly!","He also let loose the active ability of the Hydromancer’s Mantle, the [Hydromancer’s Banner] that gave an all around buff to those that could be considered to be moving with him.","RUMBLE!","This caused for a spectacular scene to occur throughout the Verittas Fortress, every single being that was standing against the Celestials gaining a unique blue runic symbol above their heads as an enormous rectangular blue transparent banner appeared above Noah’s head.","Commanding Mage Turner and the other powerful World Realm experts felt this change and slight boost to their power as their attention was taken once more from the appearing Celestial Legion and to the Infernal Lord shining with brilliant colors in the void space, their thoughts collectively being the same as they stared at this unique being.","’Just what type of Infernal Lord are you?!’","No answers would arrive to them at this moment as Noah was not done, even more abilities being cast as this was one of the few times where he could actually go all out. It was a rare opportunity to let loose and farm an abundant amount of loot, Fate Lines, and Chaos Particles that he would not let it slip by his fingers so easily!","RUMBLE!","[Chaotic Mandate], the ability from the Agent of Chaos skill tree that allowed him to be adorned in an armor of chaos similar to the Empyrean Armament of the counterpart law of fate skill tree was initiated as above the worn Hydromancer’s Mantle, the appearance of a dark armor erupted forward.","The blue and purple resplendence of colors was dyed dark as the aura of Chaos spread out fully, Noah also freely releasing the Chaos Particles swirling in his Chaos Field as his presence just continued to get brighter and brighter in front of the Verittas Fortress!","He was practically and arrogantly screaming to the now visible Celestial Legion- I am here!","But even at this point...he was not done as he now began to cast the transformation skills that came from the numerous skill trees under his command.","As the Celestial Legion appeared to kick off the start of a shocking battle, a single combatant was already causing widespread shock as the resplendence of abilities that caused the aura of this being to continue becoming more and more oppressive stole the spotlight of the whole battle!","OOOOOH!!!"]},{"number":483,"title":"Chapter 483: Chapter 482 This isnt even my final form!","paragraphs":["Already adorned with the Hydromancer’s Mantle and even the Chaos Armor from [Chaotic Mandate], Noah still went even further as he grandly used abilities freely, his abundant reserves of mana allowing it with no problems as he cast the transformation skills.","First, above the Verittas Fortress, a bloody moon appeared that released an oppressive red light, this light going on to wash around everyone, but causing a particular group to look up in immense shock.","\"What the fuck?!\"","The Royal Vampyre Rokku could not help but blurt out as he saw the appearance of the Blood Moon, recalling skills from the Ancient Vampyres of the past as he felt the red rays of this moon bolster his power rapidly, as well as the powers of all the Vampyres around him.","His shock came from the fact that this Infernal Lord also seemed to have access to the abilities of Ancient Vampyres that even he, a Royal Vampyre, did not have on top of every other spectacular abilities he had already cast!","It was just shock after shock as even though the Mages and Wizards spread out left and right of the Verittas Fortress were using their own magic as they veered Mana to go through their wands and cast terrible spells, they did not seem brighter than this singular being that just continued to cast one ability after another!","The Wizards were already summoning huge Golems and Beasts that floated grandly in the void of space, the Mages using magic circles as fearsome Elementals appeared with resplendent cries.","But all of this did not cause any eyes to open in shock as this Infernal Lord continued.","[Ancient Blood Scion] was cast first as below the layers of armor, Noah began to adopt the form of an Ancient Vampyre as his figure began to enlarge rapidly.","This enlargement only became more rapid as he wasted no time, casting [Arch Demon Lord Transformation] and then activated the form of the [Lesser Cthulhu] thereafter!","WAAA!","\"Ready to serve!\" \"Ready to destroy!\"","As his transformation took place, the Infernals below him continued their chants louder and louder, seemingly building up to a crescendo of noises that overtook the whole battle field!","The arriving Celestial Legion was looking on with serious eyes as Grandmaster Onillus had a deadly expression, his golden eyes locked onto this figure that was showing a terrible aura unlike anything he had ever seen before.","They had arrived and planned to make a grand entrance to instill fear into the hearts of their enemies with their numerous warships and forces, but this being stole the spotlight right away with a resplendent show of colors and abilities that allowed all eyes to be on him.","In the void of space, Noah’s figure continued to expand further and further, his monstrous transformation of multiple skill trees hidden beneath the Hydromancer’s Mantle and [Chaotic Mandate] armors, the many surrounding beings only seeing his figure enlarging more and more as his transformation completed at a towering 60 meters!","RIIP!","Luminous and glistening pairs or dark red wings were the only thing erupting out of the armored body as the monstrous overall shape continued to be hidden by the two sets of armor wrapping around him, with his size continuing to shoot up menacingly!","It was the height of commonly seen Behemoths in the Celestial Realm, a stature that took the breaths of many beings away as the void of space quaked and rumbled, the now gigantic figure waving his right hand as an enormous golden Trident of the Sea appeared in his hand.","DING!","The Trident of the Sea caused a ringing sound to reverberate as it resonated with the Hydromancer’s Mantle hidden below the [Chaotic Mandate] armor, the oppressive air and splendor that this Infernal Lord released only getting larger and larger as his arms moved, the enormous three pronged weapon pointing towards the stationary Celestial Legion a few miles away from the Verittas Fortress.","\"Ready to serve!\" \"Ready to destroy!\"","OOOOOH!!!","\"...\"","Instantly and eerily, the crescendo of noises from the Infernals ceased at this exact moment as the hearts of many felt a strong pull.","As the show of resplendent skills and colors ceased, silence overtook the battlefield as many looked at the larger picture around this Infernal Lord.","An enormous Golden Dragon that was now slightly smaller than him, thousands of Infernals patiently standing by, numerous figures clad in different sets of armors with each of them at the Domain Expansion Realm.","The feeling of power this group gave off was immense as all the eyes on the battle field in the void of space was on them!","Noah stared at the stably stationed vessels of Celestials that now stood opposite the Verittas Fortress as he sensed the tremendous power in his body.","His Fire and Water Origin Cores were rotating rapidly, absorbing energy and releasing their unique essence which coursed through him and made him feel simply fantastic.","His Fate Lines were expertly hidden through [Unique Origin] as only the field of chaos was apparent, the swirling Chaos Particles breaking past 400,000 at this moment as every single type of essence he held seemed to be bubbling.","But even at this point...he wasn’t done!","BRRRR!!!","Horrid vibrations released from his body as he activated yet another one of his recently gained skills. [Size Distortion] was activated from the newly gained Fledgling Aether Terror as his body vibrated rapidly, his power growing ever larger as his size began to shoot up to unimaginable heights!","Those around him watched with slack-jawed expressions as even before the war began, it seemed that this Infernal Lord was intent on baffling as many people as possible.","The forces of the Dark Expanse watched, but it wasn’t only them as similar to the Battle of Geniuses, they had their people sending numerous feeds of what was occurring here to the upper echelons that were observing the progress of this first clash closely!","From the Prime Warships of the Celestials, similar to how Grandmaster Vredral had used the vessels to show what was happening in the Magus World when Noah and Athena were raining down destruction, all the events occurring here were currently being broadcasted to the upper echelons of the Celestials!","The grandeur of resplendent abilities that Noah continued to show...was witnessed by many as the name of this 9th Infernal Lord entered the minds of all watching.","WAA!","His size erupted up as it passed 100 meters, skyrocketed to 150 meters, and continued on until it stopped at 250 meters! More than 125 times larger than the height of an average man, and more than 5 times larger than the height of even the mountainous Elite Celestial Behemoths!","His sheer size was terrifying as every around him seemed miniscule in comparison, the wondrous colors being released from the Hydromancer’s Mantle, [Aether Emission], and the [Chaotic Mandate] armor only extenuating his figure as he pointed the now enormous Trident of the Sea towards the Celestial Legion, his thunderous voice being the first thing to ring out before the first battle of the Last War was initiated.","\"I wonder if in this battle...is that little Founder of yours watching?\"","\"...\"","...!!!"]},{"number":484,"title":"Chapter 484: Chapter 483 Imposing!","paragraphs":["The words of the gigantic figure of the Infernal Lord caused shock and movements to spread throughout the battle field from their extreme arrogance, but they caused reverberations even further as many forces were ultimately watching to see the results of this first conflict!","The Grand Mage Edrusim was surrounded by numerous powerful Mages and the faction of Wizards that made up the Alliance as their eyes watched with unblinking eyes, they having already done their part of distributing their forces and now were simply waiting to see what the results of the battle would be.","In another location in the Dark Expanse, the Vampyre Ruler Vladivostok was watching the bloody moon appearing in the void of space above the army of Infernals as the sear he was on fell to the side, him being one of the more shocked beings as he recalled this skill from a long-forgotten past!","It came deep within the Letalis Expanse, with its source being from the revered Progenitor itself as it was an ability that had only shown itself in the War of the Righteous!","It had long since been lost in the dredges of time, along with the powerful beings that could use this skill.","Yet now, it was appearing once more, and in the hands of an Infernal Lord.","What exactly was happening?!","The gaze of Vladivostok shook as he recalled the only location that might have answered, waving his hands in front of him as he created a runic magic that was the prerequisite of a portal forming.","This was similar magic that the Vampyre King of the Underworld had used months ago to send a special someone into an Ancient Blood World, and Vladivostok was trying to do the same now as his thoughts led him to quickly check this Ancestral Ground that was all the Vampyres had left at this moment for answers.","Hid essence moved as he watched the runic circle complete with anticipation, but was shocked thereafter as when the red portal began to form while seeking a connection to the targeted ancestral world, it trembled and fizzled halfway through...not being able to form a connection!","\"...!\"","Vladivostok looked towards the failed connection of the Ancient Blood World he knew so clearly as his gaze turned ashen.","He tried again and again, but the magic that allowed him to form the portal with the Vampyres’ own Ancestral World was actually not working anymore! This led Vladivostok to believe that something had happened with the Ancient Blood World, and this Infernal Lord being shown in front of his eyes should have some connections to it!","What exactly had happened? Why was he able to use the skills of their Ancestors? Vladivostok would get to the bottom of this, even if he had to offend the dignity of an Infernal Lord!","The scene moves from the questioning Vampyre Ruler and goes into the wondrous Celestial Realm where yet another figure was watching the arrogant words of the Infernal Lord, a pristine wine glass in his hands as his wild countenance had changed. The Founder was not in the wildness of the Celestial Realm as he sat in a paradisiacal expansive hall that was filled with the colors of gold everywhere one’s eyes wandered to.","He sat in a pristine golden throne as he enjoyed food that very few could ever taste in their lives, the feed of the Verittas Fortress being displayed clearly from the Prime Warships of the Celestials in front of him.","This being was living the dream of all the big bosses- simply sending out his people to work hard and his behalf as he reaped most of the rewards. It was a truly rare position that very few could have the chance to enjoy.","There was an unnatural smile on his apathetic face as he heard the words of the Infernal Lord, curious words leaking out from his mouth.","\"The 9th and weakest Infernal Lord actually entered the Celestial Realm and saved those little rats earlier? Now that’s just not fair, don’t you think?\"","He was alone in the expansive golden hall, but seemed to be questioning something or someone as he continued!","He recalled the same red moon that had appeared when his palm was descending down towards the rats that had entered his cage, now confirming the identity of the being that saved them to be this Infernal Lord.","This was one of the more shocking thoughts that were spreading through the minds of many of the knowledge beings that could connect the dots- they found the identity of the being that actually stood against the Celestial Founder to save others not too long ago, and it was actually an Infernal Lord!","The question in many beings eyes was how this happened and why! How was he able to so quickly react, and why did he dave those particular beings? What history and connection were they missing?","Questions upon questions entered the minds of many as they watched the initial scene of the first battle of the Last War, the Founder himself continuing his monologue in the golden hall.","\"A creature of chaos created to oppose me, you shouldn’t have any driving emotions but destruction...hah, what exactly are you trying to do?\"","His voice was as if it was directly questioning something, but he continued to be alone!","\"You block me at every turn and stop my advancements for your own entertainment, but do you really think creating an anomaly of an Infernal Lord will help all that much? I’m very close you know. I can...\"","The gaze of Founder was bright as he reached his hands out as if grasping something only he could see in front of his eyes.","\"I can...almost touch that point now. I’m almost there. When I reach that point...I’ll be breaking out of your influence fully!\"","RUMBLE!","His strong voice reverberated out as only he knew the target of these words, his apathetic eyes turning to the feed of the Verittas Fortress as a smile curled on his lips.","\"I’m watching, little Infernal Lord. Give me a show.\""]},{"number":485,"title":"Chapter 485: Chapter 484 Like Moths to a Flame","paragraphs":["Grandmaster Onillus heard the impetuous words of the Infernal Lord as his eyes blazed red with anger, the disrespect directed towards the Founder being something he could not tolerate!","\"Destroy them all.\"","His words were simple and filled with wrath, the command going out to all the Prime Warships as the vessels had their World Cannons meant to destroy stationary worlds aimed and loaded, destructive red rays of light beginning to shoot out of the many Warships!","RUMBLE!","The forces of the Dark expanse were prepared as the aura of World Rank being erupted out, shimmering shields of all sorts of colors being created as the rushing rays of destructive lights met resistance.","If one took a larger view of the battlefield, they would notice many of these beams of destructive red light aimed towards the mountainous 250 meters Infernal Lord that stood imposingly!","To defend against this first attack by the collection Celestial Legion, the Wizards had pulled out their powerful wands as rays of red lights released from them and converged together, fully defending against the rays of light through sheer numbers and power as they worked with the World Realm experts.","Noah himself looked at the destructive rays of light that he once saw descend on the Lost World, this time their power not feeling all that oppressive for him as these rays that could destroy a world...he raised his Trident of the Sea towards them as numerous beams of plasma were released from the weapon!","These beams of plasma were actually dark in color because of the abilities under the [Agent of Chaos] that layered his attacks with the power of Chaos.","This also proved to be useful when it came to the rays of Aether that his identity as Crixus had cast as a Celestial, his enormous eyes watching carefully as he cast [Sever] and saw the released rays being balefully dark in color, their aura of Aether enveloped and reinforced by the power of chaos as they looked like terrible dark rays of light!","WAA!","What followed thereafter after was a wondrous scene of red rays of light meeting chaos rays that shattered the void of space, Noah going the route of offense being the best defense as his own attacks thundered forward!","\"HMPH!\"","A snort rang out in the battlefield as from the numerous Prime Warships, golden figures began to fly out and rapidly fill the void of space.","The golden figures were quickly overshadowed as the even larger numbers of beings from the Prime Worlds of Light Expanse also made their appearance. At the forefront of all of these forces, Grandmaster Onillus had his eyes shining with a gold splendor as he stared at Noah.","\"You all can have any of the other World Realm Commanders, but this childish Infernal Lord...is mine!\"","Words of the Grandmaster with more than 3 million Fate Lines reverberated strongly as a gold aura began to permeate around him and fill everything in the surroundings!","His eyes were dead set on Noah as the other World Rank Grandmasters and the single World Rank Expert from the force of the Prime Worlds had the Royal Vampyre Rokku, Commanding Mage Turner, and the Dark Wizard Shanora on their sights.","Each side had forces that spilled over hundreds of thousands, the numbers of those standing on the side of Celestials being slightly more as it was packed with beings across the chosen Prime Worlds of the Light Expanse.","OOOOOH!","\"Ready to Serve!\" \"Ready to Destroy!\"","The Infernal Legion had begun chanting again as they saw the appearance of the many figures, feeling the smell of battle and blood lust as their weapons called for destruction!","Noah’s eyes snaked across the void of space as he observed all the forces, everyone currently on a standstill as the staredown before everything turned into a scene of hell continued for another few seconds.","If things went according to plan, the forces would rush towards each other as the powerful World Rank figures from Celestials clashed with their respective matches on the side of the Verittas Fortress, and the moment these powerful figures began falling, the direction of the war would be decided!","Since the Celestials had more powerhouses at the World Rank, the side of the Verittas Fortress would soon be overrun as the Experts on the other side could simply group up to attack and destroy. Thus, the figures of the Dark Expanse were feeling some worry! When the two forces rushed towards each other, this scene of chaos would be one where the Celestials could take the most advantage of, and even possibly grant them a victory!","As Noah stared at the hundreds of thousands of beings, especially the golden shining Celestials that were placed at the very center of these forces- his eyes flashed a dangerous excited color.","To him, these many beings represented an expansive amount of loots and something even bigger- Fate Lines!","His heart was screaming out for him to take all of these Celestials out by himself if he could, and feeling his heart tell him this, he wanted to make it a possibility...and so he did!","\"Haha, let’s play!\"","His words were the spark that caused the forces of the Celestial Legion to begin rushing towards them, those from the Dark Expanse staying tightly around the Verittas Fortress as they fortified their defenses.","The moment Noah’s words finished though, his mountainous 250 meter figure disappeared from its position...and shockingly teleported right at the center of the Celestial Legion that was rushing forward!","Right at the very center where most Celestials were located!","Grandmaster Onillus at the forefront who was already rushing towards Noah felt this change as he turned back in shock, his wrathful face screaming out as he turned directions quickly. He wasn’t the only one as two other World Rank Grandmasters saw this, their eyes quickly communicating with each other as they also turned and went towards the Infernal Lord!","\"Vile creature!\"","The Infernal Lord has shockingly teleported to the very center of the hundreds of thousands of enemy forces, at the heart of the Celestial Legion where most Celestials were clustered. 3 World Rank Experts were heading his way as he smiled and spoke out slowly, his mind curious of a few things.","[Domain of Chaos] [Domain of Water][Domain of Fire] [Sea Domain] [Desecrate] [Essence Disruptor] [Destabilize]...","He released numerous Domains from the Laws he had control of as well as the buffing and debilitating Sea Domain from the Hydromancer’s Mantle as the mile around him became a terribly hellish place to be in for any of his enemies. The [Desecrate] and other abilities that affected enemies and surrounding space were going even more overboard as terrified looks began to appear on the faces of Celestials that were affected, their bodies feeling the horrendous effects!","At this junction when Noah stared at the thousands of Celestials trying desperately to put up their defensive abilities and the attacks from three rushing World Rank Grandmasters, his mind was actually curious to know how beautiful his next skill towards them would be.","He was naturally thinking of the extremely powerful and overly reinforced [Sever] that from a single ray of purple-blue Aether, it could now erupt with numerous rays of Aether that were drenched dark from the Chaos Element, and had even gained the quality of chaining between enemies from the [Aether Chain Support]!","He wondered just how spectacular the sight would be of this extremely destructive ability being constantly spammed amidst thousands of Celestials who would in no way have a result to defend themselves!","The result...would cause the three converging World Rank Grandmasters to have shivers run down their spine as Noah spammed the command of [Sever] in his mind, essence bubbling as blinding rays of dark aether overtook the battlefield!"]},{"number":486,"title":"Chapter 486: Chapter 485 Too OP!","paragraphs":["In a bold and shocking move, the 9th Infernal Lord had teleported in the direct center of the Celestial Legion as the surging momentum of the entire force was disrupted, three World Rank Celestials changing their directions as their bodies rushed towards him!","Even though Noah had abruptly teleported, his commands were relayed seconds before as the Infernal Legion moved forward orderly, their sharp weapons getting ready to clash with the coming army.","The Emperor Penguin, Draco, and all the others were also shooting forward with vigor as they finally got a chance to enter the same battlefield as their master!","The feelings they had currently were those of extreme happiness, the one wish that many of them longed for so long actually being achieved today.","OOOOOH!","Reverberations spread out across the void of space as essence converged in the bodies of hundreds of thousands, but all of this seemed minimal when one looked at the dark armored body of the 9th Infernal Lord that had begun releasing truly destructive dark rays of light from his hands.","RUMBLE!","The dark rays of light were rays of Aether that were drenched in the Law of Chaos, at their base having the terrible power of Aether that was backed by numerous support skills!","All of these support skills would make for a terrible sight as at first, 6 dark rays of light shot out and instantly neared 6 unlucky Celestials, their eyes filled with terror as because of already cast abilities like [Desecrate] and the numerous Domains that Noah had cast, they could not even move their energy to raise their defenses.","They watched with terror-filled eyes as the dark rays of light struck them, their bodies being hit with a violent energy that tore them all nearly in half as their lives were ended instantly from the combination of Aether and Chaos, those that were unlucky enough to not die being hit by the [Fatal Ailment Support] that caused the energy of Aether to ravage their bodies until they died!","But what was truly horrendous...was the scene that followed thereafter as from the bodies that looked like they had their strings cut, the dark rays that had hit them...actually snaked to nearby Celestials as if they had their own wills, as if they were somehow attracted to their bodies, swiftly connecting with the surrounding beings in a chain reaction!","ZAP! ZAP! ZAP! ZAP!!!","The chain reaction looked like a dark line that zigzagged from one Celestial to another, each time it made a connection causing a being to face their death as a truly fear-inducing scene opened up in front of Noah’s eyes.","From the 6 rays of Aether, more than 60 Celestials were hit and chained as they all died no matter if they were at the Void or Domain Realm, and Noah’s body had already released more than 12 rays of Aether a second later as he constantly spammed the [Sever] ability!","WAA!","Grandmaster Onillus watched with a wrathful face as in the midst of Celestials, dark rays of chaotic essence that chained from one Celestial to another began to spread wildly, droves of Celestials dropping like flies thereafter as these rays seemed unstoppable.","\"Vile Creature!\"","He screamed put as his body glittered gold, in the space around him the appearance of ridiculously large golden spears came to life as they thundered towards the figure of the Infernal Lord.","The other two World Rank experts released their own attacks, space creaking as the energies of four World Rank experts were released in the surrounding space!","\"Haha!\"","ZAP! ZAP! ZAP!","Wild laughter was the only thing that met their attacks as Noah continued to release rays of Aether that chained from one Celestial to another, his happiness not just stemming from the beautiful ability, but because of the numbers of Fate Lines that had begun to shoot up rapidly!","The percentage under the Law of Fate constantly began to change in eyes as every moment a Celestial fell, it jumped higher and higher from the effect of [Fate Stealer].","RUMBLE!","The attacks of the three World Rank experts reached his heavily armored body as a majority of them were simply deflected off, only a few managing to even pierce the swirling armor of Chaos as they hit the Hydromancer’s Mantle below that.","Onillus looked on with increasing fury as their attacks did not even reach the body of the Infernal, their bodies feeling pain in turn as they shockingly received Reflective damage from the abilities of Sea Domain! Onillus’s body began shining even brighter as he healed himself and prepared to release an attack that could be considered an Ultimate one, his fury reaching insane levels as too many things he didn’t understand occurred in this battle!","The defense of Noah that Onillus and the others were baffled by was actually something simple, as he was truly boosted by too many defensive abilities from his transformations, but especially the ones from Hydromancer’s Mantle that tripled his defense in this area where he released [Sea Domain]. He was so reinforced that he would be shocked instead if the World Rank Celestials had managed to pierce his armor on the first try.","They had to put some time into it!","OOOOH!","\"Ready to Serve!\"","From the distance, the battle cries of the Infernals could be heard as Noah’s hands continued to rain down dark rays of Aether that reaped the lives of Celestials every second, his body taking on numerous attacks from three World Rank experts as he was not bothered by it one bit.","It was a shocking scene in the battle field as one could observe a 250 meter tall figure reeling dark rays of light that wiped away hundreds of Celestials every few seconds, his body tanking the attacks of 3 other World Rank experts with ease as his chilling laugh of enjoyment rang out across the Void of space!","It was at this juncture that the bodies of the three Celestial Grandmasters shone the brightest, the varying number of Fate Lines in the millions rising from their bodies as behind the wild Infernal Lord, the palpating appearance of an enormous golden spear that was over one hundred meters materialized.","With Onillus at the center, the Celestial Grandmasters pooled in their essence to create a singular enormous spear from their combined powers, this single spear thundering down towards the Infernal Lord and finally tearing through his defenses as it rapidly rotated and drilled into his body with a splendor of gold, happy expression finally appearing in the eyes of the Grandmasters as they observed the spear to enter the chest of this Infernal Lord!","This was a spear that contained enormous amounts of the essence of Fate, something deadly to Infernal Lords that were drenched in the Law of Chaos. It pierced through the heavily armored chest of the Infernal Lord with its tip appearing drenched in blood clean through the opposite side.","With this attack, they had effectively heavily injured this monstrous figure, seeing a clear path ahead as he would be weakened to great degrees hereafter, right?","Right?!","\"Haha!\"","A wild laughter was all that met their happy expressions as even with an enormous spear piercing his chest, the mountainous Infernal Lord did not spit out blood or even stop the casting of his skills, the only thing changing being that his aura was becoming even more menacing, the Celestials not knowing they had pushed Noah to cast his next terrible skill.","He could be considered injured yes? So all he had to do was to heal himself. Now shockingly, there were a large number of beings running away from him that fit his requirements for healing very well, their minds already in disorder as he cast the wide area ability he had just gained for the first time.","It was an ability that would even cause the enthralled watching forces of the Dark Expanse feel shivers down their spine, an ability that would actually come to be commonly known in the future as one of the loved skills of the 9th Infernal Lord...it was [Domination]!"]},{"number":487,"title":"Chapter 487: Chapter 486 Rivers of Blood in the Void of Space","paragraphs":["The Vampyre Ruler Vladivostok was watching with squinting eyes at the live feed of the battle, his eyes honing in on the person that had taken a central position in this battle already, the being who could somehow cast abilities of Ancient Vampyres from a long forgotten era!","He watched with shocking eyes as an enormous golden spear pierced from the back and through the chest of the Infernal Lord, rising from his seat with worry for the battle as this was a lethal attack in his eyes.","The Infernal Lords were drenched in the law of chaos, and getting a spear filled with fate essence piercing their bodies like this meant they had taken heavy damage.","Yet under the eyes of many, the Infernal Lord actually laughed as his body was pierced through!","No scream of pain or wrath from taking heavy damage, but a laugh!","This was because his body was rapidly gaining more and more Fate Lines on top of the ones he already had, the law of fate having a home in his body- so how could it harm him in a lethal manner?","The injury was one he would consider light, but it was still an injury nonetheless so Noah chose a straightforward way to heal it. It was through...Domination!","[Domination] (5/5) :: The eyes of the Fledgling Blood Ancient release a dominating light that enthralls any with weak souls. The bodies of the dominated can then be controlled to either replenish the Blood Ancient with [Blood Bag], or deal damage to surrounding enemies by [Blood Bomb].","Under the watchful gazes of numerous beings, the appearance of red eyes beneath his armored head could be seen as a single word spread across the void of space with clarity!","[Domination].","RUMBLE!","On the 250 meter tall body, the dangerously bloody eyes were now particularly vibrant and visible, a red light releasing from them as it went on to sweep to the thousands of Celestials still remaining in the surroundings.","Vladivostok watched this light being released from this Infernal Lord as his body trembled, his heart having seen very few figures use such an ability in the past!","What Vladivostok didn’t know was that this ability was not even passed down through Noah the normal way, but unlocked from his own methods through the unique Skill Points that made skill trees possible.","The trembling eyes of Vampyre Ruler watched on as anywhere the red light passed. The beings caught within began trembling as their eyes turned cloudy.","The three World Rank Celestials were also affected by this red light, but their bodies shone gold as they pushed it out and regained their clarity. The same could not be said for the numerous other Celestials though!","Anywhere the red light passed, the beings that could not fully defend their souls fell under the influence of [Domination] as their eyes turned glossy, their gazes turning blankly to the enormous Infernal Lord as he gave a single command in his mind to all those who had fallen under his control.","He could either choose Blood Bomb or Blood Bag, and he chose the latter as he found its effects did not defer too much from the former!","Numerous powerhouses watched on as the beings affected by the red light began ballooning up as something wriggled out of their bodies...each of them shockingly bursting into a shower of blood as a gory scene overtook the battlefield.","POP! POP! POP!","In the expansive void of space, one could hear a sound as if popcorn was popping loudly in a microwave, but the things popping were the powerful beings at the Void, Soul, and Domain Rank as regardless of their realm- if they fell under [Domination], their bodies ruptured in a shower of blood as it began flowing in a straight line towards a laughing Infernal Lord!","\"Haha! Haha!\"","The laugh reverberated throughout the void of space as many beings watched rivers of blood forming from the thousands of beings affected, the mouth of the Infernal Lord opened wide as these rivers of blood rushed in endlessly!","The ability of [Blood Gourmet] was amplified as Noah tested the blood of powerful beings in proportions he never before imagined, his mouth gulping down numerous times.","Among those watching, Vladivostok looked on in shock as he affirmed his thoughts about this Infernal Lord having traits of an Ancient Vampyre as he watched him devour rivers of blood, observing as his body began to shine a brilliant shade of red, the place where a golden spear had pierced beginning to wriggle and reform as the aura of tremendous life force leaked out.","It was life force from too many powerful beings that was absorbed by a single one, the sheer scope of it causing the entire battlefield to turn into a lul as the truly powerful beings pulled themselves back to observe the battlefield on a larger scale.","To their shock, they found that by the time that this Infernal Lord had teleported amidst the forces of the Celestials and the single minute that followed, he had gone off a reign of terror that had actually decimated more than half of all of the forces of Celestials that were on the battle field!","The eyes of Grandmaster Onillus turned crazy as he glanced around the battlefield and saw the empty void of space filled with bones, numerous Celestials that were not in the scope of influence of Domination still scrambling away fearfully.","Onillus realized that since the beginning of the battle, his forces and even himself had just been scrambling around the palm of this singular Infernal Lord, and more than half of all the Celestials brought to this War had already died in the span of less than a minute!","A minute!","RUMBLE!","The vibrant color of red shone luminously from the 250-meter mountainous body as a primal yell of enjoyment and destruction was released from Noah’s mouth.","\"OOOOOOHH!!!\"","The roar echoed through out the void of space as the eardrums of weaker beings burst, the brilliantly red eyes of the Infernal Lord now turning to the wrathful expressions of three World Realm Celestial Grandmasters that could do nothing to stop him while he obliterated more than half of their forces.","As his cells screamed out from the enjoyment of devouring rivers of blood, his origin was screaming out joyfully as imperceptible wisps of gold light that signified the Fate Lines taken from all the Celestials he had defeated continued to enter his body!","When he observed the stat panel in the corner of his eyes, it shockingly showed constantly changing numbers that just continued to shoot higher and higher, the current total number of Fate Lines having already passed 1,582,295!","1,582,295!!!","Just from the massacre of thousands of Celestials from varying levels of Void to the Domain Expansion Realm, more than 1 million Fate Lines were added, his percentage in the Supreme Law of Fate quickly shooting past the 10% mark! In a matter of a single minute!","Ah!","Who could call themselves a genius in front of such a sight?!","Who could say they are talented in the Law of Fate if they knew what this single being had added more than a million Fate Lines in just a minute?!","Could the numerous exclamation points written even get across this point of grandiosity?!","It was ridiculous, improbable, and simply scary!","Noah’s eyes that were filled with bloody fervor landed on the wrathful World Rank Celestial Grandmasters as his abilities finally moved towards them, his body rumbling with joy as he moved to singularly battle against three World Rank Experts!"]},{"number":488,"title":"Chapter 488: Chapter 487 A Penguin Leads the Way!","paragraphs":["As the shocking scenes around Noah continued to play out, with his mountainous figure now turning around to pay attention to the three World Rank Experts after he had erased more than half of all the Celestials on the battlefield, the battles between the other figures were also resuming or starting with intensity!","There were in total 7 World Rank Experts from the Celestial Legion, and as 3 of them had grouped up against the Infernal Lord, there were 4 freely running rampant as they collided with the forces of the Verittas Fortress.","Even though Noah had fully disrupted the battlefield, there were still hundreds of thousands of forces that moved forward under the command of those above them to clash with each other!","Among those moving, the single World Rank Expert that wasn’t a Celestial, Master Brightstar, had a dark expression as his shining saber clashed against the magic of the Commanding Mage Turner.","The Commanding Mage had summoned a spectacular fire elemental that he stood on, blue and red flames equally covering this Elemental’s body as Turner himself stood atop it releasing terrible spells of the Fire Element.","The tens of thousands of beings from the many Prime Worlds also came in contact with the opposing Mages that stood with Turner, beginning battles of their own as a chaotic battlefield fully bloomed in the void of space!","In another location, A World Rank Celestial Grandmaster clashed with the Dark Wizard Shanora, his cast of an enormous Blade of Liberation stopped by a floating Dark Golem that Shanora stood on with an enthralled gaze, her eyes occasionally going to the mountainous figure of the Infernal Lord as hidden thoughts coursed through her mind.","She waved her Wand towards the Celestial Grandmaster as spears of darkness bloomed in front of her, keeping this World Rank combatant busy as the Wizards around her also clashed with the forces of the Celestial Legion in the area.","Another World Rank Celestial was being kept busy by the shocked and buffed Royal Vampyre Rokku who was enjoying the boosts of the recently appearing blood moon in the void of space, his mind in disarray as he observed the abilities he had only heard about in history be utilized by an Infernal Lord!","The forces of Vampyres he had with him were actually holding the toughest and tightest defense against the Celestial Legion because of this unexpected boost that remained in the void of space, a blood world blooming from Rokku’s hands as he prepared to trap the Celestial Grandmaster and finish him on his own turf.","Rooku, Shanora, and Turner were each able to match 3 World Rank Grandmasters, but this still left one Celestial Grandmaster running freely as no combatant of the same realm came to match him from the Verittas Fortress!","His eyes were cold as he carried with him two dual shining blades of light, cutting down lower ranked forces from the Dark Expanse like flies as he neared Verittas Fortress with tens of thousands of beings.","This gap in defense would be deadly if it wasn’t quickly filled, and Commanding Mage Turner was about to send commands to distribute more forces to hold this rampant Grandmaster back which would cause more lives to be lost. But he did not get a chance to do so as in front of the advancing Grandmaster, the Infernal Legion appeared strongly, going towards the tens of thousands of beings as they released fearsome war cries!","\"Ready to serve!\"","OOOOH!","\"Ready to destroy!\"","OOOOH!","A clash instantly erupted as the Celestial Grandmaster raised his hands high and prepared to unleash deadly skills upon the Infernals that only had ten Domain Rank experts at their peak, but his gaze was filled with the appearance of new beings as he actually felt a threat appear in front of him.","His eyes squinted as he observed the figure of an armored penguin appear, his body reacting to the aura of chaos released from this penguin as even more figures with similar auras appeared around him.","The other two were women, one tall with long legs and the other with a shorter stature, but their bodies still released the dreadful aura of Chaos! The Grandmaster could actually observe particles of chaos rotating around the bodies of the three figures akin to that of a storm, and it was this that made his body feel a threat!","These three figures were further reinforced as Kazuhiko, the Imperial Phoenix, the Kraken, and numerous other Spiritual World beasts appeared and surrounded the World Rank expert.","The others were either adorned in armors that actually released an aura of fate or had an aura of Infernals, their eyes locking towards the singular Celestial Grandmaster as they boldly prepared to stand against a being an entire realm above theirs!","Such a feat was normally left to their Master, and it became even harder when one reached the peak levels where the gap between realms just seemed like an expansive gulf that could never be crossed.","But they were confident enough to do it, and it was because each of them was receiving incredible boosts from two Guider Type Abilities! They were given boosts to their attack and defenses in the hundreds of percentages with the [Golden Guider] and [Dark Guider] abilities, their bodies also carrying with them the stable aura of both Chaos and Fate as they raised their weapons towards the powerful expert with no fear!","RAA! RAA! RAA!","A battle cry was released from the Emperor Penguin as he used the 6 Piece Set Bonus to the fullest and let loose the Chaos Storm, Elena and Barbatos doing the same as they layered three terrible storms of chaos to descend onto the battlefield. These three would act as the close combat fighters, with the others releasing attacks from the distance as they all worked together for the goal of bringing down a being at the World Realm, a being holding the strength of an entire World!","But their confidence did not just come from their new boosts and Item Sets, it also came from the knowledge that a few of them held abilities from the Seven Deadly Sins.","The first ability that gave them all confidence was one held by the Emperor Penguin, the holder of the Sin of Pride. It was [Pride Embodiment]!","[Pride Embodiment]- When meeting foes holding a higher level of strength, the user gains the power of hubris itself. This power can be used to strengthen attacks or defenses. The level of enhancement is dependent on the true pride lying deep in the user’s heart, which could be nurtured to grow so large that nothing is allowed to overshadow it!","RUMBLE!","This single ability caused the aura of the Emperor Penguin to continue to rise nonsensically, his body ballooning more and more as his beady eyes shining with gold splendor, [Aura of Pride] also being on full display.","With [Pride Embodiment] as well as his Item Set and boosts from the two spectacular Guider Abilities, he was confident of being able to withstand the power of this World Realm expert and act as a tank for the others!","RAA!"]},{"number":489,"title":"Chapter 489: Chapter 488 So What?!","paragraphs":["As the Emperor Penguin looked forth arrogantly, his body rushed towards the Celestial Grandmaster with no fear in his eyes as he chose the straightforward method of attacking.","But one should not forget that the holders of Wrath, Gluttony, Lust, and Greed that four Harbingers held were also present in this battle!","Kazuhiko’s eyes flashed as he used [Emperor of Greed], the two golden swords in the hand of the Grandmaster that were going to meet the dark scimitar flashing towards him from the arrogant penguin actually disappearing, the two glowing blades appearing in Kazuhiko’s hands as they changed ownership!","His body shone with the luminous gold splendor of the Item Set that released strong waves of Fate Essence as he struck forth with his newly gained weapons.","The Kraken felt the enormous amounts of wrath in the battlefield as it used [Wrath Absorption], [Rage Empowerment], [Anger Avatar], and [Fury Channeling] consecutively, its wriggling body expanding rapidly as visible rays of destructive red light shot forth from it. Its anger, its misgivings, all the unfairness it felt in the past- it released it all as a deadlier attack than any that had come before!","The Imperial Phoenix and Barbatos waited for a prime opportunity to utilize their own ultimate skills as they leashed out attacks of their own, these Harbingers actually taking and controlling the pace of the battle against a being an entire rank above them as they fought in a fashion never before seen.","Aside from the Harbingers and other beasts surrounding the World Rank Grandmaster, a particularly mountainous Draconic Fire Behemoth, the young dragon Draco, was breaking the sound barrier and swallowing the figures of celestials and any that came around him whole, his huge figure moving through the void of space with utter impunity!","ROAAR!","The eyes watching from the shadows looked on in shock at this sight as in a grand hall that Edrusim was in with many Mages who were monitoring the state of the battle, bustling discussions occurred as they observed the spectacular scenes playing throughout.","\"Even if it is in groups...being able to withstand a being an entire realm higher is exemplary!\"","\"Exemplary? It shouldn’t even be possible!\"","\"...just who are these armored beings the Infernal Lord released?\"","Numerous questions and discussions took place as the pace of battle was analyzed, the appearance of beings with spectacular Item Sets that showed off improbable levels of strength for the realms they were in taking the attention of many.","But the singular figure that remained at the center of attention for everything was the Infernal Lord himself, the being that was standing against three World Rank Celestials!","BOOM!","His mountainous figure waved the dangerously shining Trident of the Sea to sweep down at Grandmaster Onillus, who in turn stood firm as he projected a transparent golden shield that was shattered at the moment of impact!","The other two Grandmasters rained down golden spears and Blades of Liberation as they also released pure Fate Essence in efforts to overwhelm the chaotic Infernal Lord, but they found that even when his body was bathed in the golden aura of fate, he didn’t seem to be taking any injuries!","[Armageddon].","They heard a simple word that was followed by the shaking of space itself, the blue region filled with the [Sea Domain] around them turning a tinge of red as it turned hellishly hot in a matter of seconds.","Above them, the appearance of Flaming asteroids rushed towards the golden shining World Rank Celestials as their expressions hardened, using the profound power in their bodies to reinforce their defenses so they could withstand the hellish environment while surviving the attacks of the Infernal Lord.","It was a battle of three World Rank Celestials against a single World Rank Infernal Lord, and yet it was the three Grandmasters that were actually at a disadvantage as the Infernal Lord continued to senselessly release skill after skill as if his energy reserves had no limit!","So what if it was three World Rank Experts?!","So what if they each had Fate Lines in the millions?!","Against his own power that was boosted multiple times over by numerous skill trees and items, Noah could arrogantly ask- So What?!","ZAP! ZAP! ZAP!","Numerous rays of dark colored Aether were released from him as they smashed onto the body of Onillus, and then went on to chain to the two Grandmasters near him before they returned to chain to Onillus again, over and over!","They had a powerful golden aura of fate protecting their bodies, but every time an Aether ray chained between their bodies, this protective layer got thinner and thinner as their faces became more and more serious!","[Ice Age].","After using the [Armageddon] ability from the <<Herald of Fire>>, Noah vastly changed the surrounding environment once more as he brought in the polar opposite, using the ability from the <<Herald of Water>> that causes the temperature of the surrounding regions to go towards absolute zero, shimmering white frost spreading out with him at the center as the Grandmasters were hit with yet another debilitating attack.","\"Wretched devil!\"","Grandmaster Onillus howled forth while expanding more and more energy to protect himself, numerous attacks smashing into Noah’s body as bursts of armor erupted out, any strike that actually landed on his body only drawing minor injuries.","Noah paid no attention to their attacks as whenever he became even remotely injured, he uttered a few words to cast yet another ability from the <<Herald of Flames>>, it was [Rejuvenating Flames] that caused gold-colored Flames to appear next to his injuries as they became rapidly healed thereafter, his dominance over the pace of the battle field continuing!","A wide array of resplendent abilities continued to release from his body as he continued to stand against and even overwhelm the World Rank Experts, throwing out Chaos Orbs or miniaturized Shattered Stars while continuing to chain chaos-filled Aether rays between them to constantly rip apart their defenses and wear down their energy.","From the wrathful eyes of the three Grandmasters, one could see a tinge of fear appearing as they fully realized the pace of the battle as the momentum of the Infernal Lord in front of them just continued to shoot higher, a single thought crossing their minds that began to only expedite the fear!","’Are we...are we actually going to lose?’","...!!!"]},{"number":490,"title":"Chapter 490: Chapter 489 Overkill I","paragraphs":["The watchers that were observing this first battle of a long war actually watched on in stunned silence at the scenes playing themselves out in front of their eyes.","Some portions of the battlefield could be considered what one should normally expect in a war, with beings of opposing but similar levels of power fighting against each other until the other side came out on top.","Yet on other portions of the battlefield, the things they were seeing were enough to shatter any known norms!","In one area, an Infernal Legion was cutting down any beings they came across as they sang a symphony of destruction with every swing of their weapons, their path paved wide open with nobody from the Celestial Legion to stop them as shockingly, the last World Rank Celestial Grandmaster was actually being held back in a tight battle against multiple Domain Rank armored beings!","RAA! RAA! RAA!","An Emperor Penguin valiantly took the strikes that held behind them the force of an entire World as he retaliated, his body shimmering with the dark aura of the Chaos Item Set while a Chaos Storm raged around him.","It was tinged with wisps of gold as the immense aura of Pride also leaked out, the abilities of the Sin of Pride being put in full display as his very being was amplified to greater heights because he stood against an enemy a level higher than him!","Kazuhiko and the other Harbingers used the gaps created by the Emperor Penguin to land terrible attacks as those who adorned the Fate Chaos Sets, in particular, were using the Set Boost to build up Fate Charges, and allowing for the appearance of numerous blades of liberation that should have been colored gold, but they held a mix of darkness as the abundant chaos essence they had from the Dark Guider ability freely flowed to their attacks.","The World Rank Expert had no chance to slack off as he withstood attacks left and right, but this wasn’t the most shocking scene that was occurring across this battlefield!","The ongoing battle of an enormous Infernal Lord that towered over 250 meters, his body clad in an armor releasing wisps of chaos as well as the emission of baleful Aether- it was the battle with this single being at the center that took all the attention as he wildly fought against 3 beings at the same realm as him.","WAA!","The enormous trident he wielded smashed down towards the central figure of Onillus as the Grandmaster released Fate Essence to form into the shape of huge golden palms, his Fate Lines rumbling as the two palms grasped onto and stopped the descent of the vibrating weapon!","The other Grandmaster tried to use this chance to send out deadly attacks, but they seemed to simply be getting brushed off on the body of the mountainous figure as the numerous layers of armor he had on did almost all of the defending on his behalf.","The eyes of the Grandmasters held a tinge of unwilling fear as they knew what all of the far away watching forces knew as the battle continued- the three of them were actually on the path of a terrible defeat!","The Infernal Lord in front of them seemed to be jumping with boundless energy, his attacks relentless as he released one after another without any reservations. While on their side, their defenses were getting weaker and weaker as the abundant energy in their bodies was actually becoming depleted.","This meant that in the next few minutes, they would begin falling one by one if nothing changed!","Onillus knew this very well as his eyes battled the fear out to try and replace it with fury, his unwilling voice resounding out as his body began to burn a brilliant and even brighter gold color.","\"Burn your Soul!\"","\"...!\"","Unwilling looks appeared on the faces of the other two Grandmasters at these words, but they seemed to have no choice as they went to the only option that could provide them a possible victory- but at the cost of their burning their very Origins and heavily reducing their level of power permanently!","\"Burn the Soul!\"","\"Ignite your Origin!\"","RUMBLE!","They adopted valiant faces as the strong aura of fate descended towards them, their power beginning to rise rapidly as they prepared to release attacks more powerful than any they had been releasing in the past hour.","But would they really be given a chance?","For the first time ever, Noah had a cruel smile as he drenched himself in the aura of Chaos and baleful Aether, enjoying the all-around feeling of power as he went on to cast only 2 skills that would go on to figuratively cause the jaws of all those watching to drop to the floor.","The 2 skills were actually Unique Skills, ones that he had gained months ago when battling against the Demon Lords and Demon Kings of a now subjugated world.","He had not put them to much use in the past months as he had designated them to the constructed dungeons of his homeworld, their uses being further limited as they truly only worked best when he was battling enemies at the same realm as him. But any time in the past few months, he had always faced enemies that were a realm or two higher, the effectiveness of the two unique skills not being able to add much as he left them to continue their assigned tasks in his home world.","But now that he was at the World Rank, a rank that only true experts in the Novus Galaxy could enjoy, he saw himself putting these skills to use more and more in the future as he continued to test their effectiveness as well as their limitations!","RUMBLE!","Essence wildly erupted as his lips silently moved, the energy that the three Celestial Grandmasters were collecting being blown apart as around them, the figures of oppressively powerful beings were summoned with ease!","Two were large and fearsome, their bodies reeking of darkness as their eyes shone red, and three were actually fairly small and had curvaceous figures with their bodies palpating with wicked strength.","The jaws of many beings figuratively dropped to the floor with the appearance of these five figures as each of them...held the power of the World Realm!","What followed thereafter...was simply overkill!"]},{"number":491,"title":"Chapter 491: Chapter 490 Overkill II","paragraphs":["Overkill!","Overkill to an insane degree as with the appearance of 5 new World Rank Experts, all color drained from the faces of the Celestial Grandmasters.","The ones that were in their own battles against the Experts of the Verittas Fortress or the single World Rank Celestial that was actually in a sorry state while being matched against an arrogant Emperor Penguin and other armored beasts- none of them could provide any help and support as they watched on helplessly!","This was because the worlds were many, the Novus Galaxy being extremely wide. So many beings knew that many skills existed all around, but even they had not yet come across the abilities that this Infernal Lord portrayed, especially ones that allowed him to simply summon 5 combatants at the World Realm.","Many were first asking themselves, what kind of an ability was that? But the most important question to them was the natural universal law that required essence in exchange for abilities, so they knew that logically to somehow summon creatures at the level of the World Realm, the mana requirement was enormous! How could this being that was already releasing skills as freely as he could over the past hour still be able to do something as ridiculous as this?!","As the shock of those watching only increased, the beings in the actual predicament were trembling as the 5 summoned creatures at the World Rank released attacks towards them right away.","Noah himself did not relent as he went for a joined attack that would obliterate the three Grandmasters instantly, his eyes glistening as destructive Portals of Terror began to appear en masse in a circular fashion around their figures. This was on top of the rays of Dark Aether that were also thundering down, ready to chain between the bodies of the three Grandmasters as many times as they could!","Many beings watched the unfolding of all of these skills as if they were in slow motion, the other fighting Celestials trying to make their way over to the position of the Infernal Lord, but they were kept at bay by their enemies so they could only watch!","BOOOOM!!!","A space rending cry erupted out as the eardrums of any nearby beings burst, the weaker ones dying from the impact right away as their brains turned to mush.","\"...\"","Silence reigned in the battlefield as the surrounding miles around the Infernal Lord were eerily quiet. A mountainous Infernal Lord of over 250 meters floated in space, surrounded by two Abyss Phoenixes and 3 World Rank Witch Slaves. In the mile around them, only the bloodied and lifeless bodies of numerous beings floated in the void of space.","\"...\"","The silence continued as the destructive energies around them cleared, the scene of where the three World Grandmaster used to be opening itself to the eyes of many as a horrendous sight played out. Portions of dismembered body parts could be seen in a gory show of blood and bones, the only thing remotely recognizable remaining being the disfigured body of Grandmaster Onillus.","He had lost half of his body as one could notice distinct golden lines of fate trying to recreate the other half unsuccessfully, his bloody mouth where a few teeth remained moving in an incoherent fashion as only the nearest being, Noah, could hear what he was saying.","\"...my name...was going to spread across the...Novus Galaxy.\"","Noah’s eyes coldly glanced at the World Rank Grandmaster that had appeared in the skies of the Celestial Realm not even two weeks ago. He was a whole realm higher than him then, with his strength seeming oppressive and out of reach. Yet this same being was lying disfigured in the void of space just a few days later, the time of his death nearing, and by his hands at that!","\"I- I read the flow of fate...it is not supposed to go this way...\"","The words seemed to be coming from a being that had his soul taken away, seeming devoid of any feeling and emotion as they just felt like ramblings. Noah looked forth as his eyes turned bright red, casting the wondrous ability of [Domination] on this heavily injured being as he spoke out.","\"Your name will not be remembered, and things rarely go the way we plan. You can die knowing you achieved nothing.\"","The light of Domination erupted out as it reflected on Onillus’s dead eyes, his muscles spasming as they calmed down completely thereafter, his soul completely being dominated!","Noah’s eyes then shone once more as he gave a command, the body of the World Rank Celestial Grandmaster exploding in a shower of blood that soon flowed towards him enticingly!","Celestials and those from the Dark Expanse alike watched in shock and horror as in a matter of minutes, three World Rank Experts were completely decimated, all that remained of them being bits of blood and bones.","...!"]},{"number":492,"title":"Chapter 492: Chapter 491 A Grand Symphony of Chaos I","paragraphs":["The death of three World Rank Experts all at once carried a heavy toll for the Celestial Legion, the eerie silence continuing for a few seconds before they all saw the body of the Infernal Lord...actually vibrating as it began to release an even more fearsome aura of power.","Incredulous looks appeared on Commanding Mage Turner and on the expressions of many of the beings of the battlefield, their faces simply carrying sheer disbelief and confusion at this point!","What they didn’t know was that the burst of power from Noah was coming from the fact that he was at this moment gaining hundreds of thousands of Fate Lines all at once from the deaths of the three World Rank Celestial Grandmasters!","This immense flow of strength that was given as comprehension of a Supreme Law made his already fearsome power feel even more oppressive, as the number he was gaining all at once was simply too much.","From Onillus alone, he was a being that held 3,505,800 Fate Lines. 12% of this was 420,696.","420,696 Fate Lines from Onillus alone!","The other two Grandmasters had Fate Lines ranging slightly above 2 million, each of them giving Noah around 300,000 Fate Lines. This was an addition of more than 1 million Fate Lines instantly, increasing the percentage next to the Law of Fate by another 10% as it now stood at 28%!!!","And this was only mentioning the benefits in the Law of Fate. There were also the invisible streams of light that was the loot from the bodies of the three World Rank beings that shot forth into Noah’s [Expansive Space] right away, granting him numerous World Rank Cores and techniques of the same realm. There was also the disorder caused by the death of these three beings bringing their own bursts of chaos as numerous Chaos Particles were converging towards Noah senselessly.","OOOOH!","The eerie silence everyone was enthralled in was broken as the Infernal Legion felt the grand movement of chaos energies, their bodies calling forth for more destruction as they resumed their slaughter!","\"Ready to Serve!\" \"Ready to Destroy!\"","RUMBLE!","Everyone was soon returned to the foray of the battlefield as the forces of the Celestial Legion were now fighting disorderly, the loss of three Grandmasters being horrendous.","RAA! RAA! RAA!","The Emperor Penguin moved with even more vigor when he saw his Master had taken down 3 World Rank Experts, his only thoughts at the moment being,","’Am I so weak that I cannot kill even one?!’","RAA!","His attacks became more relentless as the other Harbingers piled on with even more vigor, the four remaining Celestial Grandmasters finding themselves in tight battles as their hearts were now filled with terror!","This was because they knew that the single Infernal Lord who had taken down three of them was now free and alone on the battle field.","This meant...he would be moving to choose his next targets soon, and this act would hit the nail in the coffin for this battle!","It was even more horrendous as ridiculously, there were 5 figures at the World Rank standing protectively around the Infernal Lord who at this moment...raised his head as his eyes shone a splendor of deep red.","His body felt vigorous and coursing with strength, the feeling of nearing the 50% mark of a Supreme Law, even if 22% remained to get there, made him tremble with excitement as his eyes scanned the battlefield.","He saw the figures of fighting Harbingers, the Dark Wizard Shanora, Commanding Mage Turner, and even the Royal Vampyre Rokku. All of them were fighting their own battles as Noah had already finished his!","His eyes then turned to the scrambling remaining forces of Celestials that were near their Prime Warships, some of them already rushing towards them as fear had overcome them and they wanted to run.","His lips curled up in a smile as he did not want to let any loot escape his grasp, the cruel thought he had causing his body to teleport right away towards the Prime Warships that could destroy Worlds while sending commands to the Primal Spirits and Witch Slaves to go to different directions!","The fearfully scrambling figures of Celestials rushing to their Warships felt the descent of the overpowering aura as space instantly became destabilized, chaos beginning to rain down as a grand symphony of chaos continued!","The forces from the numerous Prime World watched on helplessly as even the beings that had taken them from their homes to fight were trying to flee, yet what could they do?","Defectors had already started to appear as they laid down their weapons when faced by the tens of thousands of forces from the Dark Expanse, with others being unlucky as those that were against the Infernal Legion or the terrible dragon Draco were cut down no matter if they were holding weapons or not!","This was a war, and war...War never changes!","It was a scene of carnage that one could call cruel, but it caused the battlefield to become even more bloody as in one region, another Grandmaster was about to fall.","The World Rank Expert surrounded by an arrogant Emperor Penguin and other armored figures had expended nearly all of his energy, his expression that of hopelessness as the battle was nearing its end the moment a World Rank Witch Slave began to head his way!","He began burning his Soul unwillingly for more strength, but this was the time when tens of Blades of Liberation from the Fate Item Sets that Kazuhiko and the others wore rushed down, as well as blinding suns from the Emperor Penguin, and numerous other final attacks raining down as the Harbingers wanted to finish the battle before the aid of their Master could even arrive.","BOOM!","The life of another World Rank Celestial Grandmaster was ended as the loot from him was distributed in rapid forms of light that shot into the bodies of those that had been attacking him, the ones dealing the most damage receiving Skill Books of the World Rank as well as Cores of the same level!","RAAA!","A victorious cry emerged from a particular Emperor Penguin as it spread across the void of space and acted like the sound of the horn of the end for the Celestial Legion!"]},{"number":493,"title":"Chapter 493: Chapter 492 A Grand Symphony of Chaos II","paragraphs":["The Founder was still calmly enjoying exquisite meats that came from the bodies of Supreme Behemoths while he sat alone in the expansive golden hall atop a regal chair.","As he saw the chaotic scenes of the battle where three World Rank Celestial Grandmasters had just lost their lives, all he did was pause briefly before bringing another piece of a glistening thigh towards his mouth, his mouth slowly moving in a soliloquy thereafter!","\"I see. So that’s what that feeling was all about.\"","His gaze was as apathetic as ever as he nodded, his eyes shining gold as they focused on the figure of the Infernal Lord that was now going around destroying the Prime Warships and any of those that wanted to board them, the eyes of the Founder also focusing on the figures of World Rank beings summoned by the Infernal Lord as the golden light only became brighter.","\"The coming of this so-called 9th Infernal Lord was touted as such a big thing by Fate, that his appearance meant the beginning of the Last War and blah blah blah. But isn’t this just subpar?\"","Shocking words of extreme disdain released from him easily as his eyes observed the movements of the Infernal Lord and uncovered numerous secrets!","\"Proficient in multiple laws, sure. Transformation abilities to boost his power output, and he’s even dabbling in the law of fate as well. All made possible by your intrusion I’m sure, but the final attack he used to take out those three weaklings is just a failure, don’t you think?\"","It felt like he was talking to himself, yet he also wasn’t at the same time as his eyes shone with splendor, analyzing things in a manner that very few would be able to in their entire lifetimes!","\"A final skill that summons 5 beings at the same rank as himself. Seems scary enough, but if you peel through all the bravado and falsehoods...you can see that these beings are simply husks with no souls nor any accomplishments in the universal laws. If this creature you’ve made ever comes near me with such failure of abilities, he’ll die right away you know? Although the abilities stemming from the law of Chaos seem proficient enough, but this really is a waste of my forces to test what exactly you would throw at me as I begin this Last War.\"","Words that would cause the sent Celestials to despair released from him, his thoughts revealing this initial Legion sent forth into the Dark Expanse being only a test to observe exactly what was in store for the coming war!","\"I must say, it was thoroughly disappointing. At this point, I think your best bet would have been to strengthen the old Infernal Lords and bring a few more of them up to the Nebula Realm. Maybe then they could match me in a worthy final battle before I break out of this cage. But this little present you’ve prepared? Hah!\"","Contempt was vibrant on his face as mysteries unknown to many unfolded from him, a slight smile appearing on his apathetic face as he enjoyed his sumptuous meal while watching a battle where thousands of beings from the Light Expanse and hundreds of his Celestials were dying every second!","Yet as all of this continued, indistinct Fate Line after Fate Lines were descending from the skies and coming to tightly wrap around him, his gaze not leaving the feed showing what was occurring at the Verittas Fortress as the decimation of his forces continued!","\"Your earlier moves were very cunning. Using love to turn one of my brothers against me and making the other lose all hope as he senselessly wanders along the Letalis Expanse. But this 9th Infernal Lord that Fate is being all bubbly about...ah let’s just watch and see, maybe there is still something I haven’t seen hmm?\"","The apathetic founder continued on with his monologues in the Celestial Realm as in a completely different location, in one of the most hellish Infernal Realms where the powerful Infernal Lords resided, a singular figure clad in a white robe was floating peacefully in the blazing red skies, their gaze happily watching a similar scene as the Founder as they observed with great interest!","The figure was dressed in a white robe that was an extremely stark contrast with the hellish and chaotic atmosphere of the Infernal Realm, but it seemed to be very fitting as it matched the flowing white hair and blue eyes of this being, the happy smile being one that would cause the hearts of many to flutter.","\"Not too shabby, but still a long way to go.\"","A clear and sonorous voice rang out from her as she changed her position, waving her hands towards the illusory screen showing the ongoing battle as it faded. To her, this battle was already considered finished, all that was left thereafter being the unfortunate scene of Chaos that came from these wars, blood continuing to flow freely in the vast expanse of space.","For the truly powerful figures of the Novus Galaxy that bothered to watch the scenes at the Verittas Fortress, the first battle of the long coming war was effectively over, and they had discerned a few important things from it.","One was the appearance of the 9th Infernal Lord foretold by Fate, the other was naturally the directions of the winds of victory of this war actually going to the side nobody expected- the Dark Expanse!","In the first battle initiated by the Celestials, it actually looked like they would be taking a huge loss!","The Grand Mage Edrusim was watching the ongoing scenes of the battle with a shocked smile as he laughed jovially, the Mage’s Tower he was in turning particularly rowdy as they observed the happenings of the Verittas Fortress.","In another location, the Vampyre Ruler Vladivostok should have also been happy, but he held a troubled expression as he saw the power of this Infernal Lord that was somehow connected to the Vampyre Ancestors.","He had to find out exactly what was going on around this issue, steeling his heart as his power at the Star Forging Realm exploded, setting out to confront this Infernal Lord right away for answers!","Some were joyful, some gaining a new sense of fear, but the results remained the same.","Back in the battlefield, the symphony of Chaos continued as Noah spread his senses out wide, sweeping it across the void of space as he confirmed not a single Celestial remained.","Complete massacre!","OOOH!","He sent a command to the Infernal Legion to stand down and stop needlessly taking the lives of the surrendering beings of the Prime Worlds that accompanied the Celestial Legion, his body that was thrumming with power settling down as he looked around to the only places where battles were still ongoing.","Only the single Celestial Grandmaster matched against the Dark Wizard Shanora still stood, all the other World Rank Grandmasters facing their death! It was actually Grandmaster Ramiel who controlled the 7th Celestial Star, his character being so meaningless that he was only being mentioned now, his defeat not even needing to be expressed with more words!","The only other World Rank Expert that stemmed from the Prime Worlds, Master Brightstar, had surrendered with his gaze that of confusion and despair as Commanding Mage Turner had his essence tightly binding him.","The World Rank Summons that Noah commanded had helped rapidly bring the battlefield into order, their entrance accelerating and stopping most of the battles as only a single World Rank Grandmaster remained, the gaze of Ramiel being that of despair as he felt the auras of numerous World Rank beings coming towards him!","Noah’s eyes focused on this remaining World Rank Grandmaster as his figure teleported right away, intent on fully finishing this grand battle as he counted the enormous gains!"]},{"number":494,"title":"Chapter 494: Chapter 493 Weak!","paragraphs":["The last World Rank Grandmaster from the Celestial Legion fell as the 9th Infernal Lord himself appeared hungrily in its hopeless battle with the reinforced Dark Wizard Shanora, the enormous palms of the Infernal Lord coming forth as they grasped onto the fearful body of the being that had all of his energy spent with his eyes shining the light of [Domination].","The World Rank Celestial that was already heavily exhausted stopped struggling in his palms as he pressed down, the uncomfortable sound of flesh and bones creaking ringing out as it resoundingly closed the chapter on the strongest opposing beings of this battle!","OOOOH!","\"Ready to Serve!\"","OOOOH!","\"Ready to Destroy!\"","OOOOH!","A cacophony of noises from the Infernal Legion was the only thing ringing out as others simply stared around in confusion, happiness, fearfulness, and terror!","Noah’s mountainous body rose high as the vibrant yells of the Infernals were all that reverberated, his gaze arrogantly overlooking the battlefield and the portions where thousands of golden robed Celestials were lifelessly floating.","He then looked towards the few Prime Warships that he had not destroyed as his figure rose towards them, his grandeur causing even the chanting Infernals to come to stop as his gaze stared towards the Warships...as if he could see the beings that were peering in!","Commanding Mage Turner looked towards this Infernal Lord with a shocked expression as he and many others knew what was about to happen as this powerful being looked out into the void of space. Did he...really plan to address the powerful experts watching this battle? Was he going to give a speech to boast of his victory while slapping the face of the higher ups among the Celestials?!","They watched with bated breaths as they waited to hear the words that this Infernal Lord would use to address the watching Celestials. The armored figure’s eyes shone a luminous red splendor as he opened his mouth and spoke in an extremely domineering and reckless manner.","\"Weak.\"","RUMBLE!","...!","Only a single word!","Weak!","A single word that was filled with arrogance and disdain, but it carried with it immense meaning as it shook the minds of all those that heard it, the Infernal Lord teleporting thereafter as he did not even bother to speak a single more word!","\"...\"","OOOOOH!","The feeling of victory only came after this shocking statement as many beings looked at each other.","\"We won...\"","\"We won!\"","\"Victorious!\"","Only after a while did the feelings of victory permeate throughout the forces of the Verittas Fortress, their gazes unbelievingly staring at each other as they hugged those near.","This was because for many of them, they had inscribed the terror of Celestials into their hearts, and knew that in this battle, they were very likely to die very cruel deaths!","Yet it was not them who had this fate today, but the Celestials themselves. The yells of Victors spread throughout the battlefield as those who surrendered stayed as quiet as possible, awaiting to see exactly what their fate would be.","The World Rank Experts fighting for the Verittas Fortress looked towards the mountainous Infernal Lord that was now waving his hands, the summoned World Rank beings leaving their sight as they then observed with shining eyes as he teleported around the void of space where tens of thousands of bodies of defeated Celestials and beings from the numerous Prime Worlds laid.","They saw the Infernal Lord appear beside these bodies as a red light erupted from him and washed over the bodies in droves, their eyes not fully understanding what they were seeing, but they prepared to take a look at their forces as well as the surrendering beings that numbered in the tens of thousands from numerous Prime Worlds of Light Expanse.","The red light they saw shining as Noah moved across the void of space littered with body was actually just him reading the memories of the dead beings, his mind already planning ahead multiple steps as the memories of thousands were something extremely valuable that he was planning on using in the near future!","His body continued to feel the descent of numerous Fate Lines and Chaos Particles, but his Fate Lines were so far ahead and still constantly changing that he felt his progression in the Law of Chaos would be left in the dust if he didn’t find a way to rapidly move the progression along like in the Law of Fate.","He glanced at his Stat Panel briefly as he teleported across the battlefield and read the memories of tens of thousands of dead beings, numerous unknown thoughts moving through him!","[Noah Osmont][Title(s): Infernal Lord(Variant)]","[Bloodline(s): Vampyre Progenitor(Awakening)]","[Fate Line(s) : 3,109,498]","[Chaos Particle(s) : 794,362]","[Origin Core(s) : Fire-3, Water-3]","[Domain(s) : Fate,Chaos, Space, Fire, Water]","[Vitality: WORLD]","[Focus: - ]","[Strength: WORLD]","[Law(s) : Fate-31%,Chaos-7.9%,Space-8%, Fire-37%, Water-37%]","His Fate Lines had ridiculously risen by more than 2 million in just this single battle, his heart seeing this as the biggest boon as it actually made him look forward to even more battles like this!","The number of Chaos Particles had stably rocketed to close to 800,000, their number also rising rapidly from the chaos and destruction that was carried out in this battle.","RAA! RAA!","The Emperor Penguin was arrogantly rising in the void of space victoriously as he was followed by the other Harbingers and a mountainous Draco, their eyes set on their Master as he moved across the void of space collecting the memories of thousands.","They weren’t the only ones watching closely, the World Rank Royal Vampyre Rokku along with his forces...were also looking towards him with a difficult expression!","This was because they saw too many things that pointed to secrets of Ancient Vampyres from this Infernal Lord, but they couldn’t bring themselves to go forward and ask as the oppressive air this Infernal Lord released was heavy.","They also had a sense of intuition that told them...something big would change the moment they wanted this mystery to be addressed!","But the current forces of Vampyres at the Verittas Fortress did not have to fear, because the Vampyre Ruler himself, the being that oversaw the many Vampyre Clans in the Dark Expanse...was rushing over here at this instant to solve this mystery himself!"]},{"number":495,"title":"Chapter 495: Chapter 494 At least it will be fun!","paragraphs":["In the unknown location in the Celestial Realm, the Founder wiped his mouth with a sigh of contentment reminiscent of someone that had a really good meal, his eyes watching the fading figure of the Infernal Lord as the battle at the Verittas Fortress wrapped up.","To him, this event actually did not seem to hold much significance, the biggest emotion he released out of all it actually stemming from the lustrous meats of the Supreme Behemoths he was enjoying while watching the battle!","\"Weak, huh?\"","He held a smiling expression that looked extremely eerie with his eyes that never released an ounce of emotion themselves, numerous thoughts crossing his mind as he thought about his life.","Weakness...was actually not a familiar feeling for him, his heart not having felt it for quite some time!","Even now he only curiously thought about it, as it was not even in his mind that he would ever feel such an emotion again. This was because he knew too many things! He had achieved too much! Lastly...he had a very clear goal that was very much within his reach!","Thus, fear was not something that he ever thought about, this recent loss at the Verittas Fortress only further giving him more information that would go towards building the future he wanted to create.","\"With such a character of an Infernal Lord joining in, at least it will be fun.\"","He left behind such words as his figure turned into particles of light, moving from this location to another as he went to lead his people that were currently reeling from the shock of a loss right now!","The Celestials across the numerous Celestial Stars were receiving the news or had watched it with their own eyes in anger and horror, watching the complete obliteration of their forces as not a single one of them managed to return.","The Celestials in the 7th Celestial Star were left without a leader momentarily, Grandmaster Ramiel’s life being taken as easily as all the other Grandmasters. This student that had left a golden prison deep beneath this Celestial Star...would never get to return as he faced eternal darkness!","In the hidden underground prison on this 7th Celestial Star, the pierced figure who had revealed himself as the Karmic Sect Leader to Noah, also the being that was known as one of the Founders of the Celestials- was actually sighing with a sad smile as he sensed the passing of his disciple.","\"Which one of us ever knows what fate has in store?\"","He posed a question to nobody as on this particular day, his face was brighter than normal. This was because what little calculations he could do right now told him that with the beginning of the Last War...fate was moving rapidly once more as the shackles that bound him would soon be no more.","The person responsible for releasing him had taken his time, but one could never rush the workings of fate, as things would always occur when they were meant to.","He was reminiscing in his golden prison when at the next moment, he heard bustling movements beginning to spread out all around the 7th Celestial Star, the beings dwelling within moving with vigor as his ears perked up.","What the chained being found was the forces of this Celestial Star being riled up, having received commands that came directly from the Founder for them to prepare! His eyes shone with a bright light as he continued to observe the happenings of this Celestial Star, trying to foresee the future as this incidence was not just occurring on the 7th Celestial Star!","All across the Light Expanse and in the Celestial Realm, the millions of Celestials had received a single command from the Founder in response to the colossal first loss at the Verittas Fortress. That command was for all of them to prepare and be ready!","For the sake of bringing Order and Balance in the Universe, the loss of a single Celestial Legion could be overlooked. What they needed to do now was prepare to not just send out a single Legion, but form hundreds of Celestial Legions that would be placed under the command of worthy Generals.","In the mind of the Founder, the inconsequential loss at the Verittas Fortress was nothing, and the full war would begin soon as movements were underway to move billions of forces from the Light Expanse, place them into hundreds of Legions under the command of Celestials, and then use this terrifying force to head towards the Dark Expanse.","What was happening now was them entering into a period of an actual full scale war, a war of attrition that would span for who knew how long!","RUMBLE!","Waves of fate and chaos continued to flow through the river of time, the tides of war being fanned as those in the Dark Expanse knew what was coming.","The Grand Mage Edrusim and the Infernal Lords knew full well the strength of the Celestials, their forces being prepared in earnest as they did not let this single victory lul them into a feeling of power.","It was not a single victory that would decide the course of this war, but a balance on wins and losses over the span of months or years- how ever long it took before a deciding event took place to end this Last War.","Two of the forces who could be considered the leading figures of the Dark Expanse were now actively moving, primely being The Grand Mage Edrusim and the Infernal Lords. There was another figure that stood at the peak of the Star Forging Realm similar to Edrusim who at this point in time was not actually rallying the numerous Vampyre Clans spread out in the Dark Expanse, but he was actually nearing the Verittas Fortress to confront the 9th Infernal Lord for the mystery of why he had the abilities of Ancient Vampyres, and find out exactly what the connection was!"]},{"number":496,"title":"Chapter 496: Chapter 495 A Star Forging Expert Arrives","paragraphs":["Noah’s mountainous form had reduced as he floated in the void of space, his eyes overlooking the tens of thousands of bodies floating in a mess of bloody gore. The Harbingers were clustered around him as they sensed their Master’s introspective look, Barbatos and Kazuhiko being the ones that could still bypass the aura that Noah released to be the ones actually conversing with him at this time.","\"We’ve come a long way, little fish.\"","The fiery Barbatos had gradually become more and more docile over time, her gaze currently shaking incredulously as she observed their surroundings with sparkling eyes.","When she chose to betray her own kind and follow Noah, she had done it for her own selfish reasons of wanting to be free to do whatever she wanted, and she had thoroughly enjoyed her time since then to the point where she still could not believe it.","Traveling wondrous worlds and being a part of a unique one that was unlike anything she had ever experienced before. Enjoying the ridiculously talented being’s company and food, as well as achieve a realm of power that was out of her wildest imagination.","All of it was made possible by her decision to follow this single man, and now she floated in the void of space of the Dark Expanse, having just stood against a powerful being at an entire stage above her as she and those working with her achieved victory.","It was unbelievable, surreal, and most of all exciting!","Her wild heart was feeling calmer and calmer as she experienced so many things the past few months, her gaze towards the bloody void of space actually holding a tinge of happiness.","Behind her, the hidden face of Elena that was filled with wild fanaticism glanced at Noah, numerous thoughts crossing through her mind that only she knew! At this point in time, another voice resounded out to the right of Noah.","\"I just want something at least similar to the abilities you have. Come on, what skill tree did you unlock that gives you chaining chaos lasers? Or the abilities in the Blood Lord skill tree, I should at least be able to get those? Right?\"","Kazuhiko was looking at Noah in an imploring tone as he had observed the spectacular abilities he released to decimate the Celestials, wanting the same for himself as he also wanted to dominate the battlefield in such a way!","\"Haha, I’ll tell you the route I followed for Blood Lord, you should be able to reach it if you can raise your proficiency fast enough.\"","Noah laughed as he replied and stopped staring at the bloody expanse of space, looking at Kazuhiko and Barbatos as these were the few figures who could still converse with him with ease, reminding him that he still had those he could comfortably talk to and even joke around with!","He glanced at the rest of the Harbingers that were no doubt reveling in the victory as they counted their spoils of the battle, sending his thoughts across as he saw the forces of the Verittas Fortress look towards them.","\"You guys head back to the Spiritual World first, I’ll deal with everything else here.\"","The Harbingers ascertained his words as the numerous figures around him began to disappear one by one, where he was soon only left with the silent but sharpened Infernal Legion that floated powerfully in the expanse of space.","He sent a command for them to remain stationary as he went towards the figures of Commanding Mage Turner, the Dark Wizard Shanora, and the Royal Vampyre Rokku who was looking at him while constantly fidgeting.","These three World Rank experts had been cleaning up the battlefield while ascertaining the losses and taking care of the tens of thousands from the forces of the Prime Worlds that had surrendered, the fate of these beings that were not necessarily blameless in the war but could still be considered victims being treated in a very humane manner!","Some of them fully believed in the propaganda of the Celestials and came to the Dark Expanse with that purpose, others were skeptical and only came along because the Celestials oversaw the Light Expanse and could not really be told no when they gave a directive.","There would have to be clear distinctions in the future in how forces such as this would be handled, as those in the Dark Expanse could not just open themselves up to attacks or not defend themselves against those that didn’t have the title of Celestials but still participated in the war nonetheless.","Noah had his own thoughts for the future as he glanced at the spread forces of crestfallen beings, the memories he had collected for those that died from the many Prime Worlds set aside to be used for something grand in the near future!","\"I have to give you our heartfelt gratitude for helping us keep control of the Verittas Fortress and not allow the Celestials further into the Dark Expanse, O Infernal Lord.\"","Commanding Mage Turner had began speaking to him in a much more respectful tone than before as he neared, the other World Rank experts actually turning mute as they could not even bring themselves to address him!","Noah nodded towards them as his mission here was finished, where he would soon go back to report to the Infernal Realm. His gaze landed on the Royal Vampyre as he had an entirely separate train of thought about this being and the tens of thousands of Vampyres that still stood behind him, all of them having quizzical expressions as they looked towards him but neither of them bringing themselves to say anything.","Noah knew his display of abilities of the heavily advanced Blood Lord skill tree would catch the attention of the huge faction of Vampyres in the Dark Expanse, and he had done this intentionally as he waited to see if they would be provoked enough to move, his bloodline allowing him immense leeway when it came to Vampyres!","His red eyes turned to the Royal Vampyre Rokku as he decided he might as well begin with the Vampyres here, but at this moment, the aura of a powerful being began to descend onto the Verittas Fortress.","...!","The gazes of the World Rank experts moved as they looked up in shock, noticing a red streak of light barreling forth towards them as their bodies unconsciously moved their essence in case it was a new enemy, but they calmed down as they sensed the descending aura that felt more and more familiar.","RUMBLE!","It brought with it space rumbling majesty as the figure of aged but devilishly handsome Vampyre appeared in the void of space above the Verittas Fortress. Bright silver hair running down to his shoulders and shockingly red eyes that showed experience and age glanced around. His eyes were squinting as he locked them towards the tens of thousands of Vampyres, and then towards the being they were all wondering about!","OOOM!","His power wildly flew out as it announced grandly- the Star Forging Realm being, the Vampyre Ruler Vladivostok, had arrived!","Noah’s eyes glanced at this being calmly as a rumbling voice rolled out from the aged face.","\"I’ll have to take some of your time to ascertain a few things, O 9th Infernal Lord.\"","...!"]},{"number":497,"title":"Chapter 497: Chapter 496 Kneel!","paragraphs":["The Grand Mage Edrusim had already stopped watching the feed of the Verittas Fortress as he continued to be increasingly busy, numerous communications reaching him as he sent back even more commands to start getting the forces of the Dark Expanse ready.","He was in the middle of glancing at an enormous Star Chart which outlined the numerous stars littering the Dark Expanse, observing how he could possibly move the forces and their distribution in order to withstand the coming legions of Celestials.","He was one of the key figures who had to work and communicate with the Infernal Lords, know the movements of the clans of Vampyres, as well as manage the Mages and Wizards that were spread out across the Dark Expanse.","He was extremely busy after watching this first battle, and it was why his mood turned extremely sour when he received the news that in the Verittas Fortress where the battle had just wrapped up, the leading figure of Vampyres, Vladivostok, had appeared to confront the 9th Infernal Lord!","\"You fool, you better not sow discord right at the cusp of a war!\"","He uttered out as he also recalled the abilities he had observed from the Infernal Lord that seemed extremely similar to those from the Vampyre Clans, but he did not think they would be something major that would cause this being at the Star Forging Realm to move.","\"Bah, watch things here, I’ll be right back.\"","He sent a command to the Commanding Mages around him as his figure shimmered with the color of stars, disappearing from the Mage Tower as he also now went towards the Verittas Fortress, hoping that one of the leading figures of the Dark Expanse would not sour the relationships between the Infernal Lords!","---","The three World Rank experts from the Verittas Fortress looked towards the appearing Vampyre Ruler, Vladivostok, as their eyes opened wide in shock!","The peak Star Forging Realm being at the cusp of entering the ultimate realm in the Novus Galaxy had actually made himself appear in front of them, with his attention directed towards the brightly shining Infernal Lord.","They recalled the numerous skills that this fearsome being had displayed on the battlefield as they made some connections, watching to see exactly what hidden mysteries were about to unfold.","But they would not get a chance to, as they tensed while observing the Infernal Lord not send a single word of reply, his expression calm as if nothing had happened while he glanced at Vladivostok!","A trace of anger seemed to appear on the Star Forging being’s face, but he tried not to show it as he had to first get to the bottom of why this Infernal Lord had the abilities of Ancient Vampyres.","Vladivostok glanced at Rokku who was standing by the side awkwardly, his face shaking at this behavior as he glanced at the other World Rank beings by the side watching on in anticipation. He waved his hands and cast forth a [Blood World] to make sure whatever mystery he was about to uncover remains hidden, the expanding bloody domain going on to cover him and the figure of the Infernal Lord who still had not made a single move or uttered any words!","OOOM!","Those in the surroundings watched as a Blood World fully encased the newly arriving ruler of Vampyres as well as the Infernal Lord, whatever anticipation for them finding out the mysteries shattered as their senses could not even penetrate to see what was happening within.","Inside the blood world, Vladivostok spoke once again, this time with a more firm tone as he recalled the levels of power between him and this Infernal Lord.","\"I do not intend to cause any conflicts with the Infernals, and am only curious about the abilities that only our Ancestors knew that you have freely displayed. This is especially so because of your...unique Origin that I had to come.\"","His words were not looking down in any way as he knew the status of an Infernal Lord and what it signified, but he was still talking in manner of a senior talking to a junior because of their levels of power!","Noah glanced at this being at the Star Forging Realm as he actually adopted a light smile. This was because when he stared at this powerful being a rank above him...he actually felt not even an ounce of threat.","This was because his bloodline, his very origin- told him that this being was considered nothing more than another Vampyre in the eyes of the one holding the bloodline of the Progenitor!","One must recall that this was the Ruler overseeing the faction of Vampyres in the entirity of the Dark Expanse! This was a Star Forging Realm expert, someone that was a step away from the highest realm that anybody had achieved in the Novus Galaxy...","Noah glanced at the Vampyre that was the central figure of the numerous Vampyre Clans in the Dark Expanse as he spoke out calmly.","\"You come in front of me and do not even acknowledge me, nor do you show the respect of a junior to their Senior. Are you looking to be stripped of all your power and strength?\"","\"...!\"","Vladivostok had a startled expression as he heard ones he never expected, turning his head to the side as he wanted to confirm he heard correctly- his face gaining a trace of anger thereafter as he now spoke out while freely releasing his vibrant power.","\"I have been nothing but polit-\"","\"Do not speak.\"","RUMBLE!","In the middle of his sentence, Vladivostok was cut off as he heard the words of the 9th Infernal Lord once more, but this time around, they actually held a tinge of authority...authority that actually caused his mouth to unconsciously close!","...!","His heart shook as at this moment as he wanted to speak, but he found he was unable to! At this instant, his mind moved at extremely high speeds as he was being guided towards a shocking and terrifying conclusion as his eyes dilated more and more while he looked at the figure of the 9th Infernal Lord.","To him, an aura had begun leaking out of the being in front of him, an aura that made his very origin shake as a thought arrived in his mind that told him the truth, but he still could not believe it as his mind felt like it was exploding!","Noah moved closer and closer to the Vampyre Ruler as he floated until he was just a few inches from his face, glancing towards him with cold eyes as he understood the bloodline system of the Vampyres was really absolute. This being with a rank higher than him, could actually not do a single thing to harm him! He glanced at the shaking eyes as he spoke out with a tone befitting the ruling figure of a certain race, causing the shock of Vladivostok to only increase thereafter.","\"Kneel.\"","RUMBLE!","A simple word, a single command.","THUD!","Even though they were in the starry and dark void of space, the sound akin to someone’s knees hitting the floor resounded as Vladivostok’s body involuntarily kneeled, his thoughts finally being affirmed as the eyes of this Star Forging Being looked up towards the red glistening eyes of someone extremely special to the race of Vampyres!","\"Kneel, and properly welcome your Progenitor.\"","...!"]},{"number":498,"title":"Chapter 498: Chapter 497 A Master and Servan","paragraphs":["Vladivostok finally felt his mouth having the ability to move again as he glanced up towards Noah with a shaking face holding an unbelievable expression within the wide Blood World the two of them were in. His silver hair danced wildly atop his aged head, his facial muscles nearly spasming at the shock.","\"H-how...Ah!\"","He uttered beneath his breath only for a second before his seasoned mind adapted and he looked back down, speaking out with a shaking voice that held a tinge of respect and fear!","\"Thi- this lowly servant greets the Progenitor, and hopes you will grant me mercy of for my actions!\"","The Star Forging Vampyre Ruler hurriedly blurted out words nobody would ever expect to hear him say to someone an entire realm above him, but as the Vampyre felt his bloodline begin to boil just because he was near this being, his disbelieving thoughts finally settled as he admitted to himself that somehow, unbelievably- this Infernal Lord in front of him actually held the Bloodline of the Progenitor, a being with the purest bloodline of his race!","He did not understand why or how, but he knew it to be so! He remained on the ground as his body shook, the shock and fear he felt gradually wiping away as it soon began to turn into a sense of...excitement.","\"Rise. I’ll take the time to discuss many things with you later, but if you have made your way here, so will others soon.\"","Noah glanced at this being that was going through one emotion to another as he spoke, Vladivostok rising as his disbelieving expression was completely wiped away, now looking at Noah with an expression of reverence as his mind finally felt like it was moving freely again and he understood the importance of the Progenitor standing in front of him.","This was the Progenitor himself! His appearance here meant a great deal of things for Vampyres, as he was the singular leader of their race!","Vladivostok forgot all about his bearing of a Star Forging expert, of a being that had been overseeing the many Vampyre Clans in the Dark Expanse as he knew in front of the being with the purest bloodline, realms of power made no difference!","His heart did not feel any sense of weirdness or unwillingness the moment he affirmed the being in front of him really was the Progenitor, his tone even trying to be more servile as he spoke towards him.","\"I had no idea of your coming, O Progenitor, but it can only mean for a grand future for all of us. My rash coming here will most likely cause someone like Edrusim to come by. What are your commands?\"","A voice akin to that of a servant asking their master rang out, Noah glancing at this being as he felt the vibrant power of the Blood Progenitor grant him utter control of a being an entire realm above him.","He had many plans in mind on how he should move forward before the full scale war broke out, and he had a great deal of things to get done before then, but now he also had the Vampyres of the Dark Expanse on his plate! He thought of the skill trees to advance, the planets to connect to, and the numerous fantastic things like the upgrade of a world or worlds into a realm, his mind moving as he chose a certain point in time to fit the Vampyres as well!","\"Gather the Vampyre Clans of the Dark Expanse, their leading figures, and their most powerful forces in a week and then send me the coordinates. At that time, I will descend to properly take a look at the powerful beings of my race that have only become a mere faction of the Dark Expanse.\"","The more he spoke, the more respectful and servile the Star Forging being in front of him became, his next words causing a reaction that confirmed Noah’s choice to add the Vampyres of the Dark Expanse on his to do list even with all the things he had to do.","\"Yes, Master!\"","RUMBLE!","From Noah’s body, glimmering gold and dark essence were released as they went to wash over the now excited Vladivostok, who had heard a command to gather the Vampyres together to acknowledge their Progenitor!","This would be a momentous event of their race, something that had not happened in more than a thousand years!","His excitement only rose higher as just from being near the Progenitor, he could feel his body gaining more and more strength, this being not realizing that he was now considered a subordinate of Noah and fit the specifications of the Guider Type abilities that Noah always had active.","His body felt the unique energy of chaos as he understood that, but he was even more shocked to sense the freely flowing aura of fate as he gave the Progenitor an even more incredulous look, but did not raise a single question as he stood up, sensing the aura of a being he knew to well come from a distance.","Seeing the demeanor of the Progenitor, Vladivostok understood his wishes to remain in secrecy for now as he spoke out.","\"I will clear my mistake here first with no issues, O Progenitor, and let you know as soon as I complete your command!\"","His voice was strong as he spoke out like someone that would do whatever it took to accomplish the goal given. There was not an ounce of pride or arrogance for his mighty status of a Star Forging Expert, nor any status of a Ruler that had been overseeing billions of beings over the past hundred years. In front of the Bloodline power that was the purest, all of these distinctions were wiped away!","Noah nodded towards this powerful being as the Blood World around them began to fade.","Seeing the aura of fate and chaos descend into the body of Vladivostok, Noah confirmed that the future event with the Vampyres would have their own abundant rewards, where he only imagined the millions of powerful Vampyres who could actually fight in the war fitting the conditions to be his subordinates and gaining the boosts of the Guider Type abilities!","This would be something that would heavily influence the Dark Expanse, as well as the direction of the War that involved the lives of trillions.","To him, all this translated to was...more Fate Lines and Chaos Particles, and especially abundant ones at that as it would steer the direction of numerous powerful beings, unlike the weak ones on the numerous planets he was currently connected to!","RUMBLE!","The Blood World fully disappeared as those outside of it looked in, seeing Noah floating in the void of space calmly as Vladivostok was near him, his face seemingly trying to be serious, but one could distinctly see the trace of happiness and excitement in his red eyes.","Vladivostok glanced at the surrounding figures as he saw the materialization of the Grand Mage Edrusim in the distance with a dark face, his figure going towards this leading figure of the Dark Expanse as he telepathically bid farewell to the Progenitor.","Noah glanced at the Grand Mage he had yet to interact with, Vladivostok’s figure shooting towards this Mage instantly as he began speaking out and the face of the Grand Mage gradually calmed down.","Commanding Mage Turner, the Dark Wizard Shanora, and the incredulous Royal Vampyre Rokku were still on the side with agape expression as even now they did not understand what had just happened.","Noah glanced at Rokku and the tens of thousands of Vampyres behind him, his eyes shining as he looked forward to seeing a scene of millions of Vampyres as he sent a telepathic message to Commanding Mage Turner bidding his farewell for now, and sending another command for the Infernal Legion to head back to the Infernal Gate that led to the second Realm of Hell!","OOOOH!","\"Ready to serve!\"...","The chants of the Infernals resounded yet again as they made their way across the void of space, Noah leaving the cleaning up of the battlefield and the handling of the numerous beings from the Light Expanse to the Verittas Fortress, his mind already planning his moves the moment he returned to the Infernal Realm.","\"Ah...\"","He heard the voice of the Dark Wizard Shanora that had mentioned she wanted to discuss something with him after the battle, but he paid it no heed as he already had too many things on his plate, his discernment with Fate Traverse telling him it would simply be something else that required him to put a significant amount of time into, and it was time that he actually did not have.","He left Vladivostok to deal with the entrance of a Grand Mage as he took his forces away, bidding farewell to the location of the first battle that had granted him more than 2 million Fate Lines, his heart looking forward into the future as he moved forward!","Those left behind at the Verittas Fortress were only left with incredulousness and confusion as they asked themselves- just who exactly was this 9th Infernal Lord?"]},{"number":499,"title":"Chapter 499: Chapter 498 What Noble Fate?!","paragraphs":["In the Golden Bastion of the Celestial Realm where the 4 Geniuses were placed in to finish their training, a dark skinned girl was repeatedly watching the scenes of the recent battle at Verittas Fortress over and over again.","Her eyes were cold and filled with fighting intent as she watched a certain Infernal Lord move across the battlefield in a dominant manner, not a single creature being able to stand in his path as he obliterated anyone he came across.","She watched as this Infernal Lord caused the body of the Celestial Grandmaster that had presided over the tournament not too long ago, someone they looked up to with reverence because of their strength- she watched this being’s body exploded like a balloon with just a gesture of the Infernal Lord!","Athena glanced at this scene and the numerous other scenes as essence began converging around her body, a multitude of thoughts flowing through her mind as her Origin was unknowingly bubbling with power.","When she looked at these scenes, she did not feel any fear or horror that others would feel, nor did she feel sad or have a sense of loss at the perishing of an entire Celestial Legion. She very strongly believed in fate, and knew that it was simply the fate of those that perished to do so, their sacrifices only acting as stairs to elevate their battle to bring order and balance in an even greater fashion!","What she felt the most was actually the emotion of unwillingness and competitiveness as she looked at the figure of the Infernal Lord, ingraining it in her mind as she asked herself many questions.","She was someone that was a genius in Fate, and even held the title of a being with Noble Fate. Yet, why was it so that her power did not even match someone like her junior brother who had ascended to the World Realm? With her title, how could she be so useless that when she looked at her power and compared herself to the newly rising 9th Infernal Lord- she knew she would not even stand a chance and would be killed even faster than the dead Grandmasters!","She felt unwillingness as she looked at her very Origin and asked- why would someone with her title not have power at this level?!","RUMBLE!","Essence continued to madly converge around her as the unwillingness she felt to her core was further boosted by her battle intent as she looked at the spectacular scenes of battle, her origin madly absorbing essence as the War Princess was unconsciously raising her realm by the sheer strength of her will!","She had been enjoying numerous treasures for achieving her rank in the Tournament, even though it was nothing near the effectiveness of the [Luminescent Rainbow Dews] that Crixus and the Three-Eyed Fate Child received, she and Grandmaster Light were given numerous Elite Behemoth Materials at the World rank and even Cores of that same rank for each of them in an effort to further accelerate their realms.","Her body that was already drenched in absorbing those treasures was now madly absorbing even more essence as time passed, her rank nearing the peak of the Domain Expansion Realm as she wanted to break through to the World Realm by sheer willpower alone!","This was something only a genius holding the title of someone with a Noble Fate could do, something that only the War Princess with her strong lust for battle and unique title could achieve. As essence raged around her, she screamed in her heart for more strength, her rank continuing to shoot up as she inscribed the face of the 9th Infernal Lord to her heart.","This was the type of strength she aspired to have, so she would simply go forward to achieving it. When she did, she wanted to stand against this Infernal Lord to really test what Fate had in store for her.","She would either perish or rise above as she really lived up to the title of having a Noble Fate.","Otherwise, if she remained this weak- what use was there for her having such a title?!","RUMBLE!","---","As one genius tried making a breakthrough and enter a higher realm, an even more monstrous genius had returned to the Infernal Realm as Azula looked towards him with an exasperated expression.","This was because when Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone first entered the Infernal Realm to accept the Letter of Summons, he had shown his rank to be at the Domain Realm!","Yet when he went to battle, he revealed power at the World Rank, the same realm where the 8th and 7th Infernal Lord stood at, and now this 9th Infernal Lord returned triumphantly after wiping the floor with an entire Celestial Legion.","Azula shook her head unbelievably as she could not even bring herself to stay near this monstrous genius, returning to her castle as she wanted to increase her power even by little before the numerous Celestial Legions began making their way across the Novus Galaxy.","Noah stationed the Infernal Legion that was under his command as their eyes remained on his leaving figure, these Infernals actually feeling a strong bond with the swirling chaos that always followed this Infernal Lord!","Having completed his task as the 9th Infernal Lord, he moved to reap the full benefits of the battle as his body changed out of the shape of a crowned Infernal Lord and returned to his normal one, teleporting to a certain region in the Light Expanse.","He appeared somewhere in the starry expanse of space as his gaze landed upon a particular Prime World, this world holding no special identity besides the fact that it was one of the many worlds in the memories that he absorbed from the defeated figures of beings from the numerous Prime Worlds that made up the forces of the Celestial Legion.","One of the bigger rewards he reaped out of the recent battle were these memories of thousands of beings...memories that he planned to use to connect numerous powerful worlds of the Light Expanse to himself as they forever disappeared from the eyes of everyone!","He would also use this time to obtain the required World Core for the upgrade of the Spiritual World as the first requirement of Domain Rank beasts had been met, only this single requirement remaining.","With the goal of amassing more worlds to himself and looking forward to another world-shaking upgrade of one of the most unique treasures he owned, his eyes shone with a golden luster as his figure silently streaked towards the Prime World in front of him to get started!"]},{"number":500,"title":"Chapter 500: Chapter 499 Plucking Stars With Ease!","paragraphs":["As Noah’s Ancient Blood Clone started the connection of more worlds to expand the source of his strength even more, his main body was finishing a battle with a Supreme Behemoth in the deep unexplored regions of the Celestial Realm!","RUMBLE!","The World Rank Behemoth that was shimmering with golden light and shaped like a four-headed golden lion slumbered to the ground after falling to the horrendous attacks laced with the essence of Chaos and Aether, Noah gaining another mountainous body brimming with wondrous materials, and this time it was from a beast that was actually at the World Realm. The numerous loot for the Behemoth rushed to his [Expansive Space] as he waved his hands to cause the mountainous body to disappear.","Aside from using its materials to craft new Item Sets, the meat was extremely sumptuous to enjoy as it contained abundant essence! In conjunction with his [Cook] ability that made everything he touched into something tastier than even the food from 5-star restaurants, his time exploring the Celestial Realm had been extremely enjoyable.","This was the 4th World Rank Behemoth that he had come across in these unknown regions, where he also came across treasures in the form of fruits that rejuvenated one’s energy or came across regions that were filled with Fate Essence and conducive to training.","But soon enough, he would have an entire region filled with Fate and Chaos Essence to himself as he upgraded the Spiritual World and unlocked the next features of the Law Space, so he momentarily stopped his exploration as he calculated a better pathway to follow with the abilities of <<Herald of Fate>>!","SHAA!","In front of his eyes, a being with his original body teleported in as he waved his hands forward, a sparkling miniaturized Spiritual World flowing towards him as the clone that was currently connecting numerous worlds came to hand him the unique treasure and disappeared thereafter to continue his tasks.","This handoff of the Spiritual World to the main body while the clone continued the world connections was for Noah to use this time to steer fate towards the best direction that Fate told him to follow.","From the use of the skills under <<Herald of Fate>>, he saw once more that to increase his power the fastest while swallowing up the many things throwing themselves at him, he had to focus on a particular skill tree first, followed by the upgrade of the Spiritual World, and then he had to finally get to freeing the being that was being held in the 7th Celestial Star!","RUMBLE!","Waves of essence silently stretched out as the miniaturized Spiritual World was placed on the glimmering grass of the Celestial Realm, Noah’s figure disappearing within it as he entered the Time Space to begin right away.","The skill tree he had to focus on was actually not the [Fate’s Guardian] or [Arch Lich Ra’Zan] skill trees that were still at Soul Rank, but the [Blood Lord] skill tree that he just recently brought to the Domain Tier with the addition of Fledgling Blood Ancient!","His focus was actually directed to this right away, and he had the capability to bring it to the World Rank since he just obtained numerous sacrificial skills of that rank to use, all that was left being their requirement of proficiency as he began spamming the abilities to bring them up right away.","His Ancient Blood Clone that had just transferred the Spiritual World over to him teleported to another location in the Light Expanse, continuing the process of entering deep into the cores of these worlds as he established connections with them and then used the World Engine to teleport them vast distances across space in the quadrant where his homeworld was.","Many stars were being added to this expansive corner of Light Expanse as all of them were veiled deeply, never to be found unless someone powerful was actively passing around and looking!","He was plucking stars left and right as his movements would soon cause commotion in the already tense Light Expanse as the disappearance of numerous Prime Worlds began to gain notice.","These actions that Noah was currently undertaking were bold, but he made countless calculations as he affirmed to himself in these times of a chaotic war, the disappearance of a few planets will only be a drop in the bucket, never garnering the attention of Celestials for them to bother looking into it, and even if they did the chances of them finding anything were extremely minimal.","Thus, days passed as the clone continued the connections while looking out for a Large World to obtain a core of in a smooth manner, the main body staying within the Time Space of the Spiritual World as he got ready to upgrade the first skill tree into the World Rank!","In these past days, the regions of the Light Expanse became particularly active as Celestials began moving to amass the forces of being above Void Rank to add to their Legions, this time the process being carried out orderly and carefully as the full-scale war that would begin thereafter would be unlike anything that had happened before.","It would be a large scale attack across many regions of the Dark Expanse, with many battles being fought as the Celestials would either win many and advance further into the Dark Expanse while gaining control of more regions in the Novus Galaxy, or if the repeat of the first battle is to occur, their advancement might be halted!","Righteous fervor and strength filled the minds of the Celestials as they looked forward to wiping off the stain of losing the first battle, their hearts calling out for more order and balance as numerous Celestial Legions were being created every passing day.","In the Time Space, more than 3 months had passed with the passage of just a few days outside, Noah’s main body shining brightly as he stopped the constant casting of numerous abilities and opened his eyes sharply.","The time had arrived for the first World Rank Skill Tree!"]}]);
